import { useState, useEffect, useMemo, useRef } from "react";

const CHAPTERS = ["Arjuna's Despair", "The Yoga of Knowledge", "The Yoga of Action", "Knowledge & Renunciation of Action", "The Yoga of Renunciation", "The Yoga of Meditation", "Knowledge & Realization", "The Imperishable Absolute", "The Royal Knowledge", "Divine Glories", "The Vision of the Cosmic Form", "The Yoga of Devotion", "The Field & the Knower", "The Three Qualities", "The Supreme Self", "Divine & Demonic Natures", "The Threefold Faith", "Liberation through Renunciation"];
const CHAP_INTRO = [
"The battlefield of Kurukṣetra. Arjuna asks Krishna to drive his chariot between the two armies — and seeing teachers, cousins, and friends on both sides, he breaks down and refuses to fight. The Gītā begins not with an answer but with an honest collapse: grief and confusion are the doorway to the whole teaching.",
"Krishna's first response, and the Gītā in seed form: the Self is unborn and undying — bodies change like worn-out clothes. Then the turn to action: your right is to the work alone, never to its fruits. The chapter closes with the portrait of the person of steady wisdom, unshaken in pleasure and pain.",
"If wisdom is the goal, why act at all? Because no one can remain actionless for even a moment, Krishna answers — so act, but without attachment, as an offering. Better your own duty done imperfectly than another's done well; and know the real enemies: desire and the anger it becomes.",
"Krishna reveals how old this teaching is, and why he returns: whenever dharma declines, age after age, he comes. Action can be done as sacrifice, and knowledge is the fire that burns karma to ash. The way in: reverence, sincere questioning, and service to those who have seen.",
"Which is better — renouncing action, or acting selflessly? Both arrive, Krishna says, but the path of engaged, unattached action is surer. True renunciation is inward: the sage acts while remaining untouched, like a lotus leaf resting on water.",
"The practical manual of meditation: a steady seat, moderation in food and sleep, the mind held like a flame in a windless place. Arjuna objects honestly — the mind is as hard to hold as the wind — and Krishna agrees, offering the two tools: practice and dispassion. And a promise: no sincere effort on this path is ever lost.",
"From practice to its object: Krishna as the thread through all things — the taste in water, the light in sun and moon. Nature is his, in two aspects, material and living. Four kinds of people seek him; rare is the one who sees that all of it, everywhere, is one.",
"Arjuna asks the great final questions — what is brahman, what is karma, what happens at death? What you dwell on shapes where you go, Krishna answers: so remember Me at all times, and do what is yours to do. Behind the world's vast cycles of day and night stands the imperishable.",
"The royal secret, hidden in plain sight: all beings rest in the divine as wind rests in space. No offering is too small — a leaf, a flower, water given with love is received. And no one is disqualified: whoever turns, however late, is quickly set right.",
"Where should the eye look for the divine? Krishna names his glories: the Self seated in every heart, the Himālaya among mountains, the beginning, middle, and end of all beings. Whatever anywhere is beautiful, mighty, or excellent — know it as a spark of that splendor.",
"Arjuna asks to see it directly. Granted divine sight, he beholds the cosmic form — all worlds, all beings, all time, creation and dissolution in a single body — and awe turns to terror: 'I am Time,' the vision says. It ends gently: not spectacle but steady devotion is how this form is truly known.",
"Arjuna's practical question: worship the formless, or the personal? Those who come with faith and love are held fastest, Krishna answers — though every sincere path arrives. Then the Gītā's most beloved portrait: the devotee friendly to all beings, free of malice, equal in honor and disgrace, content.",
"A map of inner life: the body-mind is the field; what knows it is the knower. Real knowledge begins with humility and ends in seeing the one Self equally present in every being. Nature acts; the Self witnesses; confusing the two is bondage, distinguishing them is freedom.",
"All of nature moves by three strands: sattva (clarity), rajas (restless drive), tamas (inertia). Each has its signature, each binds in its own way — even clarity can bind, through attachment to knowledge and joy. Beyond them stands the one equal to praise and blame, whom the strands pass through without catching.",
"The world is pictured as a vast inverted tree — roots above, branches below — to be felled with the axe of non-attachment. Every living being is an eternal fragment of the supreme; the light in the sun, the fire that digests food, the presence in every heart are one and the same. Knowing that supreme Person, one knows all.",
"Two inner inheritances: the divine — fearlessness, purity, compassion, steadfastness — which frees; and the demonic — hypocrisy, arrogance, cruelty — which binds. Desire, anger, and greed are named the threefold gate of ruin. When in doubt about what to do, let the scriptures' wisdom be the measure.",
"Faith itself comes in three colors. The food we prefer, the discipline we practice, the gifts we give — each can be clear, driven, or dark, and each shapes us in its image. The chapter closes with oṁ tat sat: done with faith, the smallest act carries; without it, nothing does.",
"The summation. Renunciation is not quitting action but releasing attachment to its results; everyone reaches perfection through their own work, done as worship. Then the final movement: 'abandon all supports and take refuge in Me alone — do not grieve' — followed by the Gītā's last courtesy: 'reflect on this fully, then do as you choose.'",
];
const FEAT = {"2.47": {"note": "Act wholeheartedly; release your grip on the outcome.", "themes": ["Action & Duty", "Letting Go of Outcomes"], "gu": "તારો અધિકાર કેવળ કર્મ કરવામાં છે, તેનાં ફળમાં કદી નહિ. કર્મનાં ફળનો હેતુ તું ન બન, અને કર્મ ન કરવામાં પણ તારી આસક્તિ ન રહે."}, "2.48": {"note": "Balance in the face of either result is the whole discipline.", "themes": ["Equanimity", "Action & Duty"], "gu": "હે ધનંજય, યોગમાં સ્થિર થઈને, આસક્તિ છોડીને, સફળતા અને નિષ્ફળતામાં સમાન રહીને કર્મ કર; આ સમતા જ યોગ કહેવાય છે."}, "2.14": {"note": "Feelings are weather, not climate. Let them pass through.", "themes": ["Equanimity", "The Restless Mind"], "gu": "હે કૌંતેય, ઇન્દ્રિયોના વિષયો સાથેનો સંપર્ક ટાઢ-તડકો અને સુખ-દુઃખ આપે છે; એ આવે છે ને જાય છે, અનિત્ય છે. તેથી તેમને ધૈર્યથી સહન કર."}, "2.20": {"note": "What you most are was never at risk.", "themes": ["The Eternal Self", "Grief & Loss"], "gu": "આત્મા કદી જન્મતો નથી કે મરતો નથી; એ ઉત્પન્ન થઈને ફરી નષ્ટ થનાર પણ નથી. અજન્મા, નિત્ય, શાશ્વત અને પુરાતન એવો આત્મા શરીર હણાય ત્યારે પણ હણાતો નથી."}, "2.22": {"note": "Death is a changing of garments, not an ending.", "themes": ["The Eternal Self", "Grief & Loss"], "gu": "જેમ માણસ જૂનાં વસ્ત્રો ત્યજીને નવાં વસ્ત્રો ધારણ કરે છે, તેમ આત્મા જૂનાં શરીરો છોડીને નવાં શરીરો ધારણ કરે છે."}, "2.23": {"note": "There is something in you nothing outside can touch.", "themes": ["The Eternal Self", "Courage"], "gu": "આત્માને શસ્ત્રો કાપી શકતાં નથી, અગ્નિ બાળી શકતો નથી, જળ ભીંજવી શકતું નથી અને પવન સૂકવી શકતો નથી."}, "2.27": {"note": "Grieve, yes — but not the parts of life that were never yours to change.", "themes": ["Grief & Loss", "Equanimity"], "gu": "જે જન્મ્યો છે તેનું મૃત્યુ નિશ્ચિત છે, અને જે મર્યો છે તેનો જન્મ નિશ્ચિત છે. તેથી જે અટળ છે તેને માટે તું શોક ન કર."}, "2.38": {"note": "Do the hard thing with an even heart.", "themes": ["Equanimity", "Action & Duty"], "gu": "સુખ-દુઃખ, લાભ-હાનિ અને જય-પરાજયને સમાન ગણીને યુદ્ધ માટે તૈયાર થા; આમ કરવાથી તને પાપ લાગશે નહિ."}, "2.40": {"note": "Nothing you put in here is ever spent for nothing.", "themes": ["Courage", "Action & Duty"], "gu": "આ માર્ગમાં કરેલો પ્રયત્ન વ્યર્થ જતો નથી, કે કોઈ હાનિ થતી નથી. આ ધર્મનું થોડું પાલન પણ મોટા ભયથી રક્ષણ આપે છે."}, "2.50": {"note": "Yoga is skill in action: full effort, light hands.", "themes": ["Action & Duty", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "બુદ્ધિયુક્ત મનુષ્ય આ જ જીવનમાં પુણ્ય અને પાપ બંનેને ત્યજી દે છે. તેથી તું યોગમાં જોડાઈ જા; કર્મમાં કુશળતા એ જ યોગ છે."}, "2.55": {"note": "Contentment is sourced from within, not delivered from outside.", "themes": ["Peace", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "હે પાર્થ, જ્યારે મનુષ્ય મનમાં રહેલી સર્વ કામનાઓ ત્યજી દે છે અને આત્મા વડે આત્મામાં જ સંતુષ્ટ રહે છે, ત્યારે તે સ્થિતપ્રજ્ઞ કહેવાય છે."}, "2.56": {"note": "Steadiness isn't numbness; it's not being thrown.", "themes": ["Equanimity", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "જેનું મન દુઃખમાં વ્યાકુળ થતું નથી, સુખોમાં જેને તૃષ્ણા નથી, અને જે રાગ, ભય તથા ક્રોધથી મુક્ત છે, તે સ્થિરબુદ્ધિ મુનિ કહેવાય છે."}, "2.62": {"note": "Catch the chain at the first link — the dwelling.", "themes": ["Desire & Anger", "The Restless Mind"], "gu": "વિષયોનું ચિંતન કરનાર મનુષ્યને તેમના પ્રત્યે આસક્તિ જન્મે છે; આસક્તિમાંથી કામના, અને કામનામાંથી ક્રોધ ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે."}, "2.70": {"note": "Peace is the sea, not the river that runs after more.", "themes": ["Peace", "Desire & Anger"], "gu": "જેમ સદા ભરાતા છતાં અચળ રહેતા સમુદ્રમાં જળ સમાઈ જાય છે, તેમ જેનામાં સર્વ કામનાઓ સમાઈ જાય છે તે જ શાંતિ પામે છે — કામનાઓની પાછળ દોડનાર નહિ."}, "2.71": {"note": "Less 'mine,' more peace.", "themes": ["Peace", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "જે મનુષ્ય સર્વ કામનાઓ ત્યજીને નિઃસ્પૃહ બનીને વિચરે છે, જે મમતા અને અહંકારથી રહિત છે, તે શાંતિ પામે છે."}, "2.3": {"note": "Krishna's first push: rise.", "themes": ["Courage"], "gu": "હે પાર્થ, નામર્દાઈને વશ ન થા; એ તને શોભતું નથી. હૃદયની આ ક્ષુદ્ર દુર્બળતા ત્યજીને ઊભો થા, હે પરંતપ."}, "3.19": {"note": "Unattached doesn't mean uncaring — it means unowned by the result.", "themes": ["Action & Duty", "Letting Go of Outcomes"], "gu": "તેથી આસક્તિ રહિત થઈને સદા કરવાયોગ્ય કર્મ સારી રીતે કર; કારણ કે અનાસક્ત રહીને કર્મ કરનાર મનુષ્ય પરમ પદ પામે છે."}, "3.21": {"note": "You are always teaching by what you do.", "themes": ["Action & Duty", "Compassion"], "gu": "શ્રેષ્ઠ પુરુષ જે જે આચરે છે, બીજા લોકો પણ તે જ આચરે છે; તે જે પ્રમાણ સ્થાપે છે, જગત તેને અનુસરે છે."}, "3.35": {"note": "Your work, even flawed, beats a borrowed life.", "themes": ["Action & Duty", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "ગુણહીન હોવા છતાં પોતાનો ધર્મ બીજાના સારી રીતે પાળેલા ધર્મ કરતાં શ્રેષ્ઠ છે. પોતાના ધર્મમાં મૃત્યુ પણ કલ્યાણકારી છે; બીજાનો ધર્મ ભય ઉપજાવનારો છે."}, "4.7": {"note": "The turning point always comes; light answers the dark.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust", "Courage"], "gu": "હે ભારત, જ્યારે જ્યારે ધર્મની હાનિ થાય છે અને અધર્મનો ઉદય થાય છે, ત્યારે ત્યારે હું પોતાને પ્રગટ કરું છું."}, "4.8": {"note": "Restoration is built into the order of things.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust"], "gu": "સજ્જનોના રક્ષણ માટે, દુષ્ટોના વિનાશ માટે અને ધર્મની સ્થાપના માટે હું યુગે યુગે પ્રગટ થાઉં છું."}, "4.18": {"note": "Calm inside the doing; that's mastery.", "themes": ["Self-Mastery", "Equanimity"], "gu": "જે કર્મમાં અકર્મ જુએ છે અને અકર્મમાં કર્મ જુએ છે, તે મનુષ્યોમાં બુદ્ધિમાન છે અને સર્વ કર્મ કરનાર યોગી છે."}, "4.38": {"note": "Understanding purifies — and it arrives in its own time.", "themes": ["Self-Mastery", "Peace"], "gu": "જ્ઞાન સમાન પવિત્ર કરનાર આ જગતમાં બીજું કશું નથી. યોગમાં સિદ્ધ થયેલો મનુષ્ય સમય જતાં તે જ્ઞાનને પોતાના આત્મામાં પામે છે."}, "4.39": {"note": "Trust + focus + restraint leads to peace.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust", "Peace"], "gu": "શ્રદ્ધાવાન, તત્પર અને ઇન્દ્રિયોને સંયમમાં રાખનાર મનુષ્ય જ્ઞાન પામે છે; જ્ઞાન પામીને તે તુરત જ પરમ શાંતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."}, "5.10": {"note": "Be in it without being soaked by it.", "themes": ["Letting Go of Outcomes", "Devotion & Trust"], "gu": "જે મનુષ્ય આસક્તિ ત્યજીને સર્વ કર્મો બ્રહ્મને અર્પણ કરીને કરે છે, તે કમળના પાંદડાને જળ સ્પર્શતું નથી તેમ પાપથી લેપાતો નથી."}, "5.29": {"note": "You are befriended by the whole, not adrift in it.", "themes": ["Peace", "Devotion & Trust"], "gu": "મને યજ્ઞ અને તપનો ભોક્તા, સર્વ લોકોનો મહેશ્વર અને સર્વ પ્રાણીઓનો સુહૃદ જાણીને મનુષ્ય શાંતિ પામે છે."}, "6.5": {"note": "The one who can raise you is already here.", "themes": ["Self-Mastery", "Courage"], "gu": "મનુષ્યે પોતે જ પોતાનો ઉદ્ધાર કરવો, પોતાને નીચે ન પાડવો; કારણ કે પોતે જ પોતાનો મિત્ર છે અને પોતે જ પોતાનો શત્રુ છે."}, "6.6": {"note": "Make peace within first.", "themes": ["Self-Mastery"], "gu": "જેણે પોતાના વડે પોતાને જીત્યો છે, તેને માટે પોતાનો આત્મા મિત્ર છે; પણ જેણે પોતાને જીત્યો નથી, તેને માટે પોતાનો આત્મા જ શત્રુની જેમ વર્તે છે."}, "6.16": {"note": "Steadiness grows from a well-kept body and rhythm.", "themes": ["Self-Mastery", "Peace"], "gu": "હે અર્જુન, અતિશય ખાનાર કે તદ્દન ન ખાનાર, અતિશય ઊંઘનાર કે સદા જાગનાર માટે યોગ સધાતો નથી."}, "6.19": {"note": "Shelter the flame; let the mind grow still.", "themes": ["The Restless Mind", "Peace"], "gu": "વાયુ વિનાના સ્થાનમાં દીપક હાલતો નથી, એવી ઉપમા આત્મામાં લીન થયેલા સંયમિત ચિત્તવાળા યોગીને અપાય છે."}, "6.26": {"note": "Returning the mind a thousand times is the practice — not a failure of it.", "themes": ["The Restless Mind", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "આ ચંચળ અને અસ્થિર મન જ્યાં જ્યાં ભટકે, ત્યાં ત્યાંથી તેને પાછું વાળીને આત્માના વશમાં લાવવું."}, "6.30": {"note": "Connection, once seen, is never severed.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust", "Compassion"], "gu": "જે મને સર્વત્ર જુએ છે અને સર્વને મારામાં જુએ છે, તેને માટે હું કદી લુપ્ત થતો નથી, અને તે મારે માટે કદી લુપ્ત થતો નથી."}, "6.32": {"note": "Measure others by yourself; that is the whole of compassion.", "themes": ["Compassion", "Equanimity"], "gu": "હે અર્જુન, જે પોતાની ઉપમાથી સર્વત્ર સુખ અને દુઃખને સમાન રીતે જુએ છે, તે યોગી શ્રેષ્ઠ ગણાય છે."}, "6.35": {"note": "Repetition and letting go: the two reins of the mind.", "themes": ["The Restless Mind", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "હે મહાબાહો, નિઃસંદેહ મન ચંચળ છે અને તેને વશ કરવું કઠણ છે; પણ હે કૌંતેય, અભ્યાસ અને વૈરાગ્ય વડે તે વશમાં આવે છે."}, "9.22": {"note": "You are more held than you feel.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust", "Peace"], "gu": "જે અનન્ય ભક્તો મારું ચિંતન કરીને મારી ઉપાસના કરે છે, એ સદા મારામાં જોડાયેલા ભક્તોનો યોગ અને ક્ષેમ હું વહન કરું છું."}, "9.29": {"note": "Turn toward it, and the nearness is already there.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust", "Compassion"], "gu": "હું સર્વ પ્રાણીઓ પ્રત્યે સમાન છું; મને કોઈ દ્વેષપાત્ર નથી કે પ્રિય નથી. પણ જે ભક્તિથી મને ભજે છે, તેઓ મારામાં છે અને હું તેઓમાં છું."}, "9.34": {"note": "Orient the whole of yourself; the path follows.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust"], "gu": "તારું મન મારામાં લગાવ, મારો ભક્ત બન, મારું પૂજન કર, મને નમસ્કાર કર; આમ મારામાં જોડાઈને તું મને જ પામીશ."}, "11.33": {"note": "You are asked to act, not to carry the whole weight of outcome.", "themes": ["Action & Duty", "Letting Go of Outcomes"], "gu": "તેથી તું ઊભો થા અને યશ પ્રાપ્ત કર; શત્રુઓને જીતીને સમૃદ્ધ રાજ્ય ભોગવ. આ સૌને મેં પહેલેથી જ હણ્યા છે; હે સવ્યસાચી, તું તો કેવળ નિમિત્ત બન."}, "12.13": {"note": "A whole portrait of a settled heart.", "themes": ["Compassion", "Equanimity"], "gu": "જે કોઈ પ્રાણીનો દ્વેષ કરતો નથી, જે સર્વનો મિત્ર અને કરુણાવાન છે, મમતા અને અહંકારથી રહિત, સુખ-દુઃખમાં સમાન અને ક્ષમાશીલ છે —"}, "12.15": {"note": "Unprovoked and unprovoking: a quiet strength.", "themes": ["Equanimity", "Peace"], "gu": "જેનાથી જગત ઉદ્વેગ પામતું નથી અને જે જગતથી ઉદ્વેગ પામતો નથી, જે હર્ષ, ઈર્ષા, ભય અને ઉદ્વેગથી મુક્ત છે, તે મને પ્રિય છે."}, "16.21": {"note": "Name the three; guard the gates.", "themes": ["Desire & Anger", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "કામ, ક્રોધ અને લોભ — આ ત્રણ આત્માનો નાશ કરનારાં નરકનાં દ્વાર છે; તેથી આ ત્રણેયને ત્યજી દેવાં."}, "18.48": {"note": "Waiting for flawless is its own kind of quitting.", "themes": ["Action & Duty", "Courage"], "gu": "હે કૌંતેય, દોષયુક્ત હોવા છતાં સ્વાભાવિક કર્મ ત્યજવું ન જોઈએ; કારણ કે જેમ અગ્નિ ધુમાડાથી ઢંકાયેલો હોય છે, તેમ સર્વ કર્મો કોઈક દોષથી ઢંકાયેલાં હોય છે."}, "18.58": {"note": "The obstacle is often the ego that won't be helped.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust", "Self-Mastery"], "gu": "મારામાં ચિત્ત રાખવાથી તું મારી કૃપાથી સર્વ વિઘ્નોને પાર કરી જઈશ; પણ જો અહંકારને કારણે તું નહિ સાંભળે, તો તું નાશ પામીશ."}, "18.66": {"note": "The Gita's final word: you may lay it down.", "themes": ["Devotion & Trust", "Peace"], "gu": "સર્વ ધર્મોને ત્યજીને કેવળ મારે જ શરણે આવ; હું તને સર્વ પાપોમાંથી મુક્ત કરીશ, તું શોક ન કર."}, "18.78": {"note": "Wisdom plus your readiness: that is the winning pair.", "themes": ["Courage", "Devotion & Trust"], "gu": "જ્યાં યોગેશ્વર કૃષ્ણ છે અને જ્યાં ધનુર્ધારી અર્જુન છે, ત્યાં જ શ્રી, વિજય, ઐશ્વર્ય અને અચળ નીતિ છે — એવો મારો મત છે."}};
const GITA = [{"ref":"1.1","ch":1,"v":1,"sa":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच\nधर्मक्षेत्रे कुरुक्षेत्रे समवेता युयुत्सवः।\nमामकाः पाण्डवाश्चैव किमकुर्वत सञ्जय।।1.1।।","tr":"dhṛitarāśhtra uvācha\ndharma-kṣhetre kuru-kṣhetre samavetā yuyutsavaḥ\nmāmakāḥ pāṇḍavāśhchaiva kimakurvata sañjaya","en":"Dhritarashtra said, \"What did my people and the sons of Pandu do when they had assembled together, eager for battle, on the holy plain of Kurukshetra, O Sanjaya?\"","es":"Dhṛtarāṣṭra said: O Sanjaya, what did my sons and the sons of Pandu do when they assembled on the sacred field of Kurukshetra, eager for battle?","er":"Dhṛtarāṣṭra said: “O Sanjaya, what did my people and the Pāṇḍavas do, gathered together on the holy field of Kurukshetra, eager for battle?”","gu":"ધૃતરાષ્ટ્ર બોલ્યા: હે સંજય, ધર્મભૂમિ કુરુક્ષેત્રમાં ભેગા થઈ, યુદ્ધ ઈચ્છતા, મારા અને પાંડુના પુત્રોએ શું કર્યું?"},{"ref":"1.2","ch":1,"v":2,"sa":"सञ्जय उवाच\nदृष्ट्वा तु पाण्डवानीकं व्यूढं दुर्योधनस्तदा।\nआचार्यमुपसङ्गम्य राजा वचनमब्रवीत्।।1.2।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\ndṛiṣhṭvā tu pāṇḍavānīkaṁ vyūḍhaṁ duryodhanastadā\nāchāryamupasaṅgamya rājā vachanamabravīt","en":"Sanjaya said: Having seen the army of the Pandavas drawn up in battle array, King Duryodhana approached his teacher, Drona, and spoke these words.","es":"Sanjaya said: But then, seeing the army of the Pandavas in battle array, King Duryodhana approached the teacher, Drona, and spoke.","er":"Sanjaya said: King Duryodhana, upon seeing the Pandava army in battle array, approached his teacher Drona and said these words.","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: પાંડવ-સૈન્ય વ્યૂહ-રચનામાં ગોઠવાયેલું જોઈ, રાજા દુર્યોધન આચાર્ય દ્રોણ પાસે ગયો અને આ વચન બોલ્યો."},{"ref":"1.3","ch":1,"v":3,"sa":"पश्यैतां पाण्डुपुत्राणामाचार्य महतीं चमूम्।\nव्यूढां द्रुपदपुत्रेण तव शिष्येण धीमता।।1.3।।","tr":"paśhyaitāṁ pāṇḍu-putrāṇām āchārya mahatīṁ chamūm\nvyūḍhāṁ drupada-putreṇa tava śhiṣhyeṇa dhīmatā","en":"Behold, O Teacher! This mighty army of the sons of Pandu, arrayed by the son of Drupada, thy wise disciple.","es":"O teacher, behold this vast army of the sons of Pandu, arrayed for battle by the intelligent disciple of Drupada.","er":"Behold, O teacher, this mighty army of the Pandavas, arrayed by the son of Drupada, your intelligent disciple.","gu":"હે આચાર્ય, તમારા બુદ્ધિમાન શિષ્ય ધૃષ્ટદ્યુમ્ન — દ્રુપદ-પુત્ર — એ ગોઠવેલી, પાંડવોની આ વિશાળ સૈન્ય-ટોળ જુઓ."},{"ref":"1.4","ch":1,"v":4,"sa":"अत्र शूरा महेष्वासा भीमार्जुनसमा युधि।\nयुयुधानो विराटश्च द्रुपदश्च महारथः।।1.4।।","tr":"atra śhūrā maheṣhvāsā bhīmārjuna-samā yudhi\nyuyudhāno virāṭaśhcha drupadaśhcha mahā-rathaḥ","en":"Here are heroes, mighty archers, equal in battle to Bhima and Arjuna, Yuyudhana (Satyaki), Virata, and Drupada—all mighty warriors.","es":"Here are the heroes wielding great bows, who in battle are peers of Bhima and Arjuna: Yuyudhana (Satyaki) and Virata, and the maharatha (great chariot-rider) Drupada;","er":"There (in that army) are heroes, great bowmen, such as Bhima and Arjuna; Yuyudhana, Virata, and Drupada, a mighty warrior;","gu":"અહીં ભીમ-અર્જુન સમાન પ્રતાપી, મહા-ધનુર્ધારી વીર ઊભા છે — સાત્યકિ, વિરાટ, અને મહારથ દ્રુપદ."},{"ref":"1.5","ch":1,"v":5,"sa":"धृष्टकेतुश्चेकितानः काशिराजश्च वीर्यवान्।\nपुरुजित्कुन्तिभोजश्च शैब्यश्च नरपुङ्गवः।।1.5।।","tr":"dhṛiṣhṭaketuśhchekitānaḥ kāśhirājaśhcha vīryavān\npurujit kuntibhojaśhcha śhaibyaśhcha nara-puṅgavaḥ\nyudhāmanyuśhcha vikrānta uttamaujāśhcha vīryavān","en":"Dhrishtaketu, Chekitana, the valiant king of Kasi, Purujit, Kuntibhoja, and Saibya—the best of men.","es":"Dhrstaketu, Cekitana, and the valiant king of Kasi (Varanasi); Purujit, Kuntibhoja, and Saibya, the choicest of men;","er":"Dhrstaketu, Cekitana, the valiant king of Kasi, Purujit, Kuntibhoja, and Saibya, the best among men;","gu":"ધૃષ્ટકેતુ, ચેકિતાન, વીર્યવાન કાશીનરેશ, પુરુજિત, કુન્તિભોજ, અને નર-શ્રેષ્ઠ શૈબ્ય."},{"ref":"1.6","ch":1,"v":6,"sa":"युधामन्युश्च विक्रान्त उत्तमौजाश्च वीर्यवान्।\nसौभद्रो द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्व एव महारथाः।।1.6।।","tr":"saubhadro draupadeyāśhcha sarva eva mahā-rathāḥ","en":"The strong Yudhamanyu and the brave Uttamaujas, the son of Subhadra (Abhimanyu, the son of Subhadra and Arjuna), and the sons of Draupadi, all of them great charioteers (great heroes).\"","es":"And the valiant Yudhamanyu, and the chivalrous Uttamaujas; the son of Subhadra (Abhimanyu) and the sons of Draupadi—all of them are, indeed, maharathas.","er":"Yudhamanyu, the valiant one, and Uttamaujas, the strong one; and also the son of Subhadra, as well as the sons of Draupadi, all mighty warriors.","gu":"વિક્રમી યુધામન્યુ, શૌર્યવાન ઉત્તમૌજ, સૌભદ્ર અભિમન્યુ, અને દ્રૌપદીના પુત્રો — આ સૌ મહારથ છે."},{"ref":"1.7","ch":1,"v":7,"sa":"अस्माकं तु विशिष्टा ये तान्निबोध द्विजोत्तम।\nनायका मम सैन्यस्य संज्ञार्थं तान्ब्रवीमि ते।।1.7।।","tr":"asmākaṁ tu viśhiṣhṭā ye tānnibodha dwijottama\nnāyakā mama sainyasya sanjñārthaṁ tānbravīmi te","en":"Know also, O best among the twice-born! the names of those who are the most distinguished amongst ourselves, the leaders of my army; these I name to you for your information.","es":"But, O best among the Brahmanas, please be appraised of those who are foremost among us, the founders of my army. I speak of them to you by way of illustration.","er":"Know, O best of Brahmanas, those who are important on our side—those who are the commanders of my army. I shall name them to refresh your memory.","gu":"હે ઉત્તમ, અમારી સેનાના જે મુખ્ય, વિશિષ્ટ નાયકો છે, તેઓ ઓળખો — પ્રભુ, સ્મૃતિ-અ-ર-ઉ ."},{"ref":"1.8","ch":1,"v":8,"sa":"भवान्भीष्मश्च कर्णश्च कृपश्च समितिञ्जयः।\nअश्वत्थामा विकर्णश्च सौमदत्तिस्तथैव च।।1.8।।","tr":"bhavānbhīṣhmaśhcha karṇaśhcha kṛipaśhcha samitiñjayaḥ\naśhvatthāmā vikarṇaśhcha saumadattis tathaiva cha","en":"\"Thou thyself, Bhishma, Karna, Kripa, the victorious in war, Asvatthama, Vikarna, and Bhurisrava, the son of Somadatta—all these are ready for battle.\"","es":"(They are): Your venerable self, Bhisma, Karna, and Krpa, who is ever victorious in battle; Asvatthama, Vikarna, Saumadatti, and Jayadratha.","er":"Yourself, Bhisma, Karna, the victorious Krpa, Asvatthama, Vikarna, and Jayadratha, the son of Somadatta;","gu":"આપ, ભીષ્મ, કર્ણ, સમર-વિજયી કૃપ, અશ્વત્થામા, વિકર્ણ, અને ભૂરિશ્રવ — સોમદત્ત-પુત્ર."},{"ref":"1.9","ch":1,"v":9,"sa":"अन्ये च बहवः शूरा मदर्थे त्यक्तजीविताः।\nनानाशस्त्रप्रहरणाः सर्वे युद्धविशारदाः।।1.9।।","tr":"anye cha bahavaḥ śhūrā madarthe tyaktajīvitāḥ\nnānā-śhastra-praharaṇāḥ sarve yuddha-viśhāradāḥ","en":"And also many other heroes, ready to give up their lives for my sake, armed with various weapons and missiles, all well-skilled in battle.","es":"There are many heroes who have dedicated their lives to me, possessing various kinds of weapons and missiles, all of whom are skilled in battle.","er":"And there are many other heroes who are determined to give up their lives for my sake. They are all experts in using manifold missiles and dexterous in battle.","gu":"અને ઘણા અન્ય વીરો — મારા માટે પ્રાણ ત્યજવા સિદ્ધ, વિવિધ શસ્ત્ર-ધારી, સૌ રણ-નિષ્ણાત."},{"ref":"1.10","ch":1,"v":10,"sa":"अपर्याप्तं तदस्माकं बलं भीष्माभिरक्षितम्।\nपर्याप्तं त्विदमेतेषां बलं भीमाभिरक्षितम्।।1.10।।","tr":"aparyāptaṁ tadasmākaṁ balaṁ bhīṣhmābhirakṣhitam\nparyāptaṁ tvidameteṣhāṁ balaṁ bhīmābhirakṣhitam","en":"Our army, marshalled by Bhishma, is insufficient, whereas theirs, marshalled by Bhima, is sufficient.","es":"Therefore, our army, under the complete protection of Bhisma and others, is limitless. But this army of the enemies, under the protection of Bhima and others, is limited.","er":"Our force is inadequate, guarded by Bhisma, while their force is adequate, guarded by Bhima.","gu":"ભીષ્મ-સંરક્ષિત આપણી સૈન્ય-ટોળ અપૂર્ણ લાગે, ભીમ-સંરક્ષિત એ લોકોની સૈન્ય-ટોળ પૂર્ણ-સક્ષમ."},{"ref":"1.11","ch":1,"v":11,"sa":"अयनेषु च सर्वेषु यथाभागमवस्थिताः।\nभीष्ममेवाभिरक्षन्तु भवन्तः सर्व एव हि।।1.11।।","tr":"ayaneṣhu cha sarveṣhu yathā-bhāgamavasthitāḥ\nbhīṣhmamevābhirakṣhantu bhavantaḥ sarva eva hi","en":"Therefore, do all of you, stationed in your respective positions in the several divisions of the army, protect Bhishma alone.","es":"However, venerable sirs, all of you without exception, while occupying all the positions in the different directions as allotted to you respectively, please protect Bhisma in particular.","er":"Therefore, all of you, taking your places firmly in your respective divisions, should guard Bhisma at all costs.","gu":"તેથી, સૌ, સૈન્યના પોતપોતાના સ્થાન ઉપર ગોઠવાઈ, ભીષ્મ-પિતામહ ની સૌ-ઓ-ળ-ખ-ો રક્ષા કરો."},{"ref":"1.12","ch":1,"v":12,"sa":"तस्य संजनयन्हर्षं कुरुवृद्धः पितामहः।\nसिंहनादं विनद्योच्चैः शङ्खं दध्मौ प्रतापवान्।।1.12।।","tr":"tasya sañjanayan harṣhaṁ kuru-vṛiddhaḥ pitāmahaḥ\nsiṁha-nādaṁ vinadyochchaiḥ śhaṅkhaṁ dadhmau pratāpavān","en":"His glorious grandsire, the oldest of the Kauravas, roared like a lion to cheer Duryodhana and blew his conch.","es":"The valiant grandfather, the eldest of the Kurus, loudly sounding a lion's roar, blew the conch to raise his (Duryodhana's) spirits.","er":"Then the valiant grandsire Bhisma, the senior-most of the Kuru clan, roared like a lion and blew his conch with the intention of cheering up Duryodhana.","gu":"ત્યારે, પ્રભાવી ભીષ્મ — કૌરવ-કુળ-વૃદ્ધ, પ્રભ — સિંહ-ગ-ર-જ-ન-ા ."},{"ref":"1.13","ch":1,"v":13,"sa":"ततः शङ्खाश्च भेर्यश्च पणवानकगोमुखाः।\nसहसैवाभ्यहन्यन्त स शब्दस्तुमुलोऽभवत्।।1.13।।","tr":"tataḥ śhaṅkhāśhcha bheryaśhcha paṇavānaka-gomukhāḥ\nsahasaivābhyahanyanta sa śhabdastumulo ’bhavat","en":"Then, suddenly, conches, kettledrums, tabors, drums, and cow horns blared forth from the Kaurava side, and the sound was tremendous.","es":"Just immediately afterward, conch shells, kettledrums, tabors, trumpets, and cow-horns blared forth, creating a tumultuous sound.","er":"Then suddenly conchs, kettle drums, trumpets, tabors, and blow horns blared forth, and the sound was terrific.","gu":"ત્યારે કૌરવ પક્ષથી શંખ, નગારા, ઢોલ, મૃદંગ અને રણશિંગા એકી સાથે વાગ્યા — અને એ ઘોર ધ્વનિ ચારે દિશામાં ગૂંજી ઉઠ્યો."},{"ref":"1.14","ch":1,"v":14,"sa":"ततः श्वेतैर्हयैर्युक्ते महति स्यन्दने स्थितौ।\nमाधवः पाण्डवश्चैव दिव्यौ शङ्खौ प्रदध्मतुः।।1.14।।","tr":"tataḥ śhvetairhayairyukte mahati syandane sthitau\nmādhavaḥ pāṇḍavaśhchaiva divyau śhaṅkhau pradadhmatuḥ","en":"Then, Madhava (Krishna) and the son of Pandu (Arjuna), seated in the magnificent chariot yoked with white horses, blew divine conches.","es":"Then Madhava (Krishna) and the son of Pandu (Arjuna), stationed in their magnificent chariot with white horses yoked to it, blew their divine conchs loudly.","er":"Then Sri Krishna and Arjuna, stationed in their great chariot yoked with white horses, blew their divine conchs.","gu":"ત્યારે શ્વેત અશ્વોના ભવ્ય રથ પર બિરાજેલ શ્રીકૃષ્ણ અને અર્જુને પોતાના દિવ્ય શંખ ફૂંક્યા."},{"ref":"1.15","ch":1,"v":15,"sa":"पाञ्चजन्यं हृषीकेशो देवदत्तं धनंजयः।\nपौण्ड्रं दध्मौ महाशङ्खं भीमकर्मा वृकोदरः।।1.15।।","tr":"pāñchajanyaṁ hṛiṣhīkeśho devadattaṁ dhanañjayaḥ\npauṇḍraṁ dadhmau mahā-śhaṅkhaṁ bhīma-karmā vṛikodaraḥ","en":"Hrishikesha blew the Panchajanya, Arjuna blew the Devadatta, and Bhima, the wolf-bellied doer of terrible deeds, blew the great conch Paundra.","es":"Hrsikesa (Krsna) blew the conch Pancajanya; Dhananjaya (Arjuna) blew the conch Devadatta; and Vrkodara (Bhima) of terrible deeds blew the great conch Paundra.","er":"Sri Krishna blew his conch, Pancajanya, Arjuna his Devadatta, and Bhima of terrible deeds blew his great conch, Paundra.","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણે પાંચજન્ય શંખ ફૂંક્યો, અર્જુને દેવદત્ત ફૂંક્યો, અને ભયંકર ભૂખ ધરાવતા ભીમે મહાન પૌંડ્ર શંખ ફૂંક્યો."},{"ref":"1.16","ch":1,"v":16,"sa":"अनन्तविजयं राजा कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च सुघोषमणिपुष्पकौ।।1.16।।","tr":"anantavijayaṁ rājā kuntī-putro yudhiṣhṭhiraḥ\nnakulaḥ sahadevaśhcha sughoṣha-maṇipuṣhpakau","en":"King Yudhishthira, the son of Kunti, blew the Anantavijaya; Nakula and Sahadeva blew the Sughosha and the Manipushpaka.","es":"King Yudhisthira, son of Kunti, blew the Anantavijaya; Nakula and Sahadeva blew the Sughosa and the Manipuspaka, respectively.","er":"King Yudhisthira, the son of Kunti, blew his conch, Anantavijaya, and Nakula and Sahadeva blew their conchs, Sughosa and Manipuspaka.","gu":"કુંતીપુત્ર રાજા યુધિષ્ઠિરે અનંતવિજય શંખ ફૂંક્યો, અને નકુળ-સહદેવે સુઘોષ તથા મણિપુષ્પક શંખ ફૂંક્યા."},{"ref":"1.17","ch":1,"v":17,"sa":"काश्यश्च परमेष्वासः शिखण्डी च महारथः।\nधृष्टद्युम्नो विराटश्च सात्यकिश्चापराजितः।।1.17।।","tr":"kāśhyaśhcha parameṣhvāsaḥ śhikhaṇḍī cha mahā-rathaḥ\ndhṛiṣhṭadyumno virāṭaśhcha sātyakiśh chāparājitaḥ","en":"The king of Kasi, an excellent archer, Sikhandi, the mighty car-warrior, Dhrishtadyumna, Virata, and Satyaki, the unconquered.","es":"And the King of Kashi, wielding a great bow, and the great chariot-rider Sikhandin, Dhrstadyumna, Virata, and Satyaki the unconquered;","er":"And the King of Kasi, the supreme bowman, Sikandi the mighty warrior, Dhrstadyumna, and Virata; and Satyaki, the invincible;","gu":"કાશીનરેશ, મહાધનુર્ધારી શિખંડી, ધૃષ્ટદ્યુમ્ન, વિરાટ, અને અજેય સાત્યકિ — આ સૌ વીરોએ પોતપોતાના શંખ ઊઠાવ્યા."},{"ref":"1.18","ch":1,"v":18,"sa":"द्रुपदो द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्वशः पृथिवीपते।\nसौभद्रश्च महाबाहुः शङ्खान्दध्मुः पृथक्पृथक्।।1.18।।","tr":"drupado draupadeyāśhcha sarvaśhaḥ pṛithivī-pate\nsaubhadraśhcha mahā-bāhuḥ śhaṅkhāndadhmuḥ pṛithak pṛithak","en":"Drupada and the sons of Draupadi, O Lord of the Earth, and the son of Subhadra, the mighty-armed, blew their conches each separately.","es":"Drupada and the sons of Draupadi, as well as the mighty-armed son of Subhadra, all of them together, O king, blew their respective conchs.","er":"Drupada and the sons of Draupadi, as well as the strong-armed son of Subhadra—all, O King, blew their respective conchs again and again.","gu":"દ્રુપદ, દ્રૌપદીના પુત્રો, અને મહાબાહુ સુભદ્રાપુત્ર અભિમન્યુ — આ સૌએ અલગ અલગ પોતાના શંખ ફૂંક્યા."},{"ref":"1.19","ch":1,"v":19,"sa":"स घोषो धार्तराष्ट्राणां हृदयानि व्यदारयत्।\nनभश्च पृथिवीं चैव तुमुलो व्यनुनादयन्।।1.19।।","tr":"sa ghoṣho dhārtarāṣhṭrāṇāṁ hṛidayāni vyadārayat\nnabhaśhcha pṛithivīṁ chaiva tumulo nunādayan","en":"The tumultuous sound rent the hearts of Dhritarashtra's party, reverberating through both heaven and earth.","es":"That tremendous sound pierced the hearts of the sons of Dhrtarastra as it reverberated through the sky and the earth.","er":"And that tumultuous uproar, reverberating through heaven and earth, rent the hearts of Dhrtarastra's sons.","gu":"એ ભેરી ઘોષ આકાશ-ધરતી ધ્રુજાવી ગઈ, અને ધૃતરાષ્ટ્રના સૈનિકોના હૃદય ફફડી ઉઠ્યા."},{"ref":"1.20","ch":1,"v":20,"sa":"अथ व्यवस्थितान् दृष्ट्वा धार्तराष्ट्रान्कपिध्वजः।\nप्रवृत्ते शस्त्रसंपाते धनुरुद्यम्य पाण्डवः।।1.20।।","tr":"atha vyavasthitān dṛiṣhṭvā dhārtarāṣhṭrān kapi-dhwajaḥ\npravṛitte śhastra-sampāte dhanurudyamya pāṇḍavaḥ\nhṛiṣhīkeśhaṁ tadā vākyam idam āha mahī-pate","en":"Then, seeing the people of Dhritarashtra's party standing arrayed and the discharge of weapons about to begin, Arjuna, the son of Pandu whose ensign was a monkey, took up his bow and said the following to Krishna, O Lord of the Earth.","es":"O King, thereafter, seeing Dhrtarastra's men standing in their positions, with all the weapons ready for action, the son of Pandu, Arjuna, who had the insignia of Hanuman on his chariot-flag, raised his bow and said the following to Hrsikesa.","er":"Then Arjuna, whose banner crest was Hanuman, on beholding the sons of Dhrtarastra arrayed, took up his bow, while missiles were beginning to fly.","gu":"ત્યારે કપિધ્વજ અર્જુને ધૃતરાષ્ટ્રની સેનાને સામે જોઈ, શસ્ત્ર ઉઠાવવાની તૈયારી જોઈ, ધનુષ ઉઠાવ્યું અને શ્રીકૃષ્ણ સમક્ષ આ વચન કહ્યા."},{"ref":"1.21","ch":1,"v":21,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nहृषीकेशं तदा वाक्यमिदमाह महीपते।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये रथं स्थापय मेऽच्युत।।1.21।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nsenayor ubhayor madhye rathaṁ sthāpaya me ’chyuta","en":"Arjuna said, \"O Krishna, place my chariot in the middle between the two armies, so that I may behold those who stand here, desirous to fight, and know with whom I must fight when the battle is about to commence.\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Acyuta, please place my chariot between both the armies.\"","er":"And he spoke, O Lord of the Earth, these words to Sri Krishna: Arjuna said, “Draw up my chariot, O Krishna, between the two armies.","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે અચ્યુત, બંને સૈન્યોની વચ્ચે મારો રથ ઉભો રાખો."},{"ref":"1.22","ch":1,"v":22,"sa":"यावदेतान्निरीक्षेऽहं योद्धुकामानवस्थितान्।\nकैर्मया सह योद्धव्यमस्मिन्रणसमुद्यमे।।1.22।।","tr":"yāvadetān nirīkṣhe ’haṁ yoddhu-kāmān avasthitān\nkairmayā saha yoddhavyam asmin raṇa-samudyame","en":"Arjuna said, \"O Krishna, place my chariot in the middle between the two armies, so that I may behold those who stand here, desirous to fight, and know with whom I must fight when the battle is about to commence.\"","es":"Until I survey those who stand intent on fighting and those who are about to engage in battle with me in this impending war.","er":"So that I may have a good look at those who are standing, eager to fight, and know with whom I must fight in this enterprise of war.","gu":"જેથી હું અહીં યુદ્ધ ઈચ્છતા એકઠા થયેલ વીરોને જોઈ શકું, અને સમજી શકું કે આ યુદ્ધમાં મારે કોની સામે લડવાનું છે."},{"ref":"1.23","ch":1,"v":23,"sa":"योत्स्यमानानवेक्षेऽहं य एतेऽत्र समागताः।\nधार्तराष्ट्रस्य दुर्बुद्धेर्युद्धे प्रियचिकीर्षवः।।1.23।।","tr":"yotsyamānān avekṣhe ’haṁ ya ete ’tra samāgatāḥ\ndhārtarāṣhṭrasya durbuddher yuddhe priya-chikīrṣhavaḥ","en":"For I desire to observe those who are assembled here to fight, wishing to please in battle the evil-minded Duryodhana—the son of Dhritarashtra.","es":"These who have assembled here and want to accomplish in the war what is dear to the perverted son of Dhrtarastra, I find them to be intent on fighting.","er":"I wish to see those gathered here ready to fight in this battle in order to please the evil-minded son of Dhrtarashtra.","gu":"દુર્યોધનનું ભલું ઈચ્છી, આ સંગ્રામમાં ઉતરેલ સૌ રાજાઓ અને યોદ્ધાઓને હું નિહાળવા ઈચ્છું છું."},{"ref":"1.24","ch":1,"v":24,"sa":"संजय उवाच\nएवमुक्तो हृषीकेशो गुडाकेशेन भारत।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये स्थापयित्वा रथोत्तमम्।।1.24।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\nevam ukto hṛiṣhīkeśho guḍākeśhena bhārata\nsenayor ubhayor madhye sthāpayitvā rathottamam","en":"Sanjaya said, Thus addressed by Arjuna, Krishna stationed the best of chariots, O Dhritarashtra, in the midst of the two armies.","es":"Sanjaya said, \"O scion of the line of Bharata, Hrishikesa, being told so by Gudakesa (Arjuna), placed the excellent chariot between the two armies, in front of Bhishma and Drona as well as all the rulers of the earth, and said, 'O Partha, behold these assembled Kurus!'\"","er":"Sanjaya said: Thus addressed by Arjuna, Sri Krishna drew up the best of chariots between the two armies, in full view of Bhisma, Drona, and all the other kings, O Dhrtarastra. He then said, \"O Arjuna, behold these assembled Kauravas.\"","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: હે ધૃતરાષ્ટ્ર, અર્જુનના આ વચન સાંભળી, શ્રીકૃષ્ણે એ ભવ્ય રથ બંને સૈન્યોની ઠીક વચ્ચે લઈ જઈ ઉભો રાખ્યો."},{"ref":"1.25","ch":1,"v":25,"sa":"भीष्मद्रोणप्रमुखतः सर्वेषां च महीक्षिताम्।\nउवाच पार्थ पश्यैतान्समवेतान्कुरूनिति।।1.25।।","tr":"bhīṣhma-droṇa-pramukhataḥ sarveṣhāṁ cha mahī-kṣhitām\nuvācha pārtha paśhyaitān samavetān kurūn iti","en":"In front of Bhishma and Drona, and all the rulers of the earth, he said: \"O Arjuna, son of Pritha, behold these Kurus gathered together.\"","es":"Sanjaya said, \"O scion of the line of Bharata (Dhrtarashtra), Hrsikesa, being told so by Gudakesa (Arjuna), placed the excellent chariot between the two armies, in front of Bhisma and Drona as well as all the rulers of the earth, and said, 'O Partha (Arjuna), behold these assembled people of the Kuru dynasty.'\"","er":"Sanjaya said: Thus addressed by Arjuna, Sri Krishna drew up the best of chariots between the two armies, in full view of Bhisma, Drona, and all the other kings, O Dhrtarastra. He then said, \"O Arjuna, behold these assembled Kauravas.\"","gu":"ભીષ્મ, દ્રોણ, અને સઘળા રાજાઓની સામે ઉભા રહી, ભગવાને કહ્યું: હે અર્જુન, જો — આ ભેગા થયેલ કુરુઓને નિહાળ."},{"ref":"1.26","ch":1,"v":26,"sa":"तत्रापश्यत्स्थितान्पार्थः पितृ़नथ पितामहान्।\nआचार्यान्मातुलान्भ्रातृ़न्पुत्रान्पौत्रान्सखींस्तथा।।1.26।।","tr":"tatrāpaśhyat sthitān pārthaḥ pitṝīn atha pitāmahān\nāchāryān mātulān bhrātṝīn putrān pautrān sakhīṁs tathā\nśhvaśhurān suhṛidaśh chaiva senayor ubhayor api","en":"Then, Arjuna (son of Pritha) saw there (in the armies) stationed fathers, grandfathers, teachers, maternal uncles, brothers, sons, grandsons, and friends.","es":"Then Arjuna saw, marshalled among both the armies, his uncles, grandfathers, teachers, maternal uncles, brothers, cousins, sons, grandsons, comrades, fathers-in-law, and friends.","er":"Then, as Arjuna looked on, he saw standing there fathers, grandfathers, teachers, uncles, brothers, sons, grandsons, and comrades.","gu":"ત્યાં અર્જુને બંને સૈન્યોમાં — પિતા, પિતામહ, ગુરુઓ, કાકા, ભાઈઓ, પુત્રો, પૌત્રો, સસરા, અને મિત્રો — સૌ સ્વજનો ઉભેલ જોયા."},{"ref":"1.27","ch":1,"v":27,"sa":"श्वशुरान्सुहृदश्चैव सेनयोरुभयोरपि।\nतान्समीक्ष्य स कौन्तेयः सर्वान्बन्धूनवस्थितान्।।1.27।।","tr":"tān samīkṣhya sa kaunteyaḥ sarvān bandhūn avasthitān\nkṛipayā parayāviṣhṭo viṣhīdann idam abravīt","en":"He saw fathers-in-law and friends in both the armies. The son of Kunti, Arjuna, seeing all those kinsmen thus standing arrayed, spoke sorrowfully, deeply filled with pity.","es":"The son of Kunti, Arjuna, seeing all those relatives arrayed there, became overwhelmed by supreme compassion and sorrowfully said this:","er":"Fathers-in-law and dear friends in both armies, when Arjuna saw all these kinsmen arrayed,","gu":"બંને પક્ષે આ સઘળા સ્વજનોને સામસામે ઉભેલ જોઈ, અર્જુનના હૃદયમાં ઊંડી કરુણા ઉભરાઈ — અને સ્નેહ ભરી આ વાણી નીકળી."},{"ref":"1.28","ch":1,"v":28,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nकृपया परयाऽऽविष्टो विषीदन्निदमब्रवीत्।\nदृष्ट्वेमं स्वजनं कृष्ण युयुत्सुं समुपस्थितम्।।1.28।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\ndṛiṣhṭvemaṁ sva-janaṁ kṛiṣhṇa yuyutsuṁ samupasthitam","en":"Arjuna said, \"O Krishna, seeing my kinsmen arrayed here, eager to fight,","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Krsna, seeing these relatives and friends who have assembled here with the intention of fighting, my limbs become languid and my mouth becomes completely dry.\"","er":"He was filled with deep compassion and said these words in despair:","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે કૃષ્ણ, યુદ્ધ કરવા તૈયાર ઊભેલા મારા સ્વજનોને જોઈ, મારાં અંગો શિથિલ થઈ જાય છે અને મારું મોં સુકાઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"1.29","ch":1,"v":29,"sa":"सीदन्ति मम गात्राणि मुखं च परिशुष्यति।\nवेपथुश्च शरीरे मे रोमहर्षश्च जायते।।1.29।।","tr":"sīdanti mama gātrāṇi mukhaṁ cha pariśhuṣhyati\nvepathuśh cha śharīre me roma-harṣhaśh cha jāyate","en":"My limbs fail, my mouth is parched, my body quivers, and my hair stands on end.","es":"And there is trembling in my body, and my hair stands on end; the Gandiva (bow) slips from my hand and my skin burns intensely.","er":"My limbs have weakened, my mouth has become parched, my body is trembling, and my hairs are standing on end.","gu":"મારા અંગો ભાંગી પડે છે, શરીર ધ્રૂજે છે, મોં સૂકાઈ ગયું છે, અને રૂવાંટા ઊભાં થઈ ગયાં છે."},{"ref":"1.30","ch":1,"v":30,"sa":"गाण्डीवं स्रंसते हस्तात्त्वक्चैव परिदह्यते।\nन च शक्नोम्यवस्थातुं भ्रमतीव च मे मनः।।1.30।।","tr":"gāṇḍīvaṁ sraṁsate hastāt tvak chaiva paridahyate\nna cha śhaknomy avasthātuṁ bhramatīva cha me manaḥ","en":"The Gandiva slips from my hand, and my skin burns all over; I am unable to stand, and my mind is reeling, as it were.","es":"Moreover, O Kesava (Krishna), I am not able to stand firmly, and my mind seems to be whirling. And I observe the omens to be adverse.","er":"The bow Gandiva slips from my hand and my skin is burning. I can no longer stand. My mind seems to be reeling.","gu":"ગાંડીવ ધનુષ્ય મારા હાથમાંથી સરી પડે છે, ત્વચા સળગી ઊઠે છે; હું ઊભો રહી શકતો નથી અને મારું મન ભ્રમિત થઈ ગયું છે."},{"ref":"1.31","ch":1,"v":31,"sa":"निमित्तानि च पश्यामि विपरीतानि केशव।\nन च श्रेयोऽनुपश्यामि हत्वा स्वजनमाहवे।।1.31।।","tr":"nimittāni cha paśhyāmi viparītāni keśhava\nna cha śhreyo ’nupaśhyāmi hatvā sva-janam āhave","en":"And I see ill omens, O Kesava. I do not see any good in slaying my kinsmen in battle.","es":"Besides, I do not see any good to be derived from killing my own people in battle. O Krsna, I do not hanker after victory, nor even a kingdom, nor pleasures.","er":"I see, Kṛṣṇa, inauspicious omens. I foresee no good in slaying my kinsmen in battle.","gu":"હે કેશવ, હું અપશુકન જોઉં છું; આ યુદ્ધમાં સ્વજનોનો નાશ કરવામાં મને કોઈ કલ્યાણ દેખાતું નથી."},{"ref":"1.32","ch":1,"v":32,"sa":"न काङ्क्षे विजयं कृष्ण न च राज्यं सुखानि च।\nकिं नो राज्येन गोविन्द किं भोगैर्जीवितेन वा।।1.32।।","tr":"na kāṅkṣhe vijayaṁ kṛiṣhṇa na cha rājyaṁ sukhāni cha\nkiṁ no rājyena govinda kiṁ bhogair jīvitena vā","en":"I desire not victory, O Krishna, nor kingdom, nor pleasures.\nWhat use is dominion to us, O Krishna, or pleasures or even life?","es":"O Govinda! What need do we have of a kingdom, or what need of enjoyments and livelihood? Those for whom kingdom, enjoyments, and pleasures are desired by us—such as teachers, uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, as well as relatives—those very ones stand arrayed for battle, risking their lives and wealth.","er":"I desire no victory, nor empire, nor pleasures. What have we to do with empire, O Krishna, or enjoyment, or even life?","gu":"હે કૃષ્ણ, મને વિજય, રાજ્ય કે સુખ — કશું જ નથી જોઈતું; જ્યારે જેઓ માટે આ સૌ ઈચ્છીએ, તેઓ જ સામે ઊભા હોય, ત્યારે આ રાજ્ય, ભોગ કે જીવનનો પણ શો અર્થ?"},{"ref":"1.33","ch":1,"v":33,"sa":"येषामर्थे काङ्क्षितं नो राज्यं भोगाः सुखानि च।\nत इमेऽवस्थिता युद्धे प्राणांस्त्यक्त्वा धनानि च।।1.33।।","tr":"yeṣhām arthe kāṅkṣhitaṁ no rājyaṁ bhogāḥ sukhāni cha\nta ime ’vasthitā yuddhe prāṇāṁs tyaktvā dhanāni cha","en":"Those for whose sake we desire kingdom, enjoyments, and pleasures stand here in battle, having renounced life and wealth.","es":"- O Govinda! What need do we have of a kingdom, or what need of enjoyments and livelihood? Those for whom kingdom, enjoyments, and pleasures are desired by us—such as teachers, uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, as well as relatives—those very ones stand arrayed for battle, risking their lives and wealth.","er":"Those for whose sake we desire empire, enjoyment, and pleasures, stand here in war, renouncing life and wealth.","gu":"જેઓ માટે આપણે રાજ્ય, ભોગ અને સુખ ઈચ્છીએ છીએ, તે ગુરુઓ, પિતા, પુત્રો અને અન્ય સ્વજનો — પ્રાણ અને ધનની આશ છોડી — અહીં યુદ્ધભૂમિ પર ઊભા છે."},{"ref":"1.34","ch":1,"v":34,"sa":"आचार्याः पितरः पुत्रास्तथैव च पितामहाः।\nमातुलाः श्चशुराः पौत्राः श्यालाः सम्बन्धिनस्तथा।।1.34।।","tr":"āchāryāḥ pitaraḥ putrās tathaiva cha pitāmahāḥ\nmātulāḥ śhvaśhurāḥ pautrāḥ śhyālāḥ sambandhinas tathā","en":"Teachers, fathers, sons, and grandfathers, maternal uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, and other relatives—","es":"- O Govinda! What need do we have of a kingdom, or what need of enjoyments and livelihood? Those for whom kingdom, enjoyments, and pleasures are desired by us—such as teachers, uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, as well as relatives—those very ones stand arrayed for battle, risking their lives and wealth.","er":"all these are to be regarded as one's own self.\nTeachers, fathers, sons, grandfathers, uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, and other kinsmen—all these are to be regarded as one's own self.","gu":"ગુરુઓ, પિતા, પુત્રો, દાદા, કાકા, સસરા, પૌત્રો, સાળા અને અન્ય સ્વજનો — આ સૌ અહીં ઊભા છે."},{"ref":"1.35","ch":1,"v":35,"sa":"एतान्न हन्तुमिच्छामि घ्नतोऽपि मधुसूदन।\nअपि त्रैलोक्यराज्यस्य हेतोः किं नु महीकृते।।1.35।।","tr":"etān na hantum ichchhāmi ghnato ’pi madhusūdana\napi trailokya-rājyasya hetoḥ kiṁ nu mahī-kṛite","en":"These I do not wish to kill, O Krishna, even though they kill me, for the sake of dominion over the three worlds; leave alone killing them for the sake of the earth.\"","es":"O Madhusudana, even if I am killed, I do not want to kill these even for the sake of a kingdom extending across the three worlds; let alone doing so for the earth!","er":"I would not slay them, even if they might slay me, for the sovereignty of the three worlds—how much less for this earth, O Krsna?","gu":"હે કૃષ્ણ, ત્રણ લોકનું રાજ્ય મળે તો પણ, — ને આ પૃથ્વીની તો વાત જ ક્યાં? — આ સ્વજનોને હું મારવા ઈચ્છતો નથી, ભલે ને તેઓ મને મારી નાખે."},{"ref":"1.36","ch":1,"v":36,"sa":"निहत्य धार्तराष्ट्रान्नः का प्रीतिः स्याज्जनार्दन।\nपापमेवाश्रयेदस्मान्हत्वैतानाततायिनः।।1.36।।","tr":"nihatya dhārtarāṣhṭrān naḥ kā prītiḥ syāj janārdana\npāpam evāśhrayed asmān hatvaitān ātatāyinaḥ","en":"By killing these sons of Dhritarashtra, what pleasure could be ours, O Janardana? Only sin would accrue to us from killing these felons.","es":"O Janardana, what happiness will we gain by killing the sons of Dhrtarastra? We will only incur sin by killing these wrongdoers.","er":"If we were to kill the sons of Dhrtarastra, what joy would be ours, O Krsna? Sin alone would accrue to us if we killed these murderous felons.","gu":"ધૃતરાષ્ટ્રના આ પુત્રોને મારવાથી આપણને શો આનંદ મળશે? આ અધર્મીઓની હત્યા કરવાથી તો માત્ર પાપ જ ઉપજશે."},{"ref":"1.37","ch":1,"v":37,"sa":"तस्मान्नार्हा वयं हन्तुं धार्तराष्ट्रान्स्वबान्धवान्।\nस्वजनं हि कथं हत्वा सुखिनः स्याम माधव।।1.37।।","tr":"tasmān nārhā vayaṁ hantuṁ dhārtarāṣhṭrān sa-bāndhavān \nsva-janaṁ hi kathaṁ hatvā sukhinaḥ syāma mādhava","en":"Therefore, we should not kill the sons of Dhritarashtra, our relatives; for how can we be happy by killing our own kin, O Madhava (Krishna)?","es":"Therefore, it is not proper for us to kill the sons of Dhrtarastra, who are our own relatives. For, O Madhava, how can we be happy by killing our kinsmen?","er":"Therefore, it is not befitting for us to slay our kin, the sons of Dhrtarastra. For if we kill our kinsmen, O Krsna, how can we be happy?","gu":"હે માધવ, ધૃતરાષ્ટ્રના પુત્રો — આ આપણા જ સ્વજનો — ને મારીને આપણે કેવી રીતે સુખી થઈ શકીએ? પોતાના માણસોને મારવા એ આપણા માટે યોગ્ય નથી."},{"ref":"1.38","ch":1,"v":38,"sa":"यद्यप्येते न पश्यन्ति लोभोपहतचेतसः।\nकुलक्षयकृतं दोषं मित्रद्रोहे च पातकम्।।1.38।।","tr":"yady apy ete na paśhyanti lobhopahata-chetasaḥ\nkula-kṣhaya-kṛitaṁ doṣhaṁ mitra-drohe cha pātakam","en":"Though they, with intelligence overpowered by greed, see no evil in the destruction of families and no sin in hostility to friends,","es":"- O Janardana, although these people, whose hearts have become perverted by greed, do not see the evil arising from destroying the family and sinning in hostility towards friends, yet how can we, who clearly see the evil arising from destroying the family, remain unaware of the need to abstain from this sin?","er":"Though these people, whose minds are overpowered by greed, see no evil in the destruction of a clan and no sin in treachery to friends,","gu":"ભલે ને તેઓ — લોભથી આંધળા — કુળના નાશમાં કોઈ પાપ ન દેખતા હોય, અને મિત્રોને છેતરવામાં દોષ ન ગણતા હોય —"},{"ref":"1.39","ch":1,"v":39,"sa":"कथं न ज्ञेयमस्माभिः पापादस्मान्निवर्तितुम्।\nकुलक्षयकृतं दोषं प्रपश्यद्भिर्जनार्दन।।1.39।।","tr":"kathaṁ na jñeyam asmābhiḥ pāpād asmān nivartitum\nkula-kṣhaya-kṛitaṁ doṣhaṁ prapaśhyadbhir janārdana","en":"Why should we not, who clearly see the evil in the destruction of families, learn to turn away from this sin, O Janardana (Krishna)?","es":"- O Janardana, although these people, whose hearts have become perverted by greed, do not see the evil arising from destroying the family and sinning in hostility towards friends, yet how can we, who clearly see the evil arising from destroying the family, remain unaware of the need to abstain from this sin?","er":"Why should we not learn to shun this crime—we who see the evil of ruining a clan, O Krishna?","gu":"હે જનાર્દન, આપણે તો કુળના નાશમાં રહેલ દોષ સ્પષ્ટ જોઈ શકીએ છીએ; તો પછી આ પાપથી ફરી જવાનું આપણે કેમ ન શીખીએ?"},{"ref":"1.40","ch":1,"v":40,"sa":"कुलक्षये प्रणश्यन्ति कुलधर्माः सनातनाः।\nधर्मे नष्टे कुलं कृत्स्नमधर्मोऽभिभवत्युत।।1.40।।","tr":"kula-kṣhaye praṇaśhyanti kula-dharmāḥ sanātanāḥ\ndharme naṣhṭe kulaṁ kṛitsnam adharmo ’bhibhavaty uta","en":"In the destruction of a family, the immemorial religious rites of that family perish; on the destruction of spirituality, impiety indeed, overwhelms the whole family.","es":"From the ruin of the family, the traditional rites and duties are totally destroyed. When rites and duties are destroyed, vice overwhelms the entire family.","er":"With the ruin of a clan, its ancient traditions perish, and when traditions perish, lawlessness overtakes the whole clan.","gu":"જ્યારે કુળનો નાશ થાય છે, ત્યારે તેની ચિરંતન ધાર્મિક પરંપરાઓ નષ્ટ થઈ જાય છે; અને ધર્મ નષ્ટ થતાં સમગ્ર કુળ પર અધર્મ હાવી થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"1.41","ch":1,"v":41,"sa":"अधर्माभिभवात्कृष्ण प्रदुष्यन्ति कुलस्त्रियः।\nस्त्रीषु दुष्टासु वार्ष्णेय जायते वर्णसङ्करः।।1.41।।","tr":"adharmābhibhavāt kṛiṣhṇa praduṣhyanti kula-striyaḥ\nstrīṣhu duṣhṭāsu vārṣhṇeya jāyate varṇa-saṅkaraḥ","en":"O Krishna, by the prevalence of impiety, the women of the family become corrupt; and, when women are corrupted, O Varshenya (descendant of Vrishni), intermingling of castes arises.","es":"O Krishna, when vice predominates, the women of the family become corrupt. O descendant of the Vrsnis, when women become corrupted, it results in the intermingling of castes.","er":"When lawlessness prevails, O Krsna, the women of the clan become corrupted; when women become corrupted, there arises an intermixing of classes.","gu":"હે કૃષ્ણ, અધર્મ ફેલાતાં કુળની સ્ત્રીઓ ભ્રષ્ટ થઈ જાય છે, અને સ્ત્રીઓ ભ્રષ્ટ થતાં વર્ણસંકર ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે."},{"ref":"1.42","ch":1,"v":42,"sa":"सङ्करो नरकायैव कुलघ्नानां कुलस्य च।\nपतन्ति पितरो ह्येषां लुप्तपिण्डोदकक्रियाः।।1.42।।","tr":"saṅkaro narakāyaiva kula-ghnānāṁ kulasya cha\npatanti pitaro hy eṣhāṁ lupta-piṇḍodaka-kriyāḥ","en":"Confusion of castes leads to hell for the slayers of the family, for their forebears fall, deprived of the offerings of rice-balls and libations of water.","es":"And the intermingling in the family leads the ruiners of the family verily into hell. The forefathers of these fall down (into hell) due to being deprived of the offerings of rice-balls and water.","er":"This mixing of classes leads to hell for the clan itself and its destroyers; for the spirits of their ancestors fall degraded, deprived of the ritual offerings of food and water.","gu":"વર્ણસંકરથી કુળના નાશ કરનારાઓ અને તેમના પૂર્વજો — જેઓ પિંડ અને જળ-ક્રિયાથી વંચિત રહી જાય છે — નરકમાં જઈ પડે છે."},{"ref":"1.43","ch":1,"v":43,"sa":"दोषैरेतैः कुलघ्नानां वर्णसङ्करकारकैः।\nउत्साद्यन्ते जातिधर्माः कुलधर्माश्च शाश्वताः।।1.43।।","tr":"doṣhair etaiḥ kula-ghnānāṁ varṇa-saṅkara-kārakaiḥ\nutsādyante jāti-dharmāḥ kula-dharmāśh cha śhāśhvatāḥ","en":"By these evil deeds of the destroyers of the family, which cause confusion of castes, the eternal religious rites of the caste and the family are destroyed.","es":"Due to the misdeeds of the ruiners of the family, which cause intermingling of castes, the traditional rites and duties of the castes and families are destroyed.","er":"By the sins of the clan-destroyers who bring about intermixing of classes, the ancient traditions of the clans and classes are destroyed.","gu":"કુળનો નાશ કરનારાઓના પાપકર્મોથી વર્ણસંકર ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે, અને આ સંકરથી કુળની સનાતન ધાર્મિક પ્રથાઓ અને જાતિ-ધર્મ નષ્ટ થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"1.44","ch":1,"v":44,"sa":"उत्सन्नकुलधर्माणां मनुष्याणां जनार्दन।\nनरकेऽनियतं वासो भवतीत्यनुशुश्रुम।।1.44।।","tr":"utsanna-kula-dharmāṇāṁ manuṣhyāṇāṁ janārdana\nnarake ‘niyataṁ vāso bhavatītyanuśhuśhruma","en":"We have heard, O Janardana, that those men in whose families the religious practices have been destroyed are inevitably destined to dwell in hell for an unknown period.","es":"O Janardana, we have heard that living in hell is inevitable for those whose family duties are destroyed.","er":"For those whose clan laws are destroyed, dwelling in hell is ordained, O Krishna; thus, we have heard.","gu":"હે જનાર્દન, અમે સાંભળ્યું છે કે જેમના કુળ-ધર્મ નષ્ટ થઈ ગયા હોય, તેવા મનુષ્યો અનિશ્ચિત સમય સુધી નર્કમાં વાસ કરે છે."},{"ref":"1.45","ch":1,"v":45,"sa":"अहो बत महत्पापं कर्तुं व्यवसिता वयम्।\nयद्राज्यसुखलोभेन हन्तुं स्वजनमुद्यताः।।1.45।।","tr":"aho bata mahat pāpaṁ kartuṁ vyavasitā vayam\nyad rājya-sukha-lobhena hantuṁ sva-janam udyatāḥ","en":"Alas! We are involved in a great sin, for we are prepared to kill our kinsmen, out of greed for the pleasures of a kingdom.","es":"What a pity that we have resolved to commit a great sin, eager to kill our own kith and kin out of greed for the pleasures of a kingdom!","er":"Alas! We have resolved to commit a great sin, for we are ready to slay our kin out of desire for sovereignty and enjoyment.","gu":"અફસોસ! અમે રાજ્યના ભોગ-સુખની લાલચમાં આવીને, પોતાના જ સ્વજનોને મારવા તૈયાર થઈ, ઘોર પાપ કરવા જઈ રહ્યા છીએ."},{"ref":"1.46","ch":1,"v":46,"sa":"यदि मामप्रतीकारमशस्त्रं शस्त्रपाणयः।\nधार्तराष्ट्रा रणे हन्युस्तन्मे क्षेमतरं भवेत्।।1.46।।","tr":"yadi mām apratīkāram aśhastraṁ śhastra-pāṇayaḥ\ndhārtarāṣhṭrā raṇe hanyus tan me kṣhemataraṁ bhavet","en":"If the sons of Dhritarashtra, with weapons in hand, should slay me in battle, unresisting and unarmed, that would be better for me.","es":"If, in this battle, the sons of Dhrtarastra, armed with weapons, kill me, who am non-resistant and unarmed, that will be more beneficial for me.","er":"If the well-armed sons of Dhrtarastra should slay me in battle, unresisting and unarmed, that would be better for me.","gu":"જો ધૃતરાષ્ટ્રના પુત્રો શસ્ત્રરહિત અને પ્રતિકારહીન એવા મને યુદ્ધમાં મારી નાખે, તો પણ તે મારા માટે વધારે ઉત્તમ રહેશે."},{"ref":"1.47","ch":1,"v":47,"sa":"सञ्जय उवाच\nएवमुक्त्वाऽर्जुनः संख्ये रथोपस्थ उपाविशत्।\nविसृज्य सशरं चापं शोकसंविग्नमानसः।।1.47।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\nevam uktvārjunaḥ saṅkhye rathopastha upāviśhat\nvisṛijya sa-śharaṁ chāpaṁ śhoka-saṁvigna-mānasaḥ","en":"Sanjaya said, Having thus spoken in the midst of the battlefield, Arjuna cast away his bow and arrow and, his mind overwhelmed with sorrow, sat down on the seat of the chariot.","es":"Sanjaya narrated: Having said so, Arjuna, with a mind afflicted by sorrow, sat down on the chariot in the midst of the battle, casting aside his bow along with the arrows.","er":"Sanjaya said: Having spoken thus on the battlefield, Arjuna threw aside his bow and arrows and sat down on the chariot seat, his heart overwhelmed with grief.","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: યુદ્ધભૂમિની વચ્ચે આ પ્રમાણે કહીને, અર્જુને ધનુષ્ય અને બાણ છોડી દઈ, શોકથી ઘેરાયેલ મને રથના આસન પર બેસી ગયા."},{"ref":"2.1","ch":2,"v":1,"sa":"सञ्जय उवाच\nतं तथा कृपयाऽविष्टमश्रुपूर्णाकुलेक्षणम्।\nविषीदन्तमिदं वाक्यमुवाच मधुसूदनः।।2.1।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\ntaṁ tathā kṛipayāviṣhṭamaśhru pūrṇākulekṣhaṇam\nviṣhīdantamidaṁ vākyam uvācha madhusūdanaḥ","en":"Sanjaya said: To him, who was thus overcome with pity, despondent, with eyes full of tears and agitated, Madhusudana (the destroyer of Madhu) or Krishna spoke these words.","es":"Sanjaya said: To him who had been filled with pity, whose eyes were filled with tears and showed distress, and who was sorrowing, Madhusudana uttered these words.","er":"Sanjaya said: To him, who was overcome with pity, whose eyes were wet with tears, who was sorrow-stricken and bore a bewildered look, Sri Krishna spoke as follows:","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: જે કરુણાથી વ્યાકુળ, વિષાદ-ગ્રસ્ત અને અશ્રુભરી આંખોવાળા અર્જુનને, ભગવાન કૃષ્ણે આ શબ્દો કહ્યા."},{"ref":"2.2","ch":2,"v":2,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nकुतस्त्वा कश्मलमिदं विषमे समुपस्थितम्।\nअनार्यजुष्टमस्वर्ग्यमकीर्तिकरमर्जुन।।2.2।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nkutastvā kaśhmalamidaṁ viṣhame samupasthitam\nanārya-juṣhṭamaswargyam akīrti-karam arjuna","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"From whence has this perilous strait come upon you, this dejection which is unworthy of you, disgraceful, and which will close the gates of heaven upon you, O Arjuna?\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O Arjuna, in this perilous place, whence has this impurity come to you, entertained by unenlightened persons, which does not lead to heaven and brings infamy?\"","er":"The Lord said, \"Whence comes this despondency upon you, O Arjuna, in this crisis? It is unfitting for a noble person; it is disgraceful and it obstructs one's attainment of heaven.\"","gu":"કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે અર્જુન, આ કટોકટીના ક્ષણે તારામાં આ કાયરતા ક્યાંથી આવી? આ તને શોભતું નથી, આ અપ્રતિષ્ઠાકારક છે અને સ્વર્ગના દ્વાર બંધ કરનારું છે."},{"ref":"2.3","ch":2,"v":3,"sa":"क्लैब्यं मा स्म गमः पार्थ नैतत्त्वय्युपपद्यते।\nक्षुद्रं हृदयदौर्बल्यं त्यक्त्वोत्तिष्ठ परन्तप।।2.3।।","tr":"klaibyaṁ mā sma gamaḥ pārtha naitat tvayyupapadyate\nkṣhudraṁ hṛidaya-daurbalyaṁ tyaktvottiṣhṭha parantapa","en":"Do not yield to impotence, O Arjuna, son of Pritha. It does not befit you. Cast off this mean weakness of the heart! Stand up, O conqueror of foes!","es":"O Partha, do not yield to unmanliness. This does not befit you. O scorcher of foes, arise, giving up the petty weakness of heart.","er":"Do not yield to unmanliness, O Arjuna, it does not befit you. Shake off this base faint-heartedness and arise, O conqueror of foes!"},{"ref":"2.4","ch":2,"v":4,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nकथं भीष्ममहं संख्ये द्रोणं च मधुसूदन।\nइषुभिः प्रतियोत्स्यामि पूजार्हावरिसूदन।।2.4।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nkathaṁ bhīṣhmam ahaṁ sankhye droṇaṁ cha madhusūdana\niṣhubhiḥ pratiyotsyāmi pūjārhāvari-sūdana","en":"Arjuna said, \"O Madhusudana, how can I fight in battle with arrows against Bhishma and Drona, who are worthy of being worshipped, O destroyer of enemies?\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Madhusudana, O destroyer of enemies, how can I fight with arrows in battle against Bhisma and Drona, who are worthy of adoration?\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"O slayer of foes, how can I aim arrows in battle against Bhisma and Drona, who are worthy of reverence?\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે કૃષ્ણ, હે શત્રુઓના નાશ કરનાર, જે ભીષ્મ અને દ્રોણ પૂજ્ય છે, તેમની સામે હું બાણ વડે કઈ રીતે લડી શકું?"},{"ref":"2.5","ch":2,"v":5,"sa":"गुरूनहत्वा हि महानुभावान्\nश्रेयो भोक्तुं भैक्ष्यमपीह लोके।\nहत्वार्थकामांस्तु गुरूनिहैव\nभुञ्जीय भोगान् रुधिरप्रदिग्धान्।।2.5।।","tr":"gurūnahatvā hi mahānubhāvān\nśhreyo bhoktuṁ bhaikṣhyamapīha loke\nhatvārtha-kāmāṁstu gurūnihaiva\nbhuñjīya bhogān rudhira-pradigdhān","en":"Better it is, indeed, in this world to accept alms than to slay the most noble teachers. But if I were to kill them, even in this world, all my enjoyments of wealth and fulfilled desires would be stained with their blood.","es":"Rather than killing the noble-minded elders, it is better in this world to live even on alms. But by killing them, we shall only be enjoying here the pleasures of wealth and desirable things drenched in blood.","er":"It is better even to live on a beggar's fare in this world than to slay these most venerable teachers. If I were to slay my teachers, though they may be degraded by desire for wealth, I would only be enjoying blood-stained pleasures here.","gu":"આ મહાન ગુરુઓને મારી નાખવા કરતાં આ લોકમાં ભિક્ષા માગીને જીવવું વધારે સારું છે; કારણ કે, જો હું તેમને મારું, તો તેમના રક્તથી ખરડાયેલ ભોગ-ઐશ્વર્ય ભોગવવા પડશે."},{"ref":"2.6","ch":2,"v":6,"sa":"न चैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो\nयद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः।\nयानेव हत्वा न जिजीविषाम\nस्तेऽवस्थिताः प्रमुखे धार्तराष्ट्राः।।2.6।।","tr":"na chaitadvidmaḥ kataranno garīyo\nyadvā jayema yadi vā no jayeyuḥ\nyāneva hatvā na jijīviṣhāmas\nte ’vasthitāḥ pramukhe dhārtarāṣhṭrāḥ","en":"I can hardly tell which would be better, that we should conquer them or that they should conquer us. Even the sons of Dhritarashtra, whom we do not wish to slay, stand facing us.","es":"We do not know which is better for us, whether we shall win or they shall conquer us. Those very sons of Dhrtarastra, whom we do not wish to kill, stand in confrontation.","er":"We do not know which of the two is better for us: whether our vanquishing them or their vanquishing us. The very sons of Dhrtarastra, whom, if we were to slay, we would not wish to live, even they are standing in array against us.","gu":"અમે ન જાણી શકીએ કે — અમે તેમને જીતીએ કે તેઓ અમને, — બેમાં શું ઉત્તમ છે. ધૃતરાષ્ટ્રના જે પુત્રોને અમે મારવા ઈચ્છતા નથી, તે જ આપણી સામે ઊભા છે."},{"ref":"2.7","ch":2,"v":7,"sa":"कार्पण्यदोषोपहतस्वभावः\nपृच्छामि त्वां धर्मसंमूढचेताः।\nयच्छ्रेयः स्यान्निश्िचतं ब्रूहि तन्मे\nशिष्यस्तेऽहं शाधि मां त्वां प्रपन्नम्।।2.7।।","tr":"kārpaṇya-doṣhopahata-svabhāvaḥ\npṛichchhāmi tvāṁ dharma-sammūḍha-chetāḥ\nyach-chhreyaḥ syānniśhchitaṁ brūhi tanme\nśhiṣhyaste ’haṁ śhādhi māṁ tvāṁ prapannam","en":"My heart is overpowered by the taint of pity; my mind is confused as to my duty. I ask Thee: Tell me decisively what is good for me. I am Thy disciple; instruct me, who has taken refuge in Thee.","es":"With my nature overpowered by weak commiseration, my mind bewildered about duty, I supplicate You. Tell me for certain what is better; I am Your disciple, having taken refuge in You. Instruct me.","er":"With my heart stricken by the fault of weak compassion, my mind perplexed about my duty, I implore you to tell me for certain what is good for me. I am your disciple; teach me, who have taken refuge in you.","gu":"મારું હૃદય કરુણાથી ઘેરાઈ ગયું છે, ધર્મ વિષે મારી બુદ્ધિ ભ્રમિત છે; હું તારો શિષ્ય છું, તારી શરણમાં આવ્યો છું, તું મને નિર્ણાયક રૂપે કહે કે મારા માટે શું હિતકર છે."},{"ref":"2.8","ch":2,"v":8,"sa":"न हि प्रपश्यामि ममापनुद्या\nद्यच्छोकमुच्छोषणमिन्द्रियाणाम्।\nअवाप्य भूमावसपत्नमृद्धम्\nराज्यं सुराणामपि चाधिपत्यम्।।2.8।।","tr":"na hi prapaśhyāmi mamāpanudyād\nyach-chhokam uchchhoṣhaṇam-indriyāṇām\navāpya bhūmāv-asapatnamṛiddhaṁ\nrājyaṁ surāṇāmapi chādhipatyam","en":"I do not see that this sorrow that burns up my senses would be removed, even if I were to attain prosperous and unrivaled dominion on earth or lordship over the gods.","es":"For I do not see anything that, even after acquiring on this earth a prosperous kingdom free from enemies and even sovereignty over the gods, can remove my sorrow that is blasting the senses.","er":"Even if I were to win unchallenged sovereignty of a prosperous earth or even lordship over the Devas, I do not feel that it would dispel the grief that withers up my senses.","gu":"પૃથ્વી પર નિષ્કંટક રાજ્ય મળે, કે દેવો પર સ્વામિત્વ મળે, તો પણ ઇન્દ્રિયોને સળગાવતા આ શોકને શું દૂર કરી શકે, — તે હું જોઈ શકતો નથી."},{"ref":"2.9","ch":2,"v":9,"sa":"सञ्जय उवाच\nएवमुक्त्वा हृषीकेशं गुडाकेशः परन्तप।\nन योत्स्य इति गोविन्दमुक्त्वा तूष्णीं बभूव ह।।2.9।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\nevam-uktvā hṛiṣhīkeśhaṁ guḍākeśhaḥ parantapa\nna yotsya iti govindam uktvā tūṣhṇīṁ babhūva ha","en":"Sanjaya said: Having spoken thus to Hrishikesha, the Lord of the senses, Arjuna, the conqueror of sleep and destroyer of foes, said, \"I will not fight,\" and became silent.","es":"Sanjaya said: Having spoken thus to Hrsikesa (Krsna), Gudakesa (Arjuna), the afflictor of foes, verily became silent, telling Govinda, 'I shall not fight.'","er":"Sanjaya said, Having thus spoken to Sri Krsna, Arjuna, the conqueror of sleep and the scorcher of foes, said, \"I will not fight,\" and became silent.","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: હૃષીકેશ કૃષ્ણને આ પ્રમાણે કહ્યા પછી, ગુડાકેશ અર્જુન 'હું નહિ લડું' એમ કહીને મૌન ધારણ કરી ગયા."},{"ref":"2.10","ch":2,"v":10,"sa":"तमुवाच हृषीकेशः प्रहसन्निव भारत।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये विषीदन्तमिदं वचः।।2.10।।","tr":"tam-uvācha hṛiṣhīkeśhaḥ prahasanniva bhārata\nsenayorubhayor-madhye viṣhīdantam-idaṁ vachaḥ","en":"To him who was despondent in the midst of the two armies, Krishna, smiling, O Bharata, spoke these words.","es":"O descendant of Bharata, Hrsikesa, mocking as it were, said these words to him who was sorrowing between the two armies:","er":"O King, to him who was thus sorrowing between the two armies, Sri Krishna spoke the following words, as if smiling (by way of ridicule).","gu":"હે ભારત, બે સેનાઓની વચ્ચે વિષાદ-ગ્રસ્ત અર્જુનને, ભગવાન કૃષ્ણ મંદ સ્મિત સાથે આ વચન બોલ્યા."},{"ref":"2.11","ch":2,"v":11,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nअशोच्यानन्वशोचस्त्वं प्रज्ञावादांश्च भाषसे।\nगतासूनगतासूंश्च नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः।।2.11।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\naśhochyān-anvaśhochas-tvaṁ prajñā-vādānśh cha bhāṣhase\ngatāsūn-agatāsūnśh-cha nānuśhochanti paṇḍitāḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"You have grieved for those who should not be grieved for; yet, you speak words of wisdom. The wise grieve neither for the living nor for the dead.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"You grieve for those who are not to be grieved for; and you speak words of wisdom! The learned do not grieve for the departed nor for those who have not departed.","er":"The Lord said, \"You grieve for those who should not be grieved for; yet you speak words of wisdom. The wise grieve neither for the dead nor for the living.\"","gu":"કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: તું જેમને માટે શોક ન કરવો ઘટે, તેમને માટે શોક કરે છે, અને છતાં જ્ઞાનની વાતો કરે છે; પણ જ્ઞાની પુરુષ ન જીવિત માટે, ન મૃત માટે — કોઈ માટે શોક કરતો નથી."},{"ref":"2.12","ch":2,"v":12,"sa":"न त्वेवाहं जातु नासं न त्वं नेमे जनाधिपाः।\nन चैव न भविष्यामः सर्वे वयमतः परम्।।2.12।।","tr":"na tvevāhaṁ jātu nāsaṁ na tvaṁ neme janādhipāḥ\nna chaiva na bhaviṣhyāmaḥ sarve vayamataḥ param","en":"Nor, at any time, was I not, nor thou, nor these rulers of men; nor, verily, shall we ever cease to be hereafter.","es":"But certainly it is not a fact that I did not exist at any time; nor you, nor these rulers of men. And surely it is not that we all shall cease to exist after this.","er":"There never was a time when I did not exist, nor you, nor any of these kings. Nor will there be any time in the future when all of us shall cease to exist.","gu":"ભૂતકાળમાં હું, તું અને આ સૌ રાજાઓ હતા; ભવિષ્યમાં પણ આપણે સૌ રહીશું. આત્મા ક્યારેય અસ્તિત્વ-રહિત ન હતો, ન ક્યારેય થશે."},{"ref":"2.13","ch":2,"v":13,"sa":"देहिनोऽस्मिन्यथा देहे कौमारं यौवनं जरा।\nतथा देहान्तरप्राप्तिर्धीरस्तत्र न मुह्यति।।2.13।।","tr":"dehino ’smin yathā dehe kaumāraṁ yauvanaṁ jarā\ntathā dehāntara-prāptir dhīras tatra na muhyati","en":"Just as the embodied soul passes through childhood, youth, and old age in this body, so too does it pass into another body; the steadfast one does not grieve over this.","es":"As boyhood, youth, and decrepitude are to an embodied being in this present body, so is the acquisition of another body. Therefore, an intelligent person does not get deluded.","er":"Just as the self associated with a body passes through childhood, youth, and old age, so too, at death, it passes into another body. A wise man is not deluded by that.","gu":"જેમ દેહમાં આત્મા બાળપણ, યૌવન અને વૃદ્ધાવસ્થામાંથી પસાર થાય છે, તેમ મૃત્યુ પછી બીજા દેહમાં પ્રવેશ કરે છે. જ્ઞાની વ્યક્તિ આ જાણીને શોક કરતી નથી."},{"ref":"2.14","ch":2,"v":14,"sa":"मात्रास्पर्शास्तु कौन्तेय शीतोष्णसुखदुःखदाः।\nआगमापायिनोऽनित्यास्तांस्तितिक्षस्व भारत।।2.14।।","tr":"mātrā-sparśhās tu kaunteya śhītoṣhṇa-sukha-duḥkha-dāḥ\nāgamāpāyino ’nityās tans-titikṣhasva bhārata","en":"The contact of the senses with the objects, O son of Kunti, which causes heat and cold, pleasure and pain, has a beginning and an end; they are impermanent; endure them bravely, O Arjuna.","es":"But the contacts of the organs with the objects are the producers of cold and heat, happiness, and sorrow. They have a beginning and an end and are transient. Bear them, O descendant of Bharata.","er":"The contact of the senses with their objects, O Arjuna, gives rise to feelings of cold and heat, pleasure and pain. They come and go, never lasting long. Endure them, O Arjuna."},{"ref":"2.15","ch":2,"v":15,"sa":"यं हि न व्यथयन्त्येते पुरुषं पुरुषर्षभ।\nसमदुःखसुखं धीरं सोऽमृतत्वाय कल्पते।।2.15।।","tr":"yaṁ hi na vyathayantyete puruṣhaṁ puruṣharṣhabha\nsama-duḥkha-sukhaṁ dhīraṁ so ’mṛitatvāya kalpate","en":"That firm man, whom surely these afflictions do not, O chief among men, to whom pleasure and pain are the same, is fit for attaining immortality.","es":"O Arjuna, who is foremost among men, verily, the person whom these do not torment, the wise man to whom sorrow and happiness are the same—he is fit for immortality.","er":"For, he whom these do not affect, O chief of men, and to whom pain and pleasure are equal - that steadfast man alone is worthy of immortality.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે વ્યક્તિ સુખ અને દુઃખથી વિચલિત નથી થતી, જે બંનેને સમાન ભાવે સ્વીકારે છે, તે અમૃત-સ્વરૂપ મોક્ષ પ્રાપ્ત કરવા યોગ્ય છે."},{"ref":"2.16","ch":2,"v":16,"sa":"नासतो विद्यते भावो नाभावो विद्यते सतः।\nउभयोरपि दृष्टोऽन्तस्त्वनयोस्तत्त्वदर्शिभिः।।2.16।।","tr":"nāsato vidyate bhāvo nābhāvo vidyate sataḥ\nubhayorapi dṛiṣhṭo ’nta stvanayos tattva-darśhibhiḥ","en":"The unreal has no being; there is no non-being of the real; the truth about both has been seen by the knowers of the truth (or the seers of the essence).","es":"There is no being of the unreal; the real has no non-existence. Yet, the nature of both has been realized by the seers of Truth.","er":"The unreal never comes into being, the real never ceases to be. The truth about these two is seen by the seers.","gu":"અસત્‌નું અસ્તિત્વ નથી, અને સત્‌નો ક્યારેય નાશ નથી. આ બંનેનું સત્ય તત્ત્વ-જ્ઞાાનીઓ એ જાણ્યું છે."},{"ref":"2.17","ch":2,"v":17,"sa":"अविनाशि तु तद्विद्धि येन सर्वमिदं ततम्।\nविनाशमव्ययस्यास्य न कश्चित् कर्तुमर्हति।।2.17।।","tr":"avināśhi tu tadviddhi yena sarvam idaṁ tatam\nvināśham avyayasyāsya na kaśhchit kartum arhati","en":"Know that to be indestructible, by which all this is pervaded. No one can cause the destruction of that, the Imperishable.","es":"But know that to be indestructible by which all this is pervaded. No one can bring about the destruction of this immutable.","er":"Know that to be indestructible by which all this is pervaded. No one can cause the destruction of this immutable.","gu":"જે ચૈતન્ય આ સમગ્ર સૃષ્ટિમાં વ્યાપ્ત છે, તે આત્મા અવિનાશી છે. આ અવ્યયનો નાશ કોઈ કરી શકતું નથી."},{"ref":"2.18","ch":2,"v":18,"sa":"अन्तवन्त इमे देहा नित्यस्योक्ताः शरीरिणः।\nअनाशिनोऽप्रमेयस्य तस्माद्युध्यस्व भारत।।2.18।।","tr":"antavanta ime dehā nityasyoktāḥ śharīriṇaḥ\nanāśhino ’prameyasya tasmād yudhyasva bhārata","en":"These bodies of the embodied Self, which are eternal, indestructible, and immeasurable, are said to have an end. Therefore, fight, O Arjuna.","es":"These destructible bodies are said to belong to the everlasting, indestructible, and indeterminable embodied One. Therefore, O descendant of Bharata, join the battle.","er":"These bodies of the Jiva (the embodied self) are said to have an end, while the Jiva itself is eternal, indestructible, and incomprehensible. Therefore, fight, O Bharata (Arjuna).","gu":"આ દેહ નાશ પામે છે, પરંતુ આત્મા નિત્ય, અવિનાશી અને અપ્રમેય છે. તેથી, હે અર્જુન, ઊઠ અને યુદ્ધ કર."},{"ref":"2.19","ch":2,"v":19,"sa":"य एनं वेत्ति हन्तारं यश्चैनं मन्यते हतम्।\nउभौ तौ न विजानीतो नायं हन्ति न हन्यते।।2.19।।","tr":"ya enaṁ vetti hantāraṁ yaśh chainaṁ manyate hatam\nubhau tau na vijānīto nāyaṁ hanti na hanyate","en":"He who takes the Self to be the slayer and he who thinks it is slain, neither of them knows. It does not slay, nor is it slain.","es":"He who thinks of this One as the killer, and he who thinks of this One as the one being killed, both of them do not know. This One neither kills nor is It killed.","er":"He who considers It (the self) to be the slayer, and he who thinks of It as slain—both are ignorant. For, the self neither slays nor is being slain.","gu":"જે આત્માને ઘાતક માને છે અને જે તેને ઘવાયેલ માને છે — બંને અજ્ઞાાની છે. આત્મા ન મારે, ન મરે."},{"ref":"2.20","ch":2,"v":20,"sa":"न जायते म्रियते वा कदाचि\nन्नायं भूत्वा भविता वा न भूयः।\nअजो नित्यः शाश्वतोऽयं पुराणो\nन हन्यते हन्यमाने शरीरे।।2.20।।","tr":"na jāyate mriyate vā kadāchin\nnāyaṁ bhūtvā bhavitā vā na bhūyaḥ\najo nityaḥ śhāśhvato ’yaṁ purāṇo\nna hanyate hanyamāne śharīre","en":"It is not born, nor does it ever die; after having been, it again does not cease to be; unborn, eternal, changeless, and ancient, it is not killed when the body is killed.","es":"Never is this One born, nor does It ever die; nor, having come into existence, does It cease to be. This One is birthless, eternal, undecaying, and ancient; It is not killed when the body is killed.","er":"It is never born; it never dies; having come into existence once, it never ceases to exist. Unborn, eternal, perpetual, and primordial, it is not destroyed when the body is destroyed."},{"ref":"2.21","ch":2,"v":21,"sa":"वेदाविनाशिनं नित्यं य एनमजमव्ययम्।\nकथं स पुरुषः पार्थ कं घातयति हन्ति कम्।।2.21।।","tr":"vedāvināśhinaṁ nityaṁ ya enam ajam avyayam\nkathaṁ sa puruṣhaḥ pārtha kaṁ ghātayati hanti kam","en":"Whoever knows it to be indestructible, eternal, unborn, and inexhaustible, how can that person slay, O Arjuna, or cause to be slain?","es":"O Partha, he who knows this One as indestructible, eternal, birthless, and undecaying—how can that person kill, or cause to be killed, whom?","er":"He who knows this self to be indestructible, unborn, unchanging, and thus eternal—how, O Arjuna, does he cause anyone to be killed, and whom does he kill?","gu":"જે જાણે છે કે આત્મા અવિનાશી, નિત્ય, અજન્મ અને અક્ષય છે, હે અર્જુન, તે વ્યક્તિ કોને મારે અને કોને મારવા કહે?"},{"ref":"2.22","ch":2,"v":22,"sa":"वासांसि जीर्णानि यथा विहाय\nनवानि गृह्णाति नरोऽपराणि।\nतथा शरीराणि विहाय जीर्णा\nन्यन्यानि संयाति नवानि देही।।2.22।।","tr":"vāsānsi jīrṇāni yathā vihāya\nnavāni gṛihṇāti naro ’parāṇi\ntathā śharīrāṇi vihāya jīrṇānya\nnyāni sanyāti navāni dehī","en":"Just as a man casts off worn-out clothes and puts on new ones, so too the embodied Self casts off worn-out bodies and enters others that are new.","es":"As after rejecting worn-out clothes, a man takes up other new ones, likewise, after rejecting worn-out bodies, the embodied one unites with other new ones.","er":"As a man casts off worn-out garments and puts on new ones, so does the embodied self cast off its worn-out bodies and enter into new ones."},{"ref":"2.23","ch":2,"v":23,"sa":"नैनं छिन्दन्ति शस्त्राणि नैनं दहति पावकः।\nन चैनं क्लेदयन्त्यापो न शोषयति मारुतः।।2.23।।","tr":"nainaṁ chhindanti śhastrāṇi nainaṁ dahati pāvakaḥ\nna chainaṁ kledayantyāpo na śhoṣhayati mārutaḥ","en":"Weapons cannot cut it, fire cannot burn it, water cannot wet it, wind cannot dry it.","es":"Weapons cannot cut It, fire cannot burn It, water cannot moisten It, and air cannot dry It.","er":"Weapons cannot cleave It, fire cannot burn It, waters cannot wet It, and wind cannot dry It."},{"ref":"2.24","ch":2,"v":24,"sa":"अच्छेद्योऽयमदाह्योऽयमक्लेद्योऽशोष्य एव च।\nनित्यः सर्वगतः स्थाणुरचलोऽयं सनातनः।।2.24।।","tr":"achchhedyo ’yam adāhyo ’yam akledyo ’śhoṣhya eva cha\nnityaḥ sarva-gataḥ sthāṇur achalo ’yaṁ sanātanaḥ","en":"This Self cannot be cut, burned, wetted, nor dried up; it is eternal, all-pervasive, stable, immovable, and ancient.","es":"It cannot be cut, burned, moistened, or dried up; it is eternal, omnipresent, stationary, unmoving, and unchanging.","er":"It cannot be cleaved; It cannot be burned; It cannot be wetted, and It cannot be dried; It is eternal, all-pervasive, stable, immovable, and primordial.","gu":"આત્માને ન શસ્ત્ર કાપી શકે, ન અગ્નિ બાળી શકે, ન જળ ભીંજવી શકે, ન વાયુ સૂકવી શકે. તે નિત્ય, સર્વ-વ્યાપ્ત, સ્થિર, અચળ અને સનાતન છે."},{"ref":"2.25","ch":2,"v":25,"sa":"अव्यक्तोऽयमचिन्त्योऽयमविकार्योऽयमुच्यते।\nतस्मादेवं विदित्वैनं नानुशोचितुमर्हसि।।2.25।।","tr":"avyakto ’yam achintyo ’yam avikāryo ’yam uchyate\ntasmādevaṁ viditvainaṁ nānuśhochitum arhasi","en":"This Self is said to be unmanifested, unthinkable, and unchangeable. Therefore, knowing this to be so, you should not grieve.","es":"It is said that This is unmanifest; This is inconceivable; This is unchangeable. Therefore, having known This thus, you ought not to grieve.","er":"This (self) is said to be unmanifest, inconceivable, and unchanging. Therefore, knowing it thus, it does not befit you to grieve.","gu":"આત્મા અવ્યક્ત, અચિંત્ય અને અવિકારી છે — આ સત્ય જાણ્યા પછી તારે શોક કરવો ઉચિત નથી."},{"ref":"2.26","ch":2,"v":26,"sa":"अथ चैनं नित्यजातं नित्यं वा मन्यसे मृतम्।\nतथापि त्वं महाबाहो नैवं शोचितुमर्हसि।।2.26।।","tr":"atha chainaṁ nitya-jātaṁ nityaṁ vā manyase mṛitam\ntathāpi tvaṁ mahā-bāho naivaṁ śhochitum arhasi","en":"But even if thou thinkest of It as constantly being born and constantly dying, even then, O mighty-armed one, thou shouldst not grieve.","es":"On the other hand, if you think this One is born continually or constantly dies, even then, O mighty-armed one, you should not grieve.","er":"Or, if you consider this self as constantly being born and constantly dying, O mighty-armed one, it still does not become you to feel grief.","gu":"જો તું માને છે કે આત્મા વારંવાર જન્મ લે છે અને મૃત્યુ પામે છે, તો પણ, હે મહાબાહો, આ માટે શોક ન કર."},{"ref":"2.27","ch":2,"v":27,"sa":"जातस्य हि ध्रुवो मृत्युर्ध्रुवं जन्म मृतस्य च।\nतस्मादपरिहार्येऽर्थे न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि।।2.27।।","tr":"jātasya hi dhruvo mṛityur dhruvaṁ janma mṛitasya cha\ntasmād aparihārye ’rthe na tvaṁ śhochitum arhasi","en":"For the born, death is certain, and for the dead, birth is certain; therefore, you should not grieve over the inevitable.","es":"For the death of anyone born is certain, and the rebirth of the dead is certain. Therefore, you should not grieve over an inevitable fact.","er":"For, death is certain for the born, and rebirth is certain for the dead; therefore, you should not grieve for what is inevitable."},{"ref":"2.28","ch":2,"v":28,"sa":"अव्यक्तादीनि भूतानि व्यक्तमध्यानि भारत।\nअव्यक्तनिधनान्येव तत्र का परिदेवना।।2.28।।","tr":"avyaktādīni bhūtāni vyakta-madhyāni bhārata\navyakta-nidhanānyeva tatra kā paridevanā","en":"Beings are unmanifest in their beginning, manifest in their middle state, O Arjuna, and unmanifest again in their end. What is there to grieve about?","es":"O descendant of Bharata, all beings remain unmanifested in the beginning; they become manifested in the middle. After death, they certainly become unmanifested. What lamentation can there be for them?","er":"O Arjuna, beings have an unknown beginning, a known middle, and an unknown end. What is there to grieve about in all this?","gu":"પ્રાણીઓ જન્મ પહેલાં અવ્યક્ત, જીવન દરમ્યાન વ્યક્ત, અને મૃત્યુ પછી ફરી અવ્યક્ત બને છે. આ ક્રમ જ્યારે સ્વાભાવિક છે, ત્યારે શોક શા માટે?"},{"ref":"2.29","ch":2,"v":29,"sa":"आश्चर्यवत्पश्यति कश्चिदेन\nमाश्चर्यवद्वदति तथैव चान्यः।\nआश्चर्यवच्चैनमन्यः श्रृणोति\nश्रुत्वाप्येनं वेद न चैव कश्चित्।।2.29।।","tr":"āśhcharya-vat paśhyati kaśhchid enan\nāśhcharya-vad vadati tathaiva chānyaḥ\nāśhcharya-vach chainam anyaḥ śhṛiṇoti\nśhrutvāpyenaṁ veda na chaiva kaśhchit","en":"One sees this (the Self) as a wonder; another speaks of it as a wonder; another hears of it as a wonder; yet, having heard, none understands it at all.","es":"Someone visualizes it as a wonder; someone else talks of it as a wonder; someone else hears of it as a wonder; and yet someone else does not even realize it after hearing about it.","er":"One regards This (self) as a wonder; another speaks of It as a wonder; yet another hears of It as a wonder; and even after hearing of It, one does not know It.","gu":"કોઈ આ આત્માને અદ્ભૂત સ્વરૂપે જુએ છે, કોઈ તેનું વર્ણન અજ્ઞાાત તરીકે કરે છે, કોઈ સાંભળે છે — છતાં સાંભળ્યા પછી પણ ઘણા તેને સાચા અર્થમાં સમજી શક્તા નથી."},{"ref":"2.30","ch":2,"v":30,"sa":"देही नित्यमवध्योऽयं देहे सर्वस्य भारत।\nतस्मात्सर्वाणि भूतानि न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि।।2.30।।","tr":"dehī nityam avadhyo ’yaṁ dehe sarvasya bhārata\ntasmāt sarvāṇi bhūtāni na tvaṁ śhochitum arhasi","en":"This indweller in the body of everyone is ever indestructible, O Arjuna; therefore, you should not grieve for any creature.","es":"O descendant of Bharata, this embodied Self existing in everyone's body can never be killed; therefore, you ought not to grieve for all these beings.","er":"The self in the body, O Arjuna, is eternal and indestructible. This is the case for all selves in all bodies. Therefore, it is not fitting for you to feel grief for any being.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, દરેક જીવના દેહમાં વસતો આ આત્મા સર્વદા અવિનાશી છે. તેથી, કોઈ પ્રાણી માટે તારે શોક ન કરવો જોઈએ."},{"ref":"2.31","ch":2,"v":31,"sa":"स्वधर्ममपि चावेक्ष्य न विकम्पितुमर्हसि।\nधर्म्याद्धि युद्धाछ्रेयोऽन्यत्क्षत्रियस्य न विद्यते।।2.31।।","tr":"swa-dharmam api chāvekṣhya na vikampitum arhasi\ndharmyāddhi yuddhāch chhreyo ’nyat kṣhatriyasya na vidyate","en":"Further, having regard to your duty, you should not waver, for there is nothing higher for a Kshatriya than a righteous war.","es":"Even considering your own duty, you should not waver, since there is nothing better for a Ksatriya than a righteous battle.","er":"Further, considering also your own duty, it does not befit you to waver. For, to a Kshatriya, there is no greater good than a righteous war.","gu":"ધર્મ-યુદ્ધ ક્ષત્રિય માટે સૌથી ઉત્તમ કર્મ છે — તારા સ્વ-ધર્મ પ્રત્યે વિચલિત ન થા. આ ધર્મ-સ્થાપના માટેના યુદ્ધ કરતાં કોઈ ઉચ્ચ કર્તવ્ય નથી."},{"ref":"2.32","ch":2,"v":32,"sa":"यदृच्छया चोपपन्नं स्वर्गद्वारमपावृतम्।\nसुखिनः क्षत्रियाः पार्थ लभन्ते युद्धमीदृशम्।।2.32।।","tr":"yadṛichchhayā chopapannaṁ swarga-dvāram apāvṛitam\nsukhinaḥ kṣhatriyāḥ pārtha labhante yuddham īdṛiśham","en":"Happy are the Kshatriyas, O Arjuna! who are called to fight in such a battle that comes of its own accord as an open door to heaven.","es":"O son of Partha, happy are the Kshatriyas who come across such a battle, which presents itself unsought and is an open gate to heaven.","er":"Happy are the Ksatriyas, O Arjuna, to whom such a war comes of its own accord; it opens the gates to heaven.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, આવા યુદ્ધનો અવસર સ્વર્ગના ખુલ્લા દ્વાર સમાન છે — આવી લડાઈ માટે બોલાવાયેલા ક્ષત્રિયો ખરેખર ધન્ય છે."},{"ref":"2.33","ch":2,"v":33,"sa":"अथ चैत्त्वमिमं धर्म्यं संग्रामं न करिष्यसि।\nततः स्वधर्मं कीर्तिं च हित्वा पापमवाप्स्यसि।।2.33।।","tr":"atha chet tvam imaṁ dharmyaṁ saṅgrāmaṁ na kariṣhyasi\ntataḥ sva-dharmaṁ kīrtiṁ cha hitvā pāpam avāpsyasi","en":"But if you will not fight this righteous war, then having abandoned your own duty and reputation, you will incur sin.","es":"On the other hand, if you do not fight this righteous battle, then you will incur sin, forsaking your own duty and fame.","er":"But if you do not fight this righteous war, you will be turning away from your duty and honor, and will incur sin.","gu":"પરંતુ જો તું આ ધર્મયુદ્ધ નહીં લડે, તો સ્વધર્મ અને કીર્તિ ગુમાવી પાપ વહોરીશ."},{"ref":"2.34","ch":2,"v":34,"sa":"अकीर्तिं चापि भूतानि कथयिष्यन्ति तेऽव्ययाम्।\nसंभावितस्य चाकीर्तिर्मरणादतिरिच्यते।।2.34।।","tr":"akīrtiṁ chāpi bhūtāni\nkathayiṣhyanti te ’vyayām\nsambhāvitasya chākīrtir\nmaraṇād atirichyate","en":"People will also recount your everlasting dishonor; and for one who has been honored, dishonor is worse than death.","es":"People also will speak of your unending infamy, and to an honored person, infamy is worse than death.","er":"Further, people will speak ill of you for all time, and for one accustomed to being honored, dishonor is worse than death.","gu":"લોકો તારી ચિરંજીવ અપકીર્તિ ગાશે, અને જેને સન્માન મળ્યું હોય તેના માટે અપમાન મૃત્યુ કરતાં વધુ દુઃખદ છે."},{"ref":"2.35","ch":2,"v":35,"sa":"भयाद्रणादुपरतं मंस्यन्ते त्वां महारथाः।\nयेषां च त्वं बहुमतो भूत्वा यास्यसि लाघवम्।।2.35।।","tr":"bhayād raṇād uparataṁ mansyante tvāṁ mahā-rathāḥ\nyeṣhāṁ cha tvaṁ bahu-mato bhūtvā yāsyasi lāghavam","en":"The great chariot-warriors will think that you have withdrawn from the battle out of fear, and you will be held in low esteem by those who have held you in high regard.","es":"The great chariot-riders will think of you as having desisted from the fight out of fear, and you will fall into disgrace before them whom you had been estimable to.","er":"The great warriors will think that you have fled from battle out of fear. Those who held you in high esteem will now speak of you disparagingly.","gu":"મહારથીઓ ધારશે કે તેં ભયને કારણે રણ છોડ્યું, અને જેઓ તને ઊંચો ગણતા હતા તેઓ તને નીચો ગણશે."},{"ref":"2.36","ch":2,"v":36,"sa":"अवाच्यवादांश्च बहून् वदिष्यन्ति तवाहिताः।\nनिन्दन्तस्तव सामर्थ्यं ततो दुःखतरं नु किम्।।2.36।।","tr":"avāchya-vādānśh cha bahūn vadiṣhyanti tavāhitāḥ\nnindantastava sāmarthyaṁ tato duḥkhataraṁ nu kim","en":"Your enemies, scoffing at your power, will speak many abusive words—what could be more painful than this?","es":"And your enemies will speak many indecent words while denigrating your power. What can be more painful than that?","er":"Your enemies, slandering your prowess, will use words that should never be uttered. What could be more painful than that?","gu":"શત્રુઓ તારી શક્તિ પર ઠઠ્ઠો કરી ઘણા અપશબ્દો બોલશે — આથી વધુ પીડાદાયક બીજું શું હોઈ શકે?"},{"ref":"2.37","ch":2,"v":37,"sa":"हतो वा प्राप्स्यसि स्वर्गं जित्वा वा भोक्ष्यसे महीम्।\nतस्मादुत्तिष्ठ कौन्तेय युद्धाय कृतनिश्चयः।।2.37।।","tr":"hato vā prāpsyasi swargaṁ jitvā vā bhokṣhyase mahīm\ntasmād uttiṣhṭha kaunteya yuddhāya kṛita-niśhchayaḥ","en":"Slain, you will obtain heaven; victorious, you will enjoy the earth; therefore, stand up, O son of Kunti, resolved to fight.","es":"Either by being killed, you will attain heaven, or by winning, you will enjoy the earth. Therefore, O Arjuna, rise up with determination to fight.","er":"If slain, you will win heaven; or if victorious, you will enjoy the earth. Therefore, arise, O Arjuna, resolved to fight.","gu":"વીરગતિ પામ્યે સ્વર્ગ મળશે, વિજયી થઈશ તો પૃથ્વી ભોગવીશ — તેથી, હે કુંતીપુત્ર, ઊઠ અને યુદ્ધ કરવા દૃઢ થઈ જા."},{"ref":"2.38","ch":2,"v":38,"sa":"सुखदुःखे समे कृत्वा लाभालाभौ जयाजयौ।\nततो युद्धाय युज्यस्व नैवं पापमवाप्स्यसि।।2.38।।","tr":"sukha-duḥkhe same kṛitvā lābhālābhau jayājayau\ntato yuddhāya yujyasva naivaṁ pāpam avāpsyasi","en":"Having made pleasure and pain, gain and loss, victory and defeat equal, engage in battle for the sake of battle; thus, you shall not incur sin.","es":"Treating happiness and sorrow, gain and loss, and conquest and defeat with equanimity, then engage in battle. Thus, you will not incur sin.","er":"Holding pleasure and pain, gain and loss, victory and defeat as equal, gird yourself up for the battle. Thus, you shall not incur any sin."},{"ref":"2.39","ch":2,"v":39,"sa":"एषा तेऽभिहिता सांख्ये बुद्धिर्योगे त्विमां श्रृणु।\nबुद्ध्यायुक्तो यया पार्थ कर्मबन्धं प्रहास्यसि।।2.39।।","tr":"eṣhā te ’bhihitā sānkhye\nbuddhir yoge tvimāṁ śhṛiṇu\nbuddhyā yukto yayā pārtha\nkarma-bandhaṁ prahāsyasi","en":"This, which has been taught to you, is wisdom concerning Sankhya. Now listen to wisdom concerning Yoga, endowed with which, O Arjuna, you shall cast off the bonds of action.","es":"O Partha, this wisdom has been imparted to you from the standpoint of Self-realization. But listen to this wisdom from the standpoint of Yoga, endowed with which, you will get rid of the bondage of action.","er":"This Buddhi concerning the Self (Sankhya) has been imparted to you. Now listen to this with regard to Yoga, by following which you will get rid of the bondage of Karma.","gu":"સાંખ્યયોગ અનુસાર જ્ઞાન સાંભળ્યું; હવે કર્મયોગ સાંભળ — જે ધારણ કરી તું કર્મના બંધનો તોડી શકીશ."},{"ref":"2.40","ch":2,"v":40,"sa":"नेहाभिक्रमनाशोऽस्ति प्रत्यवायो न विद्यते।\nस्वल्पमप्यस्य धर्मस्य त्रायते महतो भयात्।।2.40।।","tr":"nehābhikrama-nāśho ’sti pratyavāyo na vidyate\nsvalpam apyasya dharmasya trāyate mahato bhayāt","en":"In this, there is no loss of effort, nor is there any harm produced, nor any transgression. Even a little of this knowledge protects one from great fear.","es":"Here, there is no waste of effort; nor is there any harm. Even a little of this righteousness saves one from great fear.","er":"Here, there is no loss of effort, nor any accrual of evil. Even a little of this Dharma (called Karma Yoga) protects one from the great fear."},{"ref":"2.41","ch":2,"v":41,"sa":"व्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिरेकेह कुरुनन्दन।\nबहुशाखा ह्यनन्ताश्च बुद्धयोऽव्यवसायिनाम्।।2.41।।","tr":"vyavasāyātmikā buddhir ekeha kuru-nandana\nbahu-śhākhā hyanantāśh cha buddhayo ’vyavasāyinām","en":"Here, O joy of the Kurus, there is only one single-pointed determination; many-branched and endless are the thoughts of the indecisive.","es":"O scion of the Kuru dynasty, in this there is a single, one-pointed conviction. The thoughts of the irresolute ones, however, have many branches indeed and are innumerable.","er":"In this (Karma Yoga), O Arjuna, the resolute mind is single-pointed; the minds of the irresolute are multi-branched and endless.","gu":"આ યોગમાં નિશ્ચય એક જ હોય છે, પરંતુ, હે કુરુનંદન, અનિર્ણાયક ચિત્તના વિચારો અનેક શાખાઓમાં ભટક્યા કરે છે."},{"ref":"2.42","ch":2,"v":42,"sa":"यामिमां पुष्पितां वाचं प्रवदन्त्यविपश्चितः।\nवेदवादरताः पार्थ नान्यदस्तीति वादिनः।।2.42।।","tr":"yāmimāṁ puṣhpitāṁ vāchaṁ pravadanty-avipaśhchitaḥ\nveda-vāda-ratāḥ pārtha nānyad astīti vādinaḥ\n kāmātmānaḥ swarga-parā janma-karma-phala-pradām\nkriyā-viśheṣha-bahulāṁ bhogaiśhwarya-gatiṁ prati","en":"The unwise, taking pleasure in the eulogizing words of the Vedas, utter flowery speech, saying, \"There is nothing else,\" O Arjuna.","es":"O son of Prtha, those undiscerning people who utter this flowery talk, which promises birth as a result of rites and duties, and is full of various special rites meant for the attainment of enjoyment and affluence, remain engrossed in the utterances of the Vedas and declare that nothing else exists; their minds are full of desires and they have heaven as their goal.","er":"- O Partha, the unwise, who rejoice in the letter of the Vedas, say, \"There is nothing else.\" They are full only of worldly desires and they hanker for heaven. They speak flowery words that offer mirth as the fruit of work. They look upon the Vedas as consisting entirely of varied rites for the attainment of pleasure and power. Those who cling so to pleasure and power are attracted by that speech (offering heavenly rewards) and are unable to develop the resolute will of a concentrated mind.","gu":"વેદવાણીના ફૂલ-ફ્ળ પ્રત્યે આસક્ત અવિવેકી લોકો 'આ જ સર્વ છે' કહી ભોગ-ઐશ્વર્ય માટે જટિલ ક્રિયા-કાંડ પ્રચારે છે."},{"ref":"2.43","ch":2,"v":43,"sa":"कामात्मानः स्वर्गपरा जन्मकर्मफलप्रदाम्।\nक्रियाविशेषबहुलां भोगैश्वर्यगतिं प्रति।।2.43।।","tr":"kāmātmānaḥ svarga-parā \n janma-karma-phala-pradām\n kriyā-viśeṣa-bahulāṁ\n bhogaiśvarya-gatiṁ prati","en":"Full of desires, with heaven as their goal, (they speak words that are directed to ends) leading to new births as the result of their works, and prescribe various methods abounding in specific actions, for the attainment of pleasure and power.","es":"O son of Prtha, those undiscerning people who utter this flowery talk, which promises birth as a result of rites and duties, and is full of various special rites meant for the attainment of enjoyment and affluence, remain engrossed in the utterances of the Vedas and declare that nothing else exists; their minds are full of desires and they have heaven as their goal.","er":"- O Partha, the unwise, who rejoice in the letter of the Vedas, say, \"There is nothing else.\" They are full only of worldly desires and they yearn for heaven. They speak flowery words that offer mirth as the fruit of work. They view the Vedas as consisting entirely of varied rites for the attainment of pleasure and power. Those who cling so to pleasure and power are attracted by that speech (offering heavenly rewards) and are unable to develop the resolute will of a focused mind.","gu":"ભોગ-ઐશ્વર્યની ઇચ્છાઓથી ભરેલા, સ્વર્ગ-પ્રાપ્તિને ધ્યેય માનનારા, કર્મ-ફળ રૂપે પુનર્જન્મ ગણી ભોગ-ઐશ્વર્ય માટે વિવિધ ક્રિયા-કાંડ વર્ણવે છે."},{"ref":"2.44","ch":2,"v":44,"sa":"भोगैश्वर्यप्रसक्तानां तयापहृतचेतसाम्।\nव्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिः समाधौ न विधीयते।।2.44।।","tr":"bhogaiśwvarya-prasaktānāṁ tayāpahṛita-chetasām\nvyavasāyātmikā buddhiḥ samādhau na vidhīyate","en":"For those who are attached to pleasure and power, whose minds are drawn away by such teachings, their determinate reason is not formed which is steadily bent on meditation and Samadhi (superconscious state).","es":"One-pointed conviction does not become established in the minds of those who delight in enjoyment and affluence, and whose intellects are carried away by it.","er":"- O Partha, the unwise, who rejoice in the letter of the Vedas, say, \"There is nothing else.\" They are full only of worldly desires and they hanker for heaven. They speak flowery words that offer mirth as the fruit of work. They look upon the Vedas as consisting entirely of varied rites for the attainment of pleasure and power. Those who cling so to pleasure and power are attracted by that speech (offering heavenly rewards) and are unable to develop the resolute will of a concentrated mind.","gu":"ભોગ-ઐશ્વર્યમાં આસક્ત, આવા ઉપદેશોથી ભ્રષ્ટ ચિત્ત ધરાવતા માણસોમાં સમાધિ અને ધ્યાન-સ્થિર વ્યવસાય-બુદ્ધિ ઉત્પન્ન થતી નથી."},{"ref":"2.45","ch":2,"v":45,"sa":"त्रैगुण्यविषया वेदा निस्त्रैगुण्यो भवार्जुन।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो नित्यसत्त्वस्थो निर्योगक्षेम आत्मवान्।।2.45।।","tr":"trai-guṇya-viṣhayā vedā nistrai-guṇyo bhavārjuna\nnirdvandvo nitya-sattva-stho niryoga-kṣhema ātmavān","en":"The Vedas deal with the three attributes; be thou above these three attributes. O Arjuna, free yourself from the pairs of opposites and ever remain in the quality of Sattva, freed from acquisition and preservation, and be established in the Self.","es":"O Arjuna, the Vedas [Meaning only the portion dealing with rites and duties (karma-kanda).] have the three qualities as their object. You become free from worldliness, free from the pairs of duality, ever-poised in the quality of sattva, without (desire for) acquisition and protection, and self-collected.","er":"The Vedas have the three Gunas as their sphere, O Arjuna. You must be free from the three Gunas and be free from the pairs of opposites. Abide in pure Sattva; never care to acquire things and to protect what has been acquired, but be established in the Self.","gu":"વેદ ત્રણ ગુણ — સ, ર અને ત — ના ક્ષેત્રમાં વ્યવહારે છે; હે અર્જુન, ત્રણ ગુણોથી ઉપર ઊઠ, દ્વન્દ્વ-મુક્ત, શુદ્ધ-ચિત્ત, ભ-સ્થિત થા."},{"ref":"2.46","ch":2,"v":46,"sa":"यावानर्थ उदपाने सर्वतः संप्लुतोदके।\nतावान्सर्वेषु वेदेषु ब्राह्मणस्य विजानतः।।2.46।।","tr":"yāvān artha udapāne sarvataḥ samplutodake\ntāvānsarveṣhu vedeṣhu brāhmaṇasya vijānataḥ","en":"To the Brahmana who has known the Self, all the Vedas are of as much use as a reservoir of water would be in a place where there is a flood.","es":"A Brahmana with realization has that much utility in all the Vedas as a person has in a well when there is a flood all around.","er":"What use does a thirsty person have for a water reservoir when all sides of it are flooded—that is the only use of all the Vedas for a Brahmana who knows.","gu":"જ્યારે ચોમેર પૂર હોય ત્યારે એક નાના હોજનો જેટલો ઉપયોગ, તેટલો જ બ્રહ્મ-સ્વરૂપ બ્રાહ્મણ માટે સઘળા વેદોનો ઉપયોગ."},{"ref":"2.47","ch":2,"v":47,"sa":"कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन।\nमा कर्मफलहेतुर्भूर्मा ते सङ्गोऽस्त्वकर्मणि।।2.47।।","tr":"karmaṇy-evādhikāras te mā phaleṣhu kadāchana\nmā karma-phala-hetur bhūr mā te saṅgo ’stvakarmaṇi","en":"Your right is only to work, but not to its results; do not let the results of action be your motive, nor let your attachment be to inaction.","es":"Your right is only to act, not to the results. Do not be the cause of the results of action. Do not have any inclination towards inaction.","er":"You have the right to work alone, but not to the fruits of it. Do not be driven by the results of your work, nor have attachment to inaction."},{"ref":"2.48","ch":2,"v":48,"sa":"योगस्थः कुरु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा धनञ्जय।\nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योः समो भूत्वा समत्वं योग उच्यते।।2.48।।","tr":"yoga-sthaḥ kuru karmāṇi saṅgaṁ tyaktvā dhanañjaya\nsiddhy-asiddhyoḥ samo bhūtvā samatvaṁ yoga uchyate","en":"Perform action, O Arjuna, being steadfast in Yoga, abandoning attachment and balanced in success and failure; evenness of mind is called Yoga.","es":"By being established in Yoga, O Dhananjaya (Arjuna), undertake actions, casting off attachment and remaining equanimous in success and failure. Equanimity is called Yoga.","er":"Abandoning attachment and established in Yoga, perform works, viewing success and failure with an even mind. Evenness of mind is said to be Yoga."},{"ref":"2.49","ch":2,"v":49,"sa":"दूरेण ह्यवरं कर्म बुद्धियोगाद्धनञ्जय।\nबुद्धौ शरणमन्विच्छ कृपणाः फलहेतवः।।2.49।।","tr":"dūreṇa hy-avaraṁ karma buddhi-yogād dhanañjaya\nbuddhau śharaṇam anvichchha kṛipaṇāḥ phala-hetavaḥ","en":"Far lower than the Yoga of wisdom is action, O Arjuna. Seek thou refuge in wisdom; wretched are those whose motive is the fruit.","es":"O Dhananjaya, indeed, action is inferior to the yoga of wisdom. Take refuge in wisdom. Those who thirst for rewards are pitiable.","er":"Action done with attachment, O Arjuna, is far inferior to action done with evenness of mind. Seek refuge in evenness of mind; those who act with a motive for results are miserable.","gu":"ક-ફળ ત્યાગ-રૂપ ય — બુદ્ધિ-ય — ઈચ્છા-સહિત કર્મ કરતાં ઘણો ઊંચો છે; હે અર્જુન, ય-બુદ્ધિ આશ્રય લે — ફળ-ઇચ્છાથી ચાલનારા કૃપાપાત્ર છે."},{"ref":"2.50","ch":2,"v":50,"sa":"बुद्धियुक्तो जहातीह उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते।\nतस्माद्योगाय युज्यस्व योगः कर्मसु कौशलम्।।2.50।।","tr":"buddhi-yukto jahātīha ubhe sukṛita-duṣhkṛite\ntasmād yogāya yujyasva yogaḥ karmasu kauśhalam","en":"Endowed with wisdom and evenness of mind, one casts off in this life both good and evil deeds; therefore, devote yourself to Yoga; Yoga is skill in action.","es":"Possessed of wisdom, one rejects here both virtue and vice. Therefore, devote yourself to (Karma-) yoga; for yoga is skilfulness in action.","er":"A person with an evenness of mind discards both good and evil here and now. Therefore, strive for Yoga; for Yoga is skill in action."},{"ref":"2.51","ch":2,"v":51,"sa":"कर्मजं बुद्धियुक्ता हि फलं त्यक्त्वा मनीषिणः।\nजन्मबन्धविनिर्मुक्ताः पदं गच्छन्त्यनामयम्।।2.51।।","tr":"karma-jaṁ buddhi-yuktā hi phalaṁ tyaktvā manīṣhiṇaḥ\njanma-bandha-vinirmuktāḥ padaṁ gachchhanty-anāmayam","en":"The wise, possessing knowledge, having abandoned the fruits of their actions, and being freed from the bonds of birth, go to the place which is beyond all evil.","es":"For those devoted to wisdom, they become enlightened men by giving up the fruits of their actions, and thus they reach a state beyond evil, having been freed from the bondage of birth.","er":"The wise, who possess evenness of mind, relinquish the fruits born of action, and are freed from the bondage of birth, going to the region beyond all ills.","gu":"જ્ઞાની ભક્તો, ફળ-ઇચ્છા ત્યજી, ક-ના બંધનોથી મુક્ત થઈ, જ્યાં સઘળા દોષ ઓગળી જાય છે ત્યાં — જન્મ-મૃત્યુથી પર — ગતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"2.52","ch":2,"v":52,"sa":"यदा ते मोहकलिलं बुद्धिर्व्यतितरिष्यति।\nतदा गन्तासि निर्वेदं श्रोतव्यस्य श्रुतस्य च।।2.52।।","tr":"yadā te moha-kalilaṁ buddhir vyatitariṣhyati\ntadā gantāsi nirvedaṁ śhrotavyasya śhrutasya cha","en":"When your intellect passes beyond the mire of delusion, then you will attain indifference to what has been heard and what has yet to be heard.","es":"When your mind goes beyond the turbidity of delusion, then you will acquire dispassion for what has to be heard and what has already been heard.","er":"When your intellect has passed beyond the tangle of delusion, you will yourself feel disgusted with what you have heard and what you will hear.","gu":"જ્યારે તારી બુદ્ધિ મોહની કીચડમાંથી પાર થઈ જશે, ત્યારે તું સાંભળેલું અને સાંભળવાનું છે તે બધાથી નિઃસ્પૃહ થઈ જઈશ."},{"ref":"2.53","ch":2,"v":53,"sa":"श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्ना ते यदा स्थास्यति निश्चला।\nसमाधावचला बुद्धिस्तदा योगमवाप्स्यसि।।2.53।।","tr":"śhruti-vipratipannā te yadā sthāsyati niśhchalā\nsamādhāv-achalā buddhis tadā yogam avāpsyasi","en":"When your intellect, which is perplexed by the Vedic texts you have read, stands immovable and steady in the Self, then you will attain Self-realization.","es":"When your mind, which has become bewildered by hearing, becomes unshakable and steadfast in the Self, then you will attain Yoga that arises from discrimination.","er":"When your intellect, having been well enlightened by hearing from Me and firmly placed, stands unshaken in a concentrated mind, then you will attain the vision of the Self.","gu":"જ્યારે વેદવાક્યોથી વ્યાકુળ બનેલી તારી બુદ્ધિ આત્મામાં અડગ અને સ્થિર ઊભી રહેશે, ત્યારે તને આત્મસાક્ષાત્કાર પ્રાપ્ત થશે."},{"ref":"2.54","ch":2,"v":54,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nस्थितप्रज्ञस्य का भाषा समाधिस्थस्य केशव।\nस्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत किमासीत व्रजेत किम्।।2.54।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nsthita-prajñasya kā bhāṣhā samādhi-sthasya keśhava\nsthita-dhīḥ kiṁ prabhāṣheta kim āsīta vrajeta kim","en":"Arjuna said, \"O Krishna, what is the description of one who has steady wisdom and is merged in the superconscious state? How does one of steady wisdom speak, how do they sit, and how do they walk?\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Kesava, what is the description of a man of steady wisdom who is self-absorbed? How does he speak, sit, and move about?\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"What is the mode of speech of one who is of firm wisdom, established in the control of the mind? What does a man of firm wisdom speak, O Krsna? How does he sit? How does he move?\"","gu":"અર્જુને પૂછ્યું: હે કૃષ્ણ, સ્થિતપ્રજ્ઞ — એટલે કે સમાધિમાં નિમગ્ન સ્થિર બુદ્ધિવાળા — મનુષ્યનાં શાં લક્ષણ છે? આવો પુરુષ કેવી રીતે બોલે, બેસે અને ચાલે?"},{"ref":"2.55","ch":2,"v":55,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nप्रजहाति यदा कामान् सर्वान् पार्थ मनोगतान्।\nआत्मन्येवात्मना तुष्टः स्थितप्रज्ञस्तदोच्यते।।2.55।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nprajahāti yadā kāmān sarvān pārtha mano-gatān\nātmany-evātmanā tuṣhṭaḥ sthita-prajñas tadochyate","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"When a man completely casts off, O Arjuna, all the desires of the mind and is satisfied in the Self by the Self, then he is said to be one of steady wisdom.\"","es":"The Blessed One said, \"O Partha, when one fully renounces all the desires that have entered the mind and remains satisfied in the Self alone, then he is called a man of steady wisdom.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"When a man renounces all the desires of the mind and is content with himself, then he is said to possess firm wisdom.\""},{"ref":"2.56","ch":2,"v":56,"sa":"दुःखेष्वनुद्विग्नमनाः सुखेषु विगतस्पृहः।\nवीतरागभयक्रोधः स्थितधीर्मुनिरुच्यते।।2.56।।","tr":"duḥkheṣhv-anudvigna-manāḥ sukheṣhu vigata-spṛihaḥ\nvīta-rāga-bhaya-krodhaḥ sthita-dhīr munir uchyate","en":"He whose mind is not shaken by adversity, who does not long for pleasures, and is free from attachment, fear, and anger, is called a sage of steady wisdom.","es":"That monk is called a man of steady wisdom when his mind is unperturbed even in sorrow, he is free from longing for delights, and has gone beyond attachment, fear, and anger.","er":"He whose mind is not perturbed by pain, who has no longing for pleasures, who is free from desire, fear, and anger—he is called a sage of firm wisdom."},{"ref":"2.57","ch":2,"v":57,"sa":"यः सर्वत्रानभिस्नेहस्तत्तत्प्राप्य शुभाशुभम्।\nनाभिनन्दति न द्वेष्टि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता।।2.57।।","tr":"yaḥ sarvatrānabhisnehas tat tat prāpya śhubhāśhubham\nnābhinandati na dveṣhṭi tasya prajñā pratiṣhṭhitā","en":"He who is everywhere without attachment, upon encountering anything good or bad, neither rejoices nor hastens; his wisdom is firm.","es":"The wisdom of that person remains established who has no attachment to anything anywhere, who neither welcomes nor rejects anything, whatever good or bad, when they come across it.","er":"He who has no love on any side, who, upon finding good or evil, neither rejoices nor hates—his wisdom is firmly set.","gu":"જે સર્વત્ર આસક્તિ વગર રહે છે, શુભ મળે તો હર્ષ ન પામે અને અશુભ મળે તો ક્ષોભ ન પામે — એની પ્રજ્ઞા સ્થિર છે."},{"ref":"2.58","ch":2,"v":58,"sa":"यदा संहरते चायं कूर्मोऽङ्गानीव सर्वशः।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता।।2.58।।","tr":"yadā sanharate chāyaṁ kūrmo ’ṅgānīva sarvaśhaḥ\nindriyāṇīndriyārthebhyas tasya prajñā pratiṣhṭhitā","en":"When, like the tortoise which withdraws all its limbs on all sides, he withdraws his senses from the sense-objects, then his wisdom becomes steady.","es":"And when one fully withdraws their senses from the objects of the senses, just as a tortoise withdraws its limbs, then their wisdom remains established.","er":"When one is able to draw their senses away from the objects of sense on all sides, like a tortoise draws in its limbs, then their wisdom is firmly established.","gu":"જેમ કાચબો પોતાના અંગો સંકોચી લે છે, તેમ જ્યારે કોઈ ઇન્દ્રિયોને તેમના વિષયોથી ખેંચી લે છે, ત્યારે તેની પ્રજ્ઞા સ્થિર થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"2.59","ch":2,"v":59,"sa":"विषया विनिवर्तन्ते निराहारस्य देहिनः।\nरसवर्जं रसोऽप्यस्य परं दृष्ट्वा निवर्तते।।2.59।।","tr":"viṣhayā vinivartante nirāhārasya dehinaḥ\nrasa-varjaṁ raso ’pyasya paraṁ dṛiṣhṭvā nivartate","en":"The objects of the senses turn away from the abstinent man, leaving the longing behind; but his longing also turns away upon seeing the Supreme.","es":"The objects recede from an abstinent person, except for the taste for them. Even this taste falls away after realization of the Absolute.","er":"The objects of the senses, except for the pleasure they bring, turn away from the abstinent dweller in the body. Even the pleasure turns away from him when the Self, which is supreme over the senses, is seen.","gu":"ઇન્દ્રિયોના વિષય નિવૃત્ત મનુષ્ય પાસેથી દૂર થઈ જાય છે, પણ તૃષ્ણા રહી જાય છે; પરમ તત્ત્વનાં દર્શન થતાં તે તૃષ્ણા પણ વિદાય લે છે."},{"ref":"2.60","ch":2,"v":60,"sa":"यततो ह्यपि कौन्तेय पुरुषस्य विपश्चितः।\nइन्द्रियाणि प्रमाथीनि हरन्ति प्रसभं मनः।।2.60।।","tr":"yatato hyapi kaunteya puruṣhasya vipaśhchitaḥ\nindriyāṇi pramāthīni haranti prasabhaṁ manaḥ","en":"The turbulent senses, O Arjuna, can violently carry away the mind of a wise person, even though they are striving to control them.","es":"For, O son of Kunti, the turbulent senses can violently snatch away the mind of an intelligent person, even while they are striving diligently.","er":"The turbulent senses, O Arjuna, can forcibly carry away the mind of even a wise man, though he is ever striving.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, ઇન્દ્રિયોને વશ કરવા પ્રયત્ન કરતા વિવેકી મનુષ્યના મનને પણ આ ચંચળ ઇન્દ્રિયો બળપૂર્વક ખેંચી જઈ શકે છે."},{"ref":"2.61","ch":2,"v":61,"sa":"तानि सर्वाणि संयम्य युक्त आसीत मत्परः।\nवशे हि यस्येन्द्रियाणि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता।।2.61।।","tr":"tāni sarvāṇi sanyamya yukta āsīta mat-paraḥ\nvaśhe hi yasyendriyāṇi tasya prajñā pratiṣhṭhitā","en":"Having restrained them all, he should sit steadfast, intent on Me; his wisdom is steady whose senses are under control.","es":"Controlling all of them, one should remain focused on Me as the supreme. For, the wisdom of one whose senses are under control becomes steadfast.","er":"Having controlled all the senses, let him remain in contemplation, regarding Me as supreme; for his knowledge is firmly established when his senses are under control.","gu":"સઘળી ઇન્દ્રિયોને સંયમમાં રાખીને, મને પરમ લક્ષ્ય ગણીને, યોગમાં સ્થિર થઈને બેસ; કારણ કે જેની ઇન્દ્રિયો વશ છે, તેની પ્રજ્ઞા સ્થિર છે."},{"ref":"2.62","ch":2,"v":62,"sa":"ध्यायतो विषयान्पुंसः सङ्गस्तेषूपजायते।\nसङ्गात् संजायते कामः कामात्क्रोधोऽभिजायते।।2.62।।","tr":"dhyāyato viṣhayān puṁsaḥ saṅgas teṣhūpajāyate\nsaṅgāt sañjāyate kāmaḥ kāmāt krodho ’bhijāyate","en":"When one thinks of objects, attachment to them arises; from attachment, desire is born; from desire, anger arises.","es":"- In the case of a person who dwells on objects, there arises attachment to them. From attachment grows hankering, and from hankering springs anger.","er":"To one who is thinking about sense-objects, attachment to them arises; from attachment arises desire, and from desire arises anger."},{"ref":"2.63","ch":2,"v":63,"sa":"क्रोधाद्भवति संमोहः संमोहात्स्मृतिविभ्रमः।\nस्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात्प्रणश्यति।।2.63।।","tr":"krodhād bhavati sammohaḥ sammohāt smṛiti-vibhramaḥ\nsmṛiti-bhranśhād buddhi-nāśho buddhi-nāśhāt praṇaśhyati","en":"Anger leads to delusion, which causes loss of memory; this, in turn, leads to the destruction of discrimination, resulting in destruction.","es":"From anger follows delusion; from delusion, a failure of memory; from the failure of memory, the loss of understanding; and from the loss of understanding, one perishes.","er":"Anger leads to delusion, which causes the loss of memory; the loss of memory leads to the destruction of discrimination, and with the destruction of discrimination, one is lost.","gu":"ક્રોધથી મોહ ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે, મોહથી સ્મૃતિ ભ્રષ્ટ થાય છે, સ્મૃતિ ભ્રષ્ટ થવાથી વિવેક નષ્ટ થઈ જાય છે, અને વિવેક નષ્ટ થતાં મનુષ્ય સર્વનાશ પામે છે."},{"ref":"2.64","ch":2,"v":64,"sa":"रागद्वेषवियुक्तैस्तु विषयानिन्द्रियैश्चरन्।\nआत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा प्रसादमधिगच्छति।।2.64।।","tr":"rāga-dveṣha-viyuktais tu viṣhayān indriyaiśh charan\nātma-vaśhyair-vidheyātmā prasādam adhigachchhati","en":"But the self-controlled man, moving among objects with the senses restrained and free from attraction and repulsion, attains peace.","es":"But by perceiving objects with the organs that are free from attraction and repulsion, and are under his own control, the self-controlled person attains serenity.","er":"But he who goes through the sense-objects with the senses free from love and hate, disciplined and controlled, attains serenity.","gu":"પરંતુ જે આત્મસંયમી પુરુષ રાગ-દ્વેષ વગર ઇન્દ્રિયો સ્વાધીન રાખીને વિષયો વચ્ચે વિચરે છે, તે પ્રસાદ — ચિત્તની પ્રસન્નતા — ને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"2.65","ch":2,"v":65,"sa":"प्रसादे सर्वदुःखानां हानिरस्योपजायते।\nप्रसन्नचेतसो ह्याशु बुद्धिः पर्यवतिष्ठते।।2.65।।","tr":"prasāde sarva-duḥkhānāṁ hānir asyopajāyate\nprasanna-chetaso hyāśhu buddhiḥ paryavatiṣhṭhate","en":"In that peace, all pains are destroyed; for the intellect of the tranquil-minded soon becomes steady.","es":"When there is serenity, all his sorrows are eradicated, for the wisdom of one with a serene mind soon becomes firmly established.","er":"In that serenity, all sorrow is lost; for in the case of the person with a serene mind, the Buddhi is quickly established.","gu":"એ પ્રસાદ-ચિત્તતામાં સઘળાં દુઃખો નષ્ટ થઈ જાય છે; કારણ કે પ્રસન્ન ચિત્તવાળા મનુષ્યની બુદ્ધિ શીઘ્ર સ્થિર થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"2.66","ch":2,"v":66,"sa":"नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य न चायुक्तस्य भावना।\nन चाभावयतः शान्तिरशान्तस्य कुतः सुखम्।।2.66।।","tr":"nāsti buddhir-ayuktasya na chāyuktasya bhāvanā\nna chābhāvayataḥ śhāntir aśhāntasya kutaḥ sukham","en":"There is no knowledge of the Self for the unsteady, and no meditation is possible for the unsteady, and no peace for the unmeditative, and how can there be happiness for one who has no peace?","es":"For the unsteady there is no wisdom, and there is no meditation for the unsteady person. And for an unmeditative person there is no peace. How can there be happiness for one without peace?","er":"There is no Buddhi for the unintegrated, nor is there contemplation of the self for him, and without contemplation of the self, there is no peace; and for one who lacks peace, where is the happiness?","gu":"અસ્થિર ચિત્તવાળા માટે ન જ્ઞાન છે, ન ધ્યાન; ધ્યાન વગર શાંતિ નથી, અને શાંતિ વગર સુખ ક્યાંથી હોય?"},{"ref":"2.67","ch":2,"v":67,"sa":"इन्द्रियाणां हि चरतां यन्मनोऽनुविधीयते।\nतदस्य हरति प्रज्ञां वायुर्नावमिवाम्भसि।।2.67।।","tr":"indriyāṇāṁ hi charatāṁ yan mano ’nuvidhīyate\ntadasya harati prajñāṁ vāyur nāvam ivāmbhasi","en":"For the mind, which follows in the wake of the wandering senses, carries away his discrimination, as the wind carries away a boat on the waters.","es":"For, the mind which follows in the wake of the wandering senses carries away his wisdom like a boat on the waters.","er":"For, when the mind follows the senses, experiencing their objects, his understanding is carried away by them, just as the wind carries away a ship on the waters.","gu":"જેમ પાણીમાં ચાલતી નૌકાને પવન ઉડાવી જાય છે, તેમ ચંચળ ઇન્દ્રિયો પાછળ ભટકતું મન મનુષ્યની વિવેકબુદ્ધિ હરી લે છે."},{"ref":"2.68","ch":2,"v":68,"sa":"तस्माद्यस्य महाबाहो निगृहीतानि सर्वशः।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता।।2.68।।","tr":"tasmād yasya mahā-bāho nigṛihītāni sarvaśhaḥ\nindriyāṇīndriyārthebhyas tasya prajñā pratiṣhṭhitā","en":"Therefore, O mighty-armed Arjuna, his knowledge is steady whose senses are completely restrained from sense objects.","es":"Therefore, O mighty-armed one, this wisdom becomes established when all its senses are withdrawn from their objects.","er":"Therefore, O mighty-armed one, he whose senses are restrained from going after their objects on all sides, his wisdom is firmly established.","gu":"તેથી, હે મહાબાહો અર્જુન, જેની ઇન્દ્રિયો ઇન્દ્રિયવિષયોથી સર્વ રીતે નિરોધ પામેલી છે, તેની જ પ્રજ્ઞા સ્થિર ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"2.69","ch":2,"v":69,"sa":"या निशा सर्वभूतानां तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी।\nयस्यां जाग्रति भूतानि सा निशा पश्यतो मुनेः।।2.69।।","tr":"yā niśhā sarva-bhūtānāṁ tasyāṁ jāgarti sanyamī\nyasyāṁ jāgrati bhūtāni sā niśhā paśhyato muneḥ","en":"That which is night to all beings, in that the self-controlled man is awake; when all beings are awake, that is night for the sage who sees.","es":"The self-restrained man stays awake during what is night for all creatures. That which creatures stay awake for, it is night to the discerning sage.","er":"What is night for all beings, in it the one who is controlled is awake; when all beings are awake, that is the night for the sage who sees.","gu":"સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓ માટે જે રાત છે, તે સ્થિતપ્રજ્ઞ સ્વ-સંયમી પુરુષ માટે જાગ્રત-કાળ છે; અને જ્યારે સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓ જાગ્યાં હોય, ત્યારે આત્મજ્ઞાની ઋષિ માટે તે ઘોર અંધારી રાત સમાન છે."},{"ref":"2.70","ch":2,"v":70,"sa":"आपूर्यमाणमचलप्रतिष्ठं\nसमुद्रमापः प्रविशन्ति यद्वत्।\nतद्वत्कामा यं प्रविशन्ति सर्वे\nस शान्तिमाप्नोति न कामकामी।।2.70।।","tr":"āpūryamāṇam achala-pratiṣhṭhaṁ\nsamudram āpaḥ praviśhanti yadvat\ntadvat kāmā yaṁ praviśhanti sarve\nsa śhāntim āpnoti na kāma-kāmī","en":"He attains peace into whom all desires enter, just as waters enter the ocean which, filled from all sides, remains unmoved; but not the man who is full of desires.","es":"That man attains peace into whom all desires enter, just as waters flow into the sea that remains unchanged even when filled from all sides. Not so one who is desirous of objects.","er":"He into whom all desires enter, just as the waters enter the full and undisturbed sea, attains peace, and not he who longs after objects of desire."},{"ref":"2.71","ch":2,"v":71,"sa":"विहाय कामान्यः सर्वान्पुमांश्चरति निःस्पृहः।\nनिर्ममो निरहंकारः स शांतिमधिगच्छति।।2.71।।","tr":"vihāya kāmān yaḥ sarvān pumānśh charati niḥspṛihaḥ\nnirmamo nirahankāraḥ sa śhāntim adhigachchhati","en":"That person attains peace who, abandoning all desires, moves about without longing, without the sense of ownership, and without egoism.","es":"That man attains peace who, after rejecting all desires, moves about free from hankering, without the idea of 'me' and 'mine', and devoid of pride.","er":"The one who, abandoning all desires, abides without longing, possession, and the sense of 'I' and 'mine', wins peace."},{"ref":"2.72","ch":2,"v":72,"sa":"एषा ब्राह्मी स्थितिः पार्थ नैनां प्राप्य विमुह्यति।\nस्थित्वाऽस्यामन्तकालेऽपि ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृच्छति।।2.72।।","tr":"eṣhā brāhmī sthitiḥ pārtha naināṁ prāpya vimuhyati\nsthitvāsyām anta-kāle ’pi brahma-nirvāṇam ṛichchhati","en":"O son of Pritha, this is the eternal state, the Brahmic seat. Attaining this, one is not deluded. Being established in it, one attains oneness with Brahman even at the end of life.","es":"O Partha, this is the state of being established in Brahman. One does not become deluded after attaining this; one attains identification with Brahman by being established in this state even in the closing years of one's life.","er":"This is the Brahmic state, O Arjuna. No one attaining to this is deluded. By abiding in this state even at the hour of death, one will attain the Self.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, આ બ્રહ્મની શાશ્વત સ્થિતિ છે — જે આને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે તે મોહ પામતો નથી. જીવનના અંતે પણ આ સ્થિતિમાં સ્થિર રહીને સાધક બ્રહ્મ સાથે એક થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"3.1","ch":3,"v":1,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nज्यायसी चेत्कर्मणस्ते मता बुद्धिर्जनार्दन।\nतत्किं कर्मणि घोरे मां नियोजयसि केशव।।3.1।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\njyāyasī chet karmaṇas te matā buddhir janārdana\ntat kiṁ karmaṇi ghore māṁ niyojayasi keśhava","en":"Arjuna said: If Thou thinkest that knowledge is superior to action, O Krishna, why then, O Kesava, doest Thou ask me to engage in this terrible action?","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Janardana (Krishna), if it is Your opinion that wisdom is superior to action, why do You urge me to take such horrible action, O Kesava?\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"O Krsna, if you deem knowledge to be superior to action, why then do you urge me to engage in this terrible deed?\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે કૃષ્ણ, જો તમે કર્મ કરતાં જ્ઞાનને શ્રેષ્ઠ માનો છો, તો પછી મને આ ભયંકર યુદ્ધમાં શા માટે પ્રવૃત્ત કરો છો?"},{"ref":"3.2","ch":3,"v":2,"sa":"व्यामिश्रेणेव वाक्येन बुद्धिं मोहयसीव मे।\nतदेकं वद निश्िचत्य येन श्रेयोऽहमाप्नुयाम्।।3.2।।","tr":"vyāmiśhreṇeva vākyena buddhiṁ mohayasīva me\ntad ekaṁ vada niśhchitya yena śhreyo ’ham āpnuyām","en":"With this seemingly perplexing speech, you seem to be confusing my understanding; therefore, tell me one certain way by which I may attain bliss.","es":"You bewilder my understanding, as it were, with a seemingly conflicting statement! Tell me for certain which one of these I may use to attain the highest Good.","er":"You confuse my mind with statements that seem to contradict each other; tell me for certain the one way by which I could reach the highest good.","gu":"આ ગૂઢ વચનોથી તમે મારી બુદ્ધિ ભ્રમિત કરી રહ્યા છો; માટે મને સ્પષ્ટ રીતે એ એક માર્ગ કહો કે જેનાથી હું કલ્યાણ પ્રાપ્ત કરી શકું."},{"ref":"3.3","ch":3,"v":3,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nलोकेऽस्मिन्द्विविधा निष्ठा पुरा प्रोक्ता मयानघ।\nज्ञानयोगेन सांख्यानां कर्मयोगेन योगिनाम्।।3.3।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nloke’smin dvi-vidhā niṣhṭhā purā proktā mayānagha\njñāna-yogena sāṅkhyānāṁ karma-yogena yoginām","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"In this world, there is a twofold path, as I said before, O sinless one: the path of knowledge of the Sankhyas and the path of action of the Yogins.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, O unblemished one, two kinds of steadfastness in this world were spoken of by Me in days gone by—through the Yoga of Knowledge for the men of realization; through the Yoga of Action for the yogis.","er":"The Lord said, \"In this world, a two-fold way was of yore laid down by Me, O sinless one: Jnana Yoga for the Sankhyas and Karma Yoga for the Yogins.\"","gu":"ભગવાન કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: આ સૃષ્ટિમાં મેં બે પ્રકારની નિષ્ઠા કહી છે — સાંખ્યયોગીઓ માટે જ્ઞાનનિષ્ઠા અને કર્મયોગીઓ માટે કર્મ-નિષ્ઠા."},{"ref":"3.4","ch":3,"v":4,"sa":"न कर्मणामनारम्भान्नैष्कर्म्यं पुरुषोऽश्नुते।\nन च संन्यसनादेव सिद्धिं समधिगच्छति।।3.4।।","tr":"na karmaṇām anārambhān naiṣhkarmyaṁ puruṣho ’śhnute\nna cha sannyasanād eva siddhiṁ samadhigachchhati","en":"Man does not reach actionlessness by not performing actions; nor does he attain perfection by mere renunciation.","es":"A person does not attain freedom from action by abstaining from action; nor does he attain fulfillment merely through renunciation.","er":"No one experiences freedom from action (Naiskarmya) by abstaining from work; and no one ever attains success through mere renunciation of work.","gu":"માત્ર કર્મ ન કરવાથી મનુષ્ય કર્મ-બંધનથી મુક્ત થતો નથી, અને માત્ર ત્યાગ કરવાથી તે સિદ્ધિ પ્રાપ્ત કરતો નથી."},{"ref":"3.5","ch":3,"v":5,"sa":"न हि कश्िचत्क्षणमपि जातु तिष्ठत्यकर्मकृत्।\nकार्यते ह्यवशः कर्म सर्वः प्रकृतिजैर्गुणैः।।3.5।।","tr":"na hi kaśhchit kṣhaṇam api jātu tiṣhṭhatyakarma-kṛit\nkāryate hyavaśhaḥ karma sarvaḥ prakṛiti-jair guṇaiḥ","en":"Verily, no one can remain for even a moment without performing action; for everyone is made to act helplessly, indeed, by the qualities born of Nature.","es":"For no one ever remains even for a moment without doing work, for all are made to work under compulsion by the gunas born of Nature.","er":"No one can remain still for even a moment without doing work; for everyone is compelled to act, despite themselves, by the Gunas born of Nature.","gu":"ખરેખર, કોઈ પણ મનુષ્ય એક ક્ષણ માટે પણ કર્મ વિના રહી શકતો નથી, કારણ કે પ્રકૃતિના ગુણો દ્વારા સૌ કોઈ અનિવાર્યપણે કર્મ કરવા પ્રેરાય છે."},{"ref":"3.6","ch":3,"v":6,"sa":"कर्मेन्द्रियाणि संयम्य य आस्ते मनसा स्मरन्।\nइन्द्रियार्थान्विमूढात्मा मिथ्याचारः स उच्यते।।3.6।।","tr":"karmendriyāṇi sanyamya ya āste manasā smaran\nindriyārthān vimūḍhātmā mithyāchāraḥ sa uchyate","en":"He who, restraining the organs of action, sits thinking of the sense-objects in his mind, he of deluded understanding is called a hypocrite.","es":"One who, after withdrawing the organs of action, sits mentally recollecting the objects of the senses, is called a hypocrite, for they have a deluded mind.","er":"He who, controlling the organs of action, lets his mind dwell on the objects of the senses, is a deluded person and a hypocrite.","gu":"જે મનુષ્ય ઇન્દ્રિયોને ઉપર ઉઠાવ્યા વગર, મનમાં વિષય-ભોગ ચિંતવતો બેઠો રહે છે, તેની મૂઢ-બુદ્ધિ ઢોંગી (મિથ્યાચારી) ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"3.7","ch":3,"v":7,"sa":"यस्त्विन्द्रियाणि मनसा नियम्यारभतेऽर्जुन।\nकर्मेन्द्रियैः कर्मयोगमसक्तः स विशिष्यते।।3.7।।","tr":"yas tvindriyāṇi manasā niyamyārabhate ’rjuna\nkarmendriyaiḥ karma-yogam asaktaḥ sa viśhiṣhyate","en":"But whoever, controlling the senses by the mind, O Arjuna, engages himself in Karma Yoga with the organs of action, without attachment, he excels.","es":"But, O Arjuna, one who engages in Karma-yoga, controlling the organs of action with the mind and becoming unattached, excels.","er":"But he who, subduing his senses by the mind, O Arjuna, begins to practice Karma Yoga through the organs of action and who is free from attachment, excels.","gu":"પરંતુ જે મનુષ્ય મન વડે ઇન્દ્રિયોને વશ કરીને, આસક્તિ રહિત થઈ કર્મ-ઇન્દ્રિયો દ્વારા કર્મ-યોગ આચરે છે, તે શ્રેષ્ઠ છે."},{"ref":"3.8","ch":3,"v":8,"sa":"नियतं कुरु कर्म त्वं कर्म ज्यायो ह्यकर्मणः।\nशरीरयात्रापि च ते न प्रसिद्ध्येदकर्मणः।।3.8।।","tr":"niyataṁ kuru karma tvaṁ karma jyāyo hyakarmaṇaḥ\nśharīra-yātrāpi cha te na prasiddhyed akarmaṇaḥ","en":"Perform your bounden duty, for action is superior to inaction, and even the maintenance of the body would not be possible for you through inaction.","es":"You should perform your obligatory duties, for action is superior to inaction. Moreover, even the maintenance of your body will not be possible without action.","er":"You must perform your obligatory action; for action is superior to non-action (Jñāna Yoga). For a person following non-action, not even the sustenance of the body is possible.","gu":"તારે નિયત કર્મ અવશ્ય કરવું જોઈએ, કારણ કે કર્મ ન કરવા કરતાં કર્મ કરવું ઉત્તમ છે; કર્મ-ત્યાગથી તો તારું શરીર-ધારણ કરવું પણ અશક્ય થઈ જશે."},{"ref":"3.9","ch":3,"v":9,"sa":"यज्ञार्थात्कर्मणोऽन्यत्र लोकोऽयं कर्मबन्धनः।\nतदर्थं कर्म कौन्तेय मुक्तसंगः समाचर।।3.9।।","tr":"yajñārthāt karmaṇo ’nyatra loko ’yaṁ karma-bandhanaḥ\ntad-arthaṁ karma kaunteya mukta-saṅgaḥ samāchara","en":"The world is bound by actions other than those performed for the sake of sacrifice; do thou, therefore, O son of Kunti (Arjuna), perform actions for that sake alone, free from attachment.","es":"This man becomes bound by actions other than those intended for God. Without being attached, O son of Kunti, perform actions for Him.","er":"This world is held in the bondage of work only when work is not performed as a sacrifice. O Arjuna, you must perform work for this purpose, free from attachment.","gu":"યજ્ઞ સ્વરૂપ ઈશ્વર-અર્પણ સિવાયના કર્મ જગતને બંધનમાં નાખે છે; માટે, હે અર્જુન, આસક્તિ છોડીને બધાં કર્મ યજ્ઞ-ભાવે ઈશ્વરાર્પણ કર."},{"ref":"3.10","ch":3,"v":10,"sa":"सहयज्ञाः प्रजाः सृष्ट्वा पुरोवाच प्रजापतिः।\nअनेन प्रसविष्यध्वमेष वोऽस्त्विष्टकामधुक्।।3.10।।","tr":"saha-yajñāḥ prajāḥ sṛiṣhṭvā purovācha prajāpatiḥ\nanena prasaviṣhyadhvam eṣha vo ’stviṣhṭa-kāma-dhuk","en":"The Creator, having in the beginning created mankind together with sacrifice, said, \"By this shall you propagate; let this be the milch cow of your desires—the cow that yields all the desired objects.\"","es":"In days of yore, having created the beings together with the sacrifices, Prajapati said, \"By this, you shall multiply. Let this be your yielder of coveted objects of desire.\"","er":"In the beginning, the Lord of all beings created man along with the sacrifice and said, \"By this shall you prosper; this shall be the cow of plenty, granting all your desires.\"","gu":"સૃષ્ટિના આદિ-સ્રષ્ટાએ પ્રજા અને યજ્ઞ એક સાથે ઉત્પન્ન કરીને કહ્યું: 'આ યજ્ઞ દ્વારા તમે વૃદ્ધિ પામો; આ તમારી ઇચ્છાઓ પૂર્ણ કરનારો કામધેનુ થાઓ.'"},{"ref":"3.11","ch":3,"v":11,"sa":"देवान्भावयतानेन ते देवा भावयन्तु वः।\nपरस्परं भावयन्तः श्रेयः परमवाप्स्यथ।।3.11।।","tr":"devān bhāvayatānena te devā bhāvayantu vaḥ\nparasparaṁ bhāvayantaḥ śhreyaḥ param avāpsyatha","en":"With this, nourish the gods, and may the gods nourish you; thus, nourishing each other, you shall attain the highest good.","es":"'You nourish the gods with this. Let those gods nourish you in return. By mutually nourishing each other, you shall attain the supreme Good.'","er":"By this, please the gods, and they will support you. Thus, nourishing each other, you may obtain the highest good.","gu":"આ યજ્ઞ વડે દેવોને પ્રસન્ન કરો, અને તે દેવો તમને ઉન્નત કરશે; આ રીતે પ્રેમ-ભાવે એકબીજાને પોષીને તમે પરમ કલ્યાણ પ્રાપ્ત કરો."},{"ref":"3.12","ch":3,"v":12,"sa":"इष्टान्भोगान्हि वो देवा दास्यन्ते यज्ञभाविताः।\nतैर्दत्तानप्रदायैभ्यो यो भुङ्क्ते स्तेन एव सः।।3.12।।","tr":"iṣhṭān bhogān hi vo devā dāsyante yajña-bhāvitāḥ\ntair dattān apradāyaibhyo yo bhuṅkte stena eva saḥ","en":"The gods, nourished by the sacrifice, will give you the desired objects. So, he who enjoys the objects given by the gods without offering anything in return is indeed a thief.","es":"'Being nourished by sacrifices, the gods will indeed give you the coveted enjoyments. He is certainly a thief who enjoys what has been given by them without offering it to them.'","er":"The gods, pleased by the sacrifice, will bestow upon you the enjoyments you desire. He who enjoys the bounty of the gods without giving them anything in return is but a thief.","gu":"દેવો, યજ્ઞ-ભાવ સ્વીકારીને, તમને ઇચ્છિત ભોગ-સામગ્રી આપશે; પરંતુ જે માણસ આ ભોગ-સામગ્રી ઈશ્વર-અર્પણ વિના ભોગવે છે, તે ખરે જ ચોર છે."},{"ref":"3.13","ch":3,"v":13,"sa":"यज्ञशिष्टाशिनः सन्तो मुच्यन्ते सर्वकिल्बिषैः।\nभुञ्जते ते त्वघं पापा ये पचन्त्यात्मकारणात्।।3.13।।","tr":"yajña-śhiṣhṭāśhinaḥ santo muchyante sarva-kilbiṣhaiḥ\nbhuñjate te tvaghaṁ pāpā ye pachantyātma-kāraṇāt","en":"The righteous who eat the remnants of the sacrifice are freed from all sins; but those sinful ones who cook food solely for their own sake indeed consume sin.","es":"By partaking in the remnants of sacrifices, they become freed from all sins. But those who are unholy and cook for themselves incur sin.","er":"Pious people who eat the remnants of sacrifices are freed from all sins, whereas those who are sinful and cook only for their own sake will only incur sin.","gu":"યજ્ઞ-શેષ-ભોજન ભોગવનારા સત્ત્વ-ગુણી ભક્તો સર્વ પાપ-બંધનથી મુક્ત થઈ જાય છે; પરંતુ જે સ્વાર્થ-ભાવે ફક્ત પોતાના માટે ભોજન પકવે છે, તે પાપ જ ભક્ષણ કરે છે."},{"ref":"3.14","ch":3,"v":14,"sa":"अन्नाद्भवन्ति भूतानि पर्जन्यादन्नसम्भवः।\nयज्ञाद्भवति पर्जन्यो यज्ञः कर्मसमुद्भवः।।3.14।।","tr":"annād bhavanti bhūtāni parjanyād anna-sambhavaḥ\nyajñād bhavati parjanyo yajñaḥ karma-samudbhavaḥ","en":"From food come forth beings; from rain, food is produced; from sacrifice arises rain, and sacrifice is born of action.","es":"From food are born the creatures; the origin of food is from rain; rain originates from sacrifice; sacrifice has action as its source.","er":"All beings arise from food; food is produced from rain; rain comes from sacrifice; and sacrifice is born of action.","gu":"અન્નથી પ્રાણીઓ ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે, વરસાદથી અન્ન ઊગે છે, યજ્ઞ-ભાવ-ક્રિયાથી વરસાદ પ્રગટ થાય છે, અને કર્મ-સ્ફૂર્તિ-ભક્તિ-ક્રિયા (ક્રિયા-કર્મ) થી જ યજ્ઞ-ભાવ ઉદ્ભવે છે."},{"ref":"3.15","ch":3,"v":15,"sa":"कर्म ब्रह्मोद्भवं विद्धि ब्रह्माक्षरसमुद्भवम्।\nतस्मात्सर्वगतं ब्रह्म नित्यं यज्ञे प्रतिष्ठितम्।।3.15।।","tr":"karma brahmodbhavaṁ viddhi brahmākṣhara-samudbhavam\ntasmāt sarva-gataṁ brahma nityaṁ yajñe pratiṣhṭhitam","en":"Know that action comes from Brahma, and Brahma comes from the Imperishable. Therefore, the all-pervasive Brahma ever rests in sacrifice.","es":"Know that action has the Vedas as its origin; the Vedas have the Immutable as their source. Hence, the all-pervading Vedas are forever based on sacrifice.","er":"Know that activity springs from Brahman, i.e., the physical body; Brahman arises from the imperishable Self; therefore, the all-pervading Brahman is ever established in sacrifice.","gu":"કર્મ બ્રહ્મમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે, અને બ્રહ્મ અવિનાશી પરમતત્ત્વમાંથી પ્રગટ થાય છે; તેથી સર્વવ્યાપી બ્રહ્મ સદૈવ યજ્ઞમાં પ્રતિષ્ઠિત છે."},{"ref":"3.16","ch":3,"v":16,"sa":"एवं प्रवर्तितं चक्रं नानुवर्तयतीह यः।\nअघायुरिन्द्रियारामो मोघं पार्थ स जीवति।।3.16।।","tr":"evaṁ pravartitaṁ chakraṁ nānuvartayatīha yaḥ\naghāyur indriyārāmo moghaṁ pārtha sa jīvati","en":"He who does not follow the wheel thus set in motion, who is of sinful life, rejoicing in the senses, lives in vain, O Arjuna.","es":"O Partha, he who does not follow the wheel thus set in motion lives in vain, their life is sinful, and they indulge in the senses.","er":"He who does not follow the wheel thus set in motion here, lives in sin, satisfying the senses, O Arjuna; he lives in vain.","gu":"જે આ રીતે ગતિ કરતા કર્મ-ચક્રને અનુસરતો નથી અને ઇન્દ્રિય-ભોગમાં રાચીને પાપમય જીવન જીવે છે, હે અર્જુન, તેનું જીવન નિરર્થક છે."},{"ref":"3.17","ch":3,"v":17,"sa":"यस्त्वात्मरतिरेव स्यादात्मतृप्तश्च मानवः।\nआत्मन्येव च सन्तुष्टस्तस्य कार्यं न विद्यते।।3.17।।","tr":"yas tvātma-ratir eva syād ātma-tṛiptaśh cha mānavaḥ\nātmanyeva cha santuṣhṭas tasya kāryaṁ na vidyate","en":"But for that man who rejoices only in the Self, who is satisfied with the Self and is content in the Self alone, indeed there is nothing to do.","es":"But that man who rejoices only in the Self, is satisfied with the Self, and is content only in the Self—for him there is no duty to perform.","er":"But the man whose delight is only in the Self, who is satisfied with the Self, who rejoices in the Self, for him nothing remains to be accomplished.","gu":"પરંતુ જે વ્યક્તિ માત્ર આત્મામાં જ આનંદ પામે છે, આત્મામાં જ તૃપ્ત રહે છે અને આત્મામાં જ સંતુષ્ટ છે — તેને કોઈ કર્તવ્ય બાકી રહેતું નથી."},{"ref":"3.18","ch":3,"v":18,"sa":"नैव तस्य कृतेनार्थो नाकृतेनेह कश्चन।\nन चास्य सर्वभूतेषु कश्िचदर्थव्यपाश्रयः।।3.18।।","tr":"naiva tasya kṛitenārtho nākṛiteneha kaśhchana\nna chāsya sarva-bhūteṣhu kaśhchid artha-vyapāśhrayaḥ","en":"For him, there is no interest whatsoever in what is done or not done; nor does he depend on any being for any purpose.","es":"For him, there is no concern here at all with performing action, nor any with non-performance. Moreover, he has no dependence on any object to serve any purpose.","er":"He has no purpose to gain from work done or left undone, nor does he have to rely on any end.","gu":"આ જગતમાં કર્મ કરવાથી કે ન કરવાથી તેવી વ્યક્તિને કોઈ પ્રયોજન નથી; અને કોઈ પણ પ્રાણી પર તે કોઈ ઉદ્દેશ્ય માટે આધાર રાખતી નથી."},{"ref":"3.19","ch":3,"v":19,"sa":"तस्मादसक्तः सततं कार्यं कर्म समाचर।\nअसक्तो ह्याचरन्कर्म परमाप्नोति पूरुषः।।3.19।।","tr":"tasmād asaktaḥ satataṁ kāryaṁ karma samāchara\nasakto hyācharan karma param āpnoti pūruṣhaḥ","en":"Therefore, without attachment, always perform the actions that should be done; for by performing actions without attachment, one reaches the Supreme.","es":"Therefore, remaining unattached, always perform the obligatory duty; for, by performing one's duty without attachment, a person attains the highest.","er":"Therefore, do your work without attachment, which ought to be done. For, a person who works without attachment attains the Supreme."},{"ref":"3.20","ch":3,"v":20,"sa":"कर्मणैव हि संसिद्धिमास्थिता जनकादयः।\nलोकसंग्रहमेवापि संपश्यन्कर्तुमर्हसि।।3.20।।","tr":"karmaṇaiva hi sansiddhim āsthitā janakādayaḥ\nloka-saṅgraham evāpi sampaśhyan kartum arhasi","en":"Janaka and others attained perfection indeed through action alone; even with the intention of protecting the masses, you should perform action.","es":"For Janaka and others strove to attain liberation through action itself. You should perform your duties, keeping in view the prevention of mankind from going astray.","er":"Indeed, Janaka and others reached perfection through Karma Yoga alone. Even recognizing its necessity for guiding the world, you must perform action.","gu":"જનક જેવા મહાત્માઓ માત્ર કર્મ દ્વારા જ સિદ્ધિ પ્રાપ્ત કરી; લોકકલ્યાણને ધ્યાનમાં રાખીને પણ તારે કર્મ કરવું જ જોઈએ."},{"ref":"3.21","ch":3,"v":21,"sa":"यद्यदाचरति श्रेष्ठस्तत्तदेवेतरो जनः।\nस यत्प्रमाणं कुरुते लोकस्तदनुवर्तते।।3.21।।","tr":"yad yad ācharati śhreṣhṭhas tat tad evetaro janaḥ\nsa yat pramāṇaṁ kurute lokas tad anuvartate","en":"Whatever a great man does, others also do; whatever he establishes as the standard, the world follows.","es":"Whatever a superior person does, another person does the same! Whatever they uphold as authority, an ordinary person follows that.","er":"Whatever a great man does, others do too. Whatever standard he sets, the world follows it."},{"ref":"3.22","ch":3,"v":22,"sa":"न मे पार्थास्ति कर्तव्यं त्रिषु लोकेषु किञ्चन।\nनानवाप्तमवाप्तव्यं वर्त एव च कर्मणि।।3.22।।","tr":"na me pārthāsti kartavyaṁ triṣhu lokeṣhu kiñchana\nnānavāptam avāptavyaṁ varta eva cha karmaṇi","en":"There is nothing in the three worlds, O Arjuna, that needs to be done by Me, nor is there anything unattained that needs to be attained; yet I engage Myself in action.","es":"In all the three worlds, O Partha, there is no duty for Me to fulfill; nothing remains unachieved or to be achieved. (Still,) I continue in action.","er":"For me, Arjuna, there is nothing in all the three worlds that ought to be done, nor is there anything unaccomplished that ought to be accomplished. Yet I continue to work.","gu":"ત્રણ લોકોમાં મારે કઈ કર્તવ્ય નથી, ન પ્રાપ્ત કરવા જેવું કઈ અપ્રાપ્ત છે — છતાં હું કર્મ કરતો રહું છું."},{"ref":"3.23","ch":3,"v":23,"sa":"यदि ह्यहं न वर्तेयं जातु कर्मण्यतन्द्रितः।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः।।3.23।।","tr":"yadi hyahaṁ na varteyaṁ jātu karmaṇyatandritaḥ\nmama vartmānuvartante manuṣhyāḥ pārtha sarvaśhaḥ","en":"For, should I not ever engage myself in action, unwearied, people would in every way follow my path, O Arjuna.","es":"For, O Partha, if at any time I do not continue vigilantly in action, people will follow My path in every way.","er":"If I did not continue to work unweariedly, O Arjuna, people would follow my path.","gu":"જો હું અથાક રીતે કર્મ ન કરું, તો હે અર્જુન, સર્વ રીતે લોકો મારા માર્ગને અનુસરશે."},{"ref":"3.24","ch":3,"v":24,"sa":"उत्सीदेयुरिमे लोका न कुर्यां कर्म चेदहम्।\nसङ्करस्य च कर्ता स्यामुपहन्यामिमाः प्रजाः।।3.24।।","tr":"utsīdeyur ime lokā na kuryāṁ karma ched aham\nsankarasya cha kartā syām upahanyām imāḥ prajāḥ","en":"These worlds would perish if I did not perform action; I would be the author of confusion of castes and destruction of these beings.","es":"These worlds would be ruined if I did not perform action. And I shall become the agent of intermingling (of castes), and shall be destroying these beings.","er":"If I do not do the work, these people will be lost; and I will be causing chaos in life and thereby ruining all these people.","gu":"જો હું કર્મ ન કરું, તો આ સઘળા લોકો નાશ પામે; હું વર્ણસંકરનો અને સઘળા પ્રાણીઓના વિનાશનો કારણ બની જાઉં."},{"ref":"3.25","ch":3,"v":25,"sa":"सक्ताः कर्मण्यविद्वांसो यथा कुर्वन्ति भारत।\nकुर्याद्विद्वांस्तथासक्तश्िचकीर्षुर्लोकसंग्रहम्।।3.25।।","tr":"saktāḥ karmaṇyavidvānso yathā kurvanti bhārata\nkuryād vidvāns tathāsaktaśh chikīrṣhur loka-saṅgraham","en":"As the ignorant act out of attachment to action, O Bharata, so should the wise act without attachment, wishing for the welfare of the world.","es":"O scion of the Bharata dynasty, as the unenlightened people act with attachment to work, so should the enlightened person act, without attachment, desiring to prevent people from going astray.","er":"Just as the ignorant, attached to their work, act, O Arjuna, so too the learned should act without any attachment, and only for the welfare of the world.","gu":"હે ભારત, જેમ અજ્ઞાની લોકો ફળ-આસક્તિ સહિત કર્મ કરે છે, તેમ જ્ઞાની વ્યક્તિએ અનાસક્ત ભાવે, લોકકલ્યાણ માટે કર્મ કરવું જોઈએ."},{"ref":"3.26","ch":3,"v":26,"sa":"न बुद्धिभेदं जनयेदज्ञानां कर्मसङ्गिनाम्।\nजोषयेत्सर्वकर्माणि विद्वान् युक्तः समाचरन्।।3.26।।","tr":"na buddhi-bhedaṁ janayed ajñānāṁ karma-saṅginām\njoṣhayet sarva-karmāṇi vidvān yuktaḥ samācharan","en":"Let no wise man unsettle the minds of ignorant people who are attached to action; he should engage them in all actions, himself fulfilling them with devotion.","es":"The enlightened man should not disturb the beliefs of the ignorant, who are attached to work. He should remain diligent himself and make them perform all their duties.","er":"He should not bewilder the minds of the ignorant who are attached to work; rather, he should himself perform work with devotion and cause others to do the same.","gu":"જ્ઞાની વ્યક્તિએ કર્મ-આસક્ત અજ્ઞાનીઓની બુદ્ધિ ડહોળવી ન જોઈએ; બલ્કે સ્વયં ભક્તિ સહિત સઘળાં કર્મ કરતા રહીને તેઓ દ્વારા પણ એ જ કર્મ કરાવવા જોઈએ."},{"ref":"3.27","ch":3,"v":27,"sa":"प्रकृतेः क्रियमाणानि गुणैः कर्माणि सर्वशः।\nअहङ्कारविमूढात्मा कर्ताऽहमिति मन्यते।।3.27।।","tr":"prakṛiteḥ kriyamāṇāni guṇaiḥ karmāṇi sarvaśhaḥ\nahankāra-vimūḍhātmā kartāham iti manyate","en":"All actions are wrought in all cases by the qualities of Nature alone. He whose mind is deluded by egoism thinks, \"I am the doer.\"","es":"While actions are being done in every way by the gunas (qualities) of Nature, one who is deluded by egoism thinks, \"I am the doer.\"","er":"Actions are being performed in every way by the Gunas of Prakrti; he whose nature is deluded by egoism, however, thinks, 'I am the doer.'","gu":"બધા કર્મ સર્વ પ્રસંગોમાં પ્રકૃતિના ગુણો દ્વારા જ સંપન્ન થાય છે; અહંકારથી ભ્રમિત ચિત્ત ધરાવનાર 'હું કર્તા છું' એમ માની લે છે."},{"ref":"3.28","ch":3,"v":28,"sa":"तत्त्ववित्तु महाबाहो गुणकर्मविभागयोः।\nगुणा गुणेषु वर्तन्त इति मत्वा न सज्जते।।3.28।।","tr":"tattva-vit tu mahā-bāho guṇa-karma-vibhāgayoḥ\nguṇā guṇeṣhu vartanta iti matvā na sajjate","en":"But he who knows the Truth, O mighty-armed Arjuna, about the divisions of the qualities and their functions, knowing that the Gunas, as senses, move amidst the Gunas, as the sense-objects, is not attached.","es":"But, O mighty-armed one, the one who is a knower of the facts about the varieties of the gunas and actions does not become attached, thinking thus: 'The organs act on the objects of the organs.'","er":"But he who knows the truth about the division of the Gunas and works, O mighty-armed one, through his knowledge that the Gunas 'operate on their own products,' is not attached.","gu":"હે મહાબાહો અર્જુન, ગુણોના વિભાગ અને તેમની ક્રિયાઓ અંગેનું સત્ય જાણનાર, 'ગુણ ગુણોમાં વર્તે છે' — એ સમજીને, આસક્ત થતો નથી."},{"ref":"3.29","ch":3,"v":29,"sa":"प्रकृतेर्गुणसम्मूढाः सज्जन्ते गुणकर्मसु।\nतानकृत्स्नविदो मन्दान्कृत्स्नविन्न विचालयेत्।।3.29।।","tr":"prakṛiter guṇa-sammūḍhāḥ sajjante guṇa-karmasu\ntān akṛitsna-vido mandān kṛitsna-vin na vichālayet","en":"Those deluded by the qualities of Nature are attached to the functions of the qualities. The man of perfect knowledge should not unsettle the foolish one who is of imperfect knowledge.","es":"Those who are completely deluded by the gunas of Nature become attached to the activities of the gunas. The one who knows the All should not disturb those of dull intellect, who do not know the All.","er":"Those who are deluded by the Gunas of Prakrti are attached to the works of the Gunas. But he who knows the whole truth should not disturb the ignorant who do not know the whole truth.","gu":"પ્રકૃતિના ગુણોથી ભ્રમિત મનુષ્ય ગુણ-કાર્યોમાં આસક્ત રહે છે; અધૂરા જ્ઞાન ધરાવતા એ મૂઢ જનોને જ્ઞાની વ્યક્તિએ વ્યગ્ર ન કરવા જોઈએ."},{"ref":"3.30","ch":3,"v":30,"sa":"मयि सर्वाणि कर्माणि संन्यस्याध्यात्मचेतसा।\nनिराशीर्निर्ममो भूत्वा युध्यस्व विगतज्वरः।।3.30।।","tr":"mayi sarvāṇi karmāṇi sannyasyādhyātma-chetasā\nnirāśhīr nirmamo bhūtvā yudhyasva vigata-jvaraḥ","en":"Renouncing all actions in Me, with the mind centered on the Self, free from hope and egoism, and from mental fever, fight thou.","es":"Free from the fever of the soul, dedicate all actions to Me, with your mind intent on the Self, and become free from expectations and egoism, and engage in battle.","er":"Surrender all your actions to Me, with a mind focused on the Self, free from desire and selfishness, and fight with the heat of excitement abated.","gu":"સઘળાં કર્મ મને અર્પણ કરી, આત્મ-ચિંતન સ્થિર રાખી, ઇચ્છા અને અહંકારથી મુક્ત, માનસિક સંતાપ ત્યજી — યુદ્ધ કર."},{"ref":"3.31","ch":3,"v":31,"sa":"ये मे मतमिदं नित्यमनुतिष्ठन्ति मानवाः।\nश्रद्धावन्तोऽनसूयन्तो मुच्यन्ते तेऽपि कर्मभिः।।3.31।।","tr":"ye me matam idaṁ nityam anutiṣhṭhanti mānavāḥ\nśhraddhāvanto ’nasūyanto muchyante te ’pi karmabhiḥ","en":"Those who constantly practice this teaching of Mine with faith and without caviling, they too are freed from actions.","es":"Those who faithfully follow this teaching of Mine without cavil, they too become freed from their actions.","er":"Those men who, full of faith, ever practice this teaching of Mine and those who receive it without cavil—even they are released from karma.","gu":"જે ભક્તો શ્રદ્ધા સહિત અને દોષ-દ્રષ્ટિ વિના મારી આ ઉપદેશ-ધારાને સતત આચરે છે, તેઓ પણ સઘળાં કર્મોના બંધનોથી મુક્ત થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"3.32","ch":3,"v":32,"sa":"ये त्वेतदभ्यसूयन्तो नानुतिष्ठन्ति मे मतम्।\nसर्वज्ञानविमूढांस्तान्विद्धि नष्टानचेतसः।।3.32।।","tr":"ye tvetad abhyasūyanto nānutiṣhṭhanti me matam\nsarva-jñāna-vimūḍhāns tān viddhi naṣhṭān achetasaḥ","en":"But those who criticize My teaching and do not practice it, deprived of all knowledge and lacking discernment, know them to be doomed to destruction.","es":"But those who, finding fault where there is none, do not follow My teaching, know them—who are deluded about all knowledge concerning the qualified and the unqualified Brahman and who are devoid of discrimination—to have gone to ruin.","er":"But those who slander it, and those who do not practice this teaching of Mine—know them to be utterly senseless and devoid of all knowledge, and thus lost.","gu":"જેઓ મારા ઉપદેશની ટીકા કરે છે અને તેનું પાલન કરતા નથી, તેઓ જ્ઞાનથી વંચિત અને વિવેકહીન છે — એ લોકોને નષ્ટ થયેલા જાણ."},{"ref":"3.33","ch":3,"v":33,"sa":"सदृशं चेष्टते स्वस्याः प्रकृतेर्ज्ञानवानपि।\nप्रकृतिं यान्ति भूतानि निग्रहः किं करिष्यति।।3.33।।","tr":"sadṛiśhaṁ cheṣhṭate svasyāḥ prakṛiter jñānavān api\nprakṛitiṁ yānti bhūtāni nigrahaḥ kiṁ kariṣhyati","en":"Even a wise man acts in accordance with his own nature; beings will follow their nature; what can restraint do?","es":"Even a man of wisdom behaves according to his own nature. They follow their nature. What can restraint do?","er":"Even the man of knowledge acts according to his nature; all beings follow their own nature. What will repression accomplish?","gu":"જ્ઞાની પુરુષ પણ પોતાની પ્રકૃતિ અનુસાર જ વર્તે છે; સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓ પ્રકૃતિને અનુસરે છે — પછી સંયમ શું કરી શકે?"},{"ref":"3.34","ch":3,"v":34,"sa":"इन्द्रियस्येन्द्रियस्यार्थे रागद्वेषौ व्यवस्थितौ।\nतयोर्न वशमागच्छेत्तौ ह्यस्य परिपन्थिनौ।।3.34।।","tr":"indriyasyendriyasyārthe rāga-dveṣhau vyavasthitau\ntayor na vaśham āgachchhet tau hyasya paripanthinau","en":"Attachment and aversion for the objects of the senses abide in the senses; let no one come under their sway; for, they are his enemies.","es":"Attraction and repulsion are ordained with respect to the objects of all the organs. One should not be swayed by these two, as they are adversaries.","er":"Each sense has a fixed attachment to and aversion for its corresponding object, but one should not come under their sway, for they are enemies.","gu":"ઇન્દ્રિયોના વિષયો પ્રત્યે રાગ અને દ્વેષ ઇન્દ્રિયોમાં જ વસે છે; કોઈ એ બંનેના વશમાં ન આવે, કેમ કે તેઓ સાધકના માર્ગ પરના શત્રુ છે."},{"ref":"3.35","ch":3,"v":35,"sa":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात्।\nस्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो भयावहः।।3.35।।","tr":"śhreyān swa-dharmo viguṇaḥ para-dharmāt sv-anuṣhṭhitāt\nswa-dharme nidhanaṁ śhreyaḥ para-dharmo bhayāvahaḥ","en":"Better is one's own duty, though devoid of merit, than the duty of another well discharged. Better is death in one's own duty; the duty of another is fraught with fear.","es":"One's own duty, though defective, is superior to another's duty well-performed. Death is better while engaged in one's own duty; another's duty is full of fear.","er":"Better is one's own duty, even if done poorly, than the duty of another done well. It is better to die while performing one's own duty; the duty of another is full of fear."},{"ref":"3.36","ch":3,"v":36,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nअथ केन प्रयुक्तोऽयं पापं चरति पूरुषः।\nअनिच्छन्नपि वार्ष्णेय बलादिव नियोजितः।।3.36।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\natha kena prayukto ’yaṁ pāpaṁ charati pūruṣhaḥ\nanichchhann api vārṣhṇeya balād iva niyojitaḥ","en":"Arjuna said, \"But what compels man to commit sin, even against his wishes, O Varshneya (Krishna), as if constrained by force?\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"Now then, O scion of the Vrsni dynasty (Krsna), what compels this man to commit sin even against his will, as if he were constrained by force?\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"But, O Krsna, what impels one to commit sin, even against their own will, as if constrained by force?\"","gu":"અર્જુને પૂછ્યું: હે કૃષ્ણ, કોઈ ન ઇચ્છે તો પણ, કઈ શક્તિ માણસને બળજબરીથી પાપ કરવા પ્રેરે છે?"},{"ref":"3.37","ch":3,"v":37,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nकाम एष क्रोध एष रजोगुणसमुद्भवः।\nमहाशनो महापाप्मा विद्ध्येनमिह वैरिणम्।।3.37।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nkāma eṣha krodha eṣha rajo-guṇa-samudbhavaḥ\nmahāśhano mahā-pāpmā viddhyenam iha vairiṇam","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"It is desire and it is anger, both of the quality of Rajas, all-devouring and all-sinful; know this as the foe here in this world.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"This desire, this anger, born of the quality of rajas, is a great devourer, a great source of sin. Know this to be the enemy here.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"It is desire, it is wrath, born of the guna of rajas; it is a great devourer, an impeller of sin. Know this to be the enemy here.\"","gu":"કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: આ રજોગુણથી જન્મેલ કામ અને ક્રોધ છે — સર્વભક્ષી અને મહાપાપી; આ જ સંસારમાં તારો શત્રુ છે, એમ જાણ."},{"ref":"3.38","ch":3,"v":38,"sa":"धूमेनाव्रियते वह्निर्यथाऽऽदर्शो मलेन च।\nयथोल्बेनावृतो गर्भस्तथा तेनेदमावृतम्।।3.38।।","tr":"dhūmenāvriyate vahnir yathādarśho malena cha\nyatholbenāvṛito garbhas tathā tenedam āvṛitam","en":"As fire is enveloped by smoke, as a mirror is covered by dust, and as an embryo is surrounded by the amniotic sac, so is this enveloped by that.","es":"As fire is enveloped by smoke, as a mirror is obscured by dirt, and as a fetus remains enclosed in the womb, so is this shrouded by that.","er":"As a fire is enveloped by smoke, as a mirror is covered by dust, and as an embryo is encased in the amniotic sac, so is this world enveloped by desire.","gu":"જેવી રીતે ધુમાડો અગ્નિને, ધૂળ દર્પણને અને ગર્ભ-આવરણ ગર્ભને ઢાંકે છે, તેવી જ રીતે કામ-ક્રોધ રૂપી શત્રુ જ્ઞાનને ઢાંકી દે છે."},{"ref":"3.39","ch":3,"v":39,"sa":"आवृतं ज्ञानमेतेन ज्ञानिनो नित्यवैरिणा।\nकामरूपेण कौन्तेय दुष्पूरेणानलेन च।।3.39।।","tr":"āvṛitaṁ jñānam etena jñānino nitya-vairiṇā\nkāma-rūpeṇa kaunteya duṣhpūreṇānalena cha","en":"O Arjuna, wisdom is enveloped by this constant enemy of the wise, in the form of desire, which is insatiable like fire.","es":"O son of Kunti, knowledge is covered by this constant enemy of the wise, in the form of desire, which is an insatiable fire.","er":"The knowledge of the intelligent self is enveloped by this constant enemy, O Arjuna, which is of the nature of desire and is difficult to gratify and insatiable.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, આ અગ્નિ સમાન અતૃપ્ત કામ — જ્ઞાનીઓનો ચિરંતન શત્રુ — વિવેકને ઢાંકી દે છે."},{"ref":"3.40","ch":3,"v":40,"sa":"इन्द्रियाणि मनो बुद्धिरस्याधिष्ठानमुच्यते।\nएतैर्विमोहयत्येष ज्ञानमावृत्य देहिनम्।।3.40।।","tr":"indriyāṇi mano buddhir asyādhiṣhṭhānam uchyate\netair vimohayatyeṣha jñānam āvṛitya dehinam","en":"The senses, the mind, and the intellect are said to be its seat; through these, it deludes the embodied one, veiling their wisdom.","es":"The organs, mind, and intellect are said to be its abode. This one diversely deludes the embodied being, veiling Knowledge with the help of these.","er":"The senses, the mind, and the intellect are said to be its instruments; by these, it overpowers the embodied self, enveloping its knowledge.","gu":"ઇન્દ્રિયો, મન અને બુદ્ધિ — એ ત્રણ કામના આસન કહેવાય છે; આ ત્રણ દ્વારા કામ દેહધારીના જ્ઞાનને ઢાંકી, તેને ભ્રમિત કરે છે."},{"ref":"3.41","ch":3,"v":41,"sa":"तस्मात्त्वमिन्द्रियाण्यादौ नियम्य भरतर्षभ।\nपाप्मानं प्रजहि ह्येनं ज्ञानविज्ञाननाशनम्।।3.41।।","tr":"tasmāt tvam indriyāṇyādau niyamya bharatarṣhabha\npāpmānaṁ prajahi hyenaṁ jñāna-vijñāna-nāśhanam","en":"Therefore, O best of the Bharatas, control your senses first and then kill this sinful thing, which destroys knowledge and realization.","es":"Therefore, O scion of the Bharata dynasty, after first controlling the organs, completely renounce this one which is sinful and a destroyer of learning and wisdom.","er":"Therefore, O Arjuna, control your senses from the outset and slay this sinful thing that destroys both knowledge and discernment.","gu":"તેથી હે ભરતશ્રેષ્ઠ, પ્રથમ ઇન્દ્રિયો પર સંયમ રાખ, અને પછી જ્ઞાન તથા વિજ્ઞાનના નાશ કરનાર આ પાપી કામને નષ્ટ કર."},{"ref":"3.42","ch":3,"v":42,"sa":"इन्द्रियाणि पराण्याहुरिन्द्रियेभ्यः परं मनः।\nमनसस्तु परा बुद्धिर्यो बुद्धेः परतस्तु सः।।3.42।।","tr":"indriyāṇi parāṇyāhur indriyebhyaḥ paraṁ manaḥ\nmanasas tu parā buddhir yo buddheḥ paratas tu saḥ","en":"They say that the senses are superior to the body; the mind is superior to the senses; the intellect is superior to the mind; and He (the Self) is superior even to the intellect.","es":"They say that the organs are superior to the gross body; the mind is superior to the organs; and the intellect is superior to the mind. However, He is superior to the intellect.","er":"They say that the senses are high, the mind is higher than the senses, the intellect is higher than the mind, but what is greater than the intellect is that (desire).","gu":"ઇન્દ્રિયો શરીર કરતાં શ્રેષ્ઠ કહેવાય છે; મન ઇન્દ્રિયો કરતાં શ્રેષ્ઠ છે; બુદ્ધિ મન કરતાં ઉચ્ચ છે; અને આત્મા બુદ્ધિ કરતાં પણ ઊંચો છે."},{"ref":"3.43","ch":3,"v":43,"sa":"एवं बुद्धेः परं बुद्ध्वा संस्तभ्यात्मानमात्मना।\nजहि शत्रुं महाबाहो कामरूपं दुरासदम्।।3.43।।","tr":"evaṁ buddheḥ paraṁ buddhvā sanstabhyātmānam ātmanā\njahi śhatruṁ mahā-bāho kāma-rūpaṁ durāsadam","en":"Thus, knowing Him who is superior to the intellect and restraining the self by the Self, slay thou, O mighty-armed Arjuna, the enemy in the form of desire, hard to conquer.","es":"[The Ast, introduces this verse with, 'Tatah kim, what follows from that?'-Tr.] Understanding the Self thus as superior to the intellect, and completely establishing (the Self) through spiritual absorption with the (help of) the mind, O mighty-armed one, the enemy in the form of desire, which is difficult to subdue, vanishes.","er":"Thus, knowing that which is higher than the intellect and fixing the mind with the help of the intellect in Karma Yoga, O Arjuna, slay this enemy which takes the form of desire, and which is difficult to overcome.","gu":"આ રીતે આત્માને બુદ્ધિ કરતાં ઉત્કૃષ્ટ જાણી, આત્માથી મનને સ્થિર કરીને, હે મહાબાહો અર્જુન, આ કામ-રૂપી દુર્જય શત્રુને નષ્ટ કર."},{"ref":"4.1","ch":4,"v":1,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nइमं विवस्वते योगं प्रोक्तवानहमव्ययम्।\nविवस्वान् मनवे प्राह मनुरिक्ष्वाकवेऽब्रवीत्।।4.1।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nimaṁ vivasvate yogaṁ proktavān aham avyayam\nvivasvān manave prāha manur ikṣhvākave ’bravīt","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"I taught this imperishable Yoga to Vivasvan; he then told it to Manu; Manu proclaimed it to Ikshvaku.","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"I imparted this imperishable Yoga to Vivasvan, who then taught it to Manu, who in turn transmitted it to Iksavaku.","er":"The Lord said, \"I taught this imperishable Yoga to Vivasvan; Vivasvan taught it to Manu; Manu declared it to Iksvaku.\"","gu":"કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: મેં આ અવિનાશી યોગ વિવસ્વાન (સૂર્ય)ને ઉપદેશ્યો; વિવસ્વાને મનુને શીખવ્યો; મનુએ ઇક્ષ્વાકુ પ્રત્યે પ્રગટ કર્યો."},{"ref":"4.2","ch":4,"v":2,"sa":"एवं परम्पराप्राप्तमिमं राजर्षयो विदुः।\nस कालेनेह महता योगो नष्टः परन्तप।।4.2।।","tr":"evaṁ paramparā-prāptam imaṁ rājarṣhayo viduḥ\nsa kāleneha mahatā yogo naṣhṭaḥ parantapa","en":"This, handed down in regular succession by the royal sages, was known. This Yoga, however, has been lost here over time, O Parantapa (burner of the foes).","es":"The king-sages knew this yoga, which was received in regular succession. That yoga, O destroyer of foes, is now lost due to a long lapse of time.","er":"Thus handed down in succession, the royal sages knew this (Karma Yoga). But with a long lapse of time, O Arjuna, that Yoga was lost to the world.","gu":"આ રીતે પરંપરા દ્વારા રાજર્ષિઓ સુધી ઊતરી આવેલ આ યોગ જ્ઞાત હતો, પરંતુ, હે અર્જુન, બહુ કાળ વીતવાથી આ લોકમાં તે નષ્ટ થઈ ગયો."},{"ref":"4.3","ch":4,"v":3,"sa":"स एवायं मया तेऽद्य योगः प्रोक्तः पुरातनः।\nभक्तोऽसि मे सखा चेति रहस्यं ह्येतदुत्तमम्।।4.3।।","tr":"sa evāyaṁ mayā te ’dya yogaḥ proktaḥ purātanaḥ\nbhakto ’si me sakhā cheti rahasyaṁ hyetad uttamam","en":"That same ancient yoga has been today taught to you by me, for you are my devotee and my friend; it is the supreme secret.","es":"That ancient Yoga itself, which is this, has been taught to you by Me today, considering you to be My devotee and friend, for this Yoga is a profound secret.","er":"It is the same ancient Yoga that I am now teaching you, for you are My devotee and My friend. For, this is a supreme mystery.","gu":"તું મારો ભક્ત અને મિત્ર છે, તેથી આ જ પ્રાચીન અને ઉત્તમ ગુહ્ય યોગ આજે મેં તને ઉપદેશ્યો છે."},{"ref":"4.4","ch":4,"v":4,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nअपरं भवतो जन्म परं जन्म विवस्वतः।\nकथमेतद्विजानीयां त्वमादौ प्रोक्तवानिति।।4.4।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\naparaṁ bhavato janma paraṁ janma vivasvataḥ\nkatham etad vijānīyāṁ tvam ādau proktavān iti","en":"Arjuna said, \"Later was Thy birth, and prior to it was the birth of Vivasvan (the Sun); how am I to understand that Thou hast taught this Yoga from the beginning?\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"Your birth was later, whereas Vivasvan's birth was earlier. How am I to understand that You instructed him in the beginning?\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"Your birth was later, and Vivasvan's birth was earlier. How then can I understand that you taught it in the beginning?\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યો: વિવસ્વાનનો જન્મ તો ઘણો પ્રાચીન હતો, અને આપનો જન્મ પાછળથી થયો — તો પછી હું આ કેવી રીતે સમજું કે આપે સૃષ્ટિના આરંભે આ યોગ ઉપદેશ્યો?"},{"ref":"4.5","ch":4,"v":5,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nबहूनि मे व्यतीतानि जन्मानि तव चार्जुन।\nतान्यहं वेद सर्वाणि न त्वं वेत्थ परन्तप।।4.5।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nbahūni me vyatītāni janmāni tava chārjuna\ntānyahaṁ veda sarvāṇi na tvaṁ vettha parantapa","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"Many births of Mine have passed, as well as of thine, O Arjuna; I know them all, but thou knowest not, O Parantapa (scorcher of foes).\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O Arjuna, many lives of Mine have passed, and so have yours. I know them all, but you do not know, O scorcher of enemies!\"","er":"The Lord said, \"Many of My births have passed, O Arjuna, as have yours. I know them all, but you do not know them.\"","gu":"શ્રી કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે અર્જુન, મારા અને તારા અનેક જન્મો વીતી ગયા છે. એ સૌ હું જાણું છું, પરંતુ તું જાણતો નથી."},{"ref":"4.6","ch":4,"v":6,"sa":"अजोऽपि सन्नव्ययात्मा भूतानामीश्वरोऽपि सन्।\nप्रकृतिं स्वामधिष्ठाय संभवाम्यात्ममायया।।4.6।।","tr":"ajo ’pi sannavyayātmā bhūtānām īśhvaro ’pi san\nprakṛitiṁ svām adhiṣhṭhāya sambhavāmyātma-māyayā","en":"Though I am unborn and of imperishable nature, and though I am the Lord of all beings, yet, governing my own nature, I am born by my own Maya.","es":"Though I am birthless and undecaying by nature, and the Lord of beings, yet by subjugating My Prakriti, I take birth through My own Maya.","er":"Though I am birthless and of immutable nature, and the Lord of all beings, yet by employing My own Nature (Prakrti), I am born out of My own free will.","gu":"હું જન્મ રહિત અને અવિનાશી સ્વભાવનો હોવા છતાં, સર્વ પ્રાણીઓનો ઈશ્વર હોવા છતાં, પોતાની પ્રકૃતિ પર અધિકાર રાખીને મારી માયા દ્વારા હું જગતમાં પ્રગટ થાઉં છું."},{"ref":"4.7","ch":4,"v":7,"sa":"यदा यदा हि धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति भारत।\nअभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदाऽऽत्मानं सृजाम्यहम्।।4.7।।","tr":"yadā yadā hi dharmasya glānir bhavati bhārata\nabhyutthānam adharmasya tadātmānaṁ sṛijāmyaham","en":"Whenever there is a decline of righteousness and an increase of unrighteousness, O Arjuna, then I manifest Myself.","es":"O scion of the Bharata dynasty, whenever there is a decline in virtue and an increase in vice, then I manifest Myself.","er":"Whenever there is a decline of Dharma, O Arjuna, and an uprising of Adharma, then I incarnate myself."},{"ref":"4.8","ch":4,"v":8,"sa":"परित्राणाय साधूनां विनाशाय च दुष्कृताम्।\nधर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय संभवामि युगे युगे।।4.8।।","tr":"paritrāṇāya sādhūnāṁ vināśhāya cha duṣhkṛitām\ndharma-sansthāpanārthāya sambhavāmi yuge yuge","en":"For the protection of the good, for the destruction of the wicked, and for the establishment of righteousness, I am born in every age.","es":"For the protection of the pious, the destruction of the evil-doers, and the establishment of virtue, I manifest myself in every age.","er":"For the protection of the good and the destruction of the wicked, for the establishment of Dharma, I am born from age to age."},{"ref":"4.9","ch":4,"v":9,"sa":"जन्म कर्म च मे दिव्यमेवं यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः।\nत्यक्त्वा देहं पुनर्जन्म नैति मामेति सोऽर्जुन।।4.9।।","tr":"janma karma cha me divyam evaṁ yo vetti tattvataḥ\ntyaktvā dehaṁ punar janma naiti mām eti so ’rjuna","en":"He who thus knows, in their true light, My divine birth and actions, having abandoned the body, is not born again; he comes to Me, O Arjuna.","es":"He who thus knows truly the divine birth and actions of Mine does not get rebirth after casting off the body. He attains Me, O Arjuna.","er":"He who thus knows in truth My divine birth and actions does not get rebirth after leaving the body; he will come to Me, O Arjuna.","gu":"જે માણસ મારા દિવ્ય જન્મ અને કર્મોને તત્ત્વથી જાણી લે છે, તે શરીર છોડ્યા પછી ફરી જન્મ પામતો નથી, પણ સીધો મને જ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે, હે અર્જુન."},{"ref":"4.10","ch":4,"v":10,"sa":"वीतरागभयक्रोधा मन्मया मामुपाश्रिताः।\nबहवो ज्ञानतपसा पूता मद्भावमागताः।।4.10।।","tr":"vīta-rāga-bhaya-krodhā man-mayā mām upāśhritāḥ\nbahavo jñāna-tapasā pūtā mad-bhāvam āgatāḥ","en":"Freed from attachment, fear, and anger, absorbed in Me, taking refuge in Me, purified by the fire of knowledge, many have attained My Being.","es":"Many who were devoid of attachment, fear, and anger, who were absorbed in Me, who had taken refuge in Me, and were purified by the austerity of knowledge, have attained My state.","er":"Freed from desire, fear, and wrath, absorbed in Me, depending upon Me, purified by the austerity of knowledge, many have attained My state.","gu":"આસક્તિ, ભય અને ક્રોધ છોડીને, મારામાં ચિત્ત સ્થિર કરીને, મારી શરણ લઈ, જ્ઞાનની અગ્નિથી પવિત્ર થઈ, ઘણા ભક્તો મારા સ્વરૂપને પામ્યા છે."},{"ref":"4.11","ch":4,"v":11,"sa":"ये यथा मां प्रपद्यन्ते तांस्तथैव भजाम्यहम्।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः।।4.11।।","tr":"ye yathā māṁ prapadyante tāns tathaiva bhajāmyaham\nmama vartmānuvartante manuṣhyāḥ pārtha sarvaśhaḥ","en":"In whatever way men approach Me, even so do I reward them; My path do men tread in all ways, O Arjuna.","es":"According to the manner in which they approach Me, I favor them in that same manner. O son of Partha, humans follow My path in every way.","er":"Whoever resorts to Me in any manner, I favor them in the same manner; men experience Me alone in different ways, O Arjuna.","gu":"જે જે ભાવથી લોકો મને ભજે છે, તે તે ભાવથી હું તેમને ફળ આપું છું; હે અર્જુન, બધી બાજુઓથી લોકો મારા જ માર્ગને અનુસરે છે."},{"ref":"4.12","ch":4,"v":12,"sa":"काङ्क्षन्तः कर्मणां सिद्धिं यजन्त इह देवताः।\nक्षिप्रं हि मानुषे लोके सिद्धिर्भवति कर्मजा।।4.12।।","tr":"kāṅkṣhantaḥ karmaṇāṁ siddhiṁ yajanta iha devatāḥ\nkṣhipraṁ hi mānuṣhe loke siddhir bhavati karmajā","en":"Those who long for success in action in this world sacrifice to the gods; for success is quickly attained by men through action.","es":"Longing for the fruition of their actions (of their rites and duties), they worship the gods here. For, in the human world, success from action comes quickly.","er":"Those who desire the fruits of their ritualistic acts, sacrifice to the gods here; for, success quickly accrues in the world of men.","gu":"આ લોકમાં કર્મોની સફળતા ઇચ્છનારા લોકો દેવોની પૂજા કરે છે, કારણ કે કર્મ દ્વારા મનુષ્યને ત્વરિત સફળતા મળે છે."},{"ref":"4.13","ch":4,"v":13,"sa":"चातुर्वर्ण्यं मया सृष्टं गुणकर्मविभागशः।\nतस्य कर्तारमपि मां विद्ध्यकर्तारमव्ययम्।।4.13।।","tr":"chātur-varṇyaṁ mayā sṛiṣhṭaṁ guṇa-karma-vibhāgaśhaḥ\ntasya kartāram api māṁ viddhyakartāram avyayam","en":"The fourfold caste has been created by Me according to the differentiation of Guna and Karma; though I am the author of it, know Me as non-doer and immutable.","es":"The four castes have been created by Me through a classification of the gunas and duties. Even though I am the agent of that (act of classification), still know Me to be non-agentive and changeless.","er":"The system of four stations was created by Me, according to the distinction of Gunas and Karma. Though I am their creator, know Me to be non-agent and immutable.","gu":"ગુણ અને કર્મના ભેદ અનુસાર ચાર વર્ણ મેં સર્જ્યા છે; તેનો સ્રષ્ટા હોવા છતાં, મને અકર્તા અને અવિકારી જ સમજ."},{"ref":"4.14","ch":4,"v":14,"sa":"न मां कर्माणि लिम्पन्ति न मे कर्मफले स्पृहा।\nइति मां योऽभिजानाति कर्मभिर्न स बध्यते।।4.14।।","tr":"na māṁ karmāṇi limpanti na me karma-phale spṛihā\niti māṁ yo ’bhijānāti karmabhir na sa badhyate","en":"Actions do not taint Me, nor do I have a desire for the fruit of actions. He who knows Me thus is not bound by actions.","es":"Actions do not taint Me; for I have no hankering for the results of actions. One who knows Me thus, does not become bound by their actions.","er":"Works cannot contaminate Me. There is no desire for the fruits of actions in Me. He who understands this is not bound by actions.","gu":"કર્મો મને લેપતા નથી, ફળ ભોગવવાની ઇચ્છા પણ મને નથી. જે મને આ પ્રકારે ઓળખે છે, તે કર્મ-બંધનથી મુક્ત રહે છે."},{"ref":"4.15","ch":4,"v":15,"sa":"एवं ज्ञात्वा कृतं कर्म पूर्वैरपि मुमुक्षुभिः।\nकुरु कर्मैव तस्मात्त्वं पूर्वैः पूर्वतरं कृतम्।।4.15।।","tr":"evaṁ jñātvā kṛitaṁ karma pūrvair api mumukṣhubhiḥ\nkuru karmaiva tasmāttvaṁ pūrvaiḥ pūrvataraṁ kṛitam","en":"Having known this, the ancient seekers of freedom also performed action; therefore, do thou also perform action, as the ancients did in days of yore.","es":"Thus having known, even the ancient seekers of liberation performed their duties. Therefore, you should undertake action as was performed earlier by the ancients.","er":"Knowing thus, even ancient seekers of liberation did their work. Therefore, do your work only as the ancients did in olden times.","gu":"આ સત્ય જાણીને પ્રાચીન મુમુક્ષુઓ પણ કર્મ કરતા હતા; તેથી તું પણ પૂર્વજોએ કર્યું હતું તેમ, કર્મ કર."},{"ref":"4.16","ch":4,"v":16,"sa":"किं कर्म किमकर्मेति कवयोऽप्यत्र मोहिताः।\nतत्ते कर्म प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात्।।4.16।।","tr":"kiṁ karma kim akarmeti kavayo ’pyatra mohitāḥ\ntat te karma pravakṣhyāmi yaj jñātvā mokṣhyase ’śhubhāt","en":"What is action? What is inaction? Even the wise are confused about this. Therefore, I shall teach you the nature of action and inaction, by knowing which you will be liberated from the evil of Samsara, the wheel of birth and death.","es":"Even the intelligent are confounded as to what is action and what is inaction. I shall tell you of that action, knowing which you will become free from evil.","er":"What is action? What is non-action? Even the wise are puzzled in respect of these. I shall declare to you that kind of action, knowing which you will be freed from evil.","gu":"કર્મ શું છે અને અકર્મ શું છે, એ જ્ઞાની પુરુષો પણ મૂઢ બની જાય છે. હું તને કર્મ અને અકર્મ બંનેનું સ્વરૂપ સમજાવીશ, જે જાણ્યા પછી તું સંસારના બંધનમાંથી મુક્ત થઈ જઈશ."},{"ref":"4.17","ch":4,"v":17,"sa":"कर्मणो ह्यपि बोद्धव्यं बोद्धव्यं च विकर्मणः।\nअकर्मणश्च बोद्धव्यं गहना कर्मणो गतिः।।4.17।।","tr":"karmaṇo hyapi boddhavyaṁ boddhavyaṁ cha vikarmaṇaḥ\nakarmaṇaśh cha boddhavyaṁ gahanā karmaṇo gatiḥ","en":"For verily, the true nature of action enjoined by the scriptures should be known, as well as that of forbidden or unlawful action, and of inaction; the nature of action is hard to understand.","es":"For there is something to be known even about action, and something to be known about prohibited action; and something needs to be known about inaction. The true nature of action is inscrutable.","er":"For, there is what ought to be known in action; likewise, there is what ought to be known in multi-form action; and there is what ought to be understood in non-action. Thus, mysterious is the way of action.","gu":"કર્મ, વિકર્મ અને અકર્મ — ત્રણેનું સ્વરૂપ જાણવું આવશ્યક છે; કર્મની ગતિ ઘણી ગહન અને ગૂઢ છે."},{"ref":"4.18","ch":4,"v":18,"sa":"कर्मण्यकर्म यः पश्येदकर्मणि च कर्म यः।\nस बुद्धिमान् मनुष्येषु स युक्तः कृत्स्नकर्मकृत्।।4.18।।","tr":"karmaṇyakarma yaḥ paśhyed akarmaṇi cha karma yaḥ\nsa buddhimān manuṣhyeṣhu sa yuktaḥ kṛitsna-karma-kṛit","en":"He who sees inaction in action and action in inaction, he is wise among men; he is a yogi and performer of all actions.","es":"He who finds inaction in action, and action in inaction, is the wise one [possessed of the knowledge of Brahman] among men; they are engaged in yoga and are performers of all actions!","er":"He who sees inaction in action and also action in inaction is wise among men. He is fit for release and has accomplished all actions."},{"ref":"4.19","ch":4,"v":19,"sa":"यस्य सर्वे समारम्भाः कामसङ्कल्पवर्जिताः।\nज्ञानाग्निदग्धकर्माणं तमाहुः पण्डितं बुधाः।।4.19।।","tr":"yasya sarve samārambhāḥ kāma-saṅkalpa-varjitāḥ\njñānāgni-dagdha-karmāṇaṁ tam āhuḥ paṇḍitaṁ budhāḥ","en":"He whose undertakings are all devoid of desires and selfish purposes, and whose actions have been burned by the fire of knowledge, the wise call him a sage.","es":"The wise call him learned whose actions are all devoid of desires and their thoughts, and whose actions have been burned away by the fire of wisdom.","er":"He whose every undertaking is free from desire and delusive identification (of the body with the self), whose actions are burned up in the fire of knowledge—the wise describe him as a sage.","gu":"જેના સઘળા કાર્યો ઇચ્છા અને સ્વાર્થ-ભાવ વિના હોય, જેના કર્મો જ્ઞાનની અગ્નિ દ્વારા ભસ્મ થઈ ગયા હોય, જ્ઞાનીઓ તેને પંડિત કહે છે."},{"ref":"4.20","ch":4,"v":20,"sa":"त्यक्त्वा कर्मफलासङ्गं नित्यतृप्तो निराश्रयः।\nकर्मण्यभिप्रवृत्तोऽपि नैव किञ्चित्करोति सः।।4.20।।","tr":"tyaktvā karma-phalāsaṅgaṁ nitya-tṛipto nirāśhrayaḥ\nkarmaṇyabhipravṛitto ’pi naiva kiñchit karoti saḥ","en":"Having abandoned attachment to the fruits of the action, ever content, depending on nothing, he does not do anything even while being engaged in activity.","es":"Having given up attachment to the results of action, he who is ever-content, dependent on nothing, does not really do anything even though he is engaged in action.","er":"Having renounced attachment to the fruits of their actions, ever contented with the eternal self, and dependent on none, one does not act at all, even while being engaged in action.","gu":"ફળ પ્રત્યેની આસક્તિ છોડીને, સદૈવ સંતુષ્ટ, કોઈ પણ આધ્યા વગર, કર્મ કરતો હોવા છતાં, એ વ્યક્તિ કંઈ કરતો નથી."},{"ref":"4.21","ch":4,"v":21,"sa":"निराशीर्यतचित्तात्मा त्यक्तसर्वपरिग्रहः।\nशारीरं केवलं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम्।।4.21।।","tr":"nirāśhīr yata-chittātmā tyakta-sarva-parigrahaḥ\nśhārīraṁ kevalaṁ karma kurvan nāpnoti kilbiṣham","en":"Without hope, controlling the mind and the self, having abandoned all covetousness, and performing only bodily actions, one incurs no sin.","es":"One who is without solicitation, who has the mind and senses under control, and is totally without possessions, incurs no sin by performing actions merely for the maintenance of the body.","er":"Free from desire, his intellect and mind controlled, having given up all possessions, and doing bodily work only, he is not subject to evil.","gu":"ઇચ્છા રહિત, મન અને ઇન્દ્રિયોને વશ કરી, સઘળો સ્વાર્થ છોડી, માત્ર શરીર-નિર્વાહ માટે જ કર્મ કરનાર — કોઈ પણ પાપ પામતો નથી."},{"ref":"4.22","ch":4,"v":22,"sa":"यदृच्छालाभसन्तुष्टो द्वन्द्वातीतो विमत्सरः।\nसमः सिद्धावसिद्धौ च कृत्वापि न निबध्यते।।4.22।।","tr":"yadṛichchhā-lābha-santuṣhṭo dvandvātīto vimatsaraḥ\nsamaḥ siddhāvasiddhau cha kṛitvāpi na nibadhyate","en":"Content with what comes to him without effort, free from the pairs of opposites and envy, even-minded in success and failure, he acts yet is not bound.","es":"Remaining satisfied with what comes unasked for, having transcended the dualities, being free from spite, and balanced under success and failure, he is not bound even by performing actions.","er":"Content with what chance may bring, rising above the pairs of opposites, free from ill-will, even-minded in success and failure, he acts, yet is not bound.","gu":"જે યત્ન વિના પ્રાપ્ત થાય તેમાં સંતુષ્ટ, દ્વન્દ્વ અને ઈર્ષ્યાથી મુક્ત, સફળતા-નિષ્ફળતામાં સમ-ભાવ ધરાવનાર — એ વ્યક્તિ કર્મ કરતી હોવા છતાં બંધાતી નથી."},{"ref":"4.23","ch":4,"v":23,"sa":"गतसङ्गस्य मुक्तस्य ज्ञानावस्थितचेतसः।\nयज्ञायाचरतः कर्म समग्रं प्रविलीयते।।4.23।।","tr":"gata-saṅgasya muktasya jñānāvasthita-chetasaḥ\nyajñāyācharataḥ karma samagraṁ pravilīyate","en":"To one who is devoid of attachment, who is liberated, whose mind is established in knowledge, and who works for the sake of sacrifice (for the sake of God), the whole action is dissolved.","es":"The liberated person, who has rid themselves of attachment and whose mind is fixed in knowledge, has their actions undertaken for a sacrifice completely destroyed.","er":"One whose attachments have been relinquished, who is liberated, whose mind is established in knowledge, and who works only for sacrifices—their Karma is entirely dissolved.","gu":"જે આસક્તિથી મુક્ત છે, જ્ઞાનમાં સ્થિર છે અને બધાં કર્મ યજ્ઞ તરીકે કરે છે, તેનાં સઘળાં કર્મ વિલીન થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"4.24","ch":4,"v":24,"sa":"ब्रह्मार्पणं ब्रह्महविर्ब्रह्माग्नौ ब्रह्मणा हुतम्।\nब्रह्मैव तेन गन्तव्यं ब्रह्मकर्मसमाधिना।।4.24।।","tr":"brahmārpaṇaṁ brahma havir brahmāgnau brahmaṇā hutam\nbrahmaiva tena gantavyaṁ brahma-karma-samādhinā","en":"Brahman is the oblation; Brahman is the melted butter (ghee); by Brahman is the oblation poured into the fire of Brahman; Brahman indeed shall be attained by one who always sees Brahman in action.","es":"The ladle is Brahman, the oblations are Brahman, and the offering is poured by Brahman into the fire of Brahman. He who has concentration on Brahman as the objective can only reach Brahman.","er":"Brahman is the instrument with which to offer; Brahman is the oblation. By Brahman is the oblation offered into the fire of Brahman; Brahman alone is to be attained by one who meditates on Him in their works.","gu":"બ્રહ્મ જ અર્પણ કરવાનું પાત્ર છે, બ્રહ્મ જ આહુતિ છે, બ્રહ્મ જ બ્રહ્મ-અગ્નિમાં હોમ કરે છે; જે કર્મમાં બ્રહ્મનું ધ્યાન ધરે છે, તે બ્રહ્મને જ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"4.25","ch":4,"v":25,"sa":"दैवमेवापरे यज्ञं योगिनः पर्युपासते।\nब्रह्माग्नावपरे यज्ञं यज्ञेनैवोपजुह्वति।।4.25।।","tr":"daivam evāpare yajñaṁ yoginaḥ paryupāsate\nbrahmāgnāvapare yajñaṁ yajñenaivopajuhvati","en":"Some yogis perform sacrifice to the gods alone; while others, who have realized the Self, offer the Self as sacrifice in the fire of Brahman alone.","es":"Other yogis undertake sacrifice to gods alone, while others offer the Self as a sacrifice by themselves, in the fire of Brahman.","er":"Some yogis resort only to the sacrifice relating to gods; others offer sacrifice into the fire of Brahman solely through sacrifice.","gu":"કેટલાક યોગીઓ દેવતાઓને ઉદ્દેશીને યજ્ઞ કરે છે, જ્યારે બીજા બ્રહ્મ-અગ્નિમાં આત્માને જ આત્મા વડે આહુતિ આપે છે."},{"ref":"4.26","ch":4,"v":26,"sa":"श्रोत्रादीनीन्द्रियाण्यन्ये संयमाग्निषु जुह्वति।\nशब्दादीन्विषयानन्य इन्द्रियाग्निषु जुह्वति।।4.26।।","tr":"śhrotrādīnīndriyāṇyanye sanyamāgniṣhu juhvati\nśhabdādīn viṣhayānanya indriyāgniṣhu juhvati","en":"Some again offer the organ of hearing and other senses as a sacrifice in the fire of restraint; others offer sound and other objects of the senses as a sacrifice in the fire of the senses.","es":"Others offer their organs, such as their ears, etc., in the fires of self-control. Others offer the objects, such as sound, etc., in the fires of their organs.","er":"Others offer as oblations hearing and other senses into the fires of restraint. Some others offer as oblations the objects of the senses, such as sound and the rest, into the fires of their senses.","gu":"કેટલાક સાધકો શ્રવણ અને અન્ય ઇન્દ્રિયોને સંયમ-અગ્નિમાં હોમે છે, તો કેટલાક શ્દ-સ્પર્શ-રૂપ આદિ ઇન્દ્રિય-વિષયોને ઇન્દ્રિય-અગ્નિમાં હોમે છે."},{"ref":"4.27","ch":4,"v":27,"sa":"सर्वाणीन्द्रियकर्माणि प्राणकर्माणि चापरे।\nआत्मसंयमयोगाग्नौ जुह्वति ज्ञानदीपिते।।4.27।।","tr":"sarvāṇīndriya-karmāṇi prāṇa-karmāṇi chāpare\nātma-sanyama-yogāgnau juhvati jñāna-dīpite","en":"Others again sacrifice all the functions of the senses and those of the breath (vital energy, or Prana) in the fire of the Yoga of self-restraint, kindled by knowledge.","es":"Others offer all the activities of the organs and the activities of the vital force into the fire of the yoga of self-control, lit by Knowledge.","er":"Some again offer as an oblation the functions of the senses and the activity of the vital breaths into the fire of the Yoga of restraint of the mind, kindled by knowledge.","gu":"અન્ય યોગીઓ ઇન્દ્રિયોની સઘળી ક્રિયાઓ અને પ્રાણ-ક્રિયાઓને, જ્ઞાન-પ્રજ્વલિત આત્મ-સંયમ-યોગ-અગ્નિમાં આહુતિ આપે છે."},{"ref":"4.28","ch":4,"v":28,"sa":"द्रव्ययज्ञास्तपोयज्ञा योगयज्ञास्तथापरे।\nस्वाध्यायज्ञानयज्ञाश्च यतयः संशितव्रताः।।4.28।।","tr":"dravya-yajñās tapo-yajñā yoga-yajñās tathāpare\nswādhyāya-jñāna-yajñāśh cha yatayaḥ sanśhita-vratāḥ","en":"Others again offer wealth, austerity, and Yoga as sacrifice, while ascetics of self-restraint and rigid vows offer the study of scriptures and knowledge as sacrifice.","es":"Similarly, others are performers of sacrifices through wealth, through austerity, through yoga, and through study and knowledge; others are ascetics with severe vows.","er":"Self-controlled and firm of resolve, others perform the sacrifice of material objects or austerities or yoga; while others offer their scriptural study and knowledge.","gu":"કેટલાક સાધકો ધન-સ્વરૂપ ત્યાગ-યજ્ઞ કરે છે, કેટલાક તપ અથવા યોગ-યજ્ઞ અર્પે છે, અને કઠોર વ્રતધારી અન્ય સ્વાધ્યાય તથા જ્ઞાનને યજ્ઞ રૂપે ચઢાવે છે."},{"ref":"4.29","ch":4,"v":29,"sa":"अपाने जुह्वति प्राण प्राणेऽपानं तथाऽपरे।\nप्राणापानगती रुद्ध्वा प्राणायामपरायणाः।।4.29।।","tr":"apāne juhvati prāṇaṁ prāṇe ’pānaṁ tathāpare\nprāṇāpāna-gatī ruddhvā prāṇāyāma-parāyaṇāḥ\n apare niyatāhārāḥ prāṇān prāṇeṣhu juhvati\nsarve ’pyete yajña-vido yajña-kṣhapita-kalmaṣhāḥ","en":"Others offer as sacrifice the outgoing breath into the incoming, and the incoming into the outgoing, restraining the flow of the outgoing and the incoming breaths, solely absorbed in the restraint of the breath.","es":"Constantly practicing control of the vital forces by stopping the movements of the outgoing and incoming breaths, some offer as a sacrifice the outgoing breath into the incoming breath; while still others, the incoming breath into the outgoing breath.","er":"Others, with restricted diets, are devoted to the control of breath. Some sacrifice the inward breath in the outward breath; similarly, others sacrifice the outward breath in the inward breath. Some others, stopping the flow of both the inward and outward breaths, sacrifice the inward and outward breaths.","gu":"કેટલાક પ્રાણ-ક્રિયામાં નિષ્ઠ સાધકો બહારનો શ્વાસ ભીતરના શ્વાસમાં અને ભીતરનો બહારમાં હોમે છે, આ બંનેની ગતિ અટકાવી; અન્ય આહારને નિયંત્રિત કરી, પ્રાણોને પ્રાણોમાં જ અર્પે છે."},{"ref":"4.30","ch":4,"v":30,"sa":"अपरे नियताहाराः प्राणान्प्राणेषु जुह्वति।\nसर्वेऽप्येते यज्ञविदो यज्ञक्षपितकल्मषाः।।4.30।।","tr":"apare niyatāhārāḥ prāṇān prāṇeṣu juhvati\nsarve py 'ete yajña-vido yajña-kṣapita-kalmaṣāḥ","en":"Others who regulate their diet offer life-breaths in each life-breath. All these are knowers of sacrifice, whose sins are destroyed through sacrifice.","es":"Others, having their food regulated, offer the vital forces in the vital forces. All of them are knowers of the sacrifice and have their sins destroyed by the sacrifice.","er":"All these know the meaning of sacrifices, and through sacrifices, their sins are eradicated. Those who subsist on the ambrosial food, the remnants of sacrifices, go to eternal Brahman.","gu":"આ સઘળા યજ્ઞ-જ્ઞાતાઓ છે અને યજ્ઞ-ફળ વડે તેમના પાપ નષ્ટ થાય છે; જે યજ્ઞ-શેષ અમૃત-ભોજન કરે છે, તેઓ સનાતન બ્રહ્મને પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે."},{"ref":"4.31","ch":4,"v":31,"sa":"यज्ञशिष्टामृतभुजो यान्ति ब्रह्म सनातनम्।\nनायं लोकोऽस्त्ययज्ञस्य कुतो़ऽन्यः कुरुसत्तम।।4.31।।","tr":"yajña-śhiṣhṭāmṛita-bhujo yānti brahma sanātanam\nnāyaṁ loko ’styayajñasya kuto ’nyaḥ kuru-sattama","en":"Those who eat the remnants of the sacrifice, which are like nectar, go to the eternal Brahman. This world is not for the one who does not perform sacrifice; how then can they have the other, O Arjuna?","es":"Those who partake of the nectar left over after a sacrifice reach the eternal Brahman. This world ceases to exist for one who does not perform sacrifices; what, then, to speak of the other world, O best among the Kurus (Arjuna)!","er":"This world is not for one who makes no sacrifice; how then for the other, O Arjuna?","gu":"હે કુરુ-શ્રેષ્ઠ, જે યજ્ઞ નથી કરતા, તેઓ આ લોકમાં પણ ટકી શકતા નથી, તો પછી પરલોકમાં તેમને ક્યાંથી સ્થાન મળે?"},{"ref":"4.32","ch":4,"v":32,"sa":"एवं बहुविधा यज्ञा वितता ब्रह्मणो मुखे।\nकर्मजान्विद्धि तान्सर्वानेवं ज्ञात्वा विमोक्ष्यसे।।4.32।।","tr":"evaṁ bahu-vidhā yajñā vitatā brahmaṇo mukhe\nkarma-jān viddhi tān sarvān evaṁ jñātvā vimokṣhyase","en":"Thus, manifold sacrifices are spread out before Brahman at the face of Brahman. Know them all to be born of action, and thus knowing, you shall be liberated.","es":"Thus, various kinds of sacrifices are spread at the mouth of the Vedas. Know them all to be born of action. Knowing this, you will become liberated.","er":"Thus, many forms of sacrifices have been spread out as means of reaching Brahman (individual self in its own nature). Know that all of these are born of actions. Knowing thus, you will be free.","gu":"આ રીતે અનેક પ્રકારના યજ્ઞ બ્રહ્મ(વેદ)ના મુખ આગળ પ્રસારિત છે; જાણો કે એ સૌ કર્મ-ઉદ્ભવ છે, અને આ જ્ઞાન સમજ્યા પછી તું મુક્ત થઈ જઈશ."},{"ref":"4.33","ch":4,"v":33,"sa":"श्रेयान्द्रव्यमयाद्यज्ञाज्ज्ञानयज्ञः परन्तप।\nसर्वं कर्माखिलं पार्थ ज्ञाने परिसमाप्यते।।4.33।।","tr":"śhreyān dravya-mayād yajñāj jñāna-yajñaḥ parantapa\nsarvaṁ karmākhilaṁ pārtha jñāne parisamāpyate","en":"Superior is wisdom-sacrifice to the sacrifice with objects, O Parantapa (scorcher of the foes). All actions in their entirety, O Arjuna, culminate in knowledge.","es":"O destroyer of enemies, knowledge considered as a sacrifice is greater than sacrifices requiring materials. O son of Prtha, all actions in their totality culminate in knowledge.","er":"The sacrifice of knowledge is superior to material sacrifice. O Arjuna, all actions and everything else culminate in knowledge.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, દ્રવ્ય-યજ્ઞ કરતાં જ્ઞાન-યજ્ઞ ઘણો ઉત્કૃષ્ટ છે; કારણ કે સઘળાં કર્મ, સંપૂર્ણ રૂપે, આખરે જ્ઞાનમાં જ પૂર્ણ થાય છે."},{"ref":"4.34","ch":4,"v":34,"sa":"तद्विद्धि प्रणिपातेन परिप्रश्नेन सेवया।\nउपदेक्ष्यन्ति ते ज्ञानं ज्ञानिनस्तत्त्वदर्शिनः।।4.34।।","tr":"tad viddhi praṇipātena paripraśhnena sevayā\nupadekṣhyanti te jñānaṁ jñāninas tattva-darśhinaḥ","en":"Know that the wise who have realized the truth will instruct thee in that knowledge through long prostration, supplication, and service.","es":"Know that the wise ones who have realized the Truth will impart the Knowledge to you through prostration, inquiry, and service.","er":"Know this through prostration, questioning, and service. The wise who have realized the truth will instruct you in knowledge.","gu":"ઊંડા પ્રણામ, નિષ્ઠાવાન જિજ્ઞાસા અને નિઃસ્વાર્થ સેવા વડે જ્ઞાન મેળવ; જે તત્ત્વ-દ્રષ્ટા જ્ઞાની છે, તેઓ તને પ્રત્યક્ષ જ્ઞાન ઉઘાડી આપશે."},{"ref":"4.35","ch":4,"v":35,"sa":"यज्ज्ञात्वा न पुनर्मोहमेवं यास्यसि पाण्डव।\nयेन भूतान्यशेषेण द्रक्ष्यस्यात्मन्यथो मयि।।4.35।।","tr":"yaj jñātvā na punar moham evaṁ yāsyasi pāṇḍava\nyena bhūtānyaśheṣheṇa drakṣhyasyātmanyatho mayi","en":"Knowing that thou shalt not, O Arjuna, again be deluded like this; and by that thou shalt see all beings in thyself and also in me.","es":"Knowing this, O Pandava, you will not be deluded again in this way, and through it, you will see all beings, without exception, in the Self and also in Me.","er":"Knowing this, O Arjuna, you will not fall again into delusion in this way—by that knowledge, you will see all beings without exception in yourself and then in Me.","gu":"આ જ્ઞાન પ્રાપ્ત થતાં, હે અર્જુન, તું ફરી ક્યારેય મોહમાં ફસાઈશ નહિ; આ જ્ઞાન-દ્વારા તું સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓને પ્રથમ પોતાનામાં અને ત્યાર પછી મારામાં નિહાળઈ શઈ."},{"ref":"4.36","ch":4,"v":36,"sa":"अपि चेदसि पापेभ्यः सर्वेभ्यः पापकृत्तमः।\nसर्वं ज्ञानप्लवेनैव वृजिनं सन्तरिष्यसि।।4.36।।","tr":"api ched asi pāpebhyaḥ sarvebhyaḥ pāpa-kṛit-tamaḥ\nsarvaṁ jñāna-plavenaiva vṛijinaṁ santariṣhyasi","en":"Even if thou art the most sinful of all sinners, yet thou shalt surely cross over all sins by the raft of knowledge.","es":"Even if you are the worst sinner among all sinners, you can still cross over all wickedness with the raft of Knowledge alone.","er":"Even if you are the most sinful of all sinners, you can cross over all sins by the boat of knowledge alone.","gu":"જો તું સઘળા પાપીઓ કરતાં ઘોર પાપી હોય, તો પણ જ્ઞાનની નૌકા વડે તું સઘળા પાપ-સાગરને પાર ઊતરી જઈશ."},{"ref":"4.37","ch":4,"v":37,"sa":"यथैधांसि समिद्धोऽग्निर्भस्मसात्कुरुतेऽर्जुन।\nज्ञानाग्निः सर्वकर्माणि भस्मसात्कुरुते तथा।।4.37।।","tr":"yathaidhānsi samiddho ’gnir bhasma-sāt kurute ’rjuna\njñānāgniḥ sarva-karmāṇi bhasma-sāt kurute tathā","en":"As the blazing fire reduces fuel to ashes, O Arjuna, so does the fire of knowledge reduce all actions to ash.","es":"O Arjuna, just as a blazing fire reduces wood to ashes, similarly the fire of Knowledge reduces all actions to ashes.","er":"Just as a burning fire turns fuel to ashes, O Arjuna, so does the fire of knowledge turn all karmas to ashes.","gu":"જેમ સળગતો અગ્નિ ઇંધણને રાખ કરી નાખે છે, હે અર્જુન, તેમ જ્ઞાન-અગ્નિ સઘળાં કર્મોને ભસ્મ કરી નાખે છે."},{"ref":"4.38","ch":4,"v":38,"sa":"न हि ज्ञानेन सदृशं पवित्रमिह विद्यते।\nतत्स्वयं योगसंसिद्धः कालेनात्मनि विन्दति।।4.38।।","tr":"na hi jñānena sadṛiśhaṁ pavitramiha vidyate\ntatsvayaṁ yogasansiddhaḥ kālenātmani vindati","en":"Verily, there is no purifier in this world like knowledge. He who is perfected in Yoga finds it within the Self in due time.","es":"Indeed, there is nothing purifying here comparable to Knowledge. One who has become perfected over time through yoga, realizes That in their own heart.","er":"For there is no purifier equal to knowledge; he who is perfected in Karma Yoga finds this knowledge of his own accord in himself in due time."},{"ref":"4.39","ch":4,"v":39,"sa":"श्रद्धावाँल्लभते ज्ञानं तत्परः संयतेन्द्रियः।\nज्ञानं लब्ध्वा परां शान्तिमचिरेणाधिगच्छति।।4.39।।","tr":"śhraddhāvān labhate jñānaṁ tat-paraḥ sanyatendriyaḥ\njñānaṁ labdhvā parāṁ śhāntim achireṇādhigachchhati","en":"The one who is full of faith, devoted to it, and has subdued their senses obtains this knowledge; and upon obtaining the knowledge, they attain the supreme peace immediately.","es":"The one who has faith, is diligent, and has control over their organs, attains Knowledge. Achieving Knowledge, one soon attains supreme Peace.","er":"He who has faith, is intent on it, and has mastered his senses, attains knowledge. Having attained knowledge, he quickly goes to supreme peace."},{"ref":"4.40","ch":4,"v":40,"sa":"अज्ञश्चाश्रद्दधानश्च संशयात्मा विनश्यति।\nनायं लोकोऽस्ति न परो न सुखं संशयात्मनः।।4.40।।","tr":"ajñaśh chāśhraddadhānaśh cha sanśhayātmā vinaśhyati\nnāyaṁ loko ’sti na paro na sukhaṁ sanśhayātmanaḥ","en":"The ignorant, the faithless, and the doubting self go to destruction; there is neither this world nor the other, nor happiness for the doubting one.","es":"One who is ignorant and faithless, and has a doubting mind, perishes. Neither this world nor the next, nor happiness, exists for one who has a doubting mind.","er":"The ignorant, the faithless, and the doubting one perish; for the doubting one, there is neither this world nor the one beyond, nor happiness.","gu":"જે મનુષ્ય અજ્ઞાની, શ્રદ્ધારહિત અને સંશયયુક્ત છે, તે નષ્ટ થઈ જાય છે; સંશયાત્માને આ લોક, પરલોક કે સુખ — કશું પ્રાપ્ત થતું નથી."},{"ref":"4.41","ch":4,"v":41,"sa":"योगसंन्यस्तकर्माणं ज्ञानसंछिन्नसंशयम्।\nआत्मवन्तं न कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय।।4.41।।","tr":"yoga-sannyasta-karmāṇaṁ jñāna-sañchhinna-sanśhayam\nātmavantaṁ na karmāṇi nibadhnanti dhanañjaya","en":"He who has renounced actions through Yoga, whose doubts have been dispelled by knowledge, and who is self-possessed—such a one is not bound by actions, O Arjuna.","es":"O Dhananjaya (Arjuna), actions do not bind one who has renounced actions through yoga, whose doubts have been fully dispelled by Knowledge, and who is not inattentive.","er":"Actions do not bind him, O Arjuna, who has renounced them through Karma Yoga and whose doubts have been dispelled by knowledge, and who thus possesses a steady mind.","gu":"હે ધનઞ્જય઼, યોગે કર્મ ત્યાગ કરે, જ્ઞાને સંશય઼ છેદ કરે, આત્મબાન - કર્મે બદ્ધ નય઼।"},{"ref":"4.42","ch":4,"v":42,"sa":"तस्मादज्ञानसंभूतं हृत्स्थं ज्ञानासिनाऽऽत्मनः।\nछित्त्वैनं संशयं योगमातिष्ठोत्तिष्ठ भारत।।4.42।।","tr":"tasmād ajñāna-sambhūtaṁ hṛit-sthaṁ jñānāsinātmanaḥ\nchhittvainaṁ sanśhayaṁ yogam ātiṣhṭhottiṣhṭha bhārata","en":"Therefore, with the sword of knowledge (of the Self), cut asunder the doubt of the self, born of ignorance, residing in your heart, and take refuge in Yoga. Arise, O Arjuna!","es":"Therefore, O scion of the Bharata dynasty, take recourse to yoga and rise up, cutting asunder with the sword of knowledge this doubt in your heart, arising from ignorance.","er":"Therefore, sever, with the sword of knowledge, this doubt present in your heart resulting from ignorance concerning the Self. Practice this Yoga, O Arjuna, and arise.","gu":"તાઇ અજ્ઞાન થેકે જન્મ એઇ હૃદય઼સ્થ સંશય઼ જ્ઞાન-ખડ઼્ગે છેદ કરો। યોગે ઉઠો, હે ભારત।"},{"ref":"5.1","ch":5,"v":1,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nसंन्यासं कर्मणां कृष्ण पुनर्योगं च शंससि।\nयच्छ्रेय एतयोरेकं तन्मे ब्रूहि सुनिश्िचतम्।।5.1।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nsannyāsaṁ karmaṇāṁ kṛiṣhṇa punar yogaṁ cha śhansasi\nyach chhreya etayor ekaṁ tan me brūhi su-niśhchitam","en":"Arjuna said, \"O Krishna, you praise renunciation of actions and also yoga. Please tell me conclusively which is better of the two.\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Krsna, you praise renunciation of actions and, at the same time, Karma-yoga. Please tell me for certain which one is better between these two.\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"O Krsna, you praise the renunciation of actions, and then you also praise Karma Yoga. Please tell me with certainty which of these is the superior one, leading to the ultimate good.","gu":"અર્જુને કહ્યું: હે કૃષ્ણ, આપ કર્મોના સંન્યાસ અને કર્મયોગ — બંનેની પ્રશંસા કરો છો; તો આ બેમાંથી કયું ચઢિયાતું છે તે મને નિશ્ચિતપણે કહો."},{"ref":"5.2","ch":5,"v":2,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nसंन्यासः कर्मयोगश्च निःश्रेयसकरावुभौ।\nतयोस्तु कर्मसंन्यासात्कर्मयोगो विशिष्यते।।5.2।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nsannyāsaḥ karma-yogaśh cha niḥśhreyasa-karāvubhau\ntayos tu karma-sannyāsāt karma-yogo viśhiṣhyate","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"Renunciation and the Yoga of action both lead to the highest bliss; but of the two, the Yoga of action is superior to the renunciation of action.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"Both renunciation of actions and Karma-yoga lead to liberation; however, Karma-yoga excels over renunciation of actions.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"Renunciation of actions and Karma Yoga both lead to the highest excellence; however, of the two, Karma Yoga surpasses renunciation of actions.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: સંન્યાસ અને કર્મયોગ — બંને પરમ કલ્યાણ આપનારા છે, પરંતુ તે બેમાં સંન્યાસ કરતાં કર્મયોગ શ્રેષ્ઠ છે."},{"ref":"5.3","ch":5,"v":3,"sa":"ज्ञेयः स नित्यसंन्यासी यो न द्वेष्टि न काङ्क्षति।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो हि महाबाहो सुखं बन्धात्प्रमुच्यते।।5.3।।","tr":"jñeyaḥ sa nitya-sannyāsī yo na dveṣhṭi na kāṅkṣhati\nnirdvandvo hi mahā-bāho sukhaṁ bandhāt pramuchyate","en":"He should be known as a perpetual Sannyasi who neither hates nor desires; for, free from the pairs of opposites, O mighty-armed Arjuna, he is easily freed from bondage.","es":"He who neither hates nor craves should be known as a man of constant renunciation.","er":"He who neither hates nor desires, and is beyond the pairs of opposites, is to be understood as an ever-renouncer. Therefore, he is easily set free from bondage, O Arjuna.","gu":"જે પુરુષ ન કોઈ વસ્તુ ઇચ્છે છે, ન કોઈ પ્રત્યે દ્વેષ રાખે છે, તેને નિત્ય સંન્યાસી જાણવો; હે મહાબાહો, દ્વન્દ્વોથી મુક્ત એ પ્રાણી સહેલાઈથી બંધનમાંથી મુક્ત થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"5.4","ch":5,"v":4,"sa":"सांख्ययोगौ पृथग्बालाः प्रवदन्ति न पण्डिताः।\nएकमप्यास्थितः सम्यगुभयोर्विन्दते फलम्।।5.4।।","tr":"sānkhya-yogau pṛithag bālāḥ pravadanti na paṇḍitāḥ\nekamapyāsthitaḥ samyag ubhayor vindate phalam","en":"Children, not the wise, speak of knowledge and the Yoga of action, or the performance of action, as though they are distinct and different; he who is truly established in one, obtains the fruits of both.","es":"The fools, not the learned ones, speak of Sankhya and (Karma-) yoga as being different. Anyone who properly resorts to either one of them gets the results of both.","er":"Children, not the learned, speak of Sankhya and Yoga as distinct; however, he who is firmly set in one, attains the fruit of both.","gu":"સાંખ્ય અને યોગ જુદા છે — આ વાત બાળ-બુદ્ધિના લોકો કહે છે, જ્ઞાનીઓ નહીં; બેમાંથી કોઈ એકમાં સ્થિર રહેલ સાધક બંનેનું ફળ મેળવે છે."},{"ref":"5.5","ch":5,"v":5,"sa":"यत्सांख्यैः प्राप्यते स्थानं तद्योगैरपि गम्यते।\nएकं सांख्यं च योगं च यः पश्यति स पश्यति।।5.5।।","tr":"yat sānkhyaiḥ prāpyate sthānaṁ tad yogair api gamyate\nekaṁ sānkhyaṁ cha yogaṁ cha yaḥ paśhyati sa paśhyati","en":"That place which is reached by the Sankhyas or the Jnanis is also reached by the Yogis (Karma Yogis). He who sees knowledge and the performance of action (Karma Yoga) as one, sees truly.","es":"The state that is reached by the Sankhyas, and that is also reached by the yogis, is seen by one who sees Sankhya and yoga as one.","er":"That state which is reached by the Sankhyans, the same is also attained by the Yogins; that is, the same state is achieved by those who are Karma Yogins. He alone is wise who perceives that the Sankhya and the Yoga are one and the same, due to their having the same result.","gu":"સાંખ્યયોગીઓ જે સ્થાન પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે, તે જ કર્મયોગીઓ પણ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે; જે ખરેખર જુએ છે, તે સાંખ્ય અને યોગને એક જ જુએ છે."},{"ref":"5.6","ch":5,"v":6,"sa":"संन्यासस्तु महाबाहो दुःखमाप्तुमयोगतः।\nयोगयुक्तो मुनिर्ब्रह्म नचिरेणाधिगच्छति।।5.6।।","tr":"sannyāsas tu mahā-bāho duḥkham āptum ayogataḥ\nyoga-yukto munir brahma na chireṇādhigachchhati","en":"But, O mighty-armed Arjuna, renunciation is hard to attain without Yoga; the sage who is in harmony with Yoga quickly goes to Brahman.","es":"But, O mighty-armed one, renunciation is hard to attain without (Karma-) yoga. The meditative man equipped with yoga attains Brahman without delay.","er":"But, O mighty-armed one, renunciation is hard to attain without practicing Yoga. The sage who contemplates and follows Yoga soon reaches the Brahman (the self or Atman).","gu":"પરંતુ, હે મહાબાહો, કર્મયોગ વિના સંન્યાસ પ્રાપ્ત કરવો કઠિન છે; કર્મયોગ-સંપન્ન મુનિ શીઘ્રપણે બ્રહ્મને પ્રાપ્ત થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"5.7","ch":5,"v":7,"sa":"योगयुक्तो विशुद्धात्मा विजितात्मा जितेन्द्रियः।\nसर्वभूतात्मभूतात्मा कुर्वन्नपि न लिप्यते।।5.7।।","tr":"yoga-yukto viśhuddhātmā vijitātmā jitendriyaḥ\nsarva-bhūtātma-bhūtātmā kurvann api na lipyate","en":"He who is devoted to the path of action, whose mind is pure, who has conquered the self, who has subdued his senses, and who realizes his Self as the Self in all beings, though acting, is not tainted.","es":"Endowed with yoga, pure in mind, controlled in body, a conqueror of the organs, the Self of the selves of all beings—he does not become tainted even while performing actions. When this person resorts to nitya and naimittika rites and duties as a means to the achievement of full illumination, and thus becomes fully enlightened, then, even when he acts through the apparent functions of the mind, organs, etc., he does not become affected.","er":"He who follows the Yoga and is pure in mind, who has subdued his self and has conquered his senses, and whose self has become the self of all beings, even while he is acting, remains untainted.","gu":"જે પ્રાણી કર્મયોગમાં અનુરક્ત છે, જેનું મન શુદ્ધ છે, જે સ્વ-સંયમી છે, ઇન્દ્રિયો ઉપર જેણે વિજય મેળવ્યો છે, અને સર્વ ભૂતોનો આત્મા જ જેનો આત્મા બન્યો છે — તે કર્મ કરતાં છતાં ક્યારેય લિપ્ત થતા નથી."},{"ref":"5.8","ch":5,"v":8,"sa":"नैव किंचित्करोमीति युक्तो मन्येत तत्त्ववित्।\nपश्यन् श्रृणवन्स्पृशञ्जिघ्रन्नश्नन्गच्छन्स्वपन् श्वसन्।।5.8।।","tr":"naiva kiñchit karomīti yukto manyeta tattva-vit\npaśhyañ śhṛiṇvan spṛiśhañjighrann aśhnangachchhan svapañśhvasan\n pralapan visṛijan gṛihṇann unmiṣhan nimiṣhann api\nindriyāṇīndriyārtheṣhu vartanta iti dhārayan","en":"I do nothing at all,\" thus would the harmonized knower of Truth think, seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, going, sleeping, and breathing.","es":"- Remaining absorbed in the Self, the knower of Reality should think, 'I certainly do not do anything', even while seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, moving, sleeping, breathing, speaking, releasing, holding, opening, and closing the eyes—remembering that the organs function in relation to the objects of the organs.","er":"The one who knows the truth and is devoted to yoga should think, \"I am not doing anything,\" even though they are seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, moving, sleeping, and breathing.","gu":"સત્યમાં સ્થિત, તત્ત્વ જાણનારો પુરુષ જોતાં, સાંભળતાં, સ્પર્શ કરતાં, સૂંઘતાં, ખાતાં, ચાલતાં, સૂતાં કે શ્વાસ લેતાં 'હું કંઈ જ કરતો નથી' — એ ભાવ રાખે છે."},{"ref":"5.9","ch":5,"v":9,"sa":"प्रलपन्विसृजन्गृह्णन्नुन्मिषन्निमिषन्नपि।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेषु वर्तन्त इति धारयन्।।5.9।।","tr":"pralapan visṛjan gṛhṇann unmiṣan nimiṣann api indriyāṇīndriyārtheṣu vartanta iti dhārayan","en":"Speaking, letting go, seizing, opening, and closing the eyes, one should be convinced that the senses move among the sense-objects.","es":"- Remaining absorbed in the Self, the knower of Reality should think, 'I certainly do not do anything', even while seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, moving, sleeping, breathing, speaking, releasing, holding, opening, and closing the eyes—remembering that the organs function in relation to the objects of the organs.","er":"Speaking, discharging, grasping, opening, and closing his eyes, etc., he should always bear in mind that the senses operate among sense-objects.","gu":"ઘુમાનો, શ્બાસ નેઓય઼ા, કથા બલા, ત્યાગ કરા, ધરા, ચોખ ખોલા ઓ બન્ધ કરા - ઇન્દ્રિય઼ બિષય઼ે ચલે મને કરેન।"},{"ref":"5.10","ch":5,"v":10,"sa":"ब्रह्मण्याधाय कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा करोति यः।\nलिप्यते न स पापेन पद्मपत्रमिवाम्भसा।।5.10।।","tr":"brahmaṇyādhāya karmāṇi saṅgaṁ tyaktvā karoti yaḥ\nlipyate na sa pāpena padma-patram ivāmbhasā","en":"He who does actions, offering them to Brahman and abandoning attachment, is not tainted by sin, just as a lotus leaf is not tainted by water.","es":"One who acts by dedicating their actions to Brahman and by renouncing attachment, they do not become polluted by sin, just as a lotus leaf is not by water.","er":"He who acts without attachment, reposing all actions on Brahman (Prakṛti), is untouched by evil, just as a lotus leaf is untouched by water.","gu":"જે પ્રાણી સઘળાં કર્મો બ્રહ્મને અર્પણ કરી, આસક્તિ છોડીને કાર્ય કરે છે, તે પાપ વડે તેવો જ અસ્પૃષ્ટ રહે છે, જેવી રીતે જળ કમળના પત્રને ભીનું કરી શક્તું નથી."},{"ref":"5.11","ch":5,"v":11,"sa":"कायेन मनसा बुद्ध्या केवलैरिन्द्रियैरपि।\nयोगिनः कर्म कुर्वन्ति सङ्गं त्यक्त्वाऽऽत्मशुद्धये।।5.11।।","tr":"kāyena manasā buddhyā kevalair indriyair api\nyoginaḥ karma kurvanti saṅgaṁ tyaktvātma-śhuddhaye","en":"Yogis, having abandoned attachment, perform actions only through the body, mind, intellect, and even the senses, for the purification of the self.","es":"By giving up attachment, the yogis undertake work solely through the body, mind, intellect, and even the organs, for their own purification.","er":"Yogins, renouncing attachment, do actions with merely the body, mind, intellect, and senses, for the purification of the self.","gu":"કર્મયોગીઓ શરીર, મન, બુદ્ધિ અને ઇન્દ્રિયો વડે — આસક્તિ ત્યજીને — માત્ર આત્મ-શુદ્ધિ માટે જ કર્મ કરે છે."},{"ref":"5.12","ch":5,"v":12,"sa":"युक्तः कर्मफलं त्यक्त्वा शान्तिमाप्नोति नैष्ठिकीम्।\nअयुक्तः कामकारेण फले सक्तो निबध्यते।।5.12।।","tr":"yuktaḥ karma-phalaṁ tyaktvā śhāntim āpnoti naiṣhṭhikīm\nayuktaḥ kāma-kāreṇa phale sakto nibadhyate","en":"The one who is united (the well-poised or harmonized) having abandoned the fruit of action attains eternal peace; whereas the one who is not united (the unsteady or unbalanced), impelled by desire and attached to the fruit, is bound.","es":"Giving up the results of work by becoming resolute in faith, one attains peace arising from steadfastness. One who is lacking in resolute faith, being attached to the results under the impulse of desire, becomes bound.","er":"A yogi, renouncing the fruits of their actions, attains lasting peace. But the unsteady person who is attached to the fruits of their actions, being driven by desire, is bound.","gu":"ભક્તિભાવે સ્થિર ચિત્ત ધરાવનાર સઘળાં કર્મોનાં ફળ ઇશ્વરને સોંપી, પૂર્ણ શાંતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે; પરંતુ જે ભક્તિ વિનાનો છે, ફળ પ્રત્યે આસક્ત છે, તે ઉલઝણમાં ફસાઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"5.13","ch":5,"v":13,"sa":"सर्वकर्माणि मनसा संन्यस्यास्ते सुखं वशी।\nनवद्वारे पुरे देही नैव कुर्वन्न कारयन्।।5.13।।","tr":"sarva-karmāṇi manasā sannyasyāste sukhaṁ vaśhī\nnava-dvāre pure dehī naiva kurvan na kārayan","en":"Mentally renouncing all actions and being self-controlled, the embodied one happily rests in the nine-gated city, neither acting nor causing others (body and senses) to act.","es":"The embodied man of self-control, having given up all actions mentally, continues happily in the city of nine gates, without doing or causing anyone else to do anything.","er":"The embodied self, mentally resigning all actions as belonging to the city of nine gates (i.e., the body) and becoming self-controlled, dwells happily, neither acting himself nor causing the body to act.","gu":"મનથી સઘળાં કર્મો ત્યજી, દેહધારી આત્મા નવ-દ્વારવાળા આ શરીરમાં — ન સ્વયં કાર્ય કરી, ન બીજા પાસે કરાવી — સ્વસ્થ ચિત્તે નિવાસ કરે છે."},{"ref":"5.14","ch":5,"v":14,"sa":"न कर्तृत्वं न कर्माणि लोकस्य सृजति प्रभुः।\nन कर्मफलसंयोगं स्वभावस्तु प्रवर्तते।।5.14।।","tr":"na kartṛitvaṁ na karmāṇi lokasya sṛijati prabhuḥ\nna karma-phala-saṅyogaṁ svabhāvas tu pravartate","en":"Neither does the Lord create agency nor actions for the world, nor union with the fruits of actions; rather, it is Nature that acts.","es":"The Self does not create agency or any objects of desire for anyone, nor does it associate with the results of actions; rather, it is Nature that acts.","er":"The Lord of the body (the Self, i.e., the Jiva) does not create agency, nor actions, nor union with the fruits of actions in relation to the world of selves; only the inherent tendencies function.","gu":"ભગવાન આ સૃષ્ટિમાં ન તો કર્તૃત્વ ઉત્પન્ન કરે છે, ન તો કર્મો, અને ન તો કર્મફળ સાથેનો સંયોગ — આ સઘળું પ્રકૃતિ દ્વારા જ થાય છે."},{"ref":"5.15","ch":5,"v":15,"sa":"नादत्ते कस्यचित्पापं न चैव सुकृतं विभुः।\nअज्ञानेनावृतं ज्ञानं तेन मुह्यन्ति जन्तवः।।5.15।।","tr":"nādatte kasyachit pāpaṁ na chaiva sukṛitaṁ vibhuḥ\najñānenāvṛitaṁ jñānaṁ tena muhyanti jantavaḥ","en":"The Lord takes neither the demerit nor the merit of any; knowledge is enveloped by ignorance, and beings are deluded.","es":"The Omnipresent neither accepts anyone's sin nor even virtue; knowledge remains covered by ignorance, thus the creatures become deluded.","er":"The all-pervasive One takes away neither the sin nor the merit of anyone. Knowledge is enveloped by ignorance, and creatures are thereby deluded.","gu":"સર્વવ્યાપી પરમાત્મા ન તો કોઈના પાપ ઝીલે છે, ન તો પુણ્ય; જ્ઞાન અજ્ઞાન વડે ઢંકાયેલું છે, અને તેના કારણે જ જીવો મોહ પામે છે."},{"ref":"5.16","ch":5,"v":16,"sa":"ज्ञानेन तु तदज्ञानं येषां नाशितमात्मनः।\nतेषामादित्यवज्ज्ञानं प्रकाशयति तत्परम्।।5.16।।","tr":"jñānena tu tad ajñānaṁ yeṣhāṁ nāśhitam ātmanaḥ\nteṣhām āditya-vaj jñānaṁ prakāśhayati tat param","en":"But to those whose ignorance is destroyed by knowledge of the Self, like the sun, knowledge reveals the Supreme Brahman.","es":"But in the case of those whose ignorance is destroyed by knowledge (of the Self), their knowledge, like the sun, reveals that supreme Reality.","er":"But for those in whom this ignorance is destroyed by the knowledge of the Self, that knowledge, in their case, is supreme and shines brightly like the sun.","gu":"પરંતુ જેમના અજ્ઞાનનો નાશ આત્મજ્ઞાન દ્વારા થાય છે, તેમને એ જ્ઞાન સૂર્યની જેમ પ્રકાશ આપી પરમ બ્રહ્મને પ્રગટ કરે છે."},{"ref":"5.17","ch":5,"v":17,"sa":"तद्बुद्धयस्तदात्मानस्तन्निष्ठास्तत्परायणाः।\nगच्छन्त्यपुनरावृत्तिं ज्ञाननिर्धूतकल्मषाः।।5.17।।","tr":"tad-buddhayas tad-ātmānas tan-niṣhṭhās tat-parāyaṇāḥ\ngachchhantyapunar-āvṛittiṁ jñāna-nirdhūta-kalmaṣhāḥ","en":"Their intellect absorbed in That, their self being That, established in That, with That as their supreme goal, they go whence there is no return, their sins dispelled by knowledge.","es":"Those whose intellect is absorbed in That, whose Self is That, who are steadfast in That, and who have That as their supreme Goal—they attain the state of non-returning, their impurities having been removed by Knowledge.","er":"Those whose intellects pursue it, whose minds think about it, who undergo discipline for it, and who hold it as their highest object, have their impurities cleansed by knowledge and go from whence there is no return.","gu":"જેમની બુદ્ધિ પ્રભુમય છે, જેઓ તેમનામાં જ સ્થિત છે, અને જેમણે પ્રભુને જ પોતાનું પરમ ધ્યેય બનાવ્યું છે — એ જ્ઞાન વડે પાપ ધોઈ, તેઓ એવા સ્થળે જાય છે જ્યાંથી પાછા ફરવાનું નથી."},{"ref":"5.18","ch":5,"v":18,"sa":"विद्याविनयसंपन्ने ब्राह्मणे गवि हस्तिनि।\nशुनि चैव श्वपाके च पण्डिताः समदर्शिनः।।5.18।।","tr":"vidyā-vinaya-sampanne brāhmaṇe gavi hastini\nśhuni chaiva śhva-pāke cha paṇḍitāḥ sama-darśhinaḥ","en":"Sages look with an equal eye on a Brahmana endowed with learning and humility, on a cow, an elephant, a dog, and even an outcaste.","es":"The learned ones look with equanimity on a Brahmana endowed with learning and humility, a cow, an elephant, and even a dog, as well as one who eats dog meat.","er":"The sages look with an equal eye on one endowed with learning and humility, a Brahmana, a cow, an elephant, a dog, and a dog-eater.","gu":"જ્ઞાની પુરુષ વિદ્વાન અને વિનમ્ર બ્રાહ્મણ, ગાય, હાથી, કૂતરો અને ચાંડાળ — સૌને સમભાવથી નિહાળે છે."},{"ref":"5.19","ch":5,"v":19,"sa":"इहैव तैर्जितः सर्गो येषां साम्ये स्थितं मनः।\nनिर्दोषं हि समं ब्रह्म तस्माद्ब्रह्मणि ते स्थिताः।।5.19।।","tr":"ihaiva tair jitaḥ sargo yeṣhāṁ sāmye sthitaṁ manaḥ\nnirdoṣhaṁ hi samaṁ brahma tasmād brahmaṇi te sthitāḥ","en":"Even here in this world, those whose minds rest in reality overcome birth; Brahman is indeed spotless and real; therefore they are established in Brahman.","es":"Here itself is mirth attained by those whose minds are established in sameness. Since Brahman is the same in all and free from defects, they are established in Brahman.","er":"Here itself, those whose minds rest in equanimity overcome samsara. For the Brahman (individual self), when uncontaminated by Prakriti, is the same everywhere; therefore, they abide in Brahman.","gu":"જેમનું ચિત્ત સ્થિર સમભાવમાં રહે છે, તેઓ આ જ જીવનમાં જન્મ-મૃત્યુ જીતી લે છે; બ્રહ્મ નિર્દોષ અને સમ છે, તેથી તેઓ બ્રહ્મમાં સ્થિત ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"5.20","ch":5,"v":20,"sa":"न प्रहृष्येत्प्रियं प्राप्य नोद्विजेत्प्राप्य चाप्रियम्।\nस्थिरबुद्धिरसम्मूढो ब्रह्मविद्ब्रह्मणि स्थितः।।5.20।।","tr":"na prahṛiṣhyet priyaṁ prāpya nodvijet prāpya chāpriyam\nsthira-buddhir asammūḍho brahma-vid brahmaṇi sthitaḥ","en":"Resting in Brahman, with a steady intellect and undeluded, the knower of Brahman neither rejoices upon obtaining what is pleasant nor grieves upon obtaining what is unpleasant.","es":"A knower of Brahman, who is established in Brahman, should have their intellect steady and should not be deluded. They should not get delighted by getting what is desirable, nor become dejected by getting what is undesirable.","er":"He who knows Brahman (individual self) and abides in Brahman, whose mind is steadfastly focused on the self and undeluded by body consciousness—he neither rejoices at gaining what is pleasant nor grieves on obtaining what is unpleasant.","gu":"જે પ્રિય મળે ત્યારે હર્ષ ન પામે, અને અપ્રિય મળે ત્યારે દુઃખ ન અનુભવે, જે સ્થિર બુદ્ધિ અને અમૂઢ હોય — એ બ્રહ્મ-જ્ઞાની પુરુષ બ્રહ્મમાં સ્થાપિત છે."},{"ref":"5.21","ch":5,"v":21,"sa":"बाह्यस्पर्शेष्वसक्तात्मा विन्दत्यात्मनि यत्सुखम्।\nस ब्रह्मयोगयुक्तात्मा सुखमक्षयमश्नुते।।5.21।।","tr":"bāhya-sparśheṣhvasaktātmā vindatyātmani yat sukham\nsa brahma-yoga-yuktātmā sukham akṣhayam aśhnute","en":"With the self unattached to external contacts, he finds happiness in the Self; with the self engaged in the meditation of Brahman, he attains endless happiness.","es":"With his heart unattached to external objects, he gets the bliss that is in the Self. With his heart absorbed in meditation on Brahman, he acquires undying Bliss.","er":"He whose mind is detached from external contact and finds happiness in the Self—he has his mind engaged in the contemplation of Brahman and enjoys undecaying bliss.","gu":"જે આત્મા બાહ્ય વિષયોથી આસક્ત નથી, તે આત્મામાં જ સુખ અનુભવે છે; બ્રહ્મ સાથે એકરૂપ થયેલો આવો સાધક ચિરંતન આનંદ ભોગવે છે."},{"ref":"5.22","ch":5,"v":22,"sa":"ये हि संस्पर्शजा भोगा दुःखयोनय एव ते।\nआद्यन्तवन्तः कौन्तेय न तेषु रमते बुधः।।5.22।।","tr":"ye hi sansparśha-jā bhogā duḥkha-yonaya eva te\nādyantavantaḥ kaunteya na teṣhu ramate budhaḥ","en":"The enjoyments that arise from contact are only sources of pain, for they have a beginning and an end, O Arjuna; the wise do not rejoice in them.","es":"Since enjoyments that result from contact with objects are indeed the sources of sorrow, having a beginning and an end, O son of Kunti, the wise one does not delight in them.","er":"For those pleasures that are born of contact are wombs of pain. They have a beginning and an end, O Arjuna; the wise do not rejoice in them.","gu":"ઇન્દ્રિય-સ્પર્શથી ઉત્પન્ન ભોગ માત્ર દુઃખના ઉદ્ભવ-સ્થાન છે; હે અર્જુન, તેઓ આદિ અને અંત ધરાવે છે — જ્ઞાની જન એમાં આનંદ માનતા નથી."},{"ref":"5.23","ch":5,"v":23,"sa":"शक्नोतीहैव यः सोढुं प्राक्शरीरविमोक्षणात्।\nकामक्रोधोद्भवं वेगं स युक्तः स सुखी नरः।।5.23।।","tr":"śhaknotīhaiva yaḥ soḍhuṁ prāk śharīra-vimokṣhaṇāt\nkāma-krodhodbhavaṁ vegaṁ sa yuktaḥ sa sukhī naraḥ","en":"He who is able, while still here in this world, to withstand the impulse born out of desire and anger before the liberation from the body, he is a Yogi, and he is a happy man.","es":"One who can withstand here itself, before departing from the body, the impulse arising from desire and anger, that person is a yogi; they are happy.","er":"He who is able, even here, before being released from the body, to bear the impulse generated by desire and anger, he is a Yogin (competent for self-realisation); he is the happy man.","gu":"જે મનુષ્ય શરીર છોડ્યા પહેલાં, ઇચ્છા અને ક્રોધથી ઉત્પન્ન વેગને સહન કરવામાં સમર્થ છે — તે જ ખરો યોગી છે, સાચો સુખી છે."},{"ref":"5.24","ch":5,"v":24,"sa":"योऽन्तःसुखोऽन्तरारामस्तथान्तर्ज्योतिरेव यः।\nस योगी ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं ब्रह्मभूतोऽधिगच्छति।।5.24।।","tr":"yo 'ntaḥ-sukho 'ntar-ārāmas tathāntar-jyotir eva yaḥ\nsa yogī brahma-nirvāṇaṁ brahma-bhūto 'dhigachchhati","en":"He who is happy within, who rejoices within, and who is illuminated within, that Yogi attains absolute freedom, or Moksha, becoming Brahman himself.","es":"One who is content within, whose pleasure is within, and whose light is only within, that yogi, having become Brahman, attains absorption into Brahman.","er":"He whose joy is within, whose pleasure is within, and whose light is within—he is a yogin, who, having become Brahman, attains the bliss of Brahman.","gu":"જે ભીતરથી સુખ, ભીતરથી આનંદ, અને ભીતરથી પ્રકાશ અનુભવે છે — એ બ્રહ્મ સાથે ભળેલો યોગી બ્રહ્માનંદ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"5.25","ch":5,"v":25,"sa":"लभन्ते ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृषयः क्षीणकल्मषाः।\nछिन्नद्वैधा यतात्मानः सर्वभूतहिते रताः।।5.25।।","tr":"labhante brahma-nirvāṇam ṛiṣhayaḥ kṣhīṇa-kalmaṣhāḥ\nchhinna-dvaidhā yatātmānaḥ sarva-bhūta-hite ratāḥ","en":"The sages obtain absolute freedom or Moksha when their sins have been destroyed, their dualities have been torn asunder, they are self-controlled, and they are intent on the welfare of all beings.","es":"The seers whose sins have been attenuated, who are free from doubt, whose senses are under control, who are engaged in doing good to all beings, attain absorption in Brahman.","er":"The sages, who are free from the pairs of opposites, whose minds are well subdued, and who are devoted to the welfare of all beings, become cleansed of all impurities and attain the bliss of Brahman.","gu":"જેમના પાપ નષ્ટ થઈ ગયા છે, સંશય ટળ્યા છે, જેઓ સ્વ-નિગ્રહી છે અને સઘળા જીવોના કલ્યાણમાં રત છે — એ ઋષિઓ બ્રહ્માનંદ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"5.26","ch":5,"v":26,"sa":"कामक्रोधवियुक्तानां यतीनां यतचेतसाम्।\nअभितो ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं वर्तते विदितात्मनाम्।।5.26।।","tr":"kāma-krodha-viyuktānāṁ yatīnāṁ yata-chetasām\nabhito brahma-nirvāṇaṁ vartate viditātmanām","en":"Absolute freedom exists on all sides for those self-controlled ascetics who are free from desire and anger, who have controlled their thoughts, and who have realized the Self.","es":"To those monks who have control over their internal organs, who are free from desire and anger, who have known the Self, there is absorption into Brahman either way.","er":"To those who are free from desire and wrath, who are accustomed to exerting themselves, whose thoughts are controlled, and who have conquered it—the beatitude of Brahman is close at hand.","gu":"જેઓ ઇચ્છા અને ક્રોધ રહિત છે, મનને વશ કર્યું છે, અને આત્મ-સાક્ષાત્કાર પ્રાપ્ત કર્યો છે — તેઓ સર્વ દિશામાં બ્રહ્માનંદ અનુભવે છે."},{"ref":"5.27","ch":5,"v":27,"sa":"स्पर्शान्कृत्वा बहिर्बाह्यांश्चक्षुश्चैवान्तरे भ्रुवोः।\nप्राणापानौ समौ कृत्वा नासाभ्यन्तरचारिणौ।।5.27।।","tr":"sparśhān kṛitvā bahir bāhyānśh chakṣhuśh chaivāntare bhruvoḥ\nprāṇāpānau samau kṛitvā nāsābhyantara-chāriṇau\n yatendriya-mano-buddhir munir mokṣha-parāyaṇaḥ\nvigatechchhā-bhaya-krodho yaḥ sadā mukta eva saḥ","en":"Shutting out all external contacts and fixing the gaze between the eyebrows, realizing the outgoing and incoming breaths moving within the nostrils.","es":"- Keeping external objects outside, fixing the eyes at the juncture of the eye-brows, and controlling the outgoing and incoming breaths that move through the nostrils, the contemplative who has mastery over his organs, mind, and intellect should be fully intent on Liberation and free from desire, fear, and anger. He who is ever thus is verily free.","er":"Shutting off outward contacts, fixing the gaze between the eyebrows, realizing inward and outward breaths moving in the nostrils;","gu":"બાહ્ય વિષયોને બહાર કાઢી, દ્રષ્ટિ બે ભ્રૂ-મધ્યે સ્થિર કરી, નાસિકામાં વહેતા ઉચ્છ્વાસ અને નિઃશ્વાસને સમ બનાવી."},{"ref":"5.28","ch":5,"v":28,"sa":"यतेन्द्रियमनोबुद्धिर्मुनिर्मोक्षपरायणः।\nविगतेच्छाभयक्रोधो यः सदा मुक्त एव सः।।5.28।।","tr":"yatendriya-mano-buddhir munir mokṣa-parāyaṇaḥ vigatecchā-bhaya-krodho yaḥ sadā mukta eva saḥ","en":"With the senses, mind, and intellect ever controlled, having liberation as their supreme goal, free from desire, fear, and anger, the sage is truly liberated forever.","es":"- Keeping external objects outside, fixing the eyes at the juncture of the eye-brows, and controlling the outgoing and incoming breaths that move through the nostrils, the contemplative who has mastery over his organs, mind, and intellect should be fully intent on Liberation and free from desire, fear, and anger. He who is ever thus is verily free.","er":"The sage who has controlled his senses, mind, and intellect, who is intent on release as his final goal, freed forever from desire, fear, and wrath, is indeed liberated forever.","gu":"ઇન્દ્રિય, મન, અને બુદ્ધિ — સૌને સદા સ્વાધીન રાખી, મોક્ષ-પ્રાપ્તિ જ જેનું પરમ ધ્યેય છે, ઇચ્છા, ભય, ને ક્રોધ વિનાનો — આવો મુનિ સદા મુક્ત જ છે."},{"ref":"5.29","ch":5,"v":29,"sa":"भोक्तारं यज्ञतपसां सर्वलोकमहेश्वरम्।\nसुहृदं सर्वभूतानां ज्ञात्वा मां शान्तिमृच्छति।।5.29।।","tr":"bhoktāraṁ yajña-tapasāṁ sarva-loka-maheśhvaram\nsuhṛidaṁ sarva-bhūtānāṁ jñātvā māṁ śhāntim ṛichchhati","en":"He who knows Me as the enjoyer of sacrifices and austerities, the great Lord of all the worlds, and the friend of all beings, attains peace.","es":"One attains peace by knowing Me, who am the great Lord of all the worlds, the enjoyer of sacrifices and austerities, and the friend of all creatures.","er":"Knowing Me as the enjoyer of all sacrifices and austerities, as the Supreme Lord of all worlds, as the Friend of every being, he attains peace."},{"ref":"6.1","ch":6,"v":1,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nअनाश्रितः कर्मफलं कार्यं कर्म करोति यः।\nस संन्यासी च योगी च न निरग्निर्न चाक्रियः।।6.1।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nanāśhritaḥ karma-phalaṁ kāryaṁ karma karoti yaḥ\nsa sannyāsī cha yogī cha na niragnir na chākriyaḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said: He who performs his bounden duty without depending on the fruits of his actions—he is a sannyasi and a yogi, not he who is without fire and without action.","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"He who performs an action which is his duty, without depending on the result of the action, is a monk and a yogi; not so in he who does not keep afire and is actionless.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"He who performs works that ought to be done without seeking their fruits—he is a sannyasin and yogin, and not he who maintains no sacred fires and performs no actions.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: જે વ્યક્તિ ફળની અપેક્ષા રાખ્યા વિના પોતાના નિયત કર્તવ્ય કર્મ કરે છે, તે ખરો સંન્યાસી અને યોગી છે — નહીં કે જે અગ્નિ છોડી દે અને કર્મ ન કરે."},{"ref":"6.2","ch":6,"v":2,"sa":"यं संन्यासमिति प्राहुर्योगं तं विद्धि पाण्डव।\nन ह्यसंन्यस्तसङ्कल्पो योगी भवति कश्चन।।6.2।।","tr":"yaṁ sannyāsam iti prāhur yogaṁ taṁ viddhi pāṇḍava\nna hyasannyasta-saṅkalpo yogī bhavati kaśhchana","en":"Do you, O Arjuna, know that Yoga is what they call renunciation; no one indeed becomes a Yogi who has not renounced their thoughts.","es":"That which they call monasticism, know that to be Yoga, O Pandava, for nobody who has not given up expectations can be a yogi.","er":"That which is called Sannyasa (Jnana Yoga), know that to be Yoga (Karma Yoga), O Arjuna. For no one, among Karma Yogins, whose delusive identification of the body with the self has not been abandoned, becomes a true Karma Yogin.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જેને સંન્યાસ કહે છે તેને જ યોગ સમજ; સ્વાર્થી ઇચ્છાઓ ત્યજ્યા વિના કોઈ યોગી બની શકતું નથી."},{"ref":"6.3","ch":6,"v":3,"sa":"आरुरुक्षोर्मुनेर्योगं कर्म कारणमुच्यते।\nयोगारूढस्य तस्यैव शमः कारणमुच्यते।।6.3।।","tr":"ārurukṣhor muner yogaṁ karma kāraṇam uchyate\nyogārūḍhasya tasyaiva śhamaḥ kāraṇam uchyate","en":"For a sage who wishes to attain to Yoga, action is said to be the means; for the same sage who has attained Yoga, inaction is said to be the means.","es":"For the sage who wishes to ascend to (Dhyana-) yoga, action is said to be the means. For that person, once he has ascended to (Dhyana-)yoga, inaction alone is said to be the means.","er":"Action is said to be the means for the sage who seeks to climb the heights of Yoga; but when he has climbed the heights of Yoga, tranquility is said to be the means.","gu":"જે મુમુક્ષુ ઋષિ યોગ પ્રાપ્ત કરવા ઇચ્છે છે, તેના માટે કર્મ સાધન કહેવાય છે; અને જે ઋષિ યોગ પ્રાપ્ત કરી ચૂક્યો છે, તેના માટે શાંતિ અને નિષ્ક્રિયતા સાધન કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"6.4","ch":6,"v":4,"sa":"यदा हि नेन्द्रियार्थेषु न कर्मस्वनुषज्जते।\nसर्वसङ्कल्पसंन्यासी योगारूढस्तदोच्यते।।6.4।।","tr":"yadā hi nendriyārtheṣhu na karmasv-anuṣhajjate\nsarva-saṅkalpa-sannyāsī yogārūḍhas tadochyate","en":"When a person is not attached to the sense-objects or to actions, having renounced all thoughts, then they are said to have attained Yoga.","es":"Verily, when a man who has given up thought about everything does not get attached to sense-objects or actions, he is then said to be established in Yoga.","er":"For, when one loses attachment to the things of the senses and to actions, then they have abandoned all desires and are said to have climbed the heights of Yoga.","gu":"જ્યારે માણસ ઇન્દ્રિય-વિષયો કે કર્મો પ્રત્યે આસક્તિ ધરાવતો નથી, અને સઘળી ઇચ્છાઓ ત્યજી દે છે, ત્યારે તે યોગ-સ્થિત થયો છે એમ કહેવાય."},{"ref":"6.5","ch":6,"v":5,"sa":"उद्धरेदात्मनाऽऽत्मानं नात्मानमवसादयेत्।\nआत्मैव ह्यात्मनो बन्धुरात्मैव रिपुरात्मनः।।6.5।।","tr":"uddhared ātmanātmānaṁ nātmānam avasādayet\nātmaiva hyātmano bandhur ātmaiva ripur ātmanaḥ","en":"One should raise oneself by one's own self alone; let not one lower oneself; for the self alone is one's own friend, and the self alone is one's own enemy.","es":"One should save oneself by oneself; one should not degrade oneself. For oneself is indeed one's own friend; oneself is indeed one's own enemy.","er":"One should raise oneself by one's own mind and not allow oneself to sink; for the mind alone is the friend of the self, and the mind alone is the foe of the self.","gu":"માણસે પોતે જ પોતાનો ઉદ્ધાર કરવો; પોતાને અધોગતિ ન આપવી; કારણ કે આત્મા જ પોતાનો મિત્ર છે અને આત્મા જ પોતાનો શત્રુ છે."},{"ref":"6.6","ch":6,"v":6,"sa":"बन्धुरात्माऽऽत्मनस्तस्य येनात्मैवात्मना जितः।\nअनात्मनस्तु शत्रुत्वे वर्तेतात्मैव शत्रुवत्।।6.6।।","tr":"bandhur ātmātmanas tasya yenātmaivātmanā jitaḥ\nanātmanas tu śhatrutve vartetātmaiva śhatru-vat","en":"The Self is the friend of the self of him by whom the Self has been conquered; but to the unconquered self, this Self stands in the position of an enemy, like an external foe.","es":"He who has conquered his own self by the self, his self is his own friend. But for one who has not conquered his own self, his self itself acts like an enemy.","er":"The mind is the friend of him by whom it has been conquered. But for him whose mind is not conquered, the mind, like an enemy, remains hostile.","gu":"જેણે આત્મા વડે પોતાને જીત્યો છે, તેનો આત્મા મિત્ર બને છે; પણ જેણે પોતાને જીત્યો નથી, તેનો આત્મા શત્રુ સમાન વૈરી રહે છે."},{"ref":"6.7","ch":6,"v":7,"sa":"जितात्मनः प्रशान्तस्य परमात्मा समाहितः।\nशीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु तथा मानापमानयोः।।6.7।।","tr":"jitātmanaḥ praśhāntasya paramātmā samāhitaḥ\nśhītoṣhṇa-sukha-duḥkheṣhu tathā mānāpamānayoḥ","en":"The Supreme Self of him who is self-controlled and peaceful remains balanced in cold and heat, pleasure and pain, as well as in honor and dishonor.","es":"The supreme Self of one who has control over the aggregate of his body and organs, and who is tranquil, becomes manifest. He should be poised in the midst of cold and heat, happiness and sorrow, as well as honor and dishonor.","er":"Of him whose mind is conquered and who is serene, the great self is well-secured in heat and cold, in pleasure and pain, and in honor and dishonor.","gu":"જેણે પોતાના મન પર વિજય મેળવ્યો છે અને જે શાંત છે, તેના માટે પરમ આત્મા ઠંડી-ગરમીમાં, સુખ-દુઃખમાં, સન્માન-અપમાનમાં — સ્થિર રહીને ઓળઘોળ રહે છે."},{"ref":"6.8","ch":6,"v":8,"sa":"ज्ञानविज्ञानतृप्तात्मा कूटस्थो विजितेन्द्रियः।\nयुक्त इत्युच्यते योगी समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः।।6.8।।","tr":"jñāna-vijñāna-tṛiptātmā kūṭa-stho vijitendriyaḥ\nyukta ityuchyate yogī sama-loṣhṭāśhma-kāñchanaḥ","en":"The Yogi who is satisfied with the knowledge and wisdom of the Self, who has conquered the senses, and to whom a clod of earth, a piece of stone, and gold are all the same, is said to have attained Nirvikalpa Samadhi.","es":"One whose mind is satisfied with knowledge and realization, who is unmoved, who has his organs under control, is said to be Self-absorbed. The yogi treats all alike, a lump of earth, a stone, and gold.","er":"The yogin whose mind is content with knowledge of the self and also with knowledge of the difference between the self and Prakrti, who is established in the self, whose senses are subdued, and to whom earth, stone, and gold all seem alike, is called integrated.","gu":"જ્ઞાન અને અનુભવથી તૃપ્ત, અડોલ, ઇન્દ્રિયો પર વિજય મેળવ્યો હોય, માટી, પથ્થર અને સોનાને સમાન ગણે — એવા યોગીને યોગમાં સ્થિત કહેવાય."},{"ref":"6.9","ch":6,"v":9,"sa":"सुहृन्मित्रार्युदासीनमध्यस्थद्वेष्यबन्धुषु।\nसाधुष्वपि च पापेषु समबुद्धिर्विशिष्यते।।6.9।।","tr":"suhṛin-mitrāryudāsīna-madhyastha-dveṣhya-bandhuṣhu\nsādhuṣhvapi cha pāpeṣhu sama-buddhir viśhiṣhyate","en":"He who is of the same mind towards the good-hearted, friends, enemies, the indifferent, the neutral, the hateful, the relatives, the righteous, and the unrighteous, excels.","es":"He excels who has sameness of view with regard to a benefactor, a friend, an enemy, a neutral, an arbiter, the hateful, a relative, good people, and even sinners.","er":"He who regards with an equal eye well-wishers, friends, foes, the indifferent, neutrals, the hateful, the relations, and even the good and the sinful—he excels.","gu":"સુહૃદ, મિત્ર, શત્રુ, ઉદાસીન, મધ્યસ્થ, ઘૃણ્ય, સ્બજન, સાધુ, પાપીતે સમદર્શી બિશિષ્ટ।"},{"ref":"6.10","ch":6,"v":10,"sa":"योगी युञ्जीत सततमात्मानं रहसि स्थितः।\nएकाकी यतचित्तात्मा निराशीरपरिग्रहः।।6.10।।","tr":"yogī yuñjīta satatam ātmānaṁ rahasi sthitaḥ\nekākī yata-chittātmā nirāśhīr aparigrahaḥ","en":"Let the yogi constantly strive to keep the mind steady, remaining in solitude, alone, with the body and mind controlled, and free from hope and greed.","es":"A yogi should constantly concentrate his mind by staying in a solitary place, alone, with mind and body controlled, free from expectations, and free from acquisition.","er":"The yogin should constantly fix his mind on yoga, remaining in a solitary place all alone, controlling his thoughts and mind, free from desire and a sense of possession.","gu":"યોગીએ એકાંત સ્થળે એકલા રહી, મન અને શરીરને નિયંત્રણમાં રાખી, ઇચ્છા અને સંગ્રહ વિના, સતત યોગ અભ્યાસ કરવો."},{"ref":"6.11","ch":6,"v":11,"sa":"शुचौ देशे प्रतिष्ठाप्य स्थिरमासनमात्मनः।\nनात्युच्छ्रितं नातिनीचं चैलाजिनकुशोत्तरम्।।6.11।।","tr":"śhuchau deśhe pratiṣhṭhāpya sthiram āsanam ātmanaḥ\nnātyuchchhritaṁ nāti-nīchaṁ chailājina-kuśhottaram","en":"In a clean spot, having established a firm seat of his own, neither too high nor too low, made of cloth, skin, and kusha grass layered one over the other.","es":"Having firmly established in a clean place his seat, neither too high nor too low, composed of cloth, skin, and kusa-grass placed successively one below the other;","er":"Having established for himself, in a clean spot, a firm seat that is neither too high nor too low, and covering it with cloth, deer-skin, and Kusa grass in reverse order—","gu":"પવિત્ર સ્થળમાં, ન અતિ ઊંચું ન અતિ નીચું, કુશ, મૃગચર્મ અને વસ્ત્ર વડે ઢંકાયેલ પોતાનું સ્થિર આસન ગોઠવી —"},{"ref":"6.12","ch":6,"v":12,"sa":"तत्रैकाग्रं मनः कृत्वा यतचित्तेन्द्रियक्रियः।\nउपविश्यासने युञ्ज्याद्योगमात्मविशुद्धये।।6.12।।","tr":"tatraikāgraṁ manaḥ kṛitvā yata-chittendriya-kriyaḥ\nupaviśhyāsane yuñjyād yogam ātma-viśhuddhaye","en":"There, having made the mind one-pointed, with the actions of the mind and senses controlled, let him, seated on the seat, practice Yoga for the purification of the self.","es":"Sitting on that seat, he should concentrate his mind for the purification of the internal organ, making the mind one-pointed and keeping the actions of the mind and senses under control.","er":"Sitting on the seat, with a concentrated mind, controlling the mind and senses, one should practice Yoga for the purification of the self.","gu":"ત્યાં, મન-ઇન્દ્રિયોની ક્રિયાઓ સ્થિર કરી, ચિત્ત એકાગ્ર કરી, આત્મ-શુદ્ધિ માટે યોગી આસન ઉપર બેસી ધ્યાન ધરે."},{"ref":"6.13","ch":6,"v":13,"sa":"समं कायशिरोग्रीवं धारयन्नचलं स्थिरः।\nसंप्रेक्ष्य नासिकाग्रं स्वं दिशश्चानवलोकयन्।।6.13।।","tr":"samaṁ kāya-śhiro-grīvaṁ dhārayann achalaṁ sthiraḥ\nsamprekṣhya nāsikāgraṁ svaṁ diśhaśh chānavalokayan","en":"Let him firmly hold his body, head, and neck erect and still, gazing at the tip of his nose without looking around.","es":"Holding the body, head, and neck erect and still, being steady, looking at the tip of his own nose and not looking around.","er":"Holding the trunk, head, and neck erect, motionless and steady, gazing at the tip of the nose and not looking in any direction;","gu":"શરીર, મસ્તક અને ગ્રીવા સ્થિર અને ઋજુ રાખી, નાસિકાના અગ્ર ભાગ પર દૃષ્ટિ સ્થિર કરી, ચારેય બાજુ ન જોતાં ધ્યાન ધરવું."},{"ref":"6.14","ch":6,"v":14,"sa":"प्रशान्तात्मा विगतभीर्ब्रह्मचारिव्रते स्थितः।\nमनः संयम्य मच्चित्तो युक्त आसीत मत्परः।।6.14।।","tr":"praśhāntātmā vigata-bhīr brahmachāri-vrate sthitaḥ\nmanaḥ sanyamya mach-chitto yukta āsīta mat-paraḥ","en":"Serene-minded, fearless, firm in the vow of a Brahmachari, having controlled their mind, thinking of Me and balanced in mind, let them sit, having Me as their supreme goal.","es":"He should remain seated with a placid mind, free from fear, firm in the vow of celibacy, and with the mind fixed on Me by controlling it through concentration, having Me as the supreme goal.","er":"Serene and fearless, firm in their vow of celibacy, controlling their minds and fixing their thoughts on Me, they should sit in Yoga, intent on Me.","gu":"પ્રશાંત ચિત્ત, ભયહીન, બ્રહ્મચર્ય-વ્રતમાં દૃઢ, મન નિયંત્રિત કરી, મને — શ્રેષ્ઠ લક્ષ્ય તરીકે — ચિંતન કરતો, મારામાં ભક્તિ રાખી, યોગી ઉપાસના કરે."},{"ref":"6.15","ch":6,"v":15,"sa":"युञ्जन्नेवं सदाऽऽत्मानं योगी नियतमानसः।\nशान्तिं निर्वाणपरमां मत्संस्थामधिगच्छति।।6.15।।","tr":"yuñjann evaṁ sadātmānaṁ yogī niyata-mānasaḥ\nśhantiṁ nirvāṇa-paramāṁ mat-sansthām adhigachchhati","en":"Thus, always keeping the mind balanced, the yogi, with the mind controlled, attains the peace abiding in Me, culminating in liberation.","es":"Concentrating the mind thus, forever, the yogi of a controlled mind achieves the peace that culminates in liberation and abides in Me.","er":"Applying his mind in this way, the Yogin of controlled mind, ever attains the peace which is the summit of beatitude and which abides in Me.","gu":"આ પ્રમાણે સૌ સમય મનને સ્થિર રાખી, મન-સ્વામી યોગી મારી અંદર રહેલ — નિર્વાણ તરફ જઈ પૂર્ણ થનારી — શાંતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"6.16","ch":6,"v":16,"sa":"नात्यश्नतस्तु योगोऽस्ति न चैकान्तमनश्नतः।\nन चातिस्वप्नशीलस्य जाग्रतो नैव चार्जुन।।6.16।।","tr":"nātyaśhnatastu yogo ’sti na chaikāntam anaśhnataḥ\nna chāti-svapna-śhīlasya jāgrato naiva chārjuna","en":"Verily, Yoga is not possible for him who eats too much, nor for him who does not eat at all, nor for him who sleeps too much, nor for him who is always awake, O Arjuna.","es":"But, O Arjuna, Yoga is not for one who eats excessively, nor for one who does not eat at all; neither for one who habitually sleeps too long, nor for one who stays awake.","er":"Yoga is not for him who overeats, nor for him who fasts excessively; not for him, O Arjuna, who sleeps too much, nor for him who stays awake too long.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, ઘણું ખાવા-ઓછું ખાવા, ઘણું સૂવા-જાગ્રત રહ્યા કરવા — આ સ્વભાવ ધરાવનારા માટે યોગ સિદ્ધ થતો નથી."},{"ref":"6.17","ch":6,"v":17,"sa":"युक्ताहारविहारस्य युक्तचेष्टस्य कर्मसु।\nयुक्तस्वप्नावबोधस्य योगो भवति दुःखहा।।6.17।।","tr":"yuktāhāra-vihārasya yukta-cheṣhṭasya karmasu\nyukta-svapnāvabodhasya yogo bhavati duḥkha-hā","en":"Yoga becomes the destroyer of pain for him who is moderate in eating and recreation (such as walking, etc.), who exercises moderation in action, and who is moderate in sleep and wakefulness.","es":"Yoga becomes a destroyer of sorrow for one whose eating and movements are regulated, whose effort in works is moderate, and whose sleep and wakefulness are temperate.","er":"Yoga becomes the destroyer of sorrows for those who are temperate in food and recreation, temperate in their actions, and temperate in their sleep and wakefulness.","gu":"ખાવা-મોજ-ગમ્મત-ક્રિયા-ઊઘ-જ્ઞાાન — જે સર્વ બાબત મધ્યમ માર્ગ અપનાવે, એવા યોગ-સાધક માટે યોગ સઘળા દુઃખ-સંતાપ હઠાવે."},{"ref":"6.18","ch":6,"v":18,"sa":"यदा विनियतं चित्तमात्मन्येवावतिष्ठते।\nनिःस्पृहः सर्वकामेभ्यो युक्त इत्युच्यते तदा।।6.18।।","tr":"yadā viniyataṁ chittam ātmanyevāvatiṣhṭhate\nniḥspṛihaḥ sarva-kāmebhyo yukta ityuchyate tadā","en":"When the perfectly controlled mind rests in the Self alone, free from longing for any of the objects of desire, then it is said, 'He is united'.","es":"A person who has become free from hankering for all desirable objects is said to be Self-absorbed when the controlled mind rests solely in the Self.","er":"When the subdued mind rests solely on the Self, then, free from all yearning for objects of desire, one is said to be fit for Yoga.","gu":"જ્યારે સારી રીતે સાધેલ ચિત્ત કેવળ આત્મામાં સ્થિર થઈ જાય, ઇચ્છિત વિષયો ઉપરની લાલસા છૂટી જાય — ત્યારે કહેવાય છે કે સાધક યોગ-સ્થિત થઈ ગયો."},{"ref":"6.19","ch":6,"v":19,"sa":"यथा दीपो निवातस्थो नेङ्गते सोपमा स्मृता।\nयोगिनो यतचित्तस्य युञ्जतो योगमात्मनः।।6.19।।","tr":"yathā dīpo nivāta-stho neṅgate sopamā smṛitā\nyogino yata-chittasya yuñjato yogam ātmanaḥ","en":"As a lamp placed in a windless spot does not flicker, so is the Yogi of a controlled mind, who practices Yoga in the Self, compared.","es":"As a lamp kept in a windless place does not flicker, so is the simile for the yogi whose mind is under control and who is engaged in concentration on the Self.","er":"A lamp does not flicker in a windless place\"—that is the simile used for the tranquil mind of a yogi who practices yoga."},{"ref":"6.20","ch":6,"v":20,"sa":"यत्रोपरमते चित्तं निरुद्धं योगसेवया।\nयत्र चैवात्मनाऽऽत्मानं पश्यन्नात्मनि तुष्यति।।6.20।।","tr":"yatroparamate chittaṁ niruddhaṁ yoga-sevayā\nyatra chaivātmanātmānaṁ paśhyann ātmani tuṣhyati","en":"When the mind, restrained by the practice of yoga, attains quietude, and when one sees the Self by the Self, they are satisfied in their own Self.","es":"At the time when the mind, restrained through the practice of Yoga, is withdrawn, and just when one sees the Self by the self and remains contented in the Self alone;","er":"Where the mind, controlled through the practice of Yoga, rests, and where one sees the Self by the Self and is delighted by the Self alone.","gu":"જ્યારે યોગના અભ્યાસ દ્વારા મન શાંત થઈ જાય છે, અને આત્મા વડે આત્માને નિહાળીને, સાધક આત્મામાં જ સંતુષ્ટ રહે છે."},{"ref":"6.21","ch":6,"v":21,"sa":"सुखमात्यन्तिकं यत्तद्बुद्धिग्राह्यमतीन्द्रियम्।\nवेत्ति यत्र न चैवायं स्थितश्चलति तत्त्वतः।।6.21।।","tr":"sukham ātyantikaṁ yat tad buddhi-grāhyam atīndriyam\nvetti yatra na chaivāyaṁ sthitaśh chalati tattvataḥ","en":"When he (the Yogi) feels that infinite bliss which can be grasped by the pure intellect and which transcends the senses, and is established therein, never moving away from the reality.","es":"When one experiences that absolute Bliss, which can be intuited by the intellect and which is beyond the senses, and being thus established, this person surely does not swerve from Reality.","er":"Where one knows that infinite happiness which can be grasped by the intellect but is beyond the reach of the senses, and is established in that condition, one does not swerve from it.","gu":"જ્યારે સાધક શુદ્ધ બુદ્ધિ વડે અનુભવાતા અનંત આનંદને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે, અને એ અવસ્થામાં સ્થિર થઈ સત્યથી ક્યારેય ડગે નહિ."},{"ref":"6.22","ch":6,"v":22,"sa":"यं लब्ध्वा चापरं लाभं मन्यते नाधिकं ततः।\nयस्मिन्स्थितो न दुःखेन गुरुणापि विचाल्यते।।6.22।।","tr":"yaṁ labdhvā chāparaṁ lābhaṁ manyate nādhikaṁ tataḥ\nyasmin sthito na duḥkhena guruṇāpi vichālyate","en":"Having obtained it, he thinks there is no other gain superior to it; established in it, he is not moved even by heavy sorrow.","es":"Obtaining which one does not consider any other acquisition to be superior, and being established in which one is not perturbed even by great sorrow;","er":"Having gained it, one holds that there is no greater gain; being established in it, one is not moved even by the heaviest sorrow.","gu":"તે પ્રાપ્ત કર્યા પછી એનાથી મોટો કોઈ લાભ નથી એમ સાધક માને છે, અને એ સ્થિતિમાં રહીને ભારે દુઃખ આવ્યે પણ વિચલિત થતો નથી."},{"ref":"6.23","ch":6,"v":23,"sa":"तं विद्याद् दुःखसंयोगवियोगं योगसंज्ञितम्।\nस निश्चयेन योक्तव्यो योगोऽनिर्विण्णचेतसा।।6.23।।","tr":"taṁ vidyād duḥkha-sanyoga-viyogaṁ yogasaṅjñitam\nsa niśhchayena yoktavyo yogo ’nirviṇṇa-chetasā","en":"Let this be known by the name of Yoga, the severance from union with pain. This Yoga should be practiced with determination and with an undespairing mind.","es":"One should know that severance of contact with sorrow to be what is called Yoga. That Yoga should be practiced with perseverance and with an undepressed heart.","er":"Know this deliverance from association with misery to be Yoga. This Yoga must be practiced with determination and with a mind free from despondency.","gu":"દુઃખ સાથેના સંબંધના વિચ્છેદને જ યોગ જાણો. આ યોગ નિરાશ ન થઈ, દ્રઢ મનથી અને ખંતપૂર્વક અભ્યાસ કરવો જોઈએ."},{"ref":"6.24","ch":6,"v":24,"sa":"सङ्कल्पप्रभवान्कामांस्त्यक्त्वा सर्वानशेषतः।\nमनसैवेन्द्रियग्रामं विनियम्य समन्ततः।।6.24।।","tr":"saṅkalpa-prabhavān kāmāns tyaktvā sarvān aśheṣhataḥ\nmanasaivendriya-grāmaṁ viniyamya samantataḥ","en":"Abandoning unreservedly all desires born of Sankalpa (thought and imagination) and completely restraining the whole group of senses by the mind from all sides.","es":"By totally eschewing all desires that arise from thoughts and restraining all the organs with the mind from every side;","er":"Renouncing entirely all desires born of volition and restraining the mind from all the senses on all sides,","gu":"સંકલ્પ માત્રથી ઉત્પન્ન થતી સઘળી ઇચ્છાઓ સંપૂર્ણ રીતે ત્યજીને, ચારે બાજુથી ઇન્દ્રિયોના સમૂહને એકલા મન વડે સંયમમાં રાખવા."},{"ref":"6.25","ch":6,"v":25,"sa":"शनैः शनैरुपरमेद् बुद्ध्या धृतिगृहीतया।\nआत्मसंस्थं मनः कृत्वा न किञ्चिदपि चिन्तयेत्।।6.25।।","tr":"śhanaiḥ śhanair uparamed buddhyā dhṛiti-gṛihītayā\nātma-sansthaṁ manaḥ kṛitvā na kiñchid api chintayet","en":"Little by little, let him attain steadiness of the intellect by holding it firmly; having made the mind establish itself in the Self, let him not think of anything else.","es":"One should gradually withdraw with the intellect, endowed with steadiness. Making the mind fixed in the Self, one should not think of anything at all.","er":"Little by little, one should withdraw oneself from objects other than the self, with the help of the intellect held by firm resolution; and then one should think of nothing else, having fixed the mind upon the Self.","gu":"ધૈર્યયુક્ત બુદ્ધિ વડે ધીરે ધીરે શાંતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરો; મનને આત્મામાં સ્થિર કરીને બીજા કોઈ વિચારમાં ન સરો."},{"ref":"6.26","ch":6,"v":26,"sa":"यतो यतो निश्चरति मनश्चञ्चलमस्थिरम्।\nततस्ततो नियम्यैतदात्मन्येव वशं नयेत्।।6.26।।","tr":"yato yato niśhcharati manaśh chañchalam asthiram\ntatas tato niyamyaitad ātmanyeva vaśhaṁ nayet","en":"From whatever cause the restless and unsteady mind wanders away, let him restrain it from that and bring it under the control of the Self alone.","es":"The yogi should bring this mind under the subjugation of the Self itself, restraining it from all those causes that cause the restless, unsteady mind to wander away.","er":"Wherever the fickle and unsteady mind wanders, one should subdue it and then bring it back under the control of the self alone.","gu":"ચંચળ અને અસ્થિર મન જ્યાં જ્યાં ભટકે, ત્યાંથી ત્યાંથી તેને ખેંચી પાછું લાવો અને કેવળ આત્માના નિયંત્રણ હેઠળ સ્થિર કરો."},{"ref":"6.27","ch":6,"v":27,"sa":"प्रशान्तमनसं ह्येनं योगिनं सुखमुत्तमम्।\nउपैति शान्तरजसं ब्रह्मभूतमकल्मषम्।।6.27।।","tr":"praśhānta-manasaṁ hyenaṁ yoginaṁ sukham uttamam\nupaiti śhānta-rajasaṁ brahma-bhūtam akalmaṣham","en":"Supreme Bliss indeed comes to this Yogi whose mind is made peaceful, whose passion is quelled, who has become Brahman, and who is free from sin.","es":"Supreme Bliss comes to this yogi alone whose mind has become perfectly tranquil, whose quality of rajas has been eliminated, who has become identified with Brahman, and is untainted.","er":"For supreme happiness comes to the Yogin whose mind is at peace, who is free from evil, from whom Rajas has departed, and who has become the Brahman.","gu":"જેનું મન શાંત છે, જેની વાસનાઓ ઠરી ગઈ છે, જે પાપ રહિત છે અને જે બ્રહ્મ સ્વરૂપ થઈ ગયો છે — તે યોગીને સર્વોચ્ચ આનંદ પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે."},{"ref":"6.28","ch":6,"v":28,"sa":"युञ्जन्नेवं सदाऽऽत्मानं योगी विगतकल्मषः।\nसुखेन ब्रह्मसंस्पर्शमत्यन्तं सुखमश्नुते।।6.28।।","tr":"yuñjann evaṁ sadātmānaṁ yogī vigata-kalmaṣhaḥ\nsukhena brahma-sansparśham atyantaṁ sukham aśhnute","en":"The yogi, always engaging the mind thus (in the practice of yoga), is freed from sins and easily enjoys the infinite bliss of contact with Brahman (the Eternal).","es":"By constantly concentrating his mind in this way, the taintless yogi easily attains the absolute bliss of contact with Brahman.","er":"Thus, devoting himself to the Yoga of the Self, freed from impurities, the yogin easily attains the supreme bliss of contact with the Brahman.","gu":"આ પ્રકારે સદા આત્માને યોગમાં જોડી, પાપ રહિત એવો યોગી સહેજે જ બ્રહ્મ સ્પર્શના અનંત સુખનો અનુભવ કરે છે."},{"ref":"6.29","ch":6,"v":29,"sa":"सर्वभूतस्थमात्मानं सर्वभूतानि चात्मनि।\nईक्षते योगयुक्तात्मा सर्वत्र समदर्शनः।।6.29।।","tr":"sarva-bhūta-stham ātmānaṁ sarva-bhūtāni chātmani\nīkṣhate yoga-yuktātmā sarvatra sama-darśhanaḥ","en":"With the mind harmonized by Yoga, he sees the Self abiding in all beings and all beings in the Self; he sees the same everywhere.","es":"One who has their mind Self-absorbed through Yoga, and who has the vision of sameness everywhere, sees this Self existing in everything, and everything in their Self.","er":"He whose mind is fixed in Yoga sees reality everywhere; he sees his Self as abiding in all beings and all beings in his Self.","gu":"સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓમાં આત્માને અને આત્મામાં સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓને જોનાર, યોગ દ્વારા સમ ચિત્ત થયેલો સાધક સર્વત્ર સમભાવ દ્રષ્ટિ ધરાવે છે."},{"ref":"6.30","ch":6,"v":30,"sa":"यो मां पश्यति सर्वत्र सर्वं च मयि पश्यति।\nतस्याहं न प्रणश्यामि स च मे न प्रणश्यति।।6.30।।","tr":"yo māṁ paśhyati sarvatra sarvaṁ cha mayi paśhyati\ntasyāhaṁ na praṇaśhyāmi sa cha me na praṇaśhyati","en":"He who sees Me everywhere and sees everything in Me, never becomes separated from Me, nor do I from him.","es":"One who sees Me in everything and sees all things in Me—I do not lose sight of him, and he also is not lost to My vision.","er":"To him who sees Me in every self and every self in Me—I am not lost to him, nor is he lost to Me.","gu":"જે મને સર્વત્ર જુએ છે અને સઘળું મારામાં જ જુએ છે, તેના માટે હું ક્યારેય અદ્રશ્ય નથી, અને તે મારા માટે ક્યારેય ખોવાઈ નથી જતો."},{"ref":"6.31","ch":6,"v":31,"sa":"सर्वभूतस्थितं यो मां भजत्येकत्वमास्थितः।\nसर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि स योगी मयि वर्तते।।6.31।।","tr":"sarva-bhūta-sthitaṁ yo māṁ bhajatyekatvam āsthitaḥ\nsarvathā vartamāno ’pi sa yogī mayi vartate","en":"He who, being established in unity, worships Me, who dwells in all beings, that yogi abides in Me, whatever their mode of living may be.","es":"That yogi, who, being established in unity, adores Me as existing in all things, exists in Me—in whatever condition he may be.","er":"The yogi who, fixed in oneness, worships Me dwelling in all beings—he abides in Me, no matter how he may live.","gu":"એકત્વ ભાવમાં સ્થિત થઈ, સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓમાં વસતા મારી ઉપાસના કરનારો યોગી ગમે તે રીતે જીવે — તે મારામાં જ વસે છે."},{"ref":"6.32","ch":6,"v":32,"sa":"आत्मौपम्येन सर्वत्र समं पश्यति योऽर्जुन।\nसुखं वा यदि वा दुःखं सः योगी परमो मतः।।6.32।।","tr":"ātmaupamyena sarvatra samaṁ paśhyati yo ’rjuna\nsukhaṁ vā yadi vā duḥkhaṁ sa yogī paramo mataḥ","en":"He who, through the likeness of the Self, O Arjuna, sees reality everywhere, be it pleasure or pain, is regarded as the highest Yogi.","es":"O Arjuna, that yogi is considered the best who judges what is happiness and sorrow in all beings by the same standard as they would apply to themselves.","er":"He who, due to the similarity of selves everywhere, sees pleasure or pain as the same everywhere—that yogi, O Arjuna, is considered the closest.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે સુખ-દુઃખ ઉભય અવસ્થામાં સ્વયંને ધોરણ ગણી, સઘળે સમ ભાવે જુએ છે — તે યોગી સર્વોત્તમ ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"6.33","ch":6,"v":33,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nयोऽयं योगस्त्वया प्रोक्तः साम्येन मधुसूदन।\nएतस्याहं न पश्यामि चञ्चलत्वात् स्थितिं स्थिराम्।।6.33।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nyo ’yaṁ yogas tvayā proktaḥ sāmyena madhusūdana\netasyāhaṁ na paśhyāmi chañchalatvāt sthitiṁ sthirām","en":"Arjuna said, \"O Krishna, I do not see how this Yoga of equanimity, which you have taught me, can be maintained steadily, due to the restlessness of the mind.\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Madhusudana (Krsna), this Yoga that You have spoken of as sameness, I do not see its steady continuance due to the restlessness of the mind.\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"O Krsna, this Yoga of reality, which You have declared, I do not see how it can be steady due to the fickleness of the mind.\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે કૃષ્ણ, આપે જે સમભાવ રૂપ યોગ વર્ણવ્યો, ચંચળ અને અસ્થિર મન હોવાથી તે સ્થિર કેવી રીતે રહી શકે — તે મને સમજાતું નથી."},{"ref":"6.34","ch":6,"v":34,"sa":"चञ्चलं हि मनः कृष्ण प्रमाथि बलवद्दृढम्।\nतस्याहं निग्रहं मन्ये वायोरिव सुदुष्करम्।।6.34।।","tr":"chañchalaṁ hi manaḥ kṛiṣhṇa pramāthi balavad dṛiḍham\ntasyāhaṁ nigrahaṁ manye vāyor iva su-duṣhkaram","en":"The mind is indeed restless, turbulent, strong, and unyielding, O Krishna; I consider it as difficult to control as controlling the wind.","es":"For, O Kṛṣṇa, the mind is unsteady, turbulent, strong, and obstinate; I consider its control to be as difficult as that of the wind.","er":"For the mind is fickle, O Krsna, impetuous, powerful, and stubborn; I think that restraining it is as difficult as restraining the wind.","gu":"હે કૃષ્ણ, મન ઘણું ચંચળ, ઉત્તેજિત, બળવાન અને હઠીલું છે; એને વશ કરવું, મને લાગે છે, વાયુ ને વશ કરવા જેટલું જ કઠિન છે."},{"ref":"6.35","ch":6,"v":35,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nअसंशयं महाबाहो मनो दुर्निग्रहं चलं।\nअभ्यासेन तु कौन्तेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते।।6.35।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nasanśhayaṁ mahā-bāho mano durnigrahaṁ chalam\nabhyāsena tu kaunteya vairāgyeṇa cha gṛihyate","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"Undoubtedly, O mighty-armed Arjuna, the mind is difficult to control and restless; but with practice and dispassion, it can be restrained.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, O mighty-armed one, undoubtedly the mind is untamable and restless. But, O son of Kunti, it can be brought under control through practice and detachment.","er":"The Lord said, \"The mind is indeed hard to subdue and fickle, O mighty-armed one, but, O son of Kunti, it can be brought under control through practice and the exercise of dispassion.\"","gu":"શ્રી કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે મહાબાહો, નિઃસંદેહ મન ચંચળ અને કઠિન નિયંત્રણ વાળું છે; પરંતુ, હે અર્જુન, અભ્યાસ અને વૈરાગ્ય વડે તેને વશ કરી શકાય છે."},{"ref":"6.36","ch":6,"v":36,"sa":"असंयतात्मना योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः।\nवश्यात्मना तु यतता शक्योऽवाप्तुमुपायतः।।6.36।।","tr":"asaṅyatātmanā yogo duṣhprāpa iti me matiḥ\nvaśhyātmanā tu yatatā śhakyo ’vāptum upāyataḥ","en":"I think Yoga is hard to be attained by one with an uncontrolled self, but the self-controlled and striving one can attain it by the appropriate means.","es":"My conviction is that Yoga is difficult to attain for one with an uncontrolled mind. But it is possible to attain through the aforementioned means for one who strives and has a controlled mind.","er":"In my opinion, Yoga is hard to attain by a person of an unrestrained mind; however, it can be attained through the right means by one who strives for it and has a subdued mind.","gu":"જેણે મન ઉપર સંયમ નથી, તેના માટે યોગ ખરેખર પ્રાપ્ત કરવો કઠિન છે; પરંતુ જે આત્મ-સંયમી છે, તે ઉચિત ઉપાય વડે અવશ્ય સફળ થઈ શકે — આ મારો મત છે."},{"ref":"6.37","ch":6,"v":37,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nअयतिः श्रद्धयोपेतो योगाच्चलितमानसः।\nअप्राप्य योगसंसिद्धिं कां गतिं कृष्ण गच्छति।।6.37।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nayatiḥ śhraddhayopeto yogāch chalita-mānasaḥ\naprāpya yoga-sansiddhiṁ kāṅ gatiṁ kṛiṣhṇa gachchhati","en":"Arjuna said, \"He who is unable to control himself, even though he has faith, and whose mind wanders away from Yoga, what end does he meet, having failed to attain perfection in Yoga, O Krishna?\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Krsna, what goal does one attain who, despite having faith, fails to achieve perfection in Yoga due to lack of diligence, and whose mind becomes deflected from Yoga?\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"If a person who is possessed of faith but has put in only inadequate effort finds his mind wandering away from Yoga, and then fails to attain perfection—what way does he go, O Krishna?\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે કૃષ્ણ, જે યોગ ભ્રષ્ટ થઈ ગયો — જેની શ્રદ્ધા હતી પણ ખંત ન ટક્યો, અને જેનું મન યોગ માર્ગ છોડી ભટકી ગયું — એ સાધકની શી ગતિ થાય?"},{"ref":"6.38","ch":6,"v":38,"sa":"कच्चिन्नोभयविभ्रष्टश्छिन्नाभ्रमिव नश्यति।\nअप्रतिष्ठो महाबाहो विमूढो ब्रह्मणः पथि।।6.38।।","tr":"kachchin nobhaya-vibhraṣhṭaśh chhinnābhram iva naśhyati\napratiṣhṭho mahā-bāho vimūḍho brahmaṇaḥ pathi","en":"Fallen from both, does he not perish like a rent cloud, supportless, O mighty-armed one, deluded on the path of Brahman?","es":"O Mighty-armed one, having fallen from both [paths], without support, deluded on the path to Brahman, does he not get ruined like a scattered cloud?","er":"Without any support, confused in the path leading to the Brahman, and thus having fallen from both, does he not perish, O mighty-armed one, like a rent cloud?","gu":"આ પ્રમાણે ઉભય માર્ગ ભ્રષ્ટ થઈ, આશ્રય વિના, બ્રહ્મ-પ્રાપ્તિના માર્ગ ઉપર ભ્રમિત — શું એ, વિખરાઈ ગયેલા વાદળ સમ, નષ્ટ નથી થઈ જતો?"},{"ref":"6.39","ch":6,"v":39,"sa":"एतन्मे संशयं कृष्ण छेत्तुमर्हस्यशेषतः।\nत्वदन्यः संशयस्यास्य छेत्ता न ह्युपपद्यते।।6.39।।","tr":"etan me sanśhayaṁ kṛiṣhṇa chhettum arhasyaśheṣhataḥ\ntvad-anyaḥ sanśhayasyāsya chhettā na hyupapadyate","en":"O Krishna, please completely dispel this doubt of mine, for it is not possible for anyone but You to do so.","es":"O Krsna, you should totally eradicate this doubt of mine, for none other than yourself can be the dispeller of this doubt!","er":"O Krsna, you should altogether remove this doubt of mine, for there is no other remover of this doubt than you.","gu":"હે કૃષ્ણ, મારા આ સંશયને સંપૂર્ણ રીતે દૂર કરો; કારણ કે આ સંશયને નષ્ટ કરવા માટે તમારા સિવાય બીજો કોઈ સમર્થ નથી."},{"ref":"6.40","ch":6,"v":40,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nपार्थ नैवेह नामुत्र विनाशस्तस्य विद्यते।\nनहि कल्याणकृत्कश्िचद्दुर्गतिं तात गच्छति।।6.40।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\npārtha naiveha nāmutra vināśhas tasya vidyate\nna hi kalyāṇa-kṛit kaśhchid durgatiṁ tāta gachchhati","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O Arjuna, neither in this world nor in the next will there be destruction for him; none, indeed, who does good, O my son, ever comes to grief.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O Partha, there is certainly no ruin for him here or hereafter, for no one engaged in good meets with a deplorable end, my son!\"","er":"The Lord said, \"Neither here in this world nor there in the next is there destruction for him. For no one who does good ever comes to an evil end.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે અર્જુન, આ લોકમાં કે પરલોકમાં એવા પુરુષનો નાશ થતો નથી; જે સારાં કર્મ કરે છે, હે પ્રિય, તે કદી દુઃખ પામતો નથી."},{"ref":"6.41","ch":6,"v":41,"sa":"प्राप्य पुण्यकृतां लोकानुषित्वा शाश्वतीः समाः।\nशुचीनां श्रीमतां गेहे योगभ्रष्टोऽभिजायते।।6.41।।","tr":"prāpya puṇya-kṛitāṁ lokān uṣhitvā śhāśhvatīḥ samāḥ\nśhuchīnāṁ śhrīmatāṁ gehe yoga-bhraṣhṭo’bhijāyate","en":"Having attained to the worlds of the righteous and having dwelt there for everlasting years, he who fell from Yoga is born in a house of the pure and wealthy.","es":"Attaining the worlds of the righteous and residing there for eternal years, the man who has fallen from Yoga is born in the house of the pious and prosperous.","er":"He who has fallen away from Yoga is born again in the house of the pure and prosperous, having attained to the worlds of doers of good deeds and dwelled there for many long years.","gu":"ધર્માત્માઓના ઉત્તમ લોકો પ્રાપ્ત કરીને અને ત્યાં અનેક વર્ષો સુધી નિવાસ કર્યા પછી, પતિત યોગી ધનવાન અને ઉમદા કુળમાં ફરી જન્મ ધારણ કરે છે."},{"ref":"6.42","ch":6,"v":42,"sa":"अथवा योगिनामेव कुले भवति धीमताम्।\nएतद्धि दुर्लभतरं लोके जन्म यदीदृशम्।।6.42।।","tr":"atha vā yoginām eva kule bhavati dhīmatām\netad dhi durlabhataraṁ loke janma yad īdṛiśham","en":"Or he is born in a family of even the wisest of yogis; verily, such a birth is very difficult to obtain in this world.","es":"Or, he is born in the family of wise yogis. Such a birth is indeed more difficult to come by in the world.","er":"Or he is born into a family of wise yogis. But such a birth in this world is rare.","gu":"અથવા તો તે જ્ઞાની યોગીઓના કુળમાં જ જન્મ લે છે; ખરેખર, આ જગતમાં આવો જન્મ મળવો અત્યંત દુર્લભ છે."},{"ref":"6.43","ch":6,"v":43,"sa":"तत्र तं बुद्धिसंयोगं लभते पौर्वदेहिकम्।\nयतते च ततो भूयः संसिद्धौ कुरुनन्दन।।6.43।।","tr":"tatra taṁ buddhi-sanyogaṁ labhate paurva-dehikam\nyatate cha tato bhūyaḥ sansiddhau kuru-nandana","en":"Then he comes into contact with the knowledge acquired in his former body and strives even more for perfection, O Arjuna.","es":"There he becomes endowed with the wisdom acquired in the previous body, and he strives even more than before for perfection, O scion of the Kuru dynasty.","er":"There, O Arjuna, he regains the disposition of mind that he had in his former body, and from there he strives even more for success in Yoga.","gu":"ત્યાં તે પૂર્વ જન્મોમાં ઉપાર્જિત જ્ઞાનને ફરી પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે અને, હે કુરુવંશી, પહેલાં કરતાં પણ વધુ ઉત્સાહથી સિદ્ધિ તરફ આગળ વધે છે."},{"ref":"6.44","ch":6,"v":44,"sa":"पूर्वाभ्यासेन तेनैव ह्रियते ह्यवशोऽपि सः।\nजिज्ञासुरपि योगस्य शब्दब्रह्मातिवर्तते।।6.44।।","tr":"pūrvābhyāsena tenaiva hriyate hyavaśho ’pi saḥ\njijñāsur api yogasya śhabda-brahmātivartate","en":"By that same former practice, he is borne on in spite of himself. Even he who merely wishes to know Yoga goes beyond the Brahmanic word.","es":"For, by that very past practice, he is carried forward even in spite of himself! Even a seeker of Yoga transcends the results of the performance of Vedic rituals!","er":"By the power of his earlier practice, he is carried forward even against his will. Even though he is an enquirer about Yoga, he transcends the Sabda-Brahman, i.e., Prakṛti or matter.","gu":"પૂર્વ અભ્યાસના બળે તે ઇચ્છા ન હોય તો પણ સ્વાભાવિક રીતે ખેંચાઈ જાય છે; જે કોઈ માત્ર યોગ જાણવાની ઇચ્છા રાખે, તે પણ વેદના ઉપચારિક કર્મ-ફળ-ભોગથી ઊંચો ઊઠી જાય છે."},{"ref":"6.45","ch":6,"v":45,"sa":"प्रयत्नाद्यतमानस्तु योगी संशुद्धकिल्बिषः।\nअनेकजन्मसंसिद्धस्ततो याति परां गतिम्।।6.45।।","tr":"prayatnād yatamānas tu yogī sanśhuddha-kilbiṣhaḥ\naneka-janma-sansiddhas tato yāti parāṁ gatim","en":"But the Yogi who strives assiduously, purified of sins and perfected gradually over many births, reaches the highest goal.","es":"However, the yogi, applying himself assiduously, becoming purified from sin and attaining perfection through many births, they achieve the highest Goal.","er":"But the yogi, striving earnestly, cleansed of all his stains and perfected through many births, reaches the supreme state.","gu":"પ્રયત્નપૂર્વક સાધના કરતો, પાપોથી શુદ્ધ થઈ, અનેક જન્મોમાં ક્રમશઃ સિદ્ધ બનેલ યોગી અંતતઃ પરમ ગતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"6.46","ch":6,"v":46,"sa":"तपस्विभ्योऽधिको योगी ज्ञानिभ्योऽपि मतोऽधिकः।\nकर्मिभ्यश्चाधिको योगी तस्माद्योगी भवार्जुन।।6.46।।","tr":"tapasvibhyo ’dhiko yogī\njñānibhyo ’pi mato ’dhikaḥ\nkarmibhyaśh chādhiko yogī\ntasmād yogī bhavārjuna","en":"The yogi is thought to be superior to the ascetics, even superior to those who have knowledge obtained through the study of scriptures; he is also superior to men of action; therefore, be thou a yogi, O Arjuna.","es":"A yogi is higher than those of austerity; they are considered higher even than those of knowledge. The yogi is also higher than those of action. Therefore, O Arjuna, become a yogi.","er":"Greater than the ascetics, greater than those who possess knowledge, greater than the ritualists is the Yogin. Therefore, O Arjuna, become a Yogin.","gu":"યોગી તપસ્વીઓ કરતાં, જ્ઞાનીઓ કરતાં અને કર્મ-કાંડ-નિષ્ઠ કરતાં પણ શ્રેષ્ઠ છે; માટે, હે અર્જુન, તું યોગી બન."},{"ref":"6.47","ch":6,"v":47,"sa":"योगिनामपि सर्वेषां मद्गतेनान्तरात्मना।\nश्रद्धावान्भजते यो मां स मे युक्ततमो मतः।।6.47।।","tr":"yoginām api sarveṣhāṁ mad-gatenāntar-ātmanā\nśhraddhāvān bhajate yo māṁ sa me yuktatamo mataḥ","en":"And among all the Yogis, he who, full of faith and with his inner self merged in Me, worships Me is deemed by Me to be the most devoted.","es":"Even among all the yogis, he who adores Me with his mind fixed on Me and with faith is considered by Me to be the best of the yogis.","er":"He who, with faith, worships Me, and whose innermost self is fixed in Me, I consider him to be the greatest of the Yogins.","gu":"અને સર્વ યોગીઓમાં, જે પોતાના અંતઃકરણને મારામાં ઓગાળી, શ્રદ્ધાભક્તિથી મારી ઉપાસના કરે છે — તે યોગીને હું સૌથી વધુ ભક્તિવાળો માનું છું."},{"ref":"7.1","ch":7,"v":1,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nमय्यासक्तमनाः पार्थ योगं युञ्जन्मदाश्रयः।\nअसंशयं समग्रं मां यथा ज्ञास्यसि तच्छृणु।।7.1।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nmayyāsakta-manāḥ pārtha yogaṁ yuñjan mad-āśhrayaḥ\nasanśhayaṁ samagraṁ māṁ yathā jñāsyasi tach chhṛiṇu","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O Arjuna, hear how you shall, without doubt, know Me fully, with your mind intent on Me, practicing Yoga and taking refuge in Me.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O Partha, hear how, with your mind fixed on Me, practicing the Yoga of Meditation and taking refuge in Me, you will certainly and fully know Me.","er":"The Lord said, \"With your mind focused on Me, taking Me as your support, and practicing yoga—how can you, without doubt, know Me fully? Hear, O Arjuna.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે અર્જુન, મારામાં ચિત્ત લગાડી, મારો આશ્રય લઈ, યોગ-અભ્યાસ કરતાં, તું કઈ રીતે મને સંપૂર્ણ અને નિઃસંશય જાણી શકીશ, તે સાંભળ."},{"ref":"7.2","ch":7,"v":2,"sa":"ज्ञानं तेऽहं सविज्ञानमिदं वक्ष्याम्यशेषतः।\nयज्ज्ञात्वा नेह भूयोऽन्यज्ज्ञातव्यमवशिष्यते।।7.2।।","tr":"jñānaṁ te ’haṁ sa-vijñānam idaṁ vakṣhyāmyaśheṣhataḥ\nyaj jñātvā neha bhūyo ’nyaj jñātavyam-avaśhiṣhyate","en":"I will declare to you in full this knowledge combined with realization, after knowing which nothing else remains to be known here.","es":"I shall tell you in detail of this Knowledge, which is combined with realization, after experiencing which there remains nothing else here to be known.","er":"I will declare to you in full this knowledge of God, along with the knowledge that makes it distinguished, knowing which nothing else remains to be known.","gu":"હું તને વિજ્ઞાન સહિત આ સંપૂર્ણ જ્ઞાન ઉપદેશ આપીશ, જે જાણ્યા પછી આ સંસારમાં બીજું કંઈ જાણવાનું બાકી રહેતું નથી."},{"ref":"7.3","ch":7,"v":3,"sa":"मनुष्याणां सहस्रेषु कश्िचद्यतति सिद्धये।\nयततामपि सिद्धानां कश्िचन्मां वेत्ति तत्त्वतः।।7.3।।","tr":"manuṣhyāṇāṁ sahasreṣhu kaśhchid yatati siddhaye\nyatatām api siddhānāṁ kaśhchin māṁ vetti tattvataḥ","en":"Among thousands of men, one may perchance strive for perfection; even among those successful strivers, only one may perchance know Me in essence.","es":"Among thousands of men, a rare one endeavors for perfection. Even among the perfected ones who are diligent, one perchance knows Me in truth.","er":"Among thousands of men, some strive for perfection; even among those who strive for perfection, only some know Me; and among those who know Me, only some truly know Me.","gu":"હજારો મનુષ્યોમાં ભાગ્યે જ કોઈ સિદ્ધિ માટે પ્રયત્ન કરે છે; અને એ પ્રયત્ન કરનાર, સિદ્ધ પામેલ માણસોમાં ભાગ્યે જ કોઈ મને સાચા સ્વરૂપે ઓળખે છે."},{"ref":"7.4","ch":7,"v":4,"sa":"भूमिरापोऽनलो वायुः खं मनो बुद्धिरेव च।\nअहङ्कार इतीयं मे भिन्ना प्रकृतिरष्टधा।।7.4।।","tr":"bhūmir-āpo ’nalo vāyuḥ khaṁ mano buddhir eva cha\nahankāra itīyaṁ me bhinnā prakṛitir aṣhṭadhā","en":"Earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intellect, and egoism—thus is My Nature divided eightfold.","es":"This Prakrti of Mine is divided eightfold thus: earth, water, fire, air, space, mind, intellect, and egoism.","er":"Earth, water, fire, air, ether, Manas, Buddhi, and the ego-sense—thus My Prakriti is divided into eight parts.","gu":"પૃથ્વી, જળ, અગ્નિ, વાયુ, આકાશ, મન, બુદ્ધિ અને અહંકાર — આ આઠ ભાગોમાં વિભક્ત મારી અષ્ટધા પ્રકૃતિ છે."},{"ref":"7.5","ch":7,"v":5,"sa":"अपरेयमितस्त्वन्यां प्रकृतिं विद्धि मे पराम्।\nजीवभूतां महाबाहो ययेदं धार्यते जगत्।।7.5।।","tr":"apareyam itas tvanyāṁ prakṛitiṁ viddhi me parām\njīva-bhūtāṁ mahā-bāho yayedaṁ dhāryate jagat","en":"O mighty-armed Arjuna, this is the inferior Prakriti; know it as distinct from My higher Prakriti, the very life-element, by which this world is upheld.","es":"O mighty-armed one, this is the inferior Prakrti. Know the other Prakrti of Mine, which is however higher than this, which has taken the form of individual souls, and by which this world is upheld.","er":"This is My lower Prakṛti. But, O mighty-armed one, know that My higher nature is another. It is the life-principle (Jīva-bhūta), by which this universe is sustained.","gu":"આ મારી અપરા (નિમ્ન) પ્રકૃતિ છે; આ સિવાય, હે મહાબાહો, મારી જે પરા (ઉચ્ચ) પ્રકૃતિ છે — જે ચૈતન્ય-શક્તિ રૂપે સમગ્ર સૃષ્ટિને ધારણ કરે છે — તેને જુદી જ જાણ."},{"ref":"7.6","ch":7,"v":6,"sa":"एतद्योनीनि भूतानि सर्वाणीत्युपधारय।\nअहं कृत्स्नस्य जगतः प्रभवः प्रलयस्तथा।।7.6।।","tr":"etad-yonīni bhūtāni sarvāṇītyupadhāraya\nahaṁ kṛitsnasya jagataḥ prabhavaḥ pralayas tathā","en":"Know that these two are the womb of all beings; thus, I am the source and dissolution of the whole universe.","es":"Understand thus that all things—sentient and insentient—have these as their source. I am the origin as well as the end of the entire universe.","er":"Know that all beings have these two as the source of their birth. Therefore, I am the origin and the dissolver of the whole universe.","gu":"જાણ કે આ બન્ને પ્રકૃતિઓ સર્વ ભૂત-પ્રાણીઓના ઉત્પત્તિનું મૂળ છે; હું જ સમસ્ત સૃષ્ટિનો આદિ-ઉત્પત્તિ-કર્તા અને અંત-પ્રલય-કર્તા છું."},{"ref":"7.7","ch":7,"v":7,"sa":"मत्तः परतरं नान्यत्किञ्चिदस्ति धनञ्जय।\nमयि सर्वमिदं प्रोतं सूत्रे मणिगणा इव।।7.7।।","tr":"mattaḥ parataraṁ nānyat kiñchid asti dhanañjaya\nmayi sarvam idaṁ protaṁ sūtre maṇi-gaṇā iva","en":"There is nothing higher than Me, O Arjuna. All this is strung on Me, like clusters of gems on a string.","es":"O Dhananjaya, there is nothing else higher than Myself. All this is strung on Me like pearls on a string.","er":"There is nothing higher than Me, O Arjuna. All this is strung on Me, like rows of gems on a thread.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, મારાથી ઉપર કંઈ નથી. આ સઘળું વિશ્વ મારામાં પરોવાયેલું છે, જેમ દોરામાં મણકા પરોવાયેલા હોય."},{"ref":"7.8","ch":7,"v":8,"sa":"रसोऽहमप्सु कौन्तेय प्रभास्मि शशिसूर्ययोः।\nप्रणवः सर्ववेदेषु शब्दः खे पौरुषं नृषु।।7.8।।","tr":"raso ’ham apsu kaunteya prabhāsmi śhaśhi-sūryayoḥ\npraṇavaḥ sarva-vedeṣhu śhabdaḥ khe pauruṣhaṁ nṛiṣhu","en":"I am the flavor in water, O Arjuna; I am the light in the moon and the sun; I am the syllable Om in all the Vedas, sound in the ether and virility in men.","es":"O son of Kunti, I am the taste of water, I am the effulgence of the moon and the sun; the letter 'Om' in all the Vedas, the sound in space, and manhood in men.","er":"I am the taste in the waters, O Arjuna! I am the light in the sun and the moon; the sacred syllable Om in all the Vedas; sound in the ether; and manhood in men, I am.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, હું જળમાં રસ છું, સૂર્ય અને ચંદ્રમાં પ્રકાશ છું, સર્વ વેદોમાં ઓમ્ સ્વર છું, આકાશમાં નાદ છું અને મનુષ્યોમાં પૌરુષ છું."},{"ref":"7.9","ch":7,"v":9,"sa":"पुण्यो गन्धः पृथिव्यां च तेजश्चास्मि विभावसौ।\nजीवनं सर्वभूतेषु तपश्चास्मि तपस्विषु।।7.9।।","tr":"puṇyo gandhaḥ pṛithivyāṁ cha tejaśh chāsmi vibhāvasau\njīvanaṁ sarva-bhūteṣhu tapaśh chāsmi tapasviṣhu","en":"I am the sweet fragrance in the earth and the brilliance in the fire, the life in all beings, and I am the austerity of ascetics.","es":"I am also the sweet fragrance in the earth; I am the brilliance in the fire, and the life in all beings; and I am the austerity of the ascetics.","er":"I am the pure scent in the earth; I am the radiance in the fire; I am the life-force in all beings, and austerity in ascetics.","gu":"હું પૃથ્વીમાં સુગંધ છું, અગ્નિમાં તેજ છું, સર્વ પ્રાણીઓમાં જીવન છું, અને તપસ્વીઓમાં તપ છું."},{"ref":"7.10","ch":7,"v":10,"sa":"बीजं मां सर्वभूतानां विद्धि पार्थ सनातनम्।\nबुद्धिर्बुद्धिमतामस्मि तेजस्तेजस्विनामहम्।।7.10।।","tr":"bījaṁ māṁ sarva-bhūtānāṁ viddhi pārtha sanātanam\nbuddhir buddhimatām asmi tejas tejasvinām aham","en":"Know Me, O Arjuna, as the eternal seed of all beings; I am the intelligence of the intelligent, and the splendour of the splendid objects.","es":"O Partha, know Me to be the eternal seed of all beings. I am the intellect of the intelligent, and I am the courage of the courageous.","er":"Know Me, O Arjuna, to be the primeval seed of all beings. I am the intelligence of the discerning and the brilliance of the brilliant.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, મને સઘળા પ્રાણીઓનું સનાતન બીજ જાણ. હું બુદ્ધિમાનોની બુદ્ધિ છું અને તેજસ્વી પુરુષોનું તેજ છું."},{"ref":"7.11","ch":7,"v":11,"sa":"बलं बलवतां चाहं कामरागविवर्जितम्।\nधर्माविरुद्धो भूतेषु कामोऽस्मि भरतर्षभ।।7.11।।","tr":"balaṁ balavatāṁ chāhaṁ kāma-rāga-vivarjitam\ndharmāviruddho bhūteṣhu kāmo ’smi bharatarṣhabha","en":"Of the strong, I am the strength devoid of desire and attachment, and in all beings, I am the desire in accordance with Dharma, O Arjuna.","es":"And of the strong, I am the strength that is devoid of passion and attachment. Among creatures, I am desire that is not contrary to righteousness, O scion of the Bharata dynasty.","er":"In the strong, I am strength, devoid of desire and passion. In all beings, I am the desire which is not contrary to Dharma, O Arjuna.","gu":"હું બળવાનોનું બળ છું, પરંતુ તે ઈચ્છા અને આસક્તિ રહિત છે. હે ભારતશ્રેષ્ઠ, ધર્મ વિરુદ્ધ ન હોય તેવી ઈચ્છા હું પ્રાણીઓમાં છું."},{"ref":"7.12","ch":7,"v":12,"sa":"ये चैव सात्त्विका भावा राजसास्तामसाश्च ये।\nमत्त एवेति तान्विद्धि नत्वहं तेषु ते मयि।।7.12।।","tr":"ye chaiva sāttvikā bhāvā rājasās tāmasāśh cha ye\nmatta eveti tān viddhi na tvahaṁ teṣhu te mayi","en":"Whatever beings (and objects) that are pure, active, and inert, know that they proceed from Me. They are in Me, yet I am not in them.","es":"Those things that are made of the quality of sattva, and those things that are made of the quality of rajas and tamas, know them to have sprung from Me alone. However, I am not in them; they are within Me!","er":"Know that all those states of Sattva, Rajas, and Tamas are from Me alone; however, I am not in them; rather, they are in Me.","gu":"જાણ કે સત્ત્વ, રજ અને તમ — આ ત્રણ ગુણોમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન થતા સઘળા ભાવ મારાથી જ છે. હું તેમનામાં નથી, પરંતુ તે મારામાં છે."},{"ref":"7.13","ch":7,"v":13,"sa":"त्रिभिर्गुणमयैर्भावैरेभिः सर्वमिदं जगत्।\nमोहितं नाभिजानाति मामेभ्यः परमव्ययम्।।7.13।।","tr":"tribhir guṇa-mayair bhāvair ebhiḥ sarvam idaṁ jagat\nmohitaṁ nābhijānāti māmebhyaḥ param avyayam","en":"Deluded by these Natures, composed of the three qualities of Nature, all this world does not know Me as distinct from them and immutable.","es":"All this world, deluded as it is by these three qualities made of the gunas, does not know Me, who am transcendental to these and undecaying.","er":"The entire universe is deluded by these three states originating from the Gunas (of Prakrti), and fails to recognize Me, who am beyond them and immutable.","gu":"આ ત્રણ ગુણોથી મોહિત થઈ આ સારું જગત મને — ત્રિગુણથી પર અને અવ્યયને — ઓળખી શકતું નથી."},{"ref":"7.14","ch":7,"v":14,"sa":"दैवी ह्येषा गुणमयी मम माया दुरत्यया।\nमामेव ये प्रपद्यन्ते मायामेतां तरन्ति ते।।7.14।।","tr":"daivī hyeṣhā guṇa-mayī mama māyā duratyayā\nmām eva ye prapadyante māyām etāṁ taranti te","en":"Verily, this divine illusion of Mine, composed of the three qualities, is difficult to cross over; those who take refuge in Me alone, can cross over this illusion.","es":"Since this divine Maya of Mine, which is constituted by the gunas, is difficult to cross over, those who take refuge in Me alone can transcend this Maya.","er":"(a) For this divine Maya or Mine, consisting of the three Gunas (assumed for purposes of sport), is hard to overcome.\n৷৷\n(b) ৷৷ But those who take refuge in Me alone shall pass beyond the Maya.","gu":"ત્રણ ગુણોથી બનેલી આ મારી દૈવી માયા ઓળંગવી ઘણી કઠિન છે; પરંતુ જે લોકો એકમાત્ર મારે શરણે આવે છે, તેઓ આ માયાને પાર કરી જાય છે."},{"ref":"7.15","ch":7,"v":15,"sa":"न मां दुष्कृतिनो मूढाः प्रपद्यन्ते नराधमाः।\nमाययापहृतज्ञाना आसुरं भावमाश्रिताः।।7.15।।","tr":"na māṁ duṣhkṛitino mūḍhāḥ prapadyante narādhamāḥ\nmāyayāpahṛita-jñānā āsuraṁ bhāvam āśhritāḥ","en":"The evil-doers and the deluded, who are the lowest of men, do not seek Me; those whose knowledge is destroyed by illusion follow the ways of demons.","es":"The foolish evildoers, who are the most depraved among men, who are deprived of their wisdom by Maya, and who resort to demonic ways, do not take refuge in Me.","er":"The evil-doers, the foolish, the lowest of men, those persons deprived of knowledge by delusion (Maya) and those who are dominated by a demoniac nature - they do not seek refuge in Me.","gu":"જે લોકો દુષ્ટ આચારણ કરે છે, જે મનુષ્યોમાં અધમ છે, જે માયાથી જ્ઞાન હણાઈ ગયું છે, અને જે આસુરી સ્વભાવને અનુસરે છે — તેઓ મારે શરણ આવતા નથી."},{"ref":"7.16","ch":7,"v":16,"sa":"चतुर्विधा भजन्ते मां जनाः सुकृतिनोऽर्जुन।\nआर्तो जिज्ञासुरर्थार्थी ज्ञानी च भरतर्षभ।।7.16।।","tr":"chatur-vidhā bhajante māṁ janāḥ sukṛitino ’rjuna\nārto jijñāsur arthārthī jñānī cha bharatarṣhabha","en":"Four kinds of virtuous men worship Me, O Arjuna, and they are the distressed, the seekers of knowledge, the seekers of wealth, and the wise, O Lord of the Bharatas.","es":"O Arjuna, foremost of the Bharata dynasty, four classes of people of virtuous deeds adore Me: the afflicted, the seekers of Knowledge, the seekers of wealth, and the man of Knowledge.","er":"Four types of men of good deeds worship Me, O Arjuna: the distressed, the seekers of knowledge, the seekers of wealth, and the men of knowledge.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, ચાર પ્રકારના સત્કર્મ કરનારા લોકો મારી ભક્તિ કરે છે: આર્ત, જિજ્ઞાસુ, અર્થાર્થી અને જ્ઞાની."},{"ref":"7.17","ch":7,"v":17,"sa":"तेषां ज्ञानी नित्ययुक्त एकभक्ितर्विशिष्यते।\nप्रियो हि ज्ञानिनोऽत्यर्थमहं स च मम प्रियः।।7.17।।","tr":"teṣhāṁ jñānī nitya-yukta eka-bhaktir viśhiṣhyate\npriyo hi jñānino ’tyartham ahaṁ sa cha mama priyaḥ","en":"Of them, the wise who are ever steadfast and devoted to the One, excel; for I am exceedingly dear to the wise, and they are dear to Me.","es":"Of them, the man of knowledge, endowed with constant steadfastness and one-pointed devotion, excels. For I am very dear to the man of knowledge, and he too is dear to me.","er":"Of these, the man of knowledge, who is ever with Me in Yoga and devoted to the One only, is the foremost; for I am very dear to the man of knowledge, and he is also dear to Me.","gu":"આ ચારેમાં જ્ઞાની, જે નિત્યયુક્ત અને એકભક્ત છે, તે શ્રેષ્ઠ છે. હું જ્ઞાનીને અત્યંત પ્રિય છું, અને જ્ઞાની મને પ્રિય છે."},{"ref":"7.18","ch":7,"v":18,"sa":"उदाराः सर्व एवैते ज्ञानी त्वात्मैव मे मतम्।\nआस्थितः स हि युक्तात्मा मामेवानुत्तमां गतिम्।।7.18।।","tr":"udārāḥ sarva evaite jñānī tvātmaiva me matam\nāsthitaḥ sa hi yuktātmā mām evānuttamāṁ gatim","en":"Indeed, all these are noble; however, I consider the wise man as My very Self; for, he is steadfast in mind and established in Me alone as the supreme goal.","es":"Indeed, all of these are noble, but the man of Knowledge is the Self itself. This is my opinion. For, with a steadfast mind, he is set on the path leading only to Me, who am the supreme Goal.","er":"All these are indeed generous, but I deem the man of knowledge to be My very self; for he, integrated, is devoted solely to Me as the highest end.","gu":"આ સૌ ઉદાર ભક્તો છે, પરંતુ જ્ઞાનીને હું મારો આત્મા જ ગણું છું; કારણ કે, મનને વશ રાખી, તે મને જ સર્વોચ્ચ ગતિ જાણી મારામાં સ્થિત છે."},{"ref":"7.19","ch":7,"v":19,"sa":"बहूनां जन्मनामन्ते ज्ञानवान्मां प्रपद्यते।\nवासुदेवः सर्वमिति स महात्मा सुदुर्लभः।।7.19।।","tr":"bahūnāṁ janmanām ante jñānavān māṁ prapadyate\nvāsudevaḥ sarvam iti sa mahātmā su-durlabhaḥ","en":"At the end of many births, the wise man comes to Me, realizing that all this is Vaasudeva (the innermost Self); such a great soul (Mahatma) is very hard to find.","es":"At the end of many births, the man of knowledge attains Me, realizing that Vasudeva is all. Such a high-souled one is very rare.","er":"At the end of many births, the man of knowledge finds refuge in Me, realizing that 'Vasudeva is all.' It is very difficult to find such a great-souled person.","gu":"અનેક જન્મોના અંતે જ્ઞાની 'વાસુદેવ સર્વ છે' — એ જ્ઞાન પ્રાપ્ત કરી મારે શરણ આવે છે. આવો મહાત્મા અત્યંત દુર્લભ છે."},{"ref":"7.20","ch":7,"v":20,"sa":"कामैस्तैस्तैर्हृतज्ञानाः प्रपद्यन्तेऽन्यदेवताः।\nतं तं नियममास्थाय प्रकृत्या नियताः स्वया।।7.20।।","tr":"kāmais tais tair hṛita-jñānāḥ prapadyante ’nya-devatāḥ\ntaṁ taṁ niyamam āsthāya prakṛityā niyatāḥ svayā","en":"Those whose wisdom has been taken away by this or that desire, go to other gods, following this or that rite, led by their own nature.","es":"People, deprived of their wisdom by desires for various objects and guided by their own nature, resort to other deities, following the relevant methods.","er":"Controlled by their inherent nature, and deprived of knowledge by various desires, worldly-minded people resort to other gods, observing various disciplines.","gu":"જેઓ ભૌતિક ઈચ્છાઓથી જ્ઞાન હર્યા-ભર્યા છે, તેઓ પોતાના સ્વભાવ અનુસાર ચાલીને, ભિન્ન-ભિન્ન નિયમ-વિધિઓ અપનાવી, અન્ય દેવ-દેવીઓ પ્રત્યે ઝૂકી જાય છે."},{"ref":"7.21","ch":7,"v":21,"sa":"यो यो यां यां तनुं भक्तः श्रद्धयार्चितुमिच्छति।\nतस्य तस्याचलां श्रद्धां तामेव विदधाम्यहम्।।7.21।।","tr":"yo yo yāṁ yāṁ tanuṁ bhaktaḥ śhraddhayārchitum ichchhati\ntasya tasyāchalāṁ śhraddhāṁ tām eva vidadhāmyaham","en":"Whatever form any devotee desires to worship with faith, I make that same faith of his firm and unflinching.","es":"Whichever form of a deity any devotee wants to worship with faith, I strengthen that very firm faith of theirs.","er":"Whichever devotee seeks to worship with faith whatever form, I make their faith steadfast.","gu":"ભક્ત જે પણ સ્વરૂપ પ્રત્યે શ્રદ્ધાપૂર્વક ભજન-પૂજન કરવા ઈચ્છે, તે સ્વરૂપ પ્રત્યે હું તેની શ્રદ્ધા અડગ અને દૃઢ બનાવું છું."},{"ref":"7.22","ch":7,"v":22,"sa":"स तया श्रद्धया युक्तस्तस्याराधनमीहते।\nलभते च ततः कामान्मयैव विहितान् हि तान्।।7.22।।","tr":"sa tayā śhraddhayā yuktas tasyārādhanam īhate\nlabhate cha tataḥ kāmān mayaiva vihitān hi tān","en":"Endowed with that faith, he engages in the worship of that form and obtains his desired outcome, which is ordained by Me alone.","es":"Being imbued with that faith, that person engages in worshipping that form, and they get those very desired results as dispensed by Me alone.","er":"Endowed with that faith, he worships that form and thereby gets the objects of his desire, granted in reality by Me alone.","gu":"એ શ્રદ્ધાથી યુક્ત થઈ તે ભક્ત તે દેવતાની પૂજા કરે છે અને ત્યાંથી ઇચ્છિત ફળ મેળવે છે — પરંતુ વાસ્તવમાં એ ફળ મારા દ્વારા જ અપાય છે."},{"ref":"7.23","ch":7,"v":23,"sa":"अन्तवत्तु फलं तेषां तद्भवत्यल्पमेधसाम्।\nदेवान्देवयजो यान्ति मद्भक्ता यान्ति मामपि।।7.23।।","tr":"antavat tu phalaṁ teṣhāṁ tad bhavatyalpa-medhasām\ndevān deva-yajo yānti mad-bhaktā yānti mām api","en":"Verily, the reward (fruit) that accrues to those men of small intelligence is finite. The worshippers of the gods go to them, whereas My devotees come to Me.","es":"The result of those who are of poor intellect is indeed limited. The worshippers of gods go to the gods, while My devotees go to Me alone.","er":"But the fruit gained by these men of small understanding is limited. The worshippers of the gods will go to the gods, but My devotees will come to Me.","gu":"પરંતુ અલ્પ બુદ્ધિ ધરાવતા લોકો જે ફળ મેળવે છે તે નાશવંત છે; દેવતાઓના ઉપાસકો દેવતાઓ પાસે જાય છે, જ્યારે મારા ભક્તો મારી પાસે આવે છે."},{"ref":"7.24","ch":7,"v":24,"sa":"अव्यक्तं व्यक्ितमापन्नं मन्यन्ते मामबुद्धयः।\nपरं भावमजानन्तो ममाव्ययमनुत्तमम्।।7.24।।","tr":"avyaktaṁ vyaktim āpannaṁ manyante mām abuddhayaḥ\nparaṁ bhāvam ajānanto mamāvyayam anuttamam","en":"The foolish think of Me, the Unmanifest, as having manifestation, not knowing My higher, immutable, and most excellent nature.","es":"The unintelligent, unaware of My supreme state which is immutable and unsurpassable, think of Me as having become manifest from the unmanifest.","er":"Not knowing My higher, immutable, and unsurpassed nature, the ignorant think of Me as an entity that has now become manifest, though I was previously unmanifest.","gu":"અવિવેકી મનુષ્યો મારી સર્વોચ્ચ, અવ્યય અને અત્યુત્તમ સ્વભાવને ન જાણતા, અવ્યક્ત એવા મને વ્યક્ત થયેલો સમજે છે."},{"ref":"7.25","ch":7,"v":25,"sa":"नाहं प्रकाशः सर्वस्य योगमायासमावृतः।\nमूढोऽयं नाभिजानाति लोको मामजमव्ययम्।।7.25।।","tr":"nāhaṁ prakāśhaḥ sarvasya yoga-māyā-samāvṛitaḥ\nmūḍho ’yaṁ nābhijānāti loko mām ajam avyayam","en":"I am not manifest to all, veiled as I am by the Yoga-Maya. This deluded world does not know Me, who am unborn and imperishable.","es":"Being enveloped by yoga-maya, I do not become manifest to all. This deluded world does not know Me, who am birthless and undecaying.","er":"Veiled by my Maya, I am not manifest to all; this deluded world does not recognize me as the unborn and immutable.","gu":"હું મારી દૈવી માયાથી ઢંકાયેલો હોવાથી સૌને પ્રત્યક્ષ થતો નથી; આ મૂઢ સંસાર મને — અજન્મા અને અવ્યયને — ઓળખી શકતો નથી."},{"ref":"7.26","ch":7,"v":26,"sa":"वेदाहं समतीतानि वर्तमानानि चार्जुन।\nभविष्याणि च भूतानि मां तु वेद न कश्चन।।7.26।।","tr":"vedāhaṁ samatītāni vartamānāni chārjuna\nbhaviṣhyāṇi cha bhūtāni māṁ tu veda na kaśhchana","en":"I know, O Arjuna, the beings of the past, the present, and the future; however, no one knows Me.","es":"O Arjuna, I know the past, present, and future beings; but no one knows Me!","er":"I know all beings, O Arjuna, past, present, and those to come; but no one knows Me.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, ભૂતકાળમાં થઈ ગયેલા, વર્તમાનમાં વિદ્યમાન અને ભવિષ્યમાં આવનારા સર્વ જીવોને હું જાણું છું, પરંતુ મને કોઈ જાણતું નથી."},{"ref":"7.27","ch":7,"v":27,"sa":"इच्छाद्वेषसमुत्थेन द्वन्द्वमोहेन भारत।\nसर्वभूतानि संमोहं सर्गे यान्ति परन्तप।।7.27।।","tr":"ichchhā-dveṣha-samutthena dvandva-mohena bhārata\nsarva-bhūtāni sammohaṁ sarge yānti parantapa","en":"O Bharata, all beings are subject to delusion at birth due to the delusion of the pairs of opposites arising from desire and aversion, O Parantapa.","es":"O scion of the Bharata dynasty, O destroyer of foes, due to the delusion of duality arising from likes and dislikes, all creatures become bewildered upon their birth.","er":"O Arjuna, all beings are deluded as soon as they are born, due to the delusion of the pairs of opposites springing from desire and hate.","gu":"હે ભારતવંશી, ઇચ્છા અને દ્વેષ — આ બે વિરોધી ભાવોના સંઘર્ષથી ઉત્પન્ન થતા મોહને કારણે સઘળા પ્રાણીઓ જન્મ સમયે ભ્રમમાં પડી જાય છે."},{"ref":"7.28","ch":7,"v":28,"sa":"येषां त्वन्तगतं पापं जनानां पुण्यकर्मणाम्।\nते द्वन्द्वमोहनिर्मुक्ता भजन्ते मां दृढव्रताः।।7.28।।","tr":"yeṣhāṁ tvanta-gataṁ pāpaṁ janānāṁ puṇya-karmaṇām\nte dvandva-moha-nirmuktā bhajante māṁ dṛiḍha-vratāḥ","en":"But those men of virtuous deeds, whose sins have come to an end and who are freed from the delusion of the pairs of opposites, worship Me steadfastly, with their vows.","es":"On the other hand, those persons who have done virtuous deeds, whose sin has come to an end, they, being free from the delusion of duality and firm in their convictions, adore Me.","er":"But those who have done good deeds, whose sins have come to an end, are freed from the delusion of the pairs of opposites. They steadfastly worship Me, adhering to their vows.","gu":"પરંતુ જે પુણ્યાત્માઓના પાપ નષ્ટ થઈ ગયા છે, તેઓ દ્વંદ્વ-મોહથી મુક્ત થઈ દૃઢ નિશ્ચયથી મારી ભક્તિ કરે છે."},{"ref":"7.29","ch":7,"v":29,"sa":"जरामरणमोक्षाय मामाश्रित्य यतन्ति ये।\nते ब्रह्म तद्विदुः कृत्स्नमध्यात्मं कर्म चाखिलम्।।7.29।।","tr":"jarā-maraṇa-mokṣhāya mām āśhritya yatanti ye\nte brahma tadviduḥ kṛitsnam adhyātmaṁ karma chākhilam","en":"Those who strive for liberation from old age and death, taking refuge in Me, realize in full that Brahman, the whole knowledge of the Self, and all action.","es":"Those who strive by resorting to Me for becoming free from old age and death, they know Brahman, the individual Self, and all about actions. [They know Brahman as being all the individual entities and all actions. This verse prescribes meditation on the qualified Brahman for aspirants of the middle class. Verses beginning with the 14th speak about the realization of the unqualified Brahman by aspirants of the highest class.]","er":"Those who take refuge in Me and strive for deliverance from old age and death, know Brahman (or the Self) and all about the nature of that Self, and the entire Karma (or activities leading to rebirth).","gu":"જેઓ જન્મ-મૃત્યુથી મુક્તિ માટે મારો આશ્રય લઈ પ્રયત્ન કરે છે, તેઓ બ્રહ્મ, અધ્યાત્મ અને સંપૂર્ણ કર્મ-ક્ષેત્રને જાણે છે."},{"ref":"7.30","ch":7,"v":30,"sa":"साधिभूताधिदैवं मां साधियज्ञं च ये विदुः।\nप्रयाणकालेऽपि च मां ते विदुर्युक्तचेतसः।।7.30।।","tr":"sādhibhūtādhidaivaṁ māṁ sādhiyajñaṁ cha ye viduḥ\nprayāṇa-kāle ’pi cha māṁ te vidur yukta-chetasaḥ","en":"Those who know Me with the Adhibhuta (pertaining to the elements), Adhidaiva (pertaining to the gods), and the Adhiyajna (pertaining to the sacrifice) know Me even at the time of death, remaining steadfast in mind.","es":"Those who know me as existing in both the physical and divine planes, and also in the context of the sacrifice, they with concentrated minds know me even at the time of death.","er":"And those who know Me with the Adhibhuta, Adhidaiva, and Adhiyajna, they too, with their minds fixed in meditation, know Me even at the hour of death.","gu":"જેઓ મને અધિભૂત, અધિદૈવ અને અધિયજ્ઞ સહિત જાણે છે, તેઓ મૃત્યુ-સમયે પણ સ્થિર ચિત્તે મને ઓળખે છે."},{"ref":"8.1","ch":8,"v":1,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nकिं तद्ब्रह्म किमध्यात्मं किं कर्म पुरुषोत्तम।\nअधिभूतं च किं प्रोक्तमधिदैवं किमुच्यते।।8.1।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nkiṁ tad brahma kim adhyātmaṁ kiṁ karma puruṣhottama\nadhibhūtaṁ cha kiṁ proktam adhidaivaṁ kim uchyate","en":"Arjuna said, \"What is Brahman? What is Adhyatma? What is action, O best among men? What is Adhibhuta declared to be? And, what is Adhidaiva said to be?\"","es":"Arjuna said, O Supreme Person, what is Brahman? What exists in the individual plane? What is action? What is said to exist in the physical plane? And what is said to exist in the divine plane?","er":"Arjuna said, O Supreme Person, what is Brahman? What exists in the individual plane? What is action? What is said to exist in the physical plane? And what is said to exist in the divine plane?","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે પુરુષોત્તમ, તે બ્રહ્મ શું છે? અધ્યાત્મ શું છે? કર્મ શું છે? અધિભૂત કોને કહેવાય? અધિદૈવ કોને કહેવાય?"},{"ref":"8.2","ch":8,"v":2,"sa":"अधियज्ञः कथं कोऽत्र देहेऽस्मिन्मधुसूदन।\nप्रयाणकाले च कथं ज्ञेयोऽसि नियतात्मभिः।।8.2।।","tr":"adhiyajñaḥ kathaṁ ko ’tra dehe ’smin madhusūdana\nprayāṇa-kāle cha kathaṁ jñeyo ’si niyatātmabhiḥ","en":"Who and how is Adhiyajna here in this body, O destroyer of Madhu? And how, at the time of death, are You to be known by the self-controlled?","es":"O Madhusudana, how is the entity existing in the sacrifice here in this body, and who is it? And how are You to be known by people of concentrated minds at the time of death?","er":"O Madhusudana, how is the entity existing in the sacrifice here in this body, and who is it? And how are You to be known by people of concentrated minds at the time of death?","gu":"અહીં આ શરીરમાં અધિયજ્ઞ કોણ છે અને કઈ રીતે? અને હે મધુસૂદન, આત્મ-સંયમી પુરુષો મૃત્યુ-સમયે આપને કઈ રીતે જાણે છે?"},{"ref":"8.3","ch":8,"v":3,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nअक्षरं ब्रह्म परमं स्वभावोऽध्यात्ममुच्यते।\nभूतभावोद्भवकरो विसर्गः कर्मसंज्ञितः।।8.3।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nakṣharaṁ brahma paramaṁ svabhāvo ’dhyātmam uchyate\nbhūta-bhāvodbhava-karo visargaḥ karma-sanjñitaḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"Brahman is the Imperishable, the Supreme; its essential nature is called Self-knowledge; the offering (to the gods) that causes the existence and manifestation of beings and sustains them is called action.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"The Immutable is the supreme Brahman; selfhood is said to be the entity present in the individual plane. By action is meant the offerings that bring about the origin of existence of things.\"","er":"The Blessed Lord said, \"The Immutable is the supreme Brahman; selfhood is said to be the entity present in the individual plane. By action is meant the offerings that bring about the origin of existence of things.\"","gu":"શ્રી કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: પરમ અક્ષર એ બ્રહ્મ છે; પોતાના સ્વભાવ-સ્વરૂપ અસ્તિત્વને અધ્યાત્મ કહે છે; અને પ્રાણીઓની ઉત્પત્તિ-સ્થિતિ-ગતિ કરનારી સૃષ્ટિ-શક્તિ એ કર્મ કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"8.4","ch":8,"v":4,"sa":"अधिभूतं क्षरो भावः पुरुषश्चाधिदैवतम्।\nअधियज्ञोऽहमेवात्र देहे देहभृतां वर।।8.4।।","tr":"adhibhūtaṁ kṣharo bhāvaḥ puruṣhaśh chādhidaivatam\nadhiyajño ’ham evātra dehe deha-bhṛitāṁ vara","en":"Adhibhuta—knowledge of the elements—pertains to My perishable nature, and the Purusha, or the Soul, is the Adhidaiva; I alone am the Adhiyajna here in this body, O best among the embodied.","es":"That which exists in the physical plane is the mutable entity, and what exists in the divine plane is the Person. O best among the embodied beings, I Myself am the entity that exists in the sacrifice within this body.","er":"That which exists in the physical plane is the mutable entity, and what exists in the divine plane is the Person. O best among the embodied beings, I Myself am the entity that exists in the sacrifice within this body.","gu":"ક્ષર ભૌતિક સ્વભાવ એ અધિભૂત છે; સૂર્ય-પ્રધાન ચૈતન્ય-પ્રકૃતિ એ અધિદૈવ છે; અને હે દેહધારીઓમાં શ્રેષ્ઠ, આ દેહમાં હું જ અધિયજ્ઞ છું."},{"ref":"8.5","ch":8,"v":5,"sa":"अन्तकाले च मामेव स्मरन्मुक्त्वा कलेवरम्।\nयः प्रयाति स मद्भावं याति नास्त्यत्र संशयः।।8.5।।","tr":"anta-kāle cha mām eva smaran muktvā kalevaram\nyaḥ prayāti sa mad-bhāvaṁ yāti nāstyatra sanśhayaḥ","en":"And whoever, leaving their body, goes forth remembering Me alone at the time of death, they will attain My Being; there is no doubt about this.","es":"And at the time of death, anyone who departs, giving up the body while thinking of Me alone, attains My state; there is no doubt about this.","er":"And at the time of death, anyone who departs, giving up the body while thinking of Me alone, attains My state; there is no doubt about this.","gu":"અને જે વ્યક્તિ અંત સમયે શરીર છોડતી વખતે કેવળ મને જ સ્મરણ કરે છે, તે મારા ભાવને પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે — આ વિષે કોઈ સંશય નથી."},{"ref":"8.6","ch":8,"v":6,"sa":"यं यं वापि स्मरन्भावं त्यजत्यन्ते कलेवरम्।\nतं तमेवैति कौन्तेय सदा तद्भावभावितः।।8.6।।","tr":"yaṁ yaṁ vāpi smaran bhāvaṁ tyajatyante kalevaram\ntaṁ tam evaiti kaunteya sadā tad-bhāva-bhāvitaḥ","en":"Whoever at the end leaves the body, thinking of any being, to that being only does he go, O son of Kunti (Arjuna), due to his constant thought of that being.","es":"O son of Kunti, thinking of any entity, whichever it may be, one gives up the body at the end; he attains that very one, having been always engrossed in its thought.","er":"O son of Kunti, thinking of any entity, whichever it may be, one gives up the body at the end; he attains that very one, having been always engrossed in its thought.","gu":"અંતકાળે મનુષ્ય જે ભાવ-સ્વભાવ સ્મરણ કરતો શરીર ત્યજે છે, સદૈવ એ ભાવમાં ઢળેલો હોવાથી, હે અર્જુન, તે તે ભાવ-ગતિ ને જ પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે."},{"ref":"8.7","ch":8,"v":7,"sa":"तस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु मामनुस्मर युध्य च।\nमय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्मामेवैष्यस्यसंशयम्।।8.7।।","tr":"tasmāt sarveṣhu kāleṣhu mām anusmara yudhya cha\nmayyarpita-mano-buddhir mām evaiṣhyasyasanśhayam","en":"Therefore, at all times, remember Me only and fight. With your mind and intellect fixed on Me, you will undoubtedly come to Me alone.","es":"Therefore, think of Me at all times and fight; there is no doubt that by dedicating your mind and intellect to Me, you will attain only Me.","er":"Therefore, think of Me at all times and fight; there is no doubt that by dedicating your mind and intellect to Me, you will attain only Me.","gu":"તેથી, હંમેશા મારું સ્મરણ કર અને યુદ્ધ કર. મન અને બુદ્ધિ મારામાં સ્થિર રાખીને, તું નિઃસંદેહ મને જ પ્રાપ્ત થઈશ."},{"ref":"8.8","ch":8,"v":8,"sa":"अभ्यासयोगयुक्तेन चेतसा नान्यगामिना।\nपरमं पुरुषं दिव्यं याति पार्थानुचिन्तयन्।।8.8।।","tr":"abhyāsa-yoga-yuktena chetasā nānya-gāminā\nparamaṁ puruṣhaṁ divyaṁ yāti pārthānuchintayan","en":"With the mind not moving towards any other thing, made steadfast through the practice of habitual meditation, and constantly meditating, one goes to the Supreme Person, the Resplendent, O Arjuna.","es":"O son of Prtha, by meditating with a mind engaged in the yoga of practice and not straying away to anything else, one reaches the supreme Person existing in the effulgent region.","er":"O son of Prtha, by meditating with a mind engaged in the yoga of practice and not straying away to anything else, one reaches the supreme Person existing in the effulgent region.","gu":"અભ્યાસ-યોગ વડે સ્મરણમાં સ્થિર મન, બીજે ક્યાંય ભટક્યા વિના, સ્થિર ચિત્તે જે ધ્યાન ધરે છે, તે પરમ દિવ્ય પુરુષને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે, હે અર્જુન."},{"ref":"8.9","ch":8,"v":9,"sa":"कविं पुराणमनुशासितार\nमणोरणीयांसमनुस्मरेद्यः।\nसर्वस्य धातारमचिन्त्यरूप\nमादित्यवर्णं तमसः परस्तात्।।8.9।।","tr":"kaviṁ purāṇam anuśhāsitāram\naṇor aṇīyānsam anusmared yaḥ\nsarvasya dhātāram achintya-rūpam\nāditya-varṇaṁ tamasaḥ parastāt","en":"Whosoever meditates on the Omniscient, the Ancient, the Ruler of the whole world, minuter than an atom, the supporter of all, of inconceivable form, effulgent like the sun and beyond the darkness of ignorance.","es":"He who meditates on the Omniscient, the Ancient, the Ruler, subtler than the subtle, the Ordainer of everything, of inconceivable form, effulgent like the sun, and beyond darkness—he attains the Supreme Person.","er":"He who meditates on the Omniscient, the Ancient, the Ruler, subtler than the subtle, the Ordainer of everything, of inconceivable form, effulgent like the sun, and beyond darkness—he attains the Supreme Person.","gu":"જે સર્વજ્ઞ, અનાદિ, સૌના નિયંતા, અણુ કરતાં પણ સૂક્ષ્મ, સૌના આધારરૂપ, અચિંત્ય સ્વરૂપ, સૂર્ય સમાન તેજસ્વી અને અંધકારથી પર છે — તેનું ધ્યાન ધરે છે."},{"ref":"8.10","ch":8,"v":10,"sa":"प्रयाणकाले मनसाऽचलेन\nभक्त्या युक्तो योगबलेन चैव।\nभ्रुवोर्मध्ये प्राणमावेश्य सम्यक्\nस तं परं पुरुषमुपैति दिव्यम्।।8.10।।","tr":"prayāṇa-kāle manasāchalena\nbhaktyā yukto yoga-balena chaiva\nbhruvor madhye prāṇam āveśhya samyak\nsa taṁ paraṁ puruṣham upaiti divyam","en":"At the time of death, with an unwavering mind, endowed with devotion, by the power of Yoga, fixing the whole life-breath in the middle of the two eyebrows, he reaches that resplendent Supreme Person.","es":"At the time of death, having fully fixed the Prana (vital force) between the eyebrows with an unwavering mind, and being imbued with devotion as well as the strength of concentration, he reaches that resplendent Supreme Person.","er":"At the time of death, having fully fixed the Prana (vital force) between the eyebrows with an unwavering mind, and being imbued with devotion as well as the strength of concentration, he reaches that resplendent Supreme Person.","gu":"મૃત્યુ સમયે, ભક્તિ અને યોગ-બળ સંપન્ન, અડોલ ચિત્તે, ભ્રૂ-મધ્યમાં સમગ્ર પ્રાણ-શક્તિ સ્થિર કરીને — તે પરમ દિવ્ય પુરુષને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"8.11","ch":8,"v":11,"sa":"यदक्षरं वेदविदो वदन्ति\nविशन्ति यद्यतयो वीतरागाः।\nयदिच्छन्तो ब्रह्मचर्यं चरन्ति\nतत्ते पदं संग्रहेण प्रवक्ष्ये।।8.11।।","tr":"yad akṣharaṁ veda-vido vadanti\nviśhanti yad yatayo vīta-rāgāḥ\nyad ichchhanto brahmacharyaṁ charanti\ntat te padaṁ saṅgraheṇa pravakṣhye","en":"That which is declared to be Imperishable by those who know the Vedas, that which the self-controlled (ascetics or Sannyasins) and passion-free enter, that goal, desiring which celibacy is practised, I will declare to thee in brief.","es":"I will briefly tell you about that immutable Goal which the knowers of the Vedas declare; those who are diligent, free from attachment, and aspire for it, enter into it. People practice celibacy for it.","er":"I will briefly speak to you of that immutable Goal, which the knowers of the Vedas declare; into which diligent ones, free from attachment, enter, and for which people practice celibacy, aspiring.","gu":"વેદ-જ્ઞાતાઓ જેને અવિનાશી કહે છે, જ્ઞાની સંન્યાસીઓ જ્ઞાના-અભ્યાસ સહ જ્યાં પ્રવેશ કરે છે, અને જેની ઇચ્છાથી બ્રહ્મચર્ય પળાય છે — એ ધ્યેય હું સંક્ષેપમાં કહીશ."},{"ref":"8.12","ch":8,"v":12,"sa":"सर्वद्वाराणि संयम्य मनो हृदि निरुध्य च।\nमूर्ध्न्याधायात्मनः प्राणमास्थितो योगधारणाम्।।8.12।।","tr":"sarva-dvārāṇi sanyamya mano hṛidi nirudhya cha\nmūrdhnyādhāyātmanaḥ prāṇam āsthito yoga-dhāraṇām","en":"Having closed all the gates, confined the mind in the heart, and fixed the life-breath in the head, engage in the practice of concentration.","es":"Having controlled all the senses, confined the mind in the heart, and fixed his own vital force in the head, he should remain firm in yoga.","er":"Having controlled all the senses, confined the mind in the heart, and fixed his own vital force in the head, he should remain steadfast in yoga.","gu":"શરીરના સઘળા દ્વારો બંધ કરી, ચિત્ત હૃદયમાં સ્થિર કરી, પ્રાણ-વાયુ મસ્તકમાં ધારણ કરી, ઘઢ યોગ-ધ્યાનમાં સ્થિર થઈ —"},{"ref":"8.13","ch":8,"v":13,"sa":"ओमित्येकाक्षरं ब्रह्म व्याहरन्मामनुस्मरन्।\nयः प्रयाति त्यजन्देहं स याति परमां गतिम्।।8.13।।","tr":"oṁ ityekākṣharaṁ brahma vyāharan mām anusmaran\nyaḥ prayāti tyajan dehaṁ sa yāti paramāṁ gatim","en":"Uttering the one-syllabled Om, the Brahman, and remembering Me, he who departs, leaving the body, attains the Supreme Goal.","es":"He who departs, leaving the body while uttering the single syllable, \"Om,\" which is Brahman, and thinking of Me, attains the supreme Goal.","er":"He who departs, leaving the body while uttering the single syllable, viz. \"Om,\" which is Brahman, and thinking of Me, attains the supreme Goal.","gu":"એ પ્રકારે 'ઓમ્' — બ્રહ્મ — ના એક અક્ષરનું ઉચ્ચારણ કરતાં, મારું સ્મરણ કરતાં, જે શરીર છોડી જાય છે, તે પરમ ગતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"8.14","ch":8,"v":14,"sa":"अनन्यचेताः सततं यो मां स्मरति नित्यशः।\nतस्याहं सुलभः पार्थ नित्ययुक्तस्य योगिनः।।8.14।।","tr":"ananya-chetāḥ satataṁ yo māṁ smarati nityaśhaḥ\ntasyāhaṁ sulabhaḥ pārtha nitya-yuktasya yoginaḥ","en":"I am easily attainable by that ever-steadfast yogi who constantly and daily remembers me for a long time, not thinking of anything else with a single-minded or one-pointed focus, O Partha.","es":"O son of Prtha, to that yogi of constant concentration and single-minded attention, who remembers Me uninterruptedly and for a long time, I am easily attained.","er":"O son of Prtha, to that yogi of constant concentration and single-minded attention, who remembers Me uninterruptedly and for a long time, I am easy to attain.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે અનન્ય ચિત્તે સર્વદા મારું સ્મરણ કરે છે — એ નિત્યયુક્ત ભક્ત માટે હું સહેલાઈથી પ્રાપ્ય છું."},{"ref":"8.15","ch":8,"v":15,"sa":"मामुपेत्य पुनर्जन्म दुःखालयमशाश्वतम्।\nनाप्नुवन्ति महात्मानः संसिद्धिं परमां गताः।।8.15।।","tr":"mām upetya punar janma duḥkhālayam aśhāśhvatam\nnāpnuvanti mahātmānaḥ sansiddhiṁ paramāṁ gatāḥ","en":"Having attained Me, these great souls do not take birth again here—a place of pain and impermanence—but have reached the highest perfection of liberation.","es":"As a result of reaching Me, the exalted ones who have attained the highest perfection do not get rebirth, which is an abode of sorrows and is impermanent.","er":"As a result of reaching Me, the exalted ones who have attained the highest perfection do not get birth, which is an abode of sorrows and is impermanent.","gu":"મને પ્રાપ્ત થઈ, મહાત્માઓ ફરી જન્મ ધારણ કરતા નથી — આ ક્ષણિક અને દુઃખ-ભર્યા સ્થાને — કારણ કે તેઓ સર્વોચ્ચ સિદ્ધિ પ્રાપ્ત કરી ચૂક્યા છે."},{"ref":"8.16","ch":8,"v":16,"sa":"आब्रह्मभुवनाल्लोकाः पुनरावर्तिनोऽर्जुन।\nमामुपेत्य तु कौन्तेय पुनर्जन्म न विद्यते।।8.16।।","tr":"ā-brahma-bhuvanāl lokāḥ punar āvartino ’rjuna\nmām upetya tu kaunteya punar janma na vidyate","en":"All the worlds, including the world of Brahma, are subject to return again, O Arjuna; but he who reaches Me, O son of Kunti, has no rebirth.","es":"O Arjuna, all the worlds together with the world of Brahma are subject to return. But, O son of Kunti, there is no return after reaching Me.","er":"O Arjuna, all the worlds together with the world of Brahma are subject to return. But, O son of Kunti, there is no rebirth after reaching Me.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, બ્રહ્મલોક સુધીના સઘળા લોક ફરીફરીને ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે; પરંતુ, હે કુંતી-પુત્ર, જે મને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે, તેનો ફરી જન્મ થતો નથી."},{"ref":"8.17","ch":8,"v":17,"sa":"सहस्रयुगपर्यन्तमहर्यद्ब्रह्मणो विदुः।\nरात्रिं युगसहस्रान्तां तेऽहोरात्रविदो जनाः।।8.17।।","tr":"sahasra-yuga-paryantam ahar yad brahmaṇo viduḥ\nrātriṁ yuga-sahasrāntāṁ te ’ho-rātra-vido janāḥ","en":"Those who know the day of Brahma, which lasts a thousand Yugas, and the night, which also lasts a thousand Yugas, know day and night.","es":"Those people who know what day and night are, know the day of Brahma which ends in a thousand yugas, and His night which also ends in a thousand yugas.","er":"Those people who know what day and night are, know the day of Brahma which ends in a thousand yugas [The four yugas (in the human worlds), viz Satya, Treta, Dwapara, and Kali are made up of 4,320,000 years. This period multiplied by a thousand constitutes one day of Brahma. His night also extends over a similar period. See M.S. and V.S.A.], and His night which also ends in a thousand yugas.","gu":"જેઓ જાણે છે કે બ્રહ્માનો એક દિવસ એક હજાર યુગ બરોબર છે, અને એક રાત્રિ પણ એ જ પ્રમાણ ધારણ કરે છે — તેઓ ખરા અર્થમાં દિવસ-રાતનો ભેદ જાણે છે."},{"ref":"8.18","ch":8,"v":18,"sa":"अव्यक्ताद्व्यक्तयः सर्वाः प्रभवन्त्यहरागमे।\nरात्र्यागमे प्रलीयन्ते तत्रैवाव्यक्तसंज्ञके।।8.18।।","tr":"avyaktād vyaktayaḥ sarvāḥ prabhavantyahar-āgame\nrātryāgame pralīyante tatraivāvyakta-sanjñake","en":"From the Unmanifested, all the manifested worlds proceed upon the arrival of the 'day'; upon the arrival of the 'night', they dissolve indeed into that which is known as the Unmanifested.","es":"With the coming of day, all manifested things emerge from the Unmanifest, and when night comes, they merge into that which is called the Unmanifested.","er":"With the coming of day, all manifested things emerge from the Unmanifest, and when night comes, they merge into that which is called the Unmanifested.","gu":"દિવસ આવ્યે, અવ્યક્તમાંથી સઘળી સૃષ્ટિ પ્રગટ થાય છે; રાત આવ્યે, ફરી તે 'અવ્યક્ત' નામ ધારણ કરી વિલીન થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"8.19","ch":8,"v":19,"sa":"भूतग्रामः स एवायं भूत्वा भूत्वा प्रलीयते।\nरात्र्यागमेऽवशः पार्थ प्रभवत्यहरागमे।।8.19।।","tr":"bhūta-grāmaḥ sa evāyaṁ bhūtvā bhūtvā pralīyate\nrātryāgame ’vaśhaḥ pārtha prabhavatyahar-āgame","en":"This same multitude of beings, being born again and again, helplessly dissolves, O Arjuna, into the Unmanifested at the coming of the night and comes forth at the coming of the day.","es":"O son of Prtha, after being born again and again, that very multitude of beings disappears of its own accord at the approach of night. It comes to life again at the approach of day.","er":"O son of Prtha, after being born again and again, that very multitude of beings disappears of its own accord at the approach of night. It comes to life again at the approach of day.","gu":"આ સમૂહ-સૃષ્ટિ, ઘણી ઘણી વાર ઉત્પન્ન થઈ, રાત આવ્યે વિવશ-ભાવે વિસર્જિત થઈ જાય છે, અને ફરી દિવસ ઊગ્યે પ્રગટ થઈ ઊઠે છે."},{"ref":"8.20","ch":8,"v":20,"sa":"परस्तस्मात्तु भावोऽन्योऽव्यक्तोऽव्यक्तात्सनातनः।\nयः स सर्वेषु भूतेषु नश्यत्सु न विनश्यति।।8.20।।","tr":"paras tasmāt tu bhāvo ’nyo ’vyakto ’vyaktāt sanātanaḥ\nyaḥ sa sarveṣhu bhūteṣhu naśhyatsu na vinaśhyati","en":"But verily, there exists higher than this Unmanifested, another Unmanifested Eternal, which is not destroyed even when all beings are destroyed.","es":"But distinct from that Unmanifested is the other eternal, unmanifest Reality, who does not get destroyed when all beings are destroyed.","er":"But distinct from that Unmanifested is the other eternal, unmanifest Reality, who does not get destroyed when all beings are destroyed.","gu":"પણ આ અવ્યક્તની પેલે પાર, બીજો ચિર-સ્થાયી, અવ્યક્ત ભાવ છે — જે સઘળા ભૂત-પ્રાણી નષ્ટ થાય ત્યારે પણ નષ્ટ નથી થતો."},{"ref":"8.21","ch":8,"v":21,"sa":"अव्यक्तोऽक्षर इत्युक्तस्तमाहुः परमां गतिम्।\nयं प्राप्य न निवर्तन्ते तद्धाम परमं मम।।8.21।।","tr":"avyakto ’kṣhara ityuktas tam āhuḥ paramāṁ gatim\nyaṁ prāpya na nivartante tad dhāma paramaṁ mama","en":"What is known as the Unmanifested and the Imperishable, That is said to be the highest goal. Those who reach It do not return (to this Samsara). That is My supreme abode (place or state).","es":"They call Him who has been mentioned as the Unmanifested, the Immutable, the supreme Goal. That is the supreme abode of Mine, from which they do not return once they reach it.","er":"They call Him who has been mentioned as the Unmanifested, the Immutable, the supreme Goal. That is the supreme abode of Mine, from which they do not return once they reach it.","gu":"જેને 'અવ્યક્ત' અને 'અક્ષર' કહે છે, જ્ઞાનીઓ જેને 'પરમ ધ્યેય' ગણે છે — ત્યાં પહોંચ્યા બાદ કોઈ પાછું ફરતું નથી; એ જ મારો પરમ ધામ છે."},{"ref":"8.22","ch":8,"v":22,"sa":"पुरुषः स परः पार्थ भक्त्या लभ्यस्त्वनन्यया।\nयस्यान्तःस्थानि भूतानि येन सर्वमिदं ततम्।।8.22।।","tr":"puruṣhaḥ sa paraḥ pārtha bhaktyā labhyas tvananyayā\nyasyāntaḥ-sthāni bhūtāni yena sarvam idaṁ tatam","en":"That highest Purusha, O Arjuna, is attainable by unswerving devotion to Him alone, within Whom all beings dwell and by Whom all this is pervaded.","es":"O son of Prtha, that supreme Person—in whom all beings are included and by whom all this is pervaded—is, indeed, reached through one-pointed devotion.","er":"O son of Prtha, that supreme Person—in whom all beings are included and by whom all this is pervaded—is indeed reached through one-pointed devotion.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, તે પરમ પુરુષ અવિભક્ત ભક્તિ દ્વારા પ્રાપ્ત થઈ શકે છે, જેમાં સર્વ પ્રાણીઓ વસે છે અને જેના દ્વારા આ સમગ્ર જગત વ્યાપ્ત છે."},{"ref":"8.23","ch":8,"v":23,"sa":"यत्र काले त्वनावृत्तिमावृत्तिं चैव योगिनः।\nप्रयाता यान्ति तं कालं वक्ष्यामि भरतर्षभ।।8.23।।","tr":"yatra kāle tvanāvṛittim āvṛittiṁ chaiva yoginaḥ\nprayātā yānti taṁ kālaṁ vakṣhyāmi bharatarṣhabha","en":"Now I will tell you, O chief of the Bharatas, the times of departure at which the Yogis will return or not return.","es":"O best of the Bharata dynasty, I shall now speak of that time by which the yogis depart and attain the State of Non-return, and also the State of Return.","er":"O best of the Bharata dynasty, I shall now speak of that time by which the yogis depart and attain the State of Non-return, and also the State of Return.","gu":"હે ભારતશ્રેષ્ઠ, હવે હું તને એ કાળ વિષે કહીશ જ્યારે દેહ છોડ્યા પછી યોગીઓ પુનઃ જન્મ લેતા નથી, અને એ કાળ વિષે પણ કહીશ જ્યારે તેઓ પાછા ફરે છે."},{"ref":"8.24","ch":8,"v":24,"sa":"अग्निर्ज्योतिरहः शुक्लः षण्मासा उत्तरायणम्।\nतत्र प्रयाता गच्छन्ति ब्रह्म ब्रह्मविदो जनाः।।8.24।।","tr":"agnir jyotir ahaḥ śhuklaḥ ṣhaṇ-māsā uttarāyaṇam\ntatra prayātā gachchhanti brahma brahma-vido janāḥ","en":"Fire, light, daytime, the bright fortnight, the six months of the northern path of the sun (the northern solstice) departing, then men who know Brahman go to Brahman.","es":"Fire, light, daytime, the bright fortnight, the six months of the northern solstice—by following this path, persons who are knowers of Brahman attain Brahman when they die.","er":"Fire, light, daytime, the bright fortnight, the six months of the northern solstice—by following this path, persons who are knowers of Brahman attain Brahman when they die.","gu":"અગ્નિ, પ્રકાશ, દિવસ, શુક્લ પક્ષ, અને ઉત્તરાયણના છ મહિના — આ કાળે દેહ છોડ્યા પછી બ્રહ્મ જ્ઞાનીઓ બ્રહ્મને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"8.25","ch":8,"v":25,"sa":"धूमो रात्रिस्तथा कृष्णः षण्मासा दक्षिणायनम्।\nतत्र चान्द्रमसं ज्योतिर्योगी प्राप्य निवर्तते।।8.25।।","tr":"dhūmo rātris tathā kṛiṣhṇaḥ ṣhaṇ-māsā dakṣhiṇāyanam\ntatra chāndramasaṁ jyotir yogī prāpya nivartate","en":"Attaining the lunar light through smoke, night time, the dark fortnight, and the six months of the southern path of the sun (the southern solstice), the yogi returns.","es":"Following this Path, the yogi, having reached the lunar light, returns, smoke, night, as also the dark fortnight and the six months of the Southern solstice.","er":"Following this Path, the yogi, having reached the lunar light, returns, smoke, night, as also the dark fortnight and the six months of the Southern solstice.","gu":"ધુમ્રપ, રાત્રિ, કૃષ્ણ પક્ષ, અને દક્ષિણાયનના છ મહિના — આ કાળે દેહ છોડ્યા પછી યોગી ચંદ્રલોકમાં જઈ ફરી પૃથ્વી પર પાછો આવે છે."},{"ref":"8.26","ch":8,"v":26,"sa":"शुक्लकृष्णे गती ह्येते जगतः शाश्वते मते।\nएकया यात्यनावृत्तिमन्ययाऽऽवर्तते पुनः।।8.26।।","tr":"śhukla-kṛiṣhṇe gatī hyete jagataḥ śhāśhvate mate\nekayā yātyanāvṛittim anyayāvartate punaḥ","en":"The bright and dark paths of the world are thought to be eternal; one leads to no return, and the other leads to return.","es":"These two paths of the world, which are white and black, are indeed considered eternal. Through one, a person goes to the state of non-return; through the other, they return again.","er":"These two paths of the world, which are white and black, are indeed considered eternal. Through one, a person goes to the state of non-return; through the other, they return again.","gu":"જગતમાં આ બે માર્ગો — શુક્લ અને કૃષ્ણ — સનાતન ગણાય છે; એકથી ગયેલો પાછો નથી આવતો, અને બીજાથી ગયેલો ફરી જન્મ લે છે."},{"ref":"8.27","ch":8,"v":27,"sa":"नैते सृती पार्थ जानन्योगी मुह्यति कश्चन।\nतस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु योगयुक्तो भवार्जुन।।8.27।।","tr":"naite sṛitī pārtha jānan yogī muhyati kaśhchana\ntasmāt sarveṣhu kāleṣhu yoga-yukto bhavārjuna","en":"Knowing these paths, O Arjuna, no yogi is deluded; therefore, at all times, be steadfast in yoga.","es":"O son of Prtha, no yogi—one steadfast in meditation—whosoever has known these two courses becomes deluded. Therefore, O Arjuna, be steadfast in yoga at all times.","er":"O son of Prtha, no yogi—one steadfast in meditation—whosoever has known these two courses becomes deluded. Therefore, O Arjuna, be steadfast in yoga at all times.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, આ બે માર્ગોને જાણીને યોગી ક્યારેય મોહ પામતો નથી; માટે તું સર્વ સમયે યોગમાં દૃઢ રહે."},{"ref":"8.28","ch":8,"v":28,"sa":"वेदेषु यज्ञेषु तपःसु चैव\nदानेषु यत्पुण्यफलं प्रदिष्टम्।\nअत्येति तत्सर्वमिदं विदित्वा\nयोगी परं स्थानमुपैति चाद्यम्।।8.28।।","tr":"vedeṣhu yajñeṣhu tapaḥsu chaiva\ndāneṣhu yat puṇya-phalaṁ pradiṣhṭam\natyeti tat sarvam idaṁ viditvā\nyogī paraṁ sthānam upaiti chādyam","en":"Whatever fruit of merit is declared (in the scriptures) to accrue from (the study of) the Vedas, (the performance of) sacrifices, (the practice of) austerities, and gifts, beyond all this goes the Yogi, having known this; and he attains to the Supreme, Primeval (first or ancient) Abode.","es":"Having known this, the yogi transcends all the results of righteous deeds declared in the Vedas, sacrifices, austerities, and charities, and reaches the primordial, supreme state.","er":"Having known this, the yogi transcends all the results of righteous deeds declared in the Vedas, sacrifices, austerities, and charities, and reaches the primordial, supreme state.","gu":"વેદ, યજ્ઞ, તપ અને દાનમાં જે પુણ્યફળ કહ્યું છે, તે સર્વને આ જ્ઞાન દ્વારા યોગી ઓળંગી જઈ, પરમ આદ્ય સ્થાનને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"9.1","ch":9,"v":1,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nइदं तु ते गुह्यतमं प्रवक्ष्याम्यनसूयवे।\nज्ञानं विज्ञानसहितं यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात्।।9.1।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nidaṁ tu te guhyatamaṁ pravakṣhyāmyanasūyave\njñānaṁ vijñāna-sahitaṁ yaj jñātvā mokṣhyase ’śhubhāt","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"I shall now declare to thee, who does not cavil, the greatest secret—the knowledge combined with experience (Self-realisation). Having known this, thou shalt be free from evil.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said: However, to you who are not given to cavilling, I shall speak of this highest secret itself, which is knowledge combined with experience, by realizing which you shall be free from evil.","er":"The Lord said, \"I shall declare to you, who does not cavil, this most mysterious knowledge, together with its special knowledge, knowing which you will be freed from evil.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે અર્જુન, તારા મનમાં ઈર્ષ્યા નથી એટલે હું તને આ અત્યંત ગુહ્ય જ્ઞાન અને વિજ્ઞાન સહિત ઉપદેશ આપીશ, જેને જાણ્યા પછી તું પાપ-બંધનથી મુક્ત થઈ જઈશ."},{"ref":"9.2","ch":9,"v":2,"sa":"राजविद्या राजगुह्यं पवित्रमिदमुत्तमम्।\nप्रत्यक्षावगमं धर्म्यं सुसुखं कर्तुमव्ययम्।।9.2।।","tr":"rāja-vidyā rāja-guhyaṁ pavitram idam uttamam\npratyakṣhāvagamaṁ dharmyaṁ su-sukhaṁ kartum avyayam","en":"This is the royal science, the royal secret, the supreme purifier, realizable by direct intuitive knowledge, according to righteousness, very easy to perform and imperishable.","es":"This is the sovereign knowledge, the sovereign profundity, the best sanctifier; directly realizable, righteous, very easy to practice, and imperishable.","er":"This is the royal science, the royal mystery, the supreme purifier. It is realized through direct experience, is in accord with Dharma, is pleasant to practice, and is abiding.","gu":"આ રાજવિદ્યા છે, રાજગુહ્ય છે, ઉત્તમ પાવનકારી છે; તે પ્રત્યક્ષ અનુભવ ગ્રાહ્ય, ધર્મ-સંગત, સાધવા સહેલી અને અવિનાશી છે."},{"ref":"9.3","ch":9,"v":3,"sa":"अश्रद्दधानाः पुरुषा धर्मस्यास्य परन्तप।\nअप्राप्य मां निवर्तन्ते मृत्युसंसारवर्त्मनि।।9.3।।","tr":"aśhraddadhānāḥ puruṣhā dharmasyāsya parantapa\naprāpya māṁ nivartante mṛityu-samsāra-vartmani","en":"Those who have no faith in this Dharma, O Parantapa, return to the path of this world without attaining Me.","es":"O destroyer of foes, those who are disregarding this Dharma (knowledge of the Self) certainly go round and round, without reaching Me, along the path of transmigration which is fraught with death.","er":"Men devoid of faith in this Dharma, O scorcher of foes, ever remain without attaining Me, on the mortal path of Samsara.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, આ ધર્મ પ્રત્યે જેઓને શ્રદ્ધા નથી, તેઓ મને પ્રાપ્ત કર્યા વિના મૃત્યુ-સંસારના ફેરાઓ ભોગવ્યા કરે છે."},{"ref":"9.4","ch":9,"v":4,"sa":"मया ततमिदं सर्वं जगदव्यक्तमूर्तिना।\nमत्स्थानि सर्वभूतानि न चाहं तेष्ववस्थितः।।9.4।।","tr":"mayā tatam idaṁ sarvaṁ jagad avyakta-mūrtinā\nmat-sthāni sarva-bhūtāni na chāhaṁ teṣhvavasthitaḥ","en":"All of this world is pervaded by Me in My unmanifest aspect; all beings exist within Me, but I do not dwell within them.","es":"This whole world is pervaded by Me in My unmanifest form. All beings exist in Me, but I am not contained within them!","er":"This entire universe is pervaded by Me, in an unmanifest form. All beings abide in Me, but I do not abide in them.","gu":"આ સમગ્ર જગત અવ્યક્ત સ્વરૂપે મારા વડે વ્યાપ્ત છે; સર્વ પ્રાણીઓ મારામાં સ્થિત છે, પરંતુ હું તેઓમાં સ્થિત નથી."},{"ref":"9.5","ch":9,"v":5,"sa":"न च मत्स्थानि भूतानि पश्य मे योगमैश्वरम्।\nभूतभृन्न च भूतस्थो ममात्मा भूतभावनः।।9.5।।","tr":"na cha mat-sthāni bhūtāni paśhya me yogam aiśhwaram\nbhūta-bhṛin na cha bhūta-stho mamātmā bhūta-bhāvanaḥ","en":"Nor do beings exist in Me (in reality); behold, My divine Yoga, which supports all beings, but does not dwell in them, is My Self, the efficient cause of beings.","es":"Neither do the beings dwell in Me. Behold My divine Yoga! I am the sustainer and originator of beings, but My Self is not contained within the beings.","er":"Yet, beings do not remain in Me. Behold My divine Yoga. I am the sustainer of all beings, yet I am not in them. It is My will alone that causes their existence.","gu":"છતાં ખરી રીતે સર્વ પ્રાણીઓ મારામાં વસ્યા નથી — આ મારી દિવ્ય ઈશ્વરીય શક્તિ જો; મારો આત્મા સર્વ ભૂતોને ઉત્પન્ન કરે છે અને ધારણ કરે છે, પણ તેઓમાં રહ્યો નથી."},{"ref":"9.6","ch":9,"v":6,"sa":"यथाऽऽकाशस्थितो नित्यं वायुः सर्वत्रगो महान्।\nतथा सर्वाणि भूतानि मत्स्थानीत्युपधारय।।9.6।।","tr":"yathākāśha-sthito nityaṁ vāyuḥ sarvatra-go mahān\ntathā sarvāṇi bhūtāni mat-sthānītyupadhāraya","en":"As the mighty wind, moving everywhere, always rests in the ether, so too, know that all beings rest in Me.","es":"Understand thus that just as the voluminous wind, moving everywhere, is ever present in space, similarly all beings abide in Me.","er":"As the powerful element air, moving everywhere, ever remains in the ether, know that so too all beings abide in Me.","gu":"જેવી રીતે સર્વત્ર ફરતો પ્રચંડ વાયુ આકાશમાં સ્થિત રહે છે, તેવી જ રીતે સર્વ ભૂતો મારામાં સ્થિત છે — એ રહસ્ય સમજ."},{"ref":"9.7","ch":9,"v":7,"sa":"सर्वभूतानि कौन्तेय प्रकृतिं यान्ति मामिकाम्।\nकल्पक्षये पुनस्तानि कल्पादौ विसृजाम्यहम्।।9.7।।","tr":"sarva-bhūtāni kaunteya prakṛitiṁ yānti māmikām\nkalpa-kṣhaye punas tāni kalpādau visṛijāmyaham","en":"All beings, O Arjuna, go into My Nature at the end of a Kalpa; I send them forth again at the beginning of the next Kalpa.","es":"O son of Kunti, all the beings at the end of a cycle go back to My Prakrti. At the beginning of a cycle, I project them forth again.","er":"All beings, O Arjuna, enter into My Prakriti at the end of a cycle of time; again, I send them forth at the beginning of a cycle of time.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, કલ્પ ના અંતે સર્વ ભૂતો મારી પ્રકૃતિમાં સમાઈ જાય છે, અને કલ્પ ના આરંભે હું ફરીથી તેઓને સૃષ્ટિ-રૂપે ઉત્પન્ન કરું છું."},{"ref":"9.8","ch":9,"v":8,"sa":"प्रकृतिं स्वामवष्टभ्य विसृजामि पुनः पुनः।\nभूतग्राममिमं कृत्स्नमवशं प्रकृतेर्वशात्।।9.8।।","tr":"prakṛitiṁ svām avaṣhṭabhya visṛijāmi punaḥ punaḥ\nbhūta-grāmam imaṁ kṛitsnam avaśhaṁ prakṛiter vaśhāt","en":"Animating My Nature, I again and again send forth all this multitude of beings, helpless under the force of Nature.","es":"Keeping My own prakṛti under control, I project forth again and again this multitude of beings, which are powerless due to the influence of their own nature.","er":"Controlling the Prakṛti, which is My own, I send forth again and again this multitude of beings, helpless under the sway of Prakṛti.","gu":"મારી પોતાની પ્રકૃતિને અધીન રાખી, હું વારંવાર આ સમગ્ર ભૂત-સમૂહને ઉત્પન્ન કરું છું, જેઓ પ્રકૃતિના ગુણ-દ્વારા પરવશ થઈ ગયા છે."},{"ref":"9.9","ch":9,"v":9,"sa":"न च मां तानि कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय।\nउदासीनवदासीनमसक्तं तेषु कर्मसु।।9.9।।","tr":"na cha māṁ tāni karmāṇi nibadhnanti dhanañjaya\nudāsīna-vad āsīnam asaktaṁ teṣhu karmasu","en":"These acts do not bind Me, O Arjuna, sitting as one indifferent, unattached to those acts.","es":"O Dhananjaya, those actions do not bind Me, for I remain unconcerned and unattached to them.","er":"But these actions do not bind Me, O Arjuna, for I remain detached from them, as if I were unconcerned.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, આ બધાં કાર્યો મને બાંધતાં નથી, કારણ કે હું ઉદાસીન અને આસક્તિ વિના બેઠો છું."},{"ref":"9.10","ch":9,"v":10,"sa":"मयाऽध्यक्षेण प्रकृतिः सूयते सचराचरम्।\nहेतुनाऽनेन कौन्तेय जगद्विपरिवर्तते।।9.10।।","tr":"mayādhyakṣheṇa prakṛitiḥ sūyate sa-charācharam\nhetunānena kaunteya jagad viparivartate","en":"Under Me, as supervisor, Nature produces the moving and the unmoving; therefore, O Arjuna, the world revolves.","es":"Under Me as the supervisor, the Prakrti produces the world of the moving and the non-moving things. Owing to this, O son of Kunti, the world revolves.","er":"Under My supervision, Prakrti gives birth to all mobile and immobile entities, and thus, O Arjuna, the world revolves.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, મારી દેખરેખ હેઠળ પ્રકૃતિ ચર અને અચર સૃષ્ટિ ઉત્પન્ન કરે છે; તેથી જ આ જગત ફરતું રહે છે."},{"ref":"9.11","ch":9,"v":11,"sa":"अवजानन्ति मां मूढा मानुषीं तनुमाश्रितम्।\nपरं भावमजानन्तो मम भूतमहेश्वरम्।।9.11।।","tr":"avajānanti māṁ mūḍhā mānuṣhīṁ tanum āśhritam\nparaṁ bhāvam ajānanto mama bhūta-maheśhvaram","en":"Fools disregard Me, clad in human form, not knowing My higher Being as the great Lord of all beings.","es":"Not knowing My supreme nature as the Lord of all beings, foolish people disregard Me, who have taken a human form.","er":"Fools disregard Me, dwelling in a human form, not knowing My higher nature as the Supreme Lord of all beings.","gu":"મૂર્ખ લોકો મને માનવ સ્વરૂપે ધારણ કરેલો જોઈ તિરસ્કાર કરે છે, કારણ કે તેઓ સર્વ પ્રાણીઓના મહાન ઈશ્વર રૂપ મારી ઉચ્ચ સત્તાને જાણતા નથી."},{"ref":"9.12","ch":9,"v":12,"sa":"मोघाशा मोघकर्माणो मोघज्ञाना विचेतसः।\nराक्षसीमासुरीं चैव प्रकृतिं मोहिनीं श्रिताः।।9.12।।","tr":"moghāśhā mogha-karmāṇo mogha-jñānā vichetasaḥ\nrākṣhasīm āsurīṁ chaiva prakṛitiṁ mohinīṁ śhritāḥ","en":"They are possessed of the deceitful nature of demons and undivine beings, filled with vain hopes, vain actions, and vain knowledge that is senseless.","es":"Possessed of vain hopes, vain actions, vain knowledge, and senselessness, they become verily possessed of the deceptive disposition of fiends and demons.","er":"Senseless people have a nature that is deluding and similar to that of rakshasas and asuras. Their hopes are futile, their actions are futile, and their knowledge is futile.","gu":"આવા લોકો ખોટી આશા, નિરર્થક કર્મો અને નિરર્થક જ્ઞાનથી ભરેલા, છળ-કપટ ભરી આસુરી પ્રકૃતિ ધારણ કરે છે."},{"ref":"9.13","ch":9,"v":13,"sa":"महात्मानस्तु मां पार्थ दैवीं प्रकृतिमाश्रिताः।\nभजन्त्यनन्यमनसो ज्ञात्वा भूतादिमव्ययम्।।9.13।।","tr":"mahātmānas tu māṁ pārtha daivīṁ prakṛitim āśhritāḥ\nbhajantyananya-manaso jñātvā bhūtādim avyayam","en":"But the great souls, O Arjuna, partaking of My divine nature, worship Me with a single-minded devotion, knowing Me as the imperishable source of all beings.","es":"O son of Prtha, the noble ones, being possessed of divine nature, surely adore Me with single-mindedness, knowing Me to be the immutable source of all objects.","er":"But the great-souled ones, O Arjuna, who are associated with My divine nature, worship Me with an unwavering mind, knowing Me to be the immutable source of all beings.","gu":"પરંતુ મહાત્મા લોકો મારી દૈવી પ્રકૃતિ ધારણ કરીને, મને સર્વ પ્રાણીઓના અવ્યયી ઉત્પત્તિ-સ્ત્રોત જાણીને, એકચિત્ત ભક્તિભાવ સાથે મારી ઉપાસના કરે છે."},{"ref":"9.14","ch":9,"v":14,"sa":"सततं कीर्तयन्तो मां यतन्तश्च दृढव्रताः।\nनमस्यन्तश्च मां भक्त्या नित्ययुक्ता उपासते।।9.14।।","tr":"satataṁ kīrtayanto māṁ yatantaśh cha dṛiḍha-vratāḥ\nnamasyantaśh cha māṁ bhaktyā nitya-yuktā upāsate","en":"Always glorifying Me, striving, firm in their vows, prostrating themselves before Me, they worship Me with steadfast devotion.","es":"Always glorifying Me and striving, the men of firm vows worship Me by paying obeisance to Me and being ever endowed with devotion.","er":"Aspiring for eternal communion with Me, they worship Me, always singing My praises, striving with steadfast resolution and bowing down to Me in devotion.","gu":"તેઓ હંમેશા મારો મહિમા ગાતા, દૃઢ પ્રયત્ન કરતા, પ્રતિજ્ઞામાં અટલ રહીને અને મને સાષ્ટાંગ પ્રણામ કરીને, ઉત્કટ ભક્તિ સાથે મારી આરાધના કરે છે."},{"ref":"9.15","ch":9,"v":15,"sa":"ज्ञानयज्ञेन चाप्यन्ये यजन्तो मामुपासते।\nएकत्वेन पृथक्त्वेन बहुधा विश्वतोमुखम्।।9.15।।","tr":"jñāna-yajñena chāpyanye yajanto mām upāsate\nekatvena pṛithaktvena bahudhā viśhvato-mukham","en":"Others also, sacrificing with the wisdom-sacrifice, worship Me, the All-Faced, as one, distinct, and manifold.","es":"Others indeed worship Me by exclusively adoring through the sacrifice of the knowledge of oneness; (others worship Me) in many ways, and (others) as the multiform existing in various forms.","er":"Others, besides offering the sacrifice of knowledge, also worship Me as One, who is characterized by diversity in countless ways and is multiform (in My Cosmic aspect).","gu":"અન્ય લોકો જ્ઞાનયજ્ઞ દ્વારા આહુતિ અર્પીને, મને એક, ભિન્ન અને અનેક રૂપોમાં ઉપાસે છે."},{"ref":"9.16","ch":9,"v":16,"sa":"अहं क्रतुरहं यज्ञः स्वधाऽहमहमौषधम्।\nमंत्रोऽहमहमेवाज्यमहमग्निरहं हुतम्।।9.16।।","tr":"ahaṁ kratur ahaṁ yajñaḥ svadhāham aham auṣhadham\nmantro ’ham aham evājyam aham agnir ahaṁ hutam","en":"I am Kratu; I am Yajna; I am the offering to the manes; I am the medicinal herbs and all plants; I am the Mantra; I am also the ghee or melted butter; I am the fire; I am the oblation.","es":"I am the ritual, I am the sacrifice, I am the oblation, I am the medicinal herb, I am the mantra, I am the clarified butter, I am the fire, and I am the act of offering.","er":"I am Kratu, I am the sacrifice, I am the offering to the manes, I am the herb, I am the Mantra, I am the clarified butter, I am the fire, I am the oblation.","gu":"હું જ ક્રિયા છું, યજ્ઞ છું, પિતૃ-તર્પણ છું, ઔષધિ છું, મંત્ર છું, ઘૃત છું, અગ્નિ છું અને હોમ-દ્રવ્ય પણ હું જ છું."},{"ref":"9.17","ch":9,"v":17,"sa":"पिताऽहमस्य जगतो माता धाता पितामहः।\nवेद्यं पवित्रमोंकार ऋक् साम यजुरेव च।।9.17।।","tr":"pitāham asya jagato mātā dhātā pitāmahaḥ\nvedyaṁ pavitram oṁkāra ṛik sāma yajur eva cha","en":"I am the father of this world, the mother, the dispenser of the fruits of actions, and the grandfather; the one thing to be known, the purifier, the sacred monosyllable (Om), and also the Rik, Sama, and Yajur Vedas.","es":"Of this world, I am the father, mother, ordainer, and grandfather; I am the knowable, the sanctifier, the syllable Om, as well as the Rk, Sama, and Yajus.","er":"I am the father, mother, creator, and grandfather of the universe; I am the purifier. I am the syllable Om, as well as Rk, Saman, and Yajus.","gu":"હું આ જગતનો પિતા, માતા, ફળ આપનાર, પિતામહ, જ્ઞેય, પવિત્ર કરનાર, ઓમ્ અક્ષર અને ત્રણ વેદ છું."},{"ref":"9.18","ch":9,"v":18,"sa":"गतिर्भर्ता प्रभुः साक्षी निवासः शरणं सुहृत्।\nप्रभवः प्रलयः स्थानं निधानं बीजमव्ययम्।।9.18।।","tr":"gatir bhartā prabhuḥ sākṣhī nivāsaḥ śharaṇaṁ suhṛit\nprabhavaḥ pralayaḥ sthānaṁ nidhānaṁ bījam avyayam","en":"I am the goal, the supporter, the Lord, the witness, the abode, the shelter, the friend, the origin, the dissolution, the foundation, the treasure-house, and the imperishable seed.","es":"I am the fruit of actions, the nourisher, the Lord, witness, abode, refuge, friend, origin, end, foundation, store, and the imperishable seed.","er":"I am the goal, the supporter, the Lord, the witness, the abode, the refuge, and the friend. I am the origin, the dissolution, the basis for preservation, and the imperishable seed.","gu":"હું ધ્યેય, પોષણ કર્તા, ઈશ્વર, સાક્ષી, ધામ, આશ્રય, સ્નેહી, ઉત્પત્તિ, પ્રલય, આધાર, ભંડાર અને અવ્યયી બીજ છું."},{"ref":"9.19","ch":9,"v":19,"sa":"तपाम्यहमहं वर्षं निगृह्णाम्युत्सृजामि च।\nअमृतं चैव मृत्युश्च सदसच्चाहमर्जुन।।9.19।।","tr":"tapāmyaham ahaṁ varṣhaṁ nigṛihṇāmyutsṛijāmi cha\namṛitaṁ chaiva mṛityuśh cha sad asach chāham arjuna","en":"As the sun, I give heat; I withhold and send forth the rain; I am immortality and also death, existence and non-existence, O Arjuna.","es":"O Arjuna, I give heat, I withhold and pour down rain; I am verily the nectar, and also death, existence, and non-existence.","er":"I give heat, I withhold and send forth the rain; I am immortality and also death, O Arjuna. I am the being and the non-being.","gu":"હું સૂર્ય રૂપે ઉષ્ણતા આપું છું; વૃષ્ટિ રોકું છું અને મોકલું છું; હું અમૃત અને મૃત્યુ, સત્ અને અસત્ — બન્ને છું, હે અર્જુન."},{"ref":"9.20","ch":9,"v":20,"sa":"त्रैविद्या मां सोमपाः पूतपापा\nयज्ञैरिष्ट्वा स्वर्गतिं प्रार्थयन्ते।\nते पुण्यमासाद्य सुरेन्द्रलोक\nमश्नन्ति दिव्यान्दिवि देवभोगान्।।9.20।।","tr":"trai-vidyā māṁ soma-pāḥ pūta-pāpā\nyajñair iṣhṭvā svar-gatiṁ prārthayante\nte puṇyam āsādya surendra-lokam\naśhnanti divyān divi deva-bhogān","en":"The knowers of the three Vedas, the drinkers of Soma, purified of all sins, worshipping Me through sacrifices, pray for the way to heaven; they reach the holy world of the Lord of the gods and enjoy the divine pleasures of the gods in heaven.","es":"Those who are versed in the Vedas, who drink Soma and are purified of sin, pray for the heavenly goal by worshipping Me through sacrifices. Having reached the place (world) of the king of gods, which is the result of righteousness, they enjoy the divine pleasure of the gods in heaven.","er":"Those who are versed in the three Vedas, having been purified from sin by drinking the Soma juice, pray for passage to heaven and worship Me through sacrifices. Reaching the holy realm of the chief of the gods, they enjoy celestial pleasures in heaven.","gu":"સોમ-પાન કરનારા વૈદિક કર્મ-ઉપાસકો, યજ્ઞ દ્વારા મારી પૂજા કરીને સ્વર્ગ ઇચ્છે છે; તેઓ ઇન્દ્રના પવિત્ર લોકમાં પહોંચીને ત્યાં દિવ્ય સુખ ભોગવે છે."},{"ref":"9.21","ch":9,"v":21,"sa":"ते तं भुक्त्वा स्वर्गलोकं विशालं\nक्षीणे पुण्ये मर्त्यलोकं विशन्ति।\nएव त्रयीधर्ममनुप्रपन्ना\nगतागतं कामकामा लभन्ते।।9.21।।","tr":"te taṁ bhuktvā swarga-lokaṁ viśhālaṁ\nkṣhīṇe puṇye martya-lokaṁ viśhanti\nevaṁ trayī-dharmam anuprapannā\ngatāgataṁ kāma-kāmā labhante","en":"They, having enjoyed the vast heaven, enter the world of mortals when their merit is exhausted; thus abiding by the injunctions of the three (Vedas) and desiring objects of desires, they attain to the state of coming and going.","es":"After having enjoyed that vast heavenly world, they enter into the human world upon the exhaustion of their merit. Thus, those who follow the rites and duties prescribed in the three Vedas, and are desirous of pleasures, attain the state of coming and going.","er":"Having enjoyed the spacious world of heaven, they return to the world of mortals, their merit having been exhausted. Thus, those who follow the Vedic rituals and are drawn by desires come and go.","gu":"સ્વર્ગના વિશાળ ભોગ ભોગવ્યા બાદ જ્યારે પુણ્ય ક્ષીણ થઈ જાય છે, ત્યારે તેઓ મૃત્યુ-લોકમાં પાછા આવે છે; આ રીતે વિહિત ધર્મનું પાલન કરીને, તેઓ પ્રાપ્ત કરે અને ગુમાવે છે."},{"ref":"9.22","ch":9,"v":22,"sa":"अनन्याश्चिन्तयन्तो मां ये जनाः पर्युपासते।\nतेषां नित्याभियुक्तानां योगक्षेमं वहाम्यहम्।।9.22।।","tr":"ananyāśh chintayanto māṁ ye janāḥ paryupāsate\nteṣhāṁ nityābhiyuktānāṁ yoga-kṣhemaṁ vahāmyaham","en":"For those men who worship Me alone, thinking of no one else, for those ever-united, I secure what they have not already possessed and preserve what they already possess.","es":"Those persons who, becoming non-different from Me and meditating, worship Me everywhere, for them, who are ever attached to Me, I arrange for securing what they lack and preserving what they have.","er":"Those who, excluding all else, think of Me and worship Me, aspiring after eternal union with Me, I look after their prosperity and welfare (Yoga and Ksema)."},{"ref":"9.23","ch":9,"v":23,"sa":"येऽप्यन्यदेवता भक्ता यजन्ते श्रद्धयाऽन्विताः।\nतेऽपि मामेव कौन्तेय यजन्त्यविधिपूर्वकम्।।9.23।।","tr":"ye ’pyanya-devatā-bhaktā yajante śhraddhayānvitāḥ\nte ’pi mām eva kaunteya yajantyavidhi-pūrvakam","en":"Even those devotees who, endowed with faith, worship other gods, worship Me alone, O Arjuna, but by the wrong method.","es":"Even those who, being devoted to other deities and endowed with faith, worship them, they also, O son of Kunti, worship Me alone, though following the wrong method.","er":"Even those who are devoted to other divinities with faith in their hearts, worship Me alone, O Arjuna, though not in accordance with the Sastras.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે ભક્તો શ્રદ્ધાપૂર્વક અન્ય દેવોની ઉપાસના કરે છે, તેઓ પણ મને જ ભજે છે, પરંતુ ખોટી રીતે."},{"ref":"9.24","ch":9,"v":24,"sa":"अहं हि सर्वयज्ञानां भोक्ता च प्रभुरेव च।\nन तु मामभिजानन्ति तत्त्वेनातश्च्यवन्ति ते।।9.24।।","tr":"ahaṁ hi sarva-yajñānāṁ bhoktā cha prabhureva cha\nna tu mām abhijānanti tattvenātaśh chyavanti te","en":"For I alone am the enjoyer and Lord of all sacrifices; but they do not know Me in reality, and thus they return to this mortal world.","es":"Indeed, I am the enjoyer and the Lord of all sacrifices, but they do not know Me truly. Therefore, they fall.","er":"For, I am the only enjoyer and the only Lord of all sacrifices. They do not recognize Me in My true nature; hence, they fall.","gu":"કારણ કે સર્વ યજ્ઞોનો ભોક્તા અને ઈશ્વર એકમાત્ર હું જ છું; પરંતુ તેઓ મને ખરી રીતે જાણતા નથી, તેથી તેઓ પતન પામે છે."},{"ref":"9.25","ch":9,"v":25,"sa":"यान्ति देवव्रता देवान् पितृ़न्यान्ति पितृव्रताः।\nभूतानि यान्ति भूतेज्या यान्ति मद्याजिनोऽपि माम्।।9.25।।","tr":"yānti deva-vratā devān pitṝīn yānti pitṛi-vratāḥ\nbhūtāni yānti bhūtejyā yānti mad-yājino ’pi mām","en":"The worshippers of the gods go to them; the ancestor-worshippers go to the manes; the worshippers of the deities who preside over the elements go to them; but My devotees come to Me.","es":"Those who worship the gods reach the gods; the worshippers of the manes go to the manes; the devotees of the Beings reach the Beings; and those who worship Me come to Me.","er":"Devotees of gods go to the gods; manes-worshippers go to the manes; worshippers of Bhutas go to the Bhutas; and those who worship Me come to Me.","gu":"જે દેવોની પૂજા કરે છે તે દેવોને પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે, પિતૃઓની પૂજા કરનાર પિતૃઓને જાય છે, ભૂતોની ઉપાસના કરનાર ભૂતોને પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે; પરંતુ મારા ભક્તો મને જ આવે છે."},{"ref":"9.26","ch":9,"v":26,"sa":"पत्रं पुष्पं फलं तोयं यो मे भक्त्या प्रयच्छति।\nतदहं भक्त्युपहृतमश्नामि प्रयतात्मनः।।9.26।।","tr":"patraṁ puṣhpaṁ phalaṁ toyaṁ yo me bhaktyā prayachchhati\ntadahaṁ bhaktyupahṛitam aśhnāmi prayatātmanaḥ","en":"Whoever offers Me with devotion a leaf, a flower, a fruit, or a little water, that, so offered devotedly by the pure-minded, I accept.","es":"Whoever offers Me with devotion—a leaf, a flower, a fruit, or water—I accept that gift of the pure-hearted man which has been presented devotionally.","er":"Whoever offers Me with true devotion a leaf, a flower, a fruit, or some water, I accept this offering made with devotion by them who are pure of heart.","gu":"જે કોઈ ભક્તિભાવથી મને પત્ર, ફૂલ, ફળ અથવા જળ અર્પણ કરે છે, તે પ્રેમ અને શ્રદ્ધાથી આપેલી એ પવિત્ર ભેટ હું સ્વીકાર કરું છું."},{"ref":"9.27","ch":9,"v":27,"sa":"यत्करोषि यदश्नासि यज्जुहोषि ददासि यत्।\nयत्तपस्यसि कौन्तेय तत्कुरुष्व मदर्पणम्।।9.27।।","tr":"yat karoṣhi yad aśhnāsi yaj juhoṣhi dadāsi yat\nyat tapasyasi kaunteya tat kuruṣhva mad-arpaṇam","en":"Whatever you do, whatever you eat, whatever you offer in sacrifice, whatever you give, whatever austerity you practice, O Arjuna, do it as an offering to Me.","es":"O son of Kunti, whatever you do, whatever you eat, whatever you offer as a sacrifice, whatever you give, and whatever austerities you undertake—all of that you offer to Me.","er":"Whatever you do, whatever you eat, whatever you offer, whatever you give away, whatever austerity you practice, O Arjuna, do that as an offering to Me.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, તું જે કંઈ કરે, ખાય, હોમે, દાન આપે કે તપ કરે — તે સઘળું મને અર્પણ કરીને કર."},{"ref":"9.28","ch":9,"v":28,"sa":"शुभाशुभफलैरेवं मोक्ष्यसे कर्मबन्धनैः।\nसंन्यासयोगयुक्तात्मा विमुक्तो मामुपैष्यसि।।9.28।।","tr":"śhubhāśhubha-phalair evaṁ mokṣhyase karma-bandhanaiḥ\nsannyāsa-yoga-yuktātmā vimukto mām upaiṣhyasi","en":"Thus, you shall be freed from the bonds of actions yielding good and evil fruits; with the mind steadfast in the Yoga of renunciation, and liberated, you shall come to Me.","es":"Thus, you will become free from bondage in the form of actions which are productive of good and bad results. Having your mind imbued with the yoga of renunciation and becoming free, you will attain Me.","er":"Thus equipped in mind with the Yoga of renunciation, you will free yourself from the bonds of Karma, productive of both auspicious and inauspicious fruits. Thus liberated, you will come to Me.","gu":"આ રીતે શુભ-અશુભ ફળ આપનારાં કર્મોના બંધનમાંથી મુક્ત થઈ, સંન્યાસ-યોગથી મનને સ્થિર રાખી, તું મોક્ષ પ્રાપ્ત કરીને મને આવશે."},{"ref":"9.29","ch":9,"v":29,"sa":"समोऽहं सर्वभूतेषु न मे द्वेष्योऽस्ति न प्रियः।\nये भजन्ति तु मां भक्त्या मयि ते तेषु चाप्यहम्।।9.29।।","tr":"samo ’haṁ sarva-bhūteṣhu na me dveṣhyo ’sti na priyaḥ\nye bhajanti tu māṁ bhaktyā mayi te teṣhu chāpyaham","en":"I am the same to all beings; there is none hateful or dear to Me; but those who worship Me with devotion are in Me, and I am also in them.","es":"I am impartial towards all beings; to Me there is none detestable or none dear. But those who worship Me with devotion, they exist in Me, and I too exist in them.","er":"I am the same to all creation; there is none hateful or dear to me. But those who worship me with devotion abide in me, and I in them."},{"ref":"9.30","ch":9,"v":30,"sa":"अपि चेत्सुदुराचारो भजते मामनन्यभाक्।\nसाधुरेव स मन्तव्यः सम्यग्व्यवसितो हि सः।।9.30।।","tr":"api chet su-durāchāro bhajate mām ananya-bhāk\nsādhur eva sa mantavyaḥ samyag vyavasito hi saḥ","en":"Even if the most sinful worships Me, with devotion to no one else, he should indeed be regarded as righteous, for he has rightly resolved.","es":"Even if a man of very bad conduct worships Me with single-minded devotion, he is to be considered truly good; for he has rightly resolved.","er":"If even the most sinful man worships Me with undivided devotion, he should be regarded as holy, for he has rightly resolved.","gu":"જો સૌથી મોટો પાપી પણ અનન્ય ભક્તિથી મારી ઉપાસના કરે, તો તેને ધર્માત્મા જ ગણવો જોઈએ, કારણ કે તેણે સાચો સંકલ્પ કર્યો છે."},{"ref":"9.31","ch":9,"v":31,"sa":"क्षिप्रं भवति धर्मात्मा शश्वच्छान्तिं निगच्छति।\nकौन्तेय प्रतिजानीहि न मे भक्तः प्रणश्यति।।9.31।।","tr":"kṣhipraṁ bhavati dharmātmā śhaśhvach-chhāntiṁ nigachchhati\nkaunteya pratijānīhi na me bhaktaḥ praṇaśhyati","en":"Soon he becomes righteous and attains eternal peace; O Arjuna, proclaim thou for certain that My devotee never perishes.","es":"He soon becomes possessed of a virtuous mind; he attains everlasting peace. Do you proclaim boldly, O son of Kunti, that My devotee will not be ruined.","er":"Quickly, he becomes righteous and obtains everlasting peace. Affirm on My behalf, O Arjuna, that My devotee never perishes.","gu":"તે ભક્ત ત્વરાથી ધર્માત્મા બને છે અને શાશ્વત શાંતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે; હે અર્જુન, નિ:સંદેહ જાહેર કર કે મારો ભક્ત કદી નાશ પામતો નથી."},{"ref":"9.32","ch":9,"v":32,"sa":"मां हि पार्थ व्यपाश्रित्य येऽपि स्युः पापयोनयः।\nस्त्रियो वैश्यास्तथा शूद्रास्तेऽपि यान्ति परां गतिम्।।9.32।।","tr":"māṁ hi pārtha vyapāśhritya ye ’pi syuḥ pāpa-yonayaḥ\nstriyo vaiśhyās tathā śhūdrās te ’pi yānti parāṁ gatim","en":"For, taking refuge in Me, they who, O Arjuna, may be of a sinful birth—women, Vaisyas, and Sudras—attain the Supreme Goal.","es":"For, O son of Prtha, even those who are born of sin-women, Vaisyas, as well as Sudras—[S.'s construction of this portion is: women, Vaisyas as well as Sudras, and even others who are born of sin (i.e., those who are born low and are of vile deeds, viz Mlecchas, Pukkasas and others). M.S. also takes papa-yonayah (born of sin) as a separate phrase, and classifies women and others only as those darred from Vedic study, etc.-Tr.]—even they reach the highest Goal by taking shelter under Me.","er":"By taking refuge in Me, even those of evil birth, women, Vaisyas, and Sudras, attain the supreme state.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે સ્ત્રીઓ, વૈશ્યો, શૂદ્રો અને પાપ-યોનિમાં જન્મેલા હોય, તે પણ મારી શરણ લઈ પરમ ગતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"9.33","ch":9,"v":33,"sa":"किं पुनर्ब्राह्मणाः पुण्या भक्ता राजर्षयस्तथा।\nअनित्यमसुखं लोकमिमं प्राप्य भजस्व माम्।।9.33।।","tr":"kiṁ punar brāhmaṇāḥ puṇyā bhaktā rājarṣhayas tathā\nanityam asukhaṁ lokam imaṁ prāpya bhajasva mām","en":"How much more easily, then, do Brahmins and devoted royal saints attain the goal? Having come to this impermanent and unhappy world, do thou worship Me.","es":"What of the holy Brahmanas and devoted, wise sages? Having come to this fleeting, miserable world, worship Me.","er":"How much more then, for the pure Brahmanas and royal sages who are My devotees! Having obtained this transient and joyless world, they should worship Me.","gu":"તો પછી પવિત્ર બ્રાહ્મણો અને ભક્ત રાજર્ષિઓ તે ગતિ કેટલી સહેલાઈથી પ્રાપ્ત કરે! આ અનિત્ય અને સુખ-વિહીન સંસારમાં આવ્યા છો, માટે મારી ભક્તિ કરો."},{"ref":"9.34","ch":9,"v":34,"sa":"मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु।\nमामेवैष्यसि युक्त्वैवमात्मानं मत्परायणः।।9.34।।","tr":"man-manā bhava mad-bhakto mad-yājī māṁ namaskuru\nmām evaiṣhyasi yuktvaivam ātmānaṁ mat-parāyaṇaḥ","en":"Fix your mind on Me; be devoted to Me; sacrifice to Me; bow down to Me; having thus united your whole self to Me, taking Me as the supreme goal, you will come to Me.","es":"Having your mind fixed on Me, be devoted to Me, sacrifice to Me, and bow down to Me. By concentrating your mind and accepting Me as the supreme goal, you shall surely attain Me, who am thus the Self.","er":"Focus your mind on Me, be My devotee, worship Me. Bow down to Me. Engaging your mind in this manner and regarding Me as the supreme goal, you will come to Me."},{"ref":"10.1","ch":10,"v":1,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nभूय एव महाबाहो श्रृणु मे परमं वचः।\nयत्तेऽहं प्रीयमाणाय वक्ष्यामि हितकाम्यया।।10.1।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nbhūya eva mahā-bāho śhṛiṇu me paramaṁ vachaḥ\nyatte ’haṁ prīyamāṇāya vakṣhyāmi hita-kāmyayā","en":"The Blessed Lord said, Again, O mighty-armed Arjuna, listen to my supreme word which I will declare to you, who are beloved, for your welfare.","es":"The Blessed Lord said, O mighty-armed one, listen once more to My supreme utterance, which I, wishing for your welfare, shall speak to you who take delight in it.","er":"The Lord said, \"Further, O Arjuna, listen to My Supreme word. Desiring your good, I shall speak to you who loves Me.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે મહાબાહો, ફરી એક વાર મારો પરમ ઉપદેશ સાંભળ — તારું ભલું ઇચ્છતો હું, તને પ્રિય ગણીને, આ વચન કહું છું."},{"ref":"10.2","ch":10,"v":2,"sa":"न मे विदुः सुरगणाः प्रभवं न महर्षयः।\nअहमादिर्हि देवानां महर्षीणां च सर्वशः।।10.2।।","tr":"na me viduḥ sura-gaṇāḥ prabhavaṁ na maharṣhayaḥ\naham ādir hi devānāṁ maharṣhīṇāṁ cha sarvaśhaḥ","en":"Neither the hosts of the gods nor the great sages know My origin; for I am the source of all the gods and the great sages in every way.","es":"Neither the gods nor the great sages know My majesty, for I am the source of them all in all respects.","er":"Neither the host of gods nor the great sages know My power; for I am indeed the source of the gods and the great sages.","gu":"મારી ઉત્પત્તિ ન તો દેવો જાણે છે, ન મહર્ષિઓ; કારણ કે હું સર્વ રીતે દેવો અને મહર્ષિઓનો પણ ઉગમ-સ્ત્રોત છું."},{"ref":"10.3","ch":10,"v":3,"sa":"यो मामजमनादिं च वेत्ति लोकमहेश्वरम्।\nअसम्मूढः स मर्त्येषु सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते।।10.3।।","tr":"yo māmajam anādiṁ cha vetti loka-maheśhvaram\nasammūḍhaḥ sa martyeṣhu sarva-pāpaiḥ pramuchyate","en":"He who knows Me as unborn and beginningless, as the great Lord of the worlds, he among mortals is undeluded and is liberated from all sins.","es":"He who knows Me—the birthless, beginningless, and great Lord of the worlds—he, the undeluded one among mortals, becomes freed from all sins.","er":"He who knows Me as unborn, without a beginning, and the great Lord of the worlds—he among mortals is undeluded and is released from all sin.","gu":"જે મને અજન્મા, અનાદિ અને સૌ લોકના મહાન ઈશ્વર રૂપે જાણે છે, તે મનુષ્ય મોહ-મુક્ત થઈ સઘળાં પાપોમાંથી છૂટી જાય છે."},{"ref":"10.4","ch":10,"v":4,"sa":"बुद्धिर्ज्ञानमसंमोहः क्षमा सत्यं दमः शमः।\nसुखं दुःखं भवोऽभावो भयं चाभयमेव च।।10.4।।","tr":"buddhir jñānam asammohaḥ kṣhamā satyaṁ damaḥ śhamaḥ\nsukhaṁ duḥkhaṁ bhavo ’bhāvo bhayaṁ chābhayameva cha","en":"Intellect, wisdom, non-delusion, forgiveness, truth, self-restraint, calmness, happiness, pain, existence or birth, non-existence or death, fear, and also fearlessness.","es":"Intelligence, wisdom, non-delusion, forgiveness, truth, control of the external organs, control of the internal organs, happiness, sorrow, birth, death, and fearlessness;","er":"Intelligence, knowledge, non-delusion, forbearance, truth, restraint, self-control, pleasure, pain, exaltation, and depression, fear, and fearlessness;","gu":"બુદ્ધિ, જ્ઞાન, અભ્રાંતતા, ક્ષમા, સત્ય, ઇન્દ્રિય-સંયમ, મન:શાંતિ, સુખ, દુ:ખ, ઉત્પત્તિ, મૃત્યુ, ભય અને નિર્ભયતા —"},{"ref":"10.5","ch":10,"v":5,"sa":"अहिंसा समता तुष्टिस्तपो दानं यशोऽयशः।\nभवन्ति भावा भूतानां मत्त एव पृथग्विधाः।।10.5।।","tr":"ahiṁsā samatā tuṣṭis tapo dānaṁ yaśo 'yaśaḥ bhavanti bhāvā bhūtānāṁ matta eva pṛthag-vidhāḥ","en":"Non-injury, equanimity, contentment, austerity, beneficence, fame, and ill-fame—these different qualities of beings arise from Me alone.","es":"Non-injury, equanimity, satisfaction, austerity, charity, fame, and infamy—these different dispositions of beings spring from Me alone.","er":"Non-violence, reality, cheerfulness, austerity, beneficence, fame, and infamy—these different qualities of beings arise from Me alone.","gu":"અહિંસા, સમભાવ, સંતોષ, તપ, દાન, યશ અને અપયશ — આ સઘળા ભાવો પ્રાણીઓમાં મારી પાસેથી જ ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે."},{"ref":"10.6","ch":10,"v":6,"sa":"महर्षयः सप्त पूर्वे चत्वारो मनवस्तथा।\nमद्भावा मानसा जाता येषां लोक इमाः प्रजाः।।10.6।।","tr":"maharṣhayaḥ sapta pūrve chatvāro manavas tathā\nmad-bhāvā mānasā jātā yeṣhāṁ loka imāḥ prajāḥ","en":"The seven great sages, the ancient four, and the Manus, possessing powers like Mine (due to their minds being fixed on Me), were born from My mind; from them, these creatures have been born in this world.","es":"The seven great sages, as well as the four Manus of ancient days, from whom all these creatures in the world have descended, had their thoughts fixed on Me, and they were born from My mind.","er":"The seven great seers of yore, as well as the four Manus, all possessing My mental disposition, were born from My mind. All these creatures of the world are descended from them.","gu":"સાત મહર્ષિઓ, ચાર સનકાદિ અને ચૌદ મનુઓ — આ સૌ મારી ઇચ્છાથી, મારા મનમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન થયા છે, અને આ જગતના સઘળા જીવો તેઓના વંશજ છે."},{"ref":"10.7","ch":10,"v":7,"sa":"एतां विभूतिं योगं च मम यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः।\nसोऽविकम्पेन योगेन युज्यते नात्र संशयः।।10.7।।","tr":"etāṁ vibhūtiṁ yogaṁ cha mama yo vetti tattvataḥ\nso ’vikampena yogena yujyate nātra sanśhayaḥ","en":"He who truly knows these manifold manifestations of My Being and this Yoga-power of Mine, becomes established in unshakable Yoga; there is no doubt about it.","es":"One who knows truly this majesty and yoga of Mine, he becomes imbued with unwavering yoga. There is no doubt about it.","er":"He who truly knows this supreme manifestation and splendor of My auspicious attributes, becomes united with the unshakeable Yoga of Bhakti—there is no doubt of this.","gu":"જે કોઈ મારી આ વ્યાપક વિભૂતિઓ અને યોગ-શક્તિને તત્ત્વથી જાણે છે, તે અડોલ ભક્તિ-યોગમાં સ્થિર થાય છે — આમાં કોઈ સંશય નથી."},{"ref":"10.8","ch":10,"v":8,"sa":"अहं सर्वस्य प्रभवो मत्तः सर्वं प्रवर्तते।\nइति मत्वा भजन्ते मां बुधा भावसमन्विताः।।10.8।।","tr":"ahaṁ sarvasya prabhavo mattaḥ sarvaṁ pravartate\niti matvā bhajante māṁ budhā bhāva-samanvitāḥ","en":"I am the source of all; from me everything evolves; Understanding this, the wise, endowed with meditation, worship me.","es":"I am the origin of all; everything moves on due to Me. Realizing this, the wise ones, filled with fervor, adore Me.","er":"I am the origin of all; from me everything proceeds. Thinking thus, the wise worship me with all devotion (Bhava).","gu":"હું સર્વનો ઉગમ છું; મારાથી જ સર્વ કંઈ ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે. આ સત્ય સમજીને, ધ્યાનયુક્ત બુદ્ધિમાન મનુષ્યો ભક્તિભાવથી મારી ઉપાસના કરે છે."},{"ref":"10.9","ch":10,"v":9,"sa":"मच्चित्ता मद्गतप्राणा बोधयन्तः परस्परम्।\nकथयन्तश्च मां नित्यं तुष्यन्ति च रमन्ति च।।10.9।।","tr":"mach-chittā mad-gata-prāṇā bodhayantaḥ parasparam\nkathayantaśh cha māṁ nityaṁ tuṣhyanti cha ramanti cha","en":"With their minds and lives wholly absorbed in Me, they enlighten each other and ever speak of Me, being satisfied and delighted.","es":"With their minds fixed on Me, dedicating their lives to Me, enlightening one another, and always speaking of Me, they derive satisfaction and rejoice.","er":"With their minds focused on Me, their pranas centered in Me, inspiring one another and always speaking of Me, they live in contentment and bliss at all times.","gu":"મારામાં જ મન અને પ્રાણ સ્થિર કરીને, એકબીજાને મારી મહિમા સમજાવતા અને સદા મારી વાતો કરતા, તેઓ સંતોષ અને આનંદ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"10.10","ch":10,"v":10,"sa":"तेषां सततयुक्तानां भजतां प्रीतिपूर्वकम्।\nददामि बुद्धियोगं तं येन मामुपयान्ति ते।।10.10।।","tr":"teṣhāṁ satata-yuktānāṁ bhajatāṁ prīti-pūrvakam\ndadāmi buddhi-yogaṁ taṁ yena mām upayānti te","en":"To those who are ever steadfast, worshipping me with love, I give the yoga of discrimination, by which they come to me.","es":"To those who are ever devoted and worship Me with love, I grant the possession of wisdom that leads them to Me.","er":"To those who are ceaselessly united with Me and who worship Me with immense love, I lovingly grant that mental disposition (Buddhi-yoga) which leads them to Me.","gu":"જે ભક્તો પ્રેમ અને ધ્યાનથી નિષ્ઠાપૂર્વક મારી ઉપાસના કરે છે, તેઓને હું જ્ઞાનનો યોગ આપું છું, જેના દ્વારા તેઓ મને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"10.11","ch":10,"v":11,"sa":"तेषामेवानुकम्पार्थमहमज्ञानजं तमः।\nनाशयाम्यात्मभावस्थो ज्ञानदीपेन भास्वता।।10.11।।","tr":"teṣhām evānukampārtham aham ajñāna-jaṁ tamaḥ\nnāśhayāmyātma-bhāva-stho jñāna-dīpena bhāsvatā","en":"Out of mere compassion for them, I, dwelling within their selves, destroy the darkness born of ignorance with the luminous lamp of knowledge.","es":"Out of compassion for them alone, I, residing in their hearts, destroy the darkness born of ignorance with the luminous lamp of knowledge.","er":"Out of compassion for them alone, I, abiding in their mental activity as its object, dispel the darkness born of ignorance with the brilliant lamp of knowledge.","gu":"તેઓ પ્રત્યે કરુણાથી, તેઓના હૃદયમાં વસીને, હું જ્ઞાનના પ્રકાશિત દીપડાથી અજ્ઞાનના અંધકારને નષ્ટ કરું છું."},{"ref":"10.12","ch":10,"v":12,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nपरं ब्रह्म परं धाम पवित्रं परमं भवान्।\nपुरुषं शाश्वतं दिव्यमादिदेवमजं विभुम्।।10.12।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nparaṁ brahma paraṁ dhāma pavitraṁ paramaṁ bhavān\npuruṣhaṁ śhāśhvataṁ divyam ādi-devam ajaṁ vibhum","en":"Arjuna said, \"You are the Supreme Brahman, the supreme abode, the supreme purifier, eternal, divine Person, the primeval God, unborn, and omnipresent.\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"You are the supreme Brahman, the supreme Light, the supreme Sanctifier. All the sages, as well as the divine sage Narada, Asita, Devala, and Vyasa [Although Narada and the other sages are already mentioned by the words 'all the sages', they are still named separately due to their eminence. Asita is the father of Devala.] call You the eternal divine Person, the Primal God, the Birthless, the Omnipresent; and You Yourself indeed tell me this.\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"You are the Supreme Brahman, the Supreme Light, and the Supreme Sanctifier. All the seers proclaim You as the eternal, divine Person, the Primal Lord, the unborn, and all-pervading. So too do the divine sages Narada, Asita, Devala, and Vyasa proclaim. You Yourself also proclaim this.\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યો: આપ જ પરમ બ્રહ્મ છો, પરમ ધામ છો, પરમ પવિત્ર છો; આપ શાશ્વત, દિવ્ય પુરુષ, આદિ દેવ, અજન્મા અને સર્વવ્યાપી છો."},{"ref":"10.13","ch":10,"v":13,"sa":"आहुस्त्वामृषयः सर्वे देवर्षिर्नारदस्तथा।\nअसितो देवलो व्यासः स्वयं चैव ब्रवीषि मे।।10.13।।","tr":"āhus tvām ṛiṣhayaḥ sarve devarṣhir nāradas tathā\nasito devalo vyāsaḥ svayaṁ chaiva bravīṣhi me","en":"All the sages have thus declared Thee, as also the divine sage Narada; so also Asita, Devala, and Vyasa; and now Thou Thyself dost say so to me.","es":"Arjuna said, \"You are the supreme Brahman, the supreme Light, the supreme Sanctifier. All the sages, as well as the divine sage Narada, Asita, Devala, and Vyasa [Although Narada and the other sages are already mentioned by the words 'all the sages', they are still named separately due to their eminence. Asita is the father of Devala.] call You the eternal divine Person, the Primal God, the Birthless, the Omnipresent; and You Yourself indeed tell me this.\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"You are the Supreme Brahman, the Supreme Light, and the Supreme Sanctifier. All the seers proclaim You as the eternal, divine Person, the Primal Lord, the unborn, and all-pervading. So too do the divine sages Narada, Asita, Devala, and Vyasa proclaim. You Yourself also proclaim this.\"","gu":"નારદ, અસિત, દેવલ અને વ્યાસ — આ સર્વ ઋષિઓએ આપ વિષે આ જ કહ્યું છે, અને હવે આપ સ્વયં પણ મને આ જ કહો છો."},{"ref":"10.14","ch":10,"v":14,"sa":"सर्वमेतदृतं मन्ये यन्मां वदसि केशव।\nन हि ते भगवन् व्यक्ितं विदुर्देवा न दानवाः।।10.14।।","tr":"sarvam etad ṛitaṁ manye yan māṁ vadasi keśhava\nna hi te bhagavan vyaktiṁ vidur devā na dānavāḥ","en":"I believe all that You have said to me to be true, O Krishna; indeed, O blessed Lord! Neither the gods nor the demons know Your manifestation (origin).","es":"O Kesava, I accept as true all that You have told me. Certainly, O Lord, neither the gods nor the demons can comprehend Your glory.","er":"I deem as true all that you have said to me, O Krishna. Truly, O Lord, neither the gods nor the demons know your manifestation.","gu":"હે કૃષ્ણ, આપે જે કંઈ કહ્યું છે તે સર્વ સત્ય છે, એવો મારો દૃઢ વિશ્વાસ છે. હે પ્રભો, આપના આ સ્વરૂપ-પ્રકટીકરણને ન દેવો જાણે છે, ન દાનવો."},{"ref":"10.15","ch":10,"v":15,"sa":"स्वयमेवात्मनाऽत्मानं वेत्थ त्वं पुरुषोत्तम।\nभूतभावन भूतेश देवदेव जगत्पते।।10.15।।","tr":"swayam evātmanātmānaṁ vettha tvaṁ puruṣhottama\nbhūta-bhāvana bhūteśha deva-deva jagat-pate","en":"Verily, Thou Thyself knowest Thyself by Thyself, O Supreme Person, O source and Lord of all beings, O God of gods, O ruler of the world!","es":"O Supreme Person, Creator of beings, Lord of beings, God of gods, Lord of the worlds, You alone know Yourself by Yourself.","er":"O Supreme Person, O Creator of beings, O Lord of beings, O God of gods, O Ruler of the universe, You Yourself know Yourself alone.","gu":"હે પરમ પુરુષ, આપ સ્વયં આપ દ્વારા જ આપને જાણો છો. હે સર્વ ભૂતોના ઉગમ અને ઈશ, હે દેવોના દેવ, હે જગતના પ્રભો, માત્ર આપ જ પોતાને સ્પષ્ટ જાણો છો."},{"ref":"10.16","ch":10,"v":16,"sa":"वक्तुमर्हस्यशेषेण दिव्या ह्यात्मविभूतयः।\nयाभिर्विभूतिभिर्लोकानिमांस्त्वं व्याप्य तिष्ठसि।।10.16।।","tr":"vaktum arhasyaśheṣheṇa divyā hyātma-vibhūtayaḥ\nyābhir vibhūtibhir lokān imāṁs tvaṁ vyāpya tiṣhṭhasi","en":"You should indeed tell, without reserve, of your divine glories by which you exist, pervading all these worlds. (No one else can do so.)","es":"Be pleased to speak in full of Your own divine manifestations, through which You exist pervading these worlds.","er":"You should tell Me without reserve Your divine manifestations where You abide, pervading all these worlds.","gu":"આ સઘળા વિશ્વોમાં જેના દ્વારા આપ વ્યાપ્ત છો, તે આપની દિવ્ય વિભૂતિઓ મને સંપૂર્ણ રીતે કહો."},{"ref":"10.17","ch":10,"v":17,"sa":"कथं विद्यामहं योगिंस्त्वां सदा परिचिन्तयन्।\nकेषु केषु च भावेषु चिन्त्योऽसि भगवन्मया।।10.17।।","tr":"kathaṁ vidyām ahaṁ yogins tvāṁ sadā parichintayan\nkeṣhu keṣhu cha bhāveṣhu chintyo ’si bhagavan mayā","en":"How shall I, ever meditating, know you, O Yogin? In what aspects or things, O blessed Lord, should I think of you?","es":"O Yogi, how shall I know You by remaining ever-engaged in meditation? And through what objects, O Lord, should I meditate on You?","er":"How can I, Your devotee, know You by constantly meditating on You? And in what ways, O Lord, should I meditate on You?","gu":"હે યોગી, હું સર્વદા ધ્યાન ધરતાં આપને કેવી રીતે જાણું? હે ભગવન, આપ કયા-કયા ભાવ અને વસ્તુઓ દ્વારા મારે આપનું ચિંતન કરવું?"},{"ref":"10.18","ch":10,"v":18,"sa":"विस्तरेणात्मनो योगं विभूतिं च जनार्दन।\nभूयः कथय तृप्तिर्हि श्रृण्वतो नास्ति मेऽमृतम्।।10.18।।","tr":"vistareṇātmano yogaṁ vibhūtiṁ cha janārdana\nbhūyaḥ kathaya tṛiptir hi śhṛiṇvato nāsti me ’mṛitam","en":"Tell me again in detail, O Krishna, of your yogic power and glory; for I am not satiated with what I have heard of your life-giving and nectar-like speech.","es":"O Janardana, please narrate to me again in detail Your own yoga and divine manifestations. For, while hearing Your nectar-like words, I am not satiated.","er":"Speak to me again in full, O Krishna, about Your attributes and glories. For I am not sated by hearing Your ambrosial words.","gu":"આપની યોગ-શક્તિ અને મહિમાની વિગતવાર ફરી એક વાર કહો; કારણ કે આપની જીવન-ઊર્જા ભરેલી વાણી સાંભળ્યે મારી તૃષ્ટિ થતી નથી."},{"ref":"10.19","ch":10,"v":19,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nहन्त ते कथयिष्यामि दिव्या ह्यात्मविभूतयः।\nप्राधान्यतः कुरुश्रेष्ठ नास्त्यन्तो विस्तरस्य मे।।10.19।।","tr":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\nhanta te kathayiṣhyāmi divyā hyātma-vibhūtayaḥ\nprādhānyataḥ kuru-śhreṣhṭha nāstyanto vistarasya me","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"Very well! Now I will declare to you My divine glories in their prominence, O Arjuna; there is no end to their detailed description.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, O best of the Kurus, now, according to their importance, I shall describe to you My own glories, which are indeed divine. There is no end to My manifestations.","er":"The Lord said, \"Indeed, I shall tell you, O Arjuna, My auspicious manifestations—those that are most prominent among them. There is no end to their extent.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: ઠીક છે! હે અર્જુન, હું મારી પ્રમુખ દિવ્ય વિભૂતિઓ તને જણાવીશ; મારી વિભૂતિઓનો વિસ્તાર અનંત છે."},{"ref":"10.20","ch":10,"v":20,"sa":"अहमात्मा गुडाकेश सर्वभूताशयस्थितः।\nअहमादिश्च मध्यं च भूतानामन्त एव च।।10.20।।","tr":"aham ātmā guḍākeśha sarva-bhūtāśhaya-sthitaḥ\naham ādiśh cha madhyaṁ cha bhūtānām anta eva cha","en":"I am the Self, O Gudakesa, seated in the hearts of all beings; I am the beginning, the middle, and the end of all beings.","es":"O Gudakesa, I am the Self residing in the hearts of all beings, and I am the beginning, middle, and end of all beings.","er":"I am the Self, O Arjuna, dwelling in the hearts of all beings; I am the beginning, the middle, and the end of all beings.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, હું સર્વ ભૂતોના હૃદયમાં આત્મા રૂપે વિરાજમાન છું; હું જ સઘળા ભૂતોનો આદિ, મધ્ય અને અંત છું."},{"ref":"10.21","ch":10,"v":21,"sa":"आदित्यानामहं विष्णुर्ज्योतिषां रविरंशुमान्।\nमरीचिर्मरुतामस्मि नक्षत्राणामहं शशी।।10.21।।","tr":"ādityānām ahaṁ viṣhṇur jyotiṣhāṁ ravir anśhumān\nmarīchir marutām asmi nakṣhatrāṇām ahaṁ śhaśhī","en":"Among the twelve Adityas, I am Vishnu; among luminaries, the radiant sun; among the seven or forty-nine Maruts, I am Marichi; among stars, I am the moon.","es":"Among the Adityas [viz Dhata, Mitra, Aryama, Rudra, Varuna, Surya, Bhaga, Vivasvan, Pusa, Savita, Tvasta, and Visnu.-Tr.], I am Visnu; among the luminaries, the radiant sun; among the (forty-nine) Maruts [The seven groups of Maruts are Avaha, Pravaha, Vivaha, Paravaha, Udvaha, Samvaha, and Parivaha.-Tr.], I am Marici; among the stars, I am the moon.","er":"Of the Adityas, I am Vishnu; of luminous bodies, I am the radiant sun. Of the Maruts, I am Marici, and among the constellations, I am the moon.","gu":"આદિત્યોમાં હું વિષ્ણુ છું; પ્રકાશોમાં તેજસ્વી સૂર્ય છું; મરુત-ગણોમાં હું મરીચિ છું; અને નક્ષત્રોમાં હું ચંદ્ર છું."},{"ref":"10.22","ch":10,"v":22,"sa":"वेदानां सामवेदोऽस्मि देवानामस्मि वासवः।\nइन्द्रियाणां मनश्चास्मि भूतानामस्मि चेतना।।10.22।।","tr":"vedānāṁ sāma-vedo ’smi devānām asmi vāsavaḥ\nindriyāṇāṁ manaśh chāsmi bhūtānām asmi chetanā","en":"Among the Vedas, I am the Sama-Veda; among the gods, I am Vasava; among the senses, I am the mind; and among living beings, I am intelligence.","es":"Among the Vedas, I am the Sama-Veda; among the gods, I am Indra. Among the organs, I am the mind, and I am the intelligence in creatures.","er":"Of the Vedas, I am the Samaveda; of gods, I am Indra; of sense-organs, I am the mind; and of living beings, I am consciousness.","gu":"વેદોમાં હું સામવેદ છું; દેવોમાં ઈન્દ્ર (વાસવ) છું; ઈન્દ્રિયોમાં હું મન છું; અને સર્વ પ્રાણીઓમાં હું ચૈતન્ય-બુદ્ધિ છું."},{"ref":"10.23","ch":10,"v":23,"sa":"रुद्राणां शङ्करश्चास्मि वित्तेशो यक्षरक्षसाम्।\nवसूनां पावकश्चास्मि मेरुः शिखरिणामहम्।।10.23।।","tr":"rudrāṇāṁ śhaṅkaraśh chāsmi vitteśho yakṣha-rakṣhasām\nvasūnāṁ pāvakaśh chāsmi meruḥ śhikhariṇām aham","en":"And among the Rudras, I am Sankara; among the Yakshas and Rakshasas, the Lord of Wealth (Kubera); among the Vasus, I am Pavaka (Fire); and among the seven mountains, I am Meru.","es":"Among the Rudras, I am Aja, Ekapada, Ahirbudhnya, Pinaki, Aparajita, Tryam-baka, Mahesvara, Vrsakapi, Sambhu, Harana, and Isvara; among the Yaksas and goblins, I am Kubera; among the Vasus, I am Fire; and among the mountains, I am Meru.","er":"Of the Rudras, I am Sankara. Of the Yaksas and Raksasas, I am the Lord of Wealth (Kubera). Of the Vasus, I am Agni; of the mountains, I am Meru.","gu":"રુદ્રોમાં હું શંકર છું; યક્ષો અને રાક્ષસોમાં હું કુબેર છું; વસુઓમાં હું અગ્નિ છું; પર્વતોમાં હું મેરુ છું."},{"ref":"10.24","ch":10,"v":24,"sa":"पुरोधसां च मुख्यं मां विद्धि पार्थ बृहस्पतिम्।\nसेनानीनामहं स्कन्दः सरसामस्मि सागरः।।10.24।।","tr":"purodhasāṁ cha mukhyaṁ māṁ viddhi pārtha bṛihaspatim\nsenānīnām ahaṁ skandaḥ sarasām asmi sāgaraḥ","en":"And, among the household priests of kings, O Arjuna, know Me to be the chief, Brihaspati; among the army generals, I am Skanda; among lakes, I am the ocean.","es":"O son of Prtha, know me to be Brhaspati, the foremost among the priests of kings. Among commanders of armies, I am Skanda; among large expanses of water, I am the sea.","er":"Among family priests, O Arjuna, know Me to be the chief Brhaspati; of generals, I am Skanda; of reservoirs of water, I am the ocean.","gu":"પુરોહિતોમાં મને બૃહસ્પતિ જાણો; સેનાપતિઓમાં હું સ્કંદ છું; જળરાશિઓમાં હું સમુદ્ર છું."},{"ref":"10.25","ch":10,"v":25,"sa":"महर्षीणां भृगुरहं गिरामस्म्येकमक्षरम्।\nयज्ञानां जपयज्ञोऽस्मि स्थावराणां हिमालयः।।10.25।।","tr":"maharṣhīṇāṁ bhṛigur ahaṁ girām asmyekam akṣharam\nyajñānāṁ japa-yajño ’smi sthāvarāṇāṁ himālayaḥ","en":"Among the great sages, I am Bhrigu; among words, I am the one syllable (Om); among sacrifices, I am the sacrifice of silent repetition; among the immovable things, I am the Himalayas.","es":"Among the great sages, I am Bhrgu; of words, I am the single syllable (Om). Among rituals, I am the ritual of Japa of the immovables, the Himalayas.","er":"Of the great seers, I am Bhrgu; of words, I am the single-lettered word Om; of sacrifices, I am the sacrifice of Japa; of immovable things, I am the Himalayas.","gu":"મહર્ષિઓમાં હું ભૃગુ છું; વાણીમાં હું એક અક્ષર 'ઓમ' છું; યજ્ઞોમાં હું જપ-યજ્ઞ છું; અચળ વસ્તુઓમાં હું હિમાલય છું."},{"ref":"10.26","ch":10,"v":26,"sa":"अश्वत्थः सर्ववृक्षाणां देवर्षीणां च नारदः।\nगन्धर्वाणां चित्ररथः सिद्धानां कपिलो मुनिः।।10.26।।","tr":"aśhvatthaḥ sarva-vṛikṣhāṇāṁ devarṣhīṇāṁ cha nāradaḥ\ngandharvāṇāṁ chitrarathaḥ siddhānāṁ kapilo muniḥ","en":"Among all the trees, I am the Peepul; among the divine sages, I am Narada; among the Gandharvas, I am Chitraratha; among the perfected, I am the sage Kapila.","es":"Among all trees, I am the Ashvattha tree, and among divine sages, Narada. Among the Gandharvas, I am Citraratha; among the perfected ones, I am the sage Kapila.","er":"Of trees I am the Asvattha; of celestial seers, I am Narada; of the Gandharvas, I am Citraratha; of the perfected, I am Kapila.","gu":"વૃક્ષોમાં હું અશ્વત્થ (પીપળો) છું; દેવર્ષિઓમાં હું નારદ છું; ગંધર્વોમાં હું ચિત્રરથ છું; સિદ્ધ પુરુષોમાં હું કપિલ મુનિ છું."},{"ref":"10.27","ch":10,"v":27,"sa":"उच्चैःश्रवसमश्वानां विद्धि माममृतोद्भवम्।\nऐरावतं गजेन्द्राणां नराणां च नराधिपम्।।10.27।।","tr":"uchchaiḥśhravasam aśhvānāṁ viddhi mām amṛitodbhavam\nairāvataṁ gajendrāṇāṁ narāṇāṁ cha narādhipam","en":"Know Me as Ucchaisravas, born of nectar, among horses; Airavata among lordly elephants; and the king among men.","es":"Among horses, know Me to be Uccaihsravas, born from nectar; Airavata among the lordly elephants; and among men, the King of men. [Uccaihsravas and Airavata are respectively the divine horse and elephant of Indra.]","er":"Of horses, know Me to be Uccaihsravas, the nectar-born. Of lordly elephants, I am Airavata, and of men, I am the monarch.","gu":"અશ્વોમાં મને અમૃતમંથનથી ઉત્પન્ન ઉચ્ચૈઃશ્રવા જાણો; ગજ-શ્રેષ્ઠોમાં હું ઐરાવત છું; અને મનુષ્યોમાં હું રાજા છું."},{"ref":"10.28","ch":10,"v":28,"sa":"आयुधानामहं वज्रं धेनूनामस्मि कामधुक्।\nप्रजनश्चास्मि कन्दर्पः सर्पाणामस्मि वासुकिः।।10.28।।","tr":"āyudhānām ahaṁ vajraṁ dhenūnām asmi kāmadhuk\nprajanaśh chāsmi kandarpaḥ sarpāṇām asmi vāsukiḥ","en":"Among weapons, I am the thunderbolt; among cows, I am the wish-fulfilling cow called Kamadhenu; I am the progenitor, the god of love; among serpents, I am Vasuki.","es":"Among weapons I am the thunderbolt; among cows I am Kamadhenu. I am Kandarpa, the Progenitor, and among serpents I am Vasuki.","er":"Of weapons, I am the Vajra (thunderbolt); of cows, I am Kamadhuk; I am Kandarpa, the cause of progeny; of serpents, I am Vasuki.","gu":"શસ્ત્રોમાં હું વજ્ર છું; ગાયોમાં હું કામધેનુ છું; સંતતિ-ઉત્પત્તિ-હેતુ કામદેવ (કંદર્પ) હું છું; સર્પોમાં હું વાસુકિ છું."},{"ref":"10.29","ch":10,"v":29,"sa":"अनन्तश्चास्मि नागानां वरुणो यादसामहम्।\nपितृ़णामर्यमा चास्मि यमः संयमतामहम्।।10.29।।","tr":"anantaśh chāsmi nāgānāṁ varuṇo yādasām aham\npitṝīṇām aryamā chāsmi yamaḥ sanyamatām aham","en":"I am Ananta among the Nagas; I am Varuna among water-deities; Aryaman among the Manes; I am Yama among the governors.","es":"Among snakes, I am Ananta; among gods of the waters, Varuna; among the manes, Aryama; and among the maintainers of law and order, I am Yama (King of death).","er":"Of snakes, I am Ananta; of aquatic beings, I am Varuna; of manes, I am Aryama; of subduers, I am Yama.","gu":"નાગોમાં હું અનંત છું; જળ-દેવતાઓમાં હું વરુણ છું; પિતૃઓમાં હું અર્યમા છું; નિયમન કરનારાઓમાં હું યમ છું."},{"ref":"10.30","ch":10,"v":30,"sa":"प्रह्लादश्चास्मि दैत्यानां कालः कलयतामहम्।\nमृगाणां च मृगेन्द्रोऽहं वैनतेयश्च पक्षिणाम्।।10.30।।","tr":"prahlādaśh chāsmi daityānāṁ kālaḥ kalayatām aham\nmṛigāṇāṁ cha mṛigendro ’haṁ vainateyaśh cha pakṣhiṇām","en":"And I am Prahlada among the demons, I am Time among reckoners, I am the lion among beasts, and Vainateya (Garuda) among birds.","es":"Among demons, I am Prahlada, and among reckoners of time, I am Time. Among animals, I am the lion, and among birds, I am Garuda.","er":"Of Daityas, I am Prahlada; of reckoners, I am Death; of beasts, I am the lion; and of birds, I am Garuda, the son of Vinata.","gu":"દૈત્યોમાં હું પ્રહ્લાદ છું; ગણનારાઓમાં હું કાળ છું; પ્રાણીઓમાં હું સિંહ છું; પક્ષીઓમાં હું ગરુડ છું."},{"ref":"10.31","ch":10,"v":31,"sa":"पवनः पवतामस्मि रामः शस्त्रभृतामहम्।\nझषाणां मकरश्चास्मि स्रोतसामस्मि जाह्नवी।।10.31।।","tr":"pavanaḥ pavatām asmi rāmaḥ śhastra-bhṛitām aham\njhaṣhāṇāṁ makaraśh chāsmi srotasām asmi jāhnavī","en":"Among the purifiers, I am the wind; among the warriors, I am Rama; among the fishes, I am the shark; among the streams, I am the Ganga.","es":"Of the purifiers, I am the air; among the wielders of weapons, I am Rama. Among fishes, I am the shark; among rivers, I am Ganga.","er":"Of moving things, I am the wind; of those who bear weapons, I am Rama; of fishers, I am Makara; and of rivers, I am the Ganga.","gu":"પવિત્ર કરનારાઓમાં હું પવન છું; શૂરવીરોમાં હું રામ છું; મત્સ્યોમાં હું મગર (ઝષ) છું; નદીઓમાં હું ગંગા છું."},{"ref":"10.32","ch":10,"v":32,"sa":"सर्गाणामादिरन्तश्च मध्यं चैवाहमर्जुन।\nअध्यात्मविद्या विद्यानां वादः प्रवदतामहम्।।10.32।।","tr":"sargāṇām ādir antaśh cha madhyaṁ chaivāham arjuna\nadhyātma-vidyā vidyānāṁ vādaḥ pravadatām aham","en":"Among creations I am the beginning, the middle, and the end, O Arjuna; among the sciences, I am the science of the Self; and I am the logic among controversialists.","es":"O Arjuna, of creations I am the beginning, the middle, and the end; I am the knowledge of the Self among knowledge; of those who debate, I am vada.","er":"Of creatures, I am the beginning, the middle, and the end, O Arjuna. Of sciences, I am the science of the Self (of the individual and Universal Self). Of those who argue, I am the fair reasoning.","gu":"સૃષ્ટિઓમાં હું આદિ, મધ્ય અને અંત છું; વિદ્યાઓમાં હું અધ્યાત્મ-વિદ્યા છું; તર્ક-વિતર્ક કરનારાઓમાં હું સત્યયુક્ત તર્ક (વાદ) છું."},{"ref":"10.33","ch":10,"v":33,"sa":"अक्षराणामकारोऽस्मि द्वन्द्वः सामासिकस्य च।\nअहमेवाक्षयः कालो धाताऽहं विश्वतोमुखः।।10.33।।","tr":"अहमेवाक्षय: कालो धाताहं विश्वतोमुख: || 33||\nakṣharāṇām a-kāro ’smi dvandvaḥ sāmāsikasya cha\naham evākṣhayaḥ kālo dhātāhaṁ viśhvato-mukhaḥ","en":"Among the letters of the alphabet, I am the letter 'A' and the dual among compounds. I am verily the inexhaustible and everlasting time; I am the dispenser of the fruits of actions, having faces in all directions.","es":"Of the letters, I am the letter A, and of the group of compound words, I am the compound called Dvandva. I am Myself the infinite time; I am the Dispenser with faces everywhere.","er":"Of letters, I am the alphabet 'A'; of compound words, I am the dvandva (copulative); I am myself imperishable time; I am the creator, facing all sides.","gu":"અક્ષરોમાં હું 'અ' છું; સમાસોમાં હું દ્વંદ્વ સમાસ છું; હું જ અક્ષય અને શાશ્વત કાળ છું; હું સર્વ દિશાઓ ભણી મુખ ધરાવતો ધાતા (વ્યાપ્ત ઈશ્વર) છું."},{"ref":"10.34","ch":10,"v":34,"sa":"मृत्युः सर्वहरश्चाहमुद्भवश्च भविष्यताम्।\nकीर्तिः श्रीर्वाक्च नारीणां स्मृतिर्मेधा धृतिः क्षमा।।10.34।।","tr":"mṛityuḥ sarva-haraśh chāham udbhavaśh cha bhaviṣhyatām\nkīrtiḥ śhrīr vāk cha nārīṇāṁ smṛitir medhā dhṛitiḥ kṣhamā","en":"And I am the all-devouring Death, and the source of prosperity for those who are to be prosperous; among the feminine qualities, I am fame, prosperity, speech, memory, intelligence, firmness, and forgiveness.","es":"And I am Death, the destroyer of all; and the bestower of prosperity to those destined to be prosperous. Of the feminine [Narinam may mean 'of the feminine qualities'. According to Sridhara Swami and S., the words fame etc. signify the goddesses of the respective qualities. According to M.S. these seven goddesses are the wives of the god Dharma.-Tr.] (I am) fame, beauty, speech, memory, intelligence, fortitude, and forbearance.","er":"I am also death, which snatches away all. I am the origin of all that will be born. Among women, I am fame, prosperity, speech, memory, intelligence, endurance, and forgiveness.","gu":"હું સૌને ગ્રસી લેનારો મૃત્યુ છું અને ઉદય પામવાવાળાઓની સમૃદ્ધિ છું; સ્ત્રી-ભાવ-ગુણોમાં કીર્તિ, શ્રી, વાક્, સ્મૃતિ, મેધા, ધૃતિ અને ક્ષમા — એ સૌ હું છું."},{"ref":"10.35","ch":10,"v":35,"sa":"बृहत्साम तथा साम्नां गायत्री छन्दसामहम्।\nमासानां मार्गशीर्षोऽहमृतूनां कुसुमाकरः।।10.35।।","tr":"bṛihat-sāma tathā sāmnāṁ gāyatrī chhandasām aham\nmāsānāṁ mārga-śhīrṣho ’ham ṛitūnāṁ kusumākaraḥ","en":"Among the hymns, I am the Brihatsaman; among meters, I am Gayatri; among months, I am Margasirsha; among seasons, I am the flowery season.","es":"I am also the Brhat-sama of the Sama-mantras; of the meters, Gayatri. Of the months, I am Marga-sirsa, and of the seasons, spring.","er":"Of Saman hymns, I am the Brhatsaman; of meters, I am the Gayatri; of months, I am Margasira (Nov-Dec); and of seasons, I am the season of flowers.","gu":"સ્તોત્રોમાં હું બૃહત્સામ છું; છંદોમાં હું ગાયત્રી છું; માસોમાં હું માર્ગશીર્ષ છું; ઋતુઓમાં હું ફૂલ-ખીલ ઋતુ (વસંત) છું."},{"ref":"10.36","ch":10,"v":36,"sa":"द्यूतं छलयतामस्मि तेजस्तेजस्विनामहम्।\nजयोऽस्मि व्यवसायोऽस्मि सत्त्वं सत्त्ववतामहम्।।10.36।।","tr":"dyūtaṁ chhalayatām asmi tejas tejasvinām aham\njayo ’smi vyavasāyo ’smi sattvaṁ sattvavatām aham","en":"I am the gambling of the deceitful; I am the splendor of the splendid; I am victory; I am the resolve of the resolute; I am the goodness of the good.","es":"Of the fraudulent, I am the gambling; I am the irresistible end of the mighty. I am excellence, I am effort, I am the sattva quality of those possessed of sattva.","er":"Of the fraudulent, I am gambling; I am the brilliance of the brilliant; I am victory, I am effort; I am the magnanimity of the magnanimous.","gu":"છળ કરનારાઓના જૂગટામાં હું છળ-ક્રીડા છું; તેજસ્વીઓનું તેજ હું છું; હું વિજય છું, હું સંકલ્પ છું; સત્ત્વ-ગુણ ધારણ કરનારાઓનું સત્ત્વ-ગુણ (સાત્ત્વિકતા) હું છું."},{"ref":"10.37","ch":10,"v":37,"sa":"वृष्णीनां वासुदेवोऽस्मि पाण्डवानां धनंजयः।\nमुनीनामप्यहं व्यासः कवीनामुशना कविः।।10.37।।","tr":"vṛiṣhṇīnāṁ vāsudevo ’smi pāṇḍavānāṁ dhanañjayaḥ\nmunīnām apyahaṁ vyāsaḥ kavīnām uśhanā kaviḥ","en":"Among the Vrishnis, I am Vaasudeva; among the Pandavas, I am Arjuna; among the sages, I am Vyasa; among the poets, I am Usanas, the poet.","es":"Of the Vrsnis, I am Vasudeva; of the Pandavas, Dhananjaya (Arjuna). Of the wise, I am Vyasa; of the omniscient, the omniscient Usanas.","er":"Of the Vrsnis, I am Vasudeva; of the Pandavas, I am Arjuna; of sages, I am Vyasa; and of seers, I am Usana (Sukra).","gu":"વૃષ્ણિ-વંશીઓમાં હું વાસુદેવ (કૃષ્ણ) છું; પાંડવોમાં હું અર્જુન છું; મુનિઓમાં હું વ્યાસ છું; કવિઓમાં હું ઉશના (શુક્રાચાર્ય) છું."},{"ref":"10.38","ch":10,"v":38,"sa":"दण्डो दमयतामस्मि नीतिरस्मि जिगीषताम्।\nमौनं चैवास्मि गुह्यानां ज्ञानं ज्ञानवतामहम्।।10.38।।","tr":"daṇḍo damayatām asmi nītir asmi jigīṣhatām\nmaunaṁ chaivāsmi guhyānāṁ jñānaṁ jñānavatām aham","en":"Of those who punish, I am the scepter; among those who seek victory, I am statesmanship; and among secrets, I am silence; I am knowledge among knowers.","es":"Of the punishers, I am the rod; I am the righteous policy of those who desire to conquer. And of things secret, I am verily silence; I am the knowledge of the wise.","er":"Of those who punish, I am the principle of punishment. Of those who seek victory, I am policy. Of secrets, I am also silence. And of the wise, I am wisdom.","gu":"દંડ આપનારાઓમાં હું દંડ (સત્તા) છું; વિજય ઇચ્છનારાઓમાં હું નીતિ છું; ગુપ્ત વાતોમાં હું મૌન છું; અને જ્ઞાનીઓમાં હું જ્ઞાન છું."},{"ref":"10.39","ch":10,"v":39,"sa":"यच्चापि सर्वभूतानां बीजं तदहमर्जुन।\nन तदस्ति विना यत्स्यान्मया भूतं चराचरम्।।10.39।।","tr":"yach chāpi sarva-bhūtānāṁ bījaṁ tad aham arjuna\nna tad asti vinā yat syān mayā bhūtaṁ charācharam","en":"And whatever is the seed of all beings, that too am I, O Arjuna; there is no being, be it moving or unmoving, that can exist without Me.","es":"Moreover, O Arjuna, I am the seed of all beings. There is nothing, moving or non-moving, that can exist without Me.","er":"I am also that which is the seed of all beings, O Arjuna. Nothing that moves or does not move exists without Me.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે કંઈ સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓનું બીજ છે, તે પણ હું જ છું; ચર કે અચર — કોઈ પ્રાણી મારા વિના અસ્તિત્વ ધરાવી શકતું નથી."},{"ref":"10.40","ch":10,"v":40,"sa":"नान्तोऽस्ति मम दिव्यानां विभूतीनां परंतप।\nएष तूद्देशतः प्रोक्तो विभूतेर्विस्तरो मया।।10.40।।","tr":"nānto ’sti mama divyānāṁ vibhūtīnāṁ parantapa\neṣha tūddeśhataḥ prokto vibhūter vistaro mayā","en":"There is no end to My divine glories, O Arjuna, but this is a brief statement by Me of the particulars of My divine glory.","es":"O destroyer of enemies, there is no limit to My divine manifestations. This description of My manifestations, however, has been stated by Me as an illustration.","er":"There is no limit to My divine manifestations. Here, I have briefly described the extent of such manifestations.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, મારી દૈવી વિભૂતિઓનો કોઈ અંત નથી; જે મેં કહ્યું તે તો મારી અનંત વૈભવ-સ્વરૂપ વિભૂતિઓનો માત્ર સંક્ષિપ્ત પ્રકાર છે."},{"ref":"10.41","ch":10,"v":41,"sa":"यद्यद्विभूतिमत्सत्त्वं श्रीमदूर्जितमेव वा।\nतत्तदेवावगच्छ त्वं मम तेजोंऽशसंभवम्।।10.41।।","tr":"yad yad vibhūtimat sattvaṁ śhrīmad ūrjitam eva vā\ntat tad evāvagachchha tvaṁ mama tejo ’nśha-sambhavam","en":"Whatever being there is glorious, prosperous, or powerful, know that to be a manifestation of a part of My splendor.","es":"Whatever object [all living beings] is verily endowed with majesty, possessed of prosperity, or is energetic, you know for certain each of them as having a part of My power as its source.","er":"Whatever being is possessed of power, or splendour, or energy, know that as coming from a fragment of My power.","gu":"જે કોઈ પ્રાણી કે વસ્તુ ઐશ્વર્યયુક્ત, સૌભાગ્યશાળી કે શક્તિસંપન્ન છે, તે સૌ મારા તેજના એક અંશના પ્રકાશ માત્ર છે — એવું જાણ."},{"ref":"10.42","ch":10,"v":42,"sa":"अथवा बहुनैतेन किं ज्ञातेन तवार्जुन।\nविष्टभ्याहमिदं कृत्स्नमेकांशेन स्थितो जगत्।।10.42।।","tr":"atha vā bahunaitena kiṁ jñātena tavārjuna\nviṣhṭabhyāham idaṁ kṛitsnam ekānśhena sthito jagat","en":"But, of what avail is the knowledge of all these details to you, O Arjuna? I exist, supporting this whole world with one part of Myself.","es":"Or, on the other hand, what is the need for you to know this extensively, O Arjuna? I remain sustaining this whole creation in a special way with a part of Myself.","er":"But of what use is all this extensive knowledge to you, O Arjuna? I sustain this whole universe with only a fragment of My power.","gu":"પરંતુ હે અર્જુન, આ સઘળી વિગતોના જ્ઞાનથી તને શું ફળ? હું તો આ સમગ્ર જગતને મારા એક અંશ વડે ધારણ કરીને ટકાવી રાખ્યું છું."},{"ref":"11.1","ch":11,"v":1,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nमदनुग्रहाय परमं गुह्यमध्यात्मसंज्ञितम्।\nयत्त्वयोक्तं वचस्तेन मोहोऽयं विगतो मम।।11.1।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nmad-anugrahāya paramaṁ guhyam adhyātma-sanjñitam\nyat tvayoktaṁ vachas tena moho ’yaṁ vigato mama","en":"Arjuna said, By this explanation of the highest secret concerning the Self which Thou hast spoken, for the sake of blessing me, my delusion has been dispelled.","es":"Arjuna said, \"This delusion of mine has departed as a result of that speech which is most secret and pertains to the Self, uttered by You for my benefit.\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"To show favor to me, You have told me that most profound mystery concerning the Self; by that, this delusion of mine has been dispelled.\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: આત્માના પરમ ગુહ્ય રહસ્ય વિષે આપે જે ઉપદેશ આપ્યો, તેના પ્રભાવથી મારો ભ્રમ દૂર થઈ ગયો છે."},{"ref":"11.2","ch":11,"v":2,"sa":"भवाप्ययौ हि भूतानां श्रुतौ विस्तरशो मया।\nत्वत्तः कमलपत्राक्ष माहात्म्यमपि चाव्ययम्।।11.2।।","tr":"bhavāpyayau hi bhūtānāṁ śhrutau vistaraśho mayā\ntvattaḥ kamala-patrākṣha māhātmyam api chāvyayam","en":"The origin and destruction of beings have been heard in detail from You, O lotus-eyed Lord, and also Your inexhaustible greatness.","es":"O you with eyes like lotus leaves, I have heard in detail from You the origin and dissolution of beings, as well as Your undecaying glory.","er":"O Krsna, I have heard in detail about the origin and dissolution of all beings, which come from You, as well as Your immutable greatness.","gu":"હે કમળ-નેત્ર! આપ પાસેથી મેં સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓની ઉત્પત્તિ અને વિનાશ તથા આપની અક્ષય મહિમા વિસ્તારથી સાંભળ્યાં છે."},{"ref":"11.3","ch":11,"v":3,"sa":"एवमेतद्यथात्थ त्वमात्मानं परमेश्वर।\nद्रष्टुमिच्छामि ते रूपमैश्वरं पुरुषोत्तम।।11.3।।","tr":"evam etad yathāttha tvam ātmānaṁ parameśhvara\ndraṣhṭum ichchhāmi te rūpam aiśhwaraṁ puruṣhottama","en":"Now, O Supreme Lord, as Thou hast thus described Thyself, O Supreme Person, I wish to behold Thy divine form.","es":"O Supreme Lord, so it is, as You have spoken of Yourself. O Supreme Person, I wish to behold Your divine form.","er":"O Supreme Lord, as You have described Yourself, so You are. I wish to behold Your divine form, O Supreme Person.","gu":"હે પ્રભો! આપે પોતાના સ્વરૂપનું જેવું વર્ણન કર્યું, તે સ્વ-ઘોષણ પ્રમાણે હું આપના ઐશ્વર્યયુક્ત દિવ્ય સ્વરૂપના દર્શન કરવા ઇચ્છું છું."},{"ref":"11.4","ch":11,"v":4,"sa":"मन्यसे यदि तच्छक्यं मया द्रष्टुमिति प्रभो।\nयोगेश्वर ततो मे त्वं दर्शयाऽत्मानमव्ययम्।।11.4।।","tr":"manyase yadi tach chhakyaṁ mayā draṣhṭum iti prabho\nyogeśhvara tato me tvaṁ darśhayātmānam avyayam","en":"If Thou, O Lord, thinkest it possible for me to see it, do Thou, then, O Lord of the Yogis, show me Thy imperishable Self.","es":"O Lord, if You deem it possible for me to behold You, then, O Lord of Yoga, show me Your eternal Self.","er":"If you think, O Lord, that it can be seen by me, then, O Lord of Yoga, reveal Yourself fully to me.","gu":"હે યોગેશ્વર! જો આપ એ યોગ્ય સમજો કે હું આપનું અવ્યયી (અવિનાશી) સ્વરૂપ જોઈ શકું, તો હે પ્રભો, મને દર્શન આપો."},{"ref":"11.5","ch":11,"v":5,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nपश्य मे पार्थ रूपाणि शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः।\nनानाविधानि दिव्यानि नानावर्णाकृतीनि च।।11.5।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\npaśhya me pārtha rūpāṇi śhataśho ’tha sahasraśhaḥ\nnānā-vidhāni divyāni nānā-varṇākṛitīni cha","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"Behold, O Arjuna, forms of Mine, by the hundreds and thousands, of different sorts, divine, and of various colors and shapes.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O son of Prtha, behold My forms in their hundreds and thousands, of different kinds, celestial, and of various colors and shapes.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"Behold, O Arjuna, My forms, hundreds upon thousands, manifold, divine, varied in hue and shape.\"","gu":"શ્રી કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે અર્જુન, જો, મારાં સેંકડો-હજારો અનેક પ્રકારનાં, અનેક રૂપ-રંગ અને આકારનાં દૈવી સ્વરૂપો!"},{"ref":"11.6","ch":11,"v":6,"sa":"पश्यादित्यान्वसून्रुद्रानश्िवनौ मरुतस्तथा।\nबहून्यदृष्टपूर्वाणि पश्याऽश्चर्याणि भारत।।11.6।।","tr":"paśhyādityān vasūn rudrān aśhvinau marutas tathā\nbahūny adṛiṣhṭa-pūrvāṇi paśhyāśhcharyāṇi bhārata","en":"Behold the Adityas, the Vasus, the Rudras, the two Asvins, and the Maruts; behold many wonders never before seen, O Arjuna.","es":"Behold the Adityas, the Vasus, the Rudras, the two Ashvins, and the Maruts. O scion of the Bharata dynasty, also behold the many wonders that have never been seen before.","er":"Behold, O Arjuna, the Adityas, the Vasus, the Rudras, the two Asvins, and the Maruts—many marvels never seen before.","gu":"આદિત્ય, વસુ, રુદ્ર, અશ્વિની-કુમારો અને મરુત-ગણ — આ સૌ જો; અને, હે અર્જુન, અગાઉ ક્યારેય ન નિહાળ્યાં હોય તેવાં અનેક અદ્ભુત દૃશ્ય પણ જો."},{"ref":"11.7","ch":11,"v":7,"sa":"इहैकस्थं जगत्कृत्स्नं पश्याद्य सचराचरम्।\nमम देहे गुडाकेश यच्चान्यद्द्रष्टुमिच्छसि।।11.7।।","tr":"ihaika-sthaṁ jagat kṛitsnaṁ paśhyādya sa-charācharam\nmama dehe guḍākeśha yach chānyad draṣhṭum ichchhasi","en":"Now, behold, O Arjuna, in this My body, the entire universe centered in one, including the moving and the unmoving, and whatever else you desire to see.","es":"See now, O Gudakesa, the entire Universe together with the moving and the non-moving, concentrated in the same place here in My body, as also whatever else you would like to see.","er":"Behold here, O Arjuna, the entire universe with its mobile and immobile things, all centered in My body, and whatever else you desire to see.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, આ ક્ષણે ચર અને અચર — સઘળું બ્રહ્માંડ — મારા એક જ શરીરમાં સ્થિત છે; જે અન્ય જોવા ઇચ્છતો હો, તે પણ જો."},{"ref":"11.8","ch":11,"v":8,"sa":"न तु मां शक्यसे द्रष्टुमनेनैव स्वचक्षुषा।\nदिव्यं ददामि ते चक्षुः पश्य मे योगमैश्वरम्।।11.8।।","tr":"na tu māṁ śhakyase draṣhṭum anenaiva sva-chakṣhuṣhā\ndivyaṁ dadāmi te chakṣhuḥ paśhya me yogam aiśhwaram","en":"But you are not able to behold Me with these your own eyes; I give you the divine eye; behold My lordly Yoga.","es":"But you are not able to see Me with just this eye of yours. I grant you the divine eye; behold My divine Yoga.","er":"But you will not be able to see Me with your own eyes. I give you a divine eye, so behold My Lordly Yoga!","gu":"તું સ્વ-ચક્ષુ વડે મને જોઈ શકતો નથી; હું તને દિવ્ય દૃષ્ટિ આપું છું — હવે મારા ઈશ્વરીય યોગ-ઐશ્વર્યનાં દર્શન કર."},{"ref":"11.9","ch":11,"v":9,"sa":"सञ्जय उवाच\nएवमुक्त्वा ततो राजन्महायोगेश्वरो हरिः।\nदर्शयामास पार्थाय परमं रूपमैश्वरम्।।11.9।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\nevam uktvā tato rājan mahā-yogeśhvaro hariḥ\ndarśhayām āsa pārthāya paramaṁ rūpam aiśhwaram","en":"Sanjaya said, Having thus spoken, O king, the great Lord of Yoga, Hari (Krishna), showed Arjuna His supreme form as the Lord.","es":"Sanjaya said, \"O King, having spoken thus, thereafter, Hari, the great Master of Yoga, showed to the son of Prtha the supreme divine form.\"","er":"Sanjaya said, \"O King, having spoken, Sri Krishna, the great Lord of Yoga, then revealed to Arjuna the supreme, lordly form.\"","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: હે રાજન, આ પ્રમાણે કહ્યા પછી મહાન યોગેશ્વર હરિ (શ્રી કૃષ્ણ)એ અર્જુનને પોતાનું પરમ દૈવી સ્વરૂપ પ્રગટ કર્યું."},{"ref":"11.10","ch":11,"v":10,"sa":"अनेकवक्त्रनयनमनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम्।\nअनेकदिव्याभरणं दिव्यानेकोद्यतायुधम्।।11.10।।","tr":"aneka-vaktra-nayanam anekādbhuta-darśhanam\naneka-divyābharaṇaṁ divyānekodyatāyudham","en":"With numerous mouths and eyes, with numerous wondrous sights, with numerous divine adornments, with numerous divine weapons uplifted, such a form He showed.","es":"Having many faces and eyes, possessing many wondrous sights, adorned with numerous celestial ornaments, and holding many uplifted heavenly weapons;","er":"With innumerable mouths and eyes, many marvelous aspects, numerous divine ornaments, and numerous divine weapons.","gu":"અસંખ્ય મુખ અને નેત્રોથી, અદ્ભુત દૃશ્યોથી, દૈવી અલંકારોથી, ઊંચા ઉઠેલા દૈવ-અસ્ત્રોથી, દૈવી માળ-વસ્ત્રોથી ભૂષિત, દૈવી સુગંધ-ઉબટણ ચર્ચિત — સર્વ-અદ્ભુત, સર્વ-દ્યુતિમાન, અનંત અને સર્વ દિશાઓ સામે મુખ કરીને ઊભું — એ અલૌકિક સ્વરૂપ!"},{"ref":"11.11","ch":11,"v":11,"sa":"दिव्यमाल्याम्बरधरं दिव्यगन्धानुलेपनम्।\nसर्वाश्चर्यमयं देवमनन्तं विश्वतोमुखम्।।11.11।।","tr":"divya-mālyāmbara-dharaṁ divya-gandhānulepanam\nsarvāśhcharya-mayaṁ devam anantaṁ viśhvato-mukham","en":"Wearing divine garlands and apparel, anointed with divine unguents, the all-wonderful, resplendent Being is endless with faces on all sides.","es":"Wearing heavenly garlands and apparel, anointed with heavenly scents, abounding in all kinds of wonders, resplendent, infinite, and with faces on all sides.","er":"Wearing celestial garlands and raiments, anointed with divine perfumes, full of wonders, resplendent, boundless, and facing all directions.","gu":"દિવ્ય માળાઓ અને વસ્ત્રો ધારણ કરેલ, દિવ્ય સુગંધ-લેપથી અભિષિક્ત, સર્વ-અદ્ભુત ઝળહળ, ચારે દિશામાં મુખ ધારી અને અનંત — એ અપ્રમેય સ્વરૂપ અર્જુને સાક્ષાત્ નિહાળ્યું."},{"ref":"11.12","ch":11,"v":12,"sa":"दिवि सूर्यसहस्रस्य भवेद्युगपदुत्थिता।\nयदि भाः सदृशी सा स्याद्भासस्तस्य महात्मनः।।11.12।।","tr":"divi sūrya-sahasrasya bhaved yugapad utthitā\nyadi bhāḥ sadṛiśhī sā syād bhāsas tasya mahātmanaḥ","en":"If the splendour of a thousand suns were to blaze out simultaneously in the sky, that would be the splendour of that mighty being.","es":"Should the effulgence of a thousand suns blaze forth simultaneously in the sky, that might be akin to the radiance of that exalted One.","er":"If a thousand suns were to rise at once in the sky, the resulting splendour would be like the splendour of that mighty One.","gu":"આકાશમાં એક સાથે હજાર સૂર્ય ઉદય પામે ત્યારે જે પ્રચંડ ઝળહળ-ઝળહળ પ્રકાશ ઉઠે, તે પ્રકાશ પણ આ મહા-પ્રભુના તેજ સમો ભાગ્યે જ થઈ શકે."},{"ref":"11.13","ch":11,"v":13,"sa":"तत्रैकस्थं जगत्कृत्स्नं प्रविभक्तमनेकधा।\nअपश्यद्देवदेवस्य शरीरे पाण्डवस्तदा।।11.13।।","tr":"tatraika-sthaṁ jagat kṛitsnaṁ pravibhaktam anekadhā\napaśhyad deva-devasya śharīre pāṇḍavas tadā","en":"There, in the body of the God of gods, Arjuna then saw the entire universe resting in one, with its myriad of divisions.","es":"At that time, the Pandava saw, in the body of the God of gods, the whole diversely differentiated universe united in one.","er":"There, Arjuna beheld the whole universe, with its manifold divisions gathered together in one single spot within the body of the God of gods.","gu":"ત્યારે, દેવ-અધિ-દેવ ભગવાનના દિવ્ય-દેહ ભીતર, અર્જુને સૃષ્ટિના અગણ્ય વિભાગો સહ સમસ્ત ચરાચર-જગત એક જ સ્થળે — એકત્ર ને સ્થિત — નિહાળ્યું."},{"ref":"11.14","ch":11,"v":14,"sa":"ततः स विस्मयाविष्टो हृष्टरोमा धनञ्जयः।\nप्रणम्य शिरसा देवं कृताञ्जलिरभाषत।।11.14।।","tr":"tataḥ sa vismayāviṣhṭo hṛiṣhṭa-romā dhanañjayaḥ\npraṇamya śhirasā devaṁ kṛitāñjalir abhāṣhata","en":"Then, Arjuna, filled with wonder and his hair standing on end, bowed his head to the God and spoke with palms joined.","es":"Then, filled with wonder and with hairs standing on end, Arjuna, bowing down with his head to the Lord, said with folded hands:","er":"Then, Arjuna, overcome with amazement, his hairs standing on end, bowed his head to the Lord and spoke with folded hands.","gu":"ત્યારે અર્જુન ઊંડા વિસ્મયથી ભરાઈ ગયો, અંગ-અંગ રોમ ઊભા થઈ ગયા; ભગવાન સામે શિર નમાવ્યું ને બે હાથ જોડી આ પ્રમાણે વિનમ્રભાવે બોલ્યો."},{"ref":"11.15","ch":11,"v":15,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nपश्यामि देवांस्तव देव देहे\nसर्वांस्तथा भूतविशेषसङ्घान्।\nब्रह्माणमीशं कमलासनस्थ\nमृषींश्च सर्वानुरगांश्च दिव्यान्।।11.15।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\npaśhyāmi devāns tava deva dehe\nsarvāns tathā bhūta-viśheṣha-saṅghān\nbrahmāṇam īśhaṁ kamalāsana-stham\nṛiṣhīnśh cha sarvān uragānśh cha divyān","en":"Arjuna said, \"O God, I see all the gods in Your body, as well as hosts of various classes of beings, Brahma the Lord seated on the lotus, all the sages, and the celestial serpents.\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O God, I see in Your body all the gods, as well as hosts of various classes of beings; Brahma the ruler, sitting on a lotus seat, and all the heavenly sages and serpents.","er":"Arjuna said, \"O Lord, I behold in Your body all the gods, and all the diverse hosts of beings—Brahma, Siva, who is in Brahma, the seers, and the lustrous snakes.\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યો: હે ભગવાન, આપના દિવ્ય દેહ ભીતર હું સઘળા દેવ-ગણ, સૃષ્ટિના સર્વ-વર્ગના જીવ, કમળ-આસને બ્રહ્માજી, સઘળા ઋષિઓ ને દિવ્ય સર્પ-ગણ — સૌ-ને પ્રત્યક્ષ જોઉં છું."},{"ref":"11.16","ch":11,"v":16,"sa":"अनेकबाहूदरवक्त्रनेत्रं\nपश्यामि त्वां सर्वतोऽनन्तरूपम्।\nनान्तं न मध्यं न पुनस्तवादिं\nपश्यामि विश्वेश्वर विश्वरूप।।11.16।।","tr":"aneka-bāhūdara-vaktra-netraṁ\npaśhyāmi tvāṁ sarvato ’nanta-rūpam\nnāntaṁ na madhyaṁ na punas tavādiṁ\npaśhyāmi viśhveśhvara viśhva-rūpa","en":"I see You with boundless form on every side, with many arms, stomachs, mouths, and eyes; neither the end nor the middle nor the beginning do I see, O Lord of the Universe, O Cosmic Form.","es":"I see You with numerous arms, bellies, mouths, and eyes; with infinite forms all around. O Lord of the Universe, O Cosmic Person, I see no limit, no middle, nor beginning!","er":"With manifold arms, stomachs, mouths, and eyes, I behold Your infinite form on all sides. I see no end, no middle, nor the beginning of You, O Lord of the universe, O You of Universal Form.","gu":"હે વિશ્વેશ્વર, આપને અસંખ્ય ભુજા, ઉદર, મુખ ને નેત્ર ધારી, ચારે ભણી અનંત સ્વરૂપ ધારણ કરેલ નિહાળું છું; આપનો ન આદિ, ન મધ્ય, ન અંત — ક્યાંય મને દેખાતો નથી."},{"ref":"11.17","ch":11,"v":17,"sa":"किरीटिनं गदिनं चक्रिणं च\nतेजोराशिं सर्वतोदीप्तिमन्तम्।\nपश्यामि त्वां दुर्निरीक्ष्यं समन्ता\nद्दीप्तानलार्कद्युतिमप्रमेयम्।।11.17।।","tr":"kirīṭinaṁ gadinaṁ chakriṇaṁ cha\ntejo-rāśhiṁ sarvato dīptimantam\npaśhyāmi tvāṁ durnirīkṣhyaṁ samantād\ndīptānalārka-dyutim aprameyam","en":"I see You with the diadem, club, and discus, a mass of radiance shining everywhere, very hard to look at, blazing all around like a burning fire and the sun, and immeasurable.","es":"I see You wearing a diadem, wielding a mace, and holding a disc; a mass of brilliance glowing all around, difficult to look at from all sides, possessing the radiance of the blazing fire and sun, and immeasurable.","er":"I behold You as a mass of light, shining everywhere, with a diadem, mace, and discus, hard to behold, blazing like a burning fire and the sun, and immeasurable.","gu":"આપને મુકુટ, ગદા ને ચક્ર ધારી, ચારે બાજુ ઝળહળતા પ્રકાશ-પૂંજ સ્વરૂપ; પ્રજ્વલિત અગ્નિ ને સૂર્ય સમા દેદીપ્યમાન, નેત્રો સામે ટકી ન શકાય તેવો અપ્રમેય — એ સ્વરૂપ નિહાળું છું."},{"ref":"11.18","ch":11,"v":18,"sa":"त्वमक्षरं परमं वेदितव्यं\nत्वमस्य विश्वस्य परं निधानम्।\nत्वमव्ययः शाश्वतधर्मगोप्ता\nसनातनस्त्वं पुरुषो मतो मे।।11.18।।","tr":"tvam akṣharaṁ paramaṁ veditavyaṁ\ntvam asya viśhvasya paraṁ nidhānam\ntvam avyayaḥ śhāśhvata-dharma-goptā\nsanātanas tvaṁ puruṣho mato me","en":"You are the Imperishable, the Supreme Being, worthy of being known. You are the great treasure-house of this universe; You are the imperishable protector of the eternal Dharma; You are the Primal Person, I believe.","es":"You are the Unchanging, the supreme One to be known; You are the most perfect repository of this Universe. You are the Imperishable, the Protector of the ever-existing religion; You are the eternal Person. This is my belief.","er":"You are the Imperishable, Supreme One to be realized. You are the Supreme Substratum of this universe. You are immutable, the guardian of the eternal law; I know You are the Supreme Person who is everlasting.","gu":"આપ જ અક્ષર, પરમ, આ જગતનો સર્વોચ્ચ આશ્રય; આપ જ ધર્મના સનાતન રક્ષક; આપ જ આદિ પુરુષ — આવું હું માનું છું."},{"ref":"11.19","ch":11,"v":19,"sa":"अनादिमध्यान्तमनन्तवीर्य\nमनन्तबाहुं शशिसूर्यनेत्रम्।\nपश्यामि त्वां दीप्तहुताशवक्त्रम्\nस्वतेजसा विश्वमिदं तपन्तम्।।11.19।।","tr":"स्वतेजसा विश्वमिदं तपन्तम् || 19||","en":"I see You without beginning, middle, or end, infinite in power, with endless arms, the sun and moon as Your eyes, the burning fire Your mouth, heating the entire universe with Your radiance.","es":"I see You as having no beginning, middle, or end, possessing infinite valor, with innumerable arms, the sun and moon as eyes, a mouth like a blazing fire, and heating up this universe with Your own brilliance.","er":"I behold You as having no beginning, middle, or end; Your might is infinite. You are endowed with an innumerable number of arms. The sun and moon are Your eyes, and Your mouth emits burning fire. With Your own radiance, You are warning the entire universe.","gu":"આપને આદિ, મધ્ય કે અંત વિના, અનંત શક્તિ ધારી, ચંદ્ર-સૂર્ય નેત્રો ધારી, પ્રજ્વલિત અગ્નિ-મુખ ધારી, સ્વ-તેજ વડે આ સર્વ સૃષ્ટિ તપાવતા — એ સ્વરૂપ નિહાળું છું."},{"ref":"11.20","ch":11,"v":20,"sa":"द्यावापृथिव्योरिदमन्तरं हि\nव्याप्तं त्वयैकेन दिशश्च सर्वाः।\nदृष्ट्वाऽद्भुतं रूपमुग्रं तवेदं\nलोकत्रयं प्रव्यथितं महात्मन्।।11.20।।","tr":"dyāv ā-pṛithivyor idam antaraṁ hi\nvyāptaṁ tvayaikena diśhaśh cha sarvāḥ\ndṛiṣhṭvādbhutaṁ rūpam ugraṁ tavedaṁ\nloka-trayaṁ pravyathitaṁ mahātman","en":"This space between the earth and the heavens, and all the quarters, is filled by You alone; having seen this, Your wonderful and terrible form, the three worlds are trembling with fear, O great-souled Being.","es":"Indeed, this intermediate space between heaven and earth, as well as all the directions, are pervaded by You alone. O exalted One, the three worlds are struck with fear upon seeing this strange and fearful form of Yours.","er":"You alone have pervaded the interspace between heaven and earth, and all the quarters. Beholding your marvelous and terrible form, O Mahatman, the three worlds are greatly overwhelmed with fear.","gu":"પૃથ્વી અને આકાશ વચ્ચેનો સઘળો અવકાશ અને સર્વ દિશાઓ — તે સઘળું ફક્ત આપ એકળાએ ભરી દીધું છે; હે મહાત્મા, આપનું આ અદ્ભુત ને ભયંકર સ્વરૂપ જોઈ ત્રણેય ભુવન કંપી ઊઠ્યા છે."},{"ref":"11.21","ch":11,"v":21,"sa":"अमी हि त्वां सुरसङ्घाः विशन्ति\nकेचिद्भीताः प्राञ्जलयो गृणन्ति।\nस्वस्तीत्युक्त्वा महर्षिसिद्धसङ्घाः\nस्तुवन्ति त्वां स्तुतिभिः पुष्कलाभिः।।11.21।।","tr":"amī hi tvāṁ sura-saṅghā viśhanti\nkechid bhītāḥ prāñjalayo gṛiṇanti\nsvastīty uktvā maharṣhi-siddha-saṅghāḥ\nstuvanti tvāṁ stutibhiḥ puṣhkalābhiḥ","en":"Verily, these hosts of gods enter into Thee; some extol Thee with joined palms in fear, saying, 'May it be well!' Bands of great sages and perfected ones praise Thee with complete hymns.","es":"Those very groups of gods enter into You; struck with fear, some extol You with joined palms. Groups of great sages and perfected beings praise You with elaborate hymns, saying, 'May it be well!'","er":"Verily, the hosts of Devas enter into You. Some, in fear, extol You with clasped hands, crying \"Hail!\" The bands of great seers and Siddhas praise You with meaningful hymns.","gu":"દેવોના સમૂહ આપની ભીતર ધસી રહ્યા છે; ભયભીત થઈ, હાથ જોડી, કેટલાક 'સ્વસ્તિ' ગાઈ આપની સ્તુતિ કરે છે; ઋષિઓ અને સિદ્ધોના ગણ ઉત્તમ સ્તોત્ર ગાઈ આપને વંદી રહ્યા છે."},{"ref":"11.22","ch":11,"v":22,"sa":"रुद्रादित्या वसवो ये च साध्या\nविश्वेऽश्िवनौ मरुतश्चोष्मपाश्च।\nगन्धर्वयक्षासुरसिद्धसङ्घा\nवीक्षन्ते त्वां विस्मिताश्चैव सर्वे।।11.22।।","tr":"rudrādityā vasavo ye cha sādhyā\nviśhve ’śhvinau marutaśh choṣhmapāśh cha\ngandharva-yakṣhāsura-siddha-saṅghā\nvīkṣhante tvāṁ vismitāśh chaiva sarve","en":"The Rudras, Adityas, Vasus, Sadhyas, Visvedevas, the two Asvins, Maruts, the Manus, and the hosts of celestial singers, Yakshas, demons, and the perfected ones, all look upon Thee with great amazement.","es":"Those who are the Rudras, the Adityas, the Vasus, and the Sadhyas, the Visvedevas, the two Asvins, the Maruts, and the Usmapas, and hosts of Gandharvas, Yaksas, demons, and Siddhas—all of those very ones gaze at You, being indeed struck with wonder.","er":"The Rudras, the Adityas, the Vasus, the Sadhyas, the Visvas, the Asvins, the Maruts, and the Manes, as well as the hosts of Gandharvas, Yaksas, Asuras, and Siddhas—all gaze upon You in amazement.","gu":"રુદ્રો, આદિત્યો, વસુઓ, સાધ્યો, વિશ્વદેવો, અશ્વિની-કુમારો, મરુતો ને સર્વ દિવ્ય-ગણ — સૌ આશ્ચર્યચકિત થઈ આપને નિહાળી રહ્યા છે."},{"ref":"11.23","ch":11,"v":23,"sa":"रूपं महत्ते बहुवक्त्रनेत्रं\nमहाबाहो बहुबाहूरुपादम्।\nबहूदरं बहुदंष्ट्राकरालं\nदृष्ट्वा लोकाः प्रव्यथितास्तथाऽहम्।।11.23।।","tr":"rūpaṁ mahat te bahu-vaktra-netraṁ\nmahā-bāho bahu-bāhūru-pādam\nbahūdaraṁ bahu-danṣhṭrā-karālaṁ\ndṛiṣhṭvā lokāḥ pravyathitās tathāham","en":"Having seen Your immeasurable form with many mouths and eyes, O mighty-armed one, with many arms, thighs, and feet, with many stomachs and fearsome with many teeth, the worlds are terrified, and so am I.","es":"O Mighty-Armed One, seeing Your immense form with many mouths, eyes, arms, thighs, feet, bellies, and teeth, the creatures are struck with terror, and so am I.","er":"Beholding Your great form with many mouths and eyes, many arms, thighs, and feet, many stomachs, and terrible with many teeth, the worlds tremble, and I too quake, O mighty-armed one.","gu":"હે મહાબાહુ, આપના અગણ્ય મુખ, નેત્ર, ભુજા, ઊરુ, ચરણ, ઉદર ને ભયંકર દાઢ ધારાવતા અપ્રમેય સ્વરૂપ નિહાળી સર્વ લોક ભયભીત છે, તેમ હું પણ ભયભીત છું."},{"ref":"11.24","ch":11,"v":24,"sa":"नभःस्पृशं दीप्तमनेकवर्णं\nव्यात्ताननं दीप्तविशालनेत्रम्।\nदृष्ट्वा हि त्वां प्रव्यथितान्तरात्मा\nधृतिं न विन्दामि शमं च विष्णो।।11.24।।","tr":"nabhaḥ-spṛiśhaṁ dīptam aneka-varṇaṁ\nvyāttānanaṁ dīpta-viśhāla-netram\ndṛiṣhṭvā hi tvāṁ pravyathitāntar-ātmā\ndhṛitiṁ na vindāmi śhamaṁ cha viṣhṇo","en":"On seeing Thee, touching the sky, shining in many colors, with mouths wide open, with large fiery eyes, I am terrified at heart and find neither courage nor peace, O Vishnu.","es":"O Vishnu, indeed, upon seeing Your form touching the heavens, blazing with many colors, open-mouthed, with fiery, large eyes, I become terrified in my mind and do not find steadiness and peace.","er":"When I behold You touching the Supreme Heaven, shining, multicolored, with yawning mouths and large, resplendent eyes, my inner being trembles in fear. I am unable to find support or peace, O Vishnu.","gu":"હે વિષ્ણુ, આકાશ સ્પર્શતા, અનેક રંગો ઝળળતા, ખુલા મોટા મુખ ને પ્રચંડ અગ્નિ-નેત્રો ધારી આપને નિહાળી મારો ભાવ ભયભીત છે; ધૈર્ય ને શાંતિ ક્યાંય મળતી નથી."},{"ref":"11.25","ch":11,"v":25,"sa":"दंष्ट्राकरालानि च ते मुखानि\nदृष्ट्वैव कालानलसन्निभानि।\nदिशो न जाने न लभे च शर्म\nप्रसीद देवेश जगन्निवास।।11.25।।","tr":"danṣhṭrā-karālāni cha te mukhāni\ndṛiṣhṭvaiva kālānala-sannibhāni\ndiśho na jāne na labhe cha śharma\nprasīda deveśha jagan-nivāsa","en":"Having seen Thy mouths fearful with teeth blazing like the fires of cosmic dissolution, I know not the four quarters, nor do I find peace. Have mercy, O Lord of the gods, O abode of the universe.","es":"Having merely seen Your mouths made terrible with their teeth and resembling the fire of Dissolution, I have lost my sense of direction and find no comfort. Be gracious, O Lord of gods, O Abode of the Universe.","er":"Viewing Your mouths, presenting awe-generating fangs and looking like the consuming fire of final destruction, I know not the quarters of the globe nor do I find repose. Be gracious, O Lord of the Devas! O Abode of the universe!","gu":"પ્રલયની અગ્નિ સમ ઝળહળતી દાઢો ધારાવતા આપના ભયંકર મુખો નિહાળી ચારેય દિશા ભૂલી ગયો છું; ક્યાંય શાંતિ મળતી નથી — હે દેવોના પ્રભુ, હે વિશ્વના આધાર, કૃપા કરો."},{"ref":"11.26","ch":11,"v":26,"sa":"अमी च त्वां धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्राः\nसर्वे सहैवावनिपालसङ्घैः।\nभीष्मो द्रोणः सूतपुत्रस्तथाऽसौ\nसहास्मदीयैरपि योधमुख्यैः।।11.26।।","tr":"amī cha tvāṁ dhṛitarāśhtrasya putrāḥ\nsarve sahaivāvani-pāla-saṅghaiḥ\nbhīṣhmo droṇaḥ sūta-putras tathāsau\nsahāsmadīyair api yodha-mukhyaiḥ\n vaktrāṇi te tvaramāṇā viśhanti\ndanṣhṭrā-karālāni bhayānakāni\nkechid vilagnā daśhanāntareṣhu\nsandṛiśhyante chūrṇitair uttamāṅgaiḥ","en":"All the sons of Dhritarashtra, along with the hosts of kings of the earth, Bhishma, Drona, and Karna, as well as the chief among our warriors.","es":"And into You enter all those sons of Dhrtarastra, along with multitudes of the rulers of the earth, Bhisma, Drona, and that son of a Suta, Karna, together with our prominent warriors.","er":"All these sons of Dhrtarastra, together with the hosts of monarchs, Bhisma, Drona, and Karna, along with the leading warriors of our side,","gu":"ધૃતરાષ્ટ્રના સર્વ પુત્રો, રાજાઓના સૈન્ય સહિત, ભીષ્મ, દ્રોણ, કર્ણ અને આપણા મુખ્ય યોદ્ધાઓ — સૌ આપના ભયાનક, ભયયુક્ત મુખોમાં ધસી રહ્યા છે. એ વિકરાળ મુખો જોઈ અર્જુનનું હૃદય ધ્રૂજી ઊઠ્યું."},{"ref":"11.27","ch":11,"v":27,"sa":"वक्त्राणि ते त्वरमाणा विशन्ति\nदंष्ट्राकरालानि भयानकानि।\nकेचिद्विलग्ना दशनान्तरेषु\nसंदृश्यन्ते चूर्णितैरुत्तमाङ्गैः।।11.27।।","tr":"vaktrāṇi te tvaramāṇā viśanti daṁṣṭrā-karālāni bhayānakāni kecid vilagnā daśanāntareṣu sandṛśyante cūrṇitair uttamāṅgaiḥ","en":"Some hurry into Your mouths with their terrible teeth, fearful to behold. Some are found stuck in the gaps between the teeth, their heads crushed to powder.","es":"They rapidly enter into Your terrible mouths with cruel teeth! Some are seen sticking in the gaps between the teeth, with their heads crushed!","er":"Hasten to enter Your fearful mouths with terrible fangs, crushing some of those caught between the teeth to powder.","gu":"કેટલાક યોદ્ધાઓ દાંત વચ્ચે ચૂરાઈ રહ્યા છે, તેમના મસ્તક ભૂકો થઈ જઈ રહ્યા છે. જેમ નદીઓ સમુદ્ર તરફ ધસે, તેમ આ સૌ વીરો આપના પ્રજ્વળિત મુખોમાં ધસી રહ્યા છે."},{"ref":"11.28","ch":11,"v":28,"sa":"यथा नदीनां बहवोऽम्बुवेगाः\nसमुद्रमेवाभिमुखाः द्रवन्ति।\nतथा तवामी नरलोकवीरा\nविशन्ति वक्त्राण्यभिविज्वलन्ति।।11.28।।","tr":"yathā nadīnāṁ bahavo ’mbu-vegāḥ\nsamudram evābhimukhā dravanti\ntathā tavāmī nara-loka-vīrā\nviśhanti vaktrāṇy abhivijvalanti","en":"Verily, just as many torrents of rivers flow towards the ocean, so too these heroes in the world of men enter Thy flaming mouths.","es":"As the numerous currents of the waters of rivers rush towards the sea alone, so too do those heroes of the human world enter into Your blazing mouths.","er":"As many torrents of rivers flow towards the ocean, so do these heroes of the world of men enter into Your flaming mouths.","gu":"જેમ પતંગિયાં પ્રદીપ્ત અગ્નિ તરફ ઝડપથી ધસી પોતાનો નાશ કરે છે, તેમ આ સૌ પ્રાણીઓ પણ પોતાના વિનાશ માટે આપના મુખોમાં ઝડપભેર ધસી રહ્યા છે."},{"ref":"11.29","ch":11,"v":29,"sa":"यथा प्रदीप्तं ज्वलनं पतङ्गा\nविशन्ति नाशाय समृद्धवेगाः।\nतथैव नाशाय विशन्ति लोका\nस्तवापि वक्त्राणि समृद्धवेगाः।।11.29।।","tr":"yathā pradīptaṁ jvalanaṁ pataṅgā\nviśhanti nāśhāya samṛiddha-vegāḥ\ntathaiva nāśhāya viśhanti lokās\ntavāpi vaktrāṇi samṛiddha-vegāḥ","en":"As moths hurriedly rush into a blazing fire, leading to their own destruction, so too these creatures hurry into Your mouths, leading to their own destruction.","es":"As moths hasten with increased speed into a blazing fire for destruction, so too do creatures hasten into Your mouths with increased speed for destruction.","er":"As moths rush swiftly into a blazing fire, leading to their destruction, so do these men swiftly rush into Your mouths, leading to their destruction.","gu":"આપ પ્રજ્વળિત મુખોથી સર્વ લોકોને ચાટીને ગ્રસી લો છો. આપના પ્રચંડ તેજ-પ્રવાહ સમગ્ર બ્રહ્માંડને પ્રકાશિત કરીને ભસ્મ કરી રહ્યા છે."},{"ref":"11.30","ch":11,"v":30,"sa":"लेलिह्यसे ग्रसमानः समन्ता\nल्लोकान्समग्रान्वदनैर्ज्वलद्भिः।\nतेजोभिरापूर्य जगत्समग्रं\nभासस्तवोग्राः प्रतपन्ति विष्णो।।11.30।।","tr":"lelihyase grasamānaḥ samantāl\nlokān samagrān vadanair jvaladbhiḥ\ntejobhir āpūrya jagat samagraṁ\nbhāsas tavogrāḥ pratapanti viṣhṇo","en":"Thou lickest up, devouring all the worlds on every side with Thy flaming mouths. Thy fierce rays, filling the whole world with radiance, burn, O Vishnu!","es":"You lick Your lips as You devour all creatures from every side with flaming mouths that fill the entire world with heat.","er":"Devouring all the worlds on every side with your flaming mouths, you lick them up. Your fiery rays, filling the whole universe with their radiance, scorch it, O Vishnu.","gu":"આ ઘોર સ્વરૂપ ધારણ કરનારા, આપ કોણ છો — તે મને કહો. હે પરમ ઈશ્વર, હું આપને નમસ્કાર કરું છું; આપ મારા પ્રત્યે કૃપા કરો. હે આદ્ય પ્રભુ, હું આપને ઓળખવા ઇચ્છું છું."},{"ref":"11.31","ch":11,"v":31,"sa":"आख्याहि मे को भवानुग्ररूपो\nनमोऽस्तु ते देववर प्रसीद।\nविज्ञातुमिच्छामि भवन्तमाद्यं\nन हि प्रजानामि तव प्रवृत्तिम्।।11.31।।","tr":"ākhyāhi me ko bhavān ugra-rūpo\nnamo ’stu te deva-vara prasīda\nvijñātum ichchhāmi bhavantam ādyaṁ\nna hi prajānāmi tava pravṛittim","en":"Tell me, who you are, so fierce of form. I offer my salutations to you, O God Supreme; have mercy on me. I desire to know you, the original Being. I do not indeed know your workings.","es":"Tell me who You are, fierce in form. Salutations to You, O Supreme God; be gracious. I desire to fully know You, who are the Prime One. For I do not understand Your actions!","er":"Tell me, who are You with this terrible form? Salutations to You, O Supreme God. Be gracious to me. I desire to know You, the Primal One. I do not know Your activities.","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હું પ્રચંડ, સર્વ-સંહારક કાળ છું, જે હાલ સમસ્ત લોકોનો નાશ કરવામાં પ્રવૃત્ત છું. તારા વિના પણ, સામેના સૈન્યમાં ઊભેલા આ સૌ યોદ્ધાઓ નષ્ટ થવાના જ છે."},{"ref":"11.32","ch":11,"v":32,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nकालोऽस्मि लोकक्षयकृत्प्रवृद्धो\nलोकान्समाहर्तुमिह प्रवृत्तः।\nऋतेऽपि त्वां न भविष्यन्ति सर्वे\nयेऽवस्थिताः प्रत्यनीकेषु योधाः।।11.32।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nkālo ’smi loka-kṣhaya-kṛit pravṛiddho\nlokān samāhartum iha pravṛittaḥ\nṛite ’pi tvāṁ na bhaviṣhyanti sarve\nye ’vasthitāḥ pratyanīkeṣhu yodhāḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"I am the full-grown, world-destroying Time, now engaged in destroying the worlds. Even without you, none of the warriors arrayed in the hostile armies will live.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"I am the world-destroying Time, grown in stature and now engaged in annihilating the creatures. Even without you, all the warriors arrayed in the confronting armies will cease to exist!\"","er":"The Lord said, \"I am the world-destroying Time. Manifesting myself fully, I have begun to destroy the worlds here. Even without you, none of the warriors arrayed in the hostile ranks will survive.\"","gu":"કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: આમિ બિશ્બનાશકારી મહાકાલ। એઇ યોદ્ધારા તુમિ છાડ઼ાઓ નષ્ટ હબે।"},{"ref":"11.33","ch":11,"v":33,"sa":"तस्मात्त्वमुत्तिष्ठ यशो लभस्व\nजित्वा शत्रून् भुङ्क्ष्व राज्यं समृद्धम्।\nमयैवैते निहताः पूर्वमेव\nनिमित्तमात्रं भव सव्यसाचिन्।।11.33।।","tr":"tasmāt tvam uttiṣhṭha yaśho labhasva\njitvā śhatrūn bhuṅkṣhva rājyaṁ samṛiddham\nmayaivaite nihatāḥ pūrvam eva\nnimitta-mātraṁ bhava savya-sāchin","en":"Therefore, stand up and obtain fame. Conquer the enemies and enjoy the unparalleled kingdom. Verily, by Me they have already been slain; be thou a mere instrument, O Arjuna.","es":"Therefore, rise up and gain fame; and, defeating the enemies, enjoy a prosperous kingdom. These have been killed by Me even earlier; be you merely an instrument, O Savyasacin (Arjuna).","er":"Therefore, arise, win glory. Conquering your foes, enjoy a prosperous kingdom. By Me they have already been slain. You be merely an instrument, O Arjuna, you great archer!"},{"ref":"11.34","ch":11,"v":34,"sa":"द्रोणं च भीष्मं च जयद्रथं च\nकर्णं तथाऽन्यानपि योधवीरान्।\nमया हतांस्त्वं जहि मा व्यथिष्ठा\nयुध्यस्व जेतासि रणे सपत्नान्।।11.34।।","tr":"droṇaṁ cha bhīṣhmaṁ cha jayadrathaṁ cha\nkarṇaṁ tathānyān api yodha-vīrān\nmayā hatāṁs tvaṁ jahi mā vyathiṣhṭhā\nyudhyasva jetāsi raṇe sapatnān","en":"Drona, Bhishma, Jayadratha, Karna, and other brave warriors have already been slain by Me; do not be distressed with fear; fight and you shall conquer your enemies in battle.","es":"You destroy Drona, Bhisma, Jayadratha, Karna, and the other heroic warriors who have been killed by Me. Do not be afraid. Fight! You will conquer the enemies in battle.","er":"Slay Drona, Bhisma, Jayadratha, Karna, as well as other mighty warriors who have been doomed by Me. Do not feel distressed. Fight; you shall conquer your rivals in the battle.","gu":"દ્રોણ, ભીષ્મ, જયદ્રથ, કર્ણ અને અન્ય બળવાન વીરો મારા વડે પહેલેથી જ હણાઈ ચૂક્યા છે; ભય પામ્યા વિના યુદ્ધ કર. તું સંગ્રામમાં શત્રુઓ ઉપર અવશ્ય વિજય મેળવીશ."},{"ref":"11.35","ch":11,"v":35,"sa":"सञ्जय उवाच\nएतच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं केशवस्य\nकृताञ्जलिर्वेपमानः किरीटी।\nनमस्कृत्वा भूय एवाह कृष्णं\nसगद्गदं भीतभीतः प्रणम्य।।11.35।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\netach chhrutvā vachanaṁ keśhavasya\nkṛitāñjalir vepamānaḥ kirīṭī\nnamaskṛitvā bhūya evāha kṛiṣhṇaṁ\nsa-gadgadaṁ bhīta-bhītaḥ praṇamya","en":"Sanjaya said, Having heard that speech of Lord Krishna, Arjuna, with joined palms, trembling, prostrated himself, again addressing Krishna in a choked voice, bowing down, overwhelmed with fear.","es":"Sanjaya said: Hearing this utterance of Kesava, Kiriti (Arjuna), with joined palms and trembling, prostrated himself, and then, with a faltering voice, bowed down and overcome by fits of fear, said again to Krsna:","er":"Sanjaya said, Having heard this speech of Krsna, Arjuna did Him obeisance; and trembling with awe, he bowed down again, and with folded palms, his voice choked with emotion, he spoke to Krsna.","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: શ્રીકૃષ્ણનાં એ વચનો સાંભળી, ધ્રૂજતા અર્જુને ભારે ભય સાથે હાથ જોડ્યા, ફરી નમ્રતાથી નમ્યા, અને ગળગળા, ધ્રૂજતા સ્વરે બોલ્યા."},{"ref":"11.36","ch":11,"v":36,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nस्थाने हृषीकेश तव प्रकीर्त्या\nजगत् प्रहृष्यत्यनुरज्यते च।\nरक्षांसि भीतानि दिशो द्रवन्ति\nसर्वे नमस्यन्ति च सिद्धसङ्घाः।।11.36।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nsthāne hṛiṣhīkeśha tava prakīrtyā\njagat prahṛiṣhyaty anurajyate cha\nrakṣhānsi bhītāni diśho dravanti\nsarve namasyanti cha siddha-saṅghāḥ","en":"Arjuna said, \"It is fitting, O Krishna, that the world delights and rejoices in Your praise; demons fly in fear in all directions and the hosts of the perfected ones bow to You.\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Hrsikesa, it is proper that the world be delighted and attracted by Your praise; that the Raksasas, stricken with fear, run in all directions; and that all the groups of the Siddhas bow down to You.\"","er":"Arjuna said, Rightly it is, O Krsna, that Your praise should move the world to joy and love. The rakshasas flee in fear on all sides, and all the hosts of siddhas bow down to You.","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે ઈશ્વર, આ જગત આપની સ્તુતિ કરીને આનંદ પામે તે સ્વાભાવિક છે; રાક્ષસો ભયભીત થઈ ચારે દિશામાં ભાગે છે, અને સિદ્ધ-સંઘ સર્વ આપને ભક્તિભાવથી નમે છે."},{"ref":"11.37","ch":11,"v":37,"sa":"कस्माच्च ते न नमेरन्महात्मन्\nगरीयसे ब्रह्मणोऽप्यादिकर्त्रे।\nअनन्त देवेश जगन्निवास\nत्वमक्षरं सदसत्तत्परं यत्।।11.37।।","tr":"kasmāch cha te na nameran mahātman\ngarīyase brahmaṇo ’py ādi-kartre\nananta deveśha jagan-nivāsa\ntvam akṣharaṁ sad-asat tat paraṁ yat","en":"And why should they not, O great Soul, bow to Thee Who art greater than all else, the primal cause even of the Creator (Brahma), O Infinite Being, O Lord of the gods, O Abode of the universe; Thou art the imperishable, the Being, the non-being, and That which is supreme—that which is beyond the Being and the non-being.","es":"And why should they not bow down to You, O exalted One, who are greater than all and who are the first Creator even of Brahma! O infinite One, supreme God, Abode of the Universe, You are the Immutable, being and non-being, and that which is Transcendental.","er":"(a) And why should they not, O Mahatma, bow down to You who are great, being the first Creator, even of Brahma?\n(b) O Infinite, Lord of gods, O You who have the universe as Your abode! You are the imperishable individual self, the existent and the non-existent, and that which is beyond both.","gu":"હે મહાત્મા, સૌથી પ્રથમ સ્રષ્ટા, બ્રહ્માથી પણ મહાન, તેઓ આપને કેમ ન નમે? હે અનંત, હે દેવોના સ્વામી, હે વિશ્વના નિવાસસ્થાન — આપ સૌ કારણોથી નમવા યોગ્ય છો."},{"ref":"11.38","ch":11,"v":38,"sa":"त्वमादिदेवः पुरुषः पुराण\nस्त्वमस्य विश्वस्य परं निधानम्।\nवेत्तासि वेद्यं च परं च धाम\nत्वया ततं विश्वमनन्तरूप।।11.38।।","tr":"tvam ādi-devaḥ puruṣhaḥ purāṇas\ntvam asya viśhvasya paraṁ nidhānam\nvettāsi vedyaṁ cha paraṁ cha dhāma\ntvayā tataṁ viśhvam ananta-rūpa","en":"You are the primal God, the ancient Purusha, the supreme refuge of this universe, the knower, the knowable, and the supreme Abode. Through You, the universe is pervaded, O Being of infinite forms.","es":"You are the primal Deity, the ancient Person; You are the supreme Refuge of this world. You are the knower and the object of knowledge, and the supreme Abode. O You of infinite forms, You pervade the Universe!","er":"(a) You are the Primal God and the Ancient One. You are the Supreme resting place of the universe...\n(b)...You are the Knower and the object of knowledge, and the Supreme Abode. Through You, O infinite of form, is this universe pervaded.","gu":"આપ આદ્ય ઈશ્વર, સનાતન પુરુષ, આ સૃષ્ટિના પરમ આશ્રય છો; આપ જ્ઞાતા, જ્ઞેય અને પરમ ધામ છો. હે અનંત, આ સમગ્ર વિશ્વ આપ વડે જ વ્યાપ્ત છે."},{"ref":"11.39","ch":11,"v":39,"sa":"वायुर्यमोऽग्निर्वरुणः शशाङ्कः\nप्रजापतिस्त्वं प्रपितामहश्च।\nनमो नमस्तेऽस्तु सहस्रकृत्वः\nपुनश्च भूयोऽपि नमो नमस्ते।।11.39।।","tr":"vāyur yamo ’gnir varuṇaḥ śhaśhāṅkaḥ\nprajāpatis tvaṁ prapitāmahaśh cha\nnamo namas te ’stu sahasra-kṛitvaḥ\npunaśh cha bhūyo ’pi namo namas te","en":"You are Vayu, Yama, Agni, Varuna, the moon, the Creator, and the great-grandfather. I offer my salutations to You a thousand times, and again I offer my salutations to You.","es":"You are air, death, fire, the god of the waters, the moon, the Lord of creatures, and the great-grandfather. Salutations to you a thousand times! Salutations to you again and again! Salutations!","er":"(a) You are Yayu, Yama, Agni, Varuna, Sashanka, Prajapati, and the great-grandsire.\n(b) Hail to You a thousand times! Hail to You again and yet again!","gu":"આપ વાયુ, યમ, અગ્નિ, વરુણ, ચંદ્ર, પ્રજાપતિ અને પ્રપિતામહ — સૌ-સ્વરૂપ છો. આપને હજારો વાર, વારંવાર, ફરી-ફરી નમસ્કાર હો."},{"ref":"11.40","ch":11,"v":40,"sa":"नमः पुरस्तादथ पृष्ठतस्ते\nनमोऽस्तु ते सर्वत एव सर्व।\nअनन्तवीर्यामितविक्रमस्त्वं\nसर्वं समाप्नोषि ततोऽसि सर्वः।।11.40।।","tr":"namaḥ purastād atha pṛiṣhṭhatas te\nnamo ’stu te sarvata eva sarva\nananta-vīryāmita-vikramas tvaṁ\nsarvaṁ samāpnoṣhi tato ’si sarvaḥ","en":"Salutations to You in front and behind! Salutations to You on every side! O All! You, infinite in power and prowess, pervade all; therefore You are all.","es":"Salutations to You in the East and behind. Salutations to You on all sides indeed, O All! You possess infinite strength and infinite heroism. You pervade everything; thus You are all!","er":"(a) Salutations to You from before and behind! Salutations to You from all sides, O All!৷৷.\n(b) ৷৷. O You of infinite prowess and heroic action, which are measureless! You pervade all beings, and therefore, You are all.","gu":"આગળથી અને પાછળથી, ચારે બાજુ, હે સર્વ-સ્વરૂપ — આપને નમ:; આપ સર્વ-શક્તિ, સર્વ-વ્યાપ્ત, સર્વ-ક્ષમ છો. આપ સઘળું સિદ્ધ કરો છો."},{"ref":"11.41","ch":11,"v":41,"sa":"सखेति मत्वा प्रसभं यदुक्तं\nहे कृष्ण हे यादव हे सखेति।\nअजानता महिमानं तवेदं\nमया प्रमादात्प्रणयेन वापि।।11.41।।","tr":"sakheti matvā prasabhaṁ yad uktaṁ\nhe kṛiṣhṇa he yādava he sakheti\najānatā mahimānaṁ tavedaṁ\nmayā pramādāt praṇayena vāpi","en":"Whatever I have presumptuously said from carelessness or love, addressing You as O Krishna! O Yadava! O Friend! regarding You merely as a friend, unknowing of Your greatness.","es":"Without knowing Your greatness, whatever I said rashly, inadvertently, or even out of familiarity, thinking You to be a friend, addressing You as 'O Krsna,' 'O Yadava,' 'O friend,' etc.","er":"Unaware of Your majesty, and either out of negligence or love, or considering You to be a friend, whatever I have said rudely, such as 'O Krsna, O Yadava, O Comrade,'","gu":"હે અચ્યુત, હે યદુ-શ્રેષ્ઠ, હે સખા — એ સંબોધનોથી, ગાફેલપણે કે પ્રેમવશ, જે કંઈ બેફામ બોલ્યો હોઉં, હે અમાપ, તે સૌ ક્ષમા કરો."},{"ref":"11.42","ch":11,"v":42,"sa":"यच्चावहासार्थमसत्कृतोऽसि\nविहारशय्यासनभोजनेषु।\nएकोऽथवाप्यच्युत तत्समक्षं\nतत्क्षामये त्वामहमप्रमेयम्।।11.42।।","tr":"yach chāvahāsārtham asat-kṛito ’si\nvihāra-śhayyāsana-bhojaneṣhu\neko ’tha vāpy achyuta tat-samakṣhaṁ\ntat kṣhāmaye tvām aham aprameyam","en":"In whatever way I may have insulted You for the sake of fun, while at play, reposing, sitting, or at meals, when alone (with You), O Krishna, or in company, that I implore You, immeasurable one, to forgive.","es":"And that You have been discourteously treated out of fun—while walking, while on a bed, while on a seat, while eating, in privacy, or, O Acyuta, even in public—for that, I beg pardon of You, the incomprehensible One.","er":"And whatever disrespect has been shown to You in jest, while playing, resting, sitting, or eating, whether alone or in the presence of others, O Acyuta—I implore You for forgiveness, You who are incomprehensible.","gu":"હે અપ્રમેય! રમત-ગમત, આરામ, બેઠક કે ભોજન દરમ્યાન — એકાંતમાં અથવા સૌ સમક્ષ — મેં જે કોઈ રીતે આપનું અપમાન કર્યું હોય, તે સઘળા માટે હું આપ પાસે ક્ષમા માંગું છું. હે ભગવન, મારી ભૂલો ક્ષમા કરો."},{"ref":"11.43","ch":11,"v":43,"sa":"पितासि लोकस्य चराचरस्य\nत्वमस्य पूज्यश्च गुरुर्गरीयान्।\nन त्वत्समोऽस्त्यभ्यधिकः कुतोऽन्यो\nलोकत्रयेऽप्यप्रतिमप्रभाव।।11.43।।","tr":"pitāsi lokasya charācharasya\ntvam asya pūjyaśh cha gurur garīyān\nna tvat-samo ’sty abhyadhikaḥ kuto ’nyo\nloka-traye ’py apratima-prabhāva","en":"Thou art the Father of this world, both moving and unmoving. Thou art to be adored by this world; Thou, the greatest Guru; for none exists who is equal to Thee; how then could there be another superior to Thee in the three worlds, O Being of unrivaled power?","es":"You are the Father of all beings, both moving and non-moving; to You, the Teacher, are they worthy of worship, and You are greater than a teacher. There is none equal to You; how can there be anyone greater even in all the three worlds, O You of unrivaled power?","er":"You are the father of this world, of all that moves and does not move. You are its teacher and the one most worthy of reverence. There is none equal to You. How then could there be in the three worlds another greater than You, O Being of matchless greatness?","gu":"આ ચર-અચર જગતના આપ પિતા છો, આપ સૌથી મહાન ગુરુ છો; ત્રણેય લોકમાં આપ જેવું સામર્થ્ય ધરાવનાર કોઈ નથી, તો આપ સમોવડિયું ક્યાંથી હોય? હે પ્રભો, આ સૃષ્ટિમાં આપ અતુલ્ય અને અનન્ય છો."},{"ref":"11.44","ch":11,"v":44,"sa":"तस्मात्प्रणम्य प्रणिधाय कायं\nप्रसादये त्वामहमीशमीड्यम्।\nपितेव पुत्रस्य सखेव सख्युः\nप्रियः प्रियायार्हसि देव सोढुम्।।11.44।।","tr":"tasmāt praṇamya praṇidhāya kāyaṁ\nprasādaye tvām aham īśham īḍyam\npiteva putrasya sakheva sakhyuḥ\npriyaḥ priyāyārhasi deva soḍhum","en":"Therefore, bowing down and prostrating my body, I crave Thy forgiveness, O adorable Lord. As a father forgives his son, a friend his dear friend, a lover his beloved, even so may Thou forgive me, O God.","es":"Therefore, by bowing down and prostrating my body, I seek to propitiate You who are God and are adorable. O Lord, You should forgive my faults as a father would forgive the faults of a son, as a friend would forgive the faults of a friend, and as a lover would forgive the faults of a beloved.","er":"Therefore, bowing down and prostrating my body, I implore Your mercy, O adorable Lord. As a father listens to his son or a friend to his friend, it is fitting, O Lord, that You, who are dear to me, should bear with me who am dear to You.","gu":"તેથી, મારા શરીરને ભૂમિ પર નમાવી, હે આરાધ્ય પ્રભો, હું આપ પાસે ક્ષમાની ભિક્ષા માંગું છું. જેમ પિતા પુત્રને, મિત્ર સખાને, અને પ્રિયજન પ્રિયતમને ક્ષમા આપે છે, તેમ હે ઈશ્વર, આપ મને ક્ષમા કરો."},{"ref":"11.45","ch":11,"v":45,"sa":"अदृष्टपूर्वं हृषितोऽस्मि दृष्ट्वा\nभयेन च प्रव्यथितं मनो मे।\nतदेव मे दर्शय देव रूपं\nप्रसीद देवेश जगन्निवास।।11.45।।","tr":"adṛiṣhṭa-pūrvaṁ hṛiṣhito ’smi dṛiṣhṭvā\nbhayena cha pravyathitaṁ mano me\ntad eva me darśhaya deva rūpaṁ\nprasīda deveśha jagan-nivāsa","en":"I am delighted, having seen something never seen before; yet my mind is distressed with fear. Show me that form only, O God; have mercy, O God of gods, O Abode of the universe.","es":"I am delighted by seeing something I have not seen before, and my mind is stricken with fear. O Lord, show me that very form; O Supreme God, O Abode of the Universe, be gracious!","er":"Seeing something never seen before, I am delighted. But my mind is also filled with awe. Show me, O Lord! Your other form. O Lord of the gods! Be gracious, O Abode of the universe!","gu":"પ્રથમ ક્યારેય ન જોયેલ રૂપ નિહાળી હું આનંદિત થયો, પરંતુ ભયથી મારું મન વ્યાકુળ થઈ ગયું છે. હે દેવેશ, હે જગન્નિવાસ, મહેર કરો — મને ફરી તે ચતુર્ભુજ, સૌમ્ય સ્વરૂપ જ દેખાડો."},{"ref":"11.46","ch":11,"v":46,"sa":"किरीटिनं गदिनं चक्रहस्त\nमिच्छामि त्वां द्रष्टुमहं तथैव।\nतेनैव रूपेण चतुर्भुजेन\nसहस्रबाहो भव विश्वमूर्ते।।11.46।।","tr":"kirīṭinaṁ gadinaṁ chakra-hastam\nichchhāmi tvāṁ draṣhṭum ahaṁ tathaiva\ntenaiva rūpeṇa chatur-bhujena\nsahasra-bāho bhava viśhva-mūrte","en":"I desire to see You as before, crowned, bearing a mace, with the discus in hand, in Your former form only, having four arms, O thousand-armed, Cosmic Being.","es":"I want to see You just as before, wearing a crown, wielding a mace, and holding a disc in hand. O You with a thousand arms, O You of Cosmic form, appear with that very form with four hands.","er":"I wish to see You ever as before, with crown and mace and discus in hand. Assume again that four-armed shape, O Thou the thousand-armed, of Universal Form!","gu":"હું આપને પૂર્વ-નિહારેલ સ્વરૂપે — કિરીટ, ગદા અને ચક્ર ધારણ કરેલ, ચાર ભુજાવાળા — જ જોવા ઈચ્છું છું. હે સહસ્ત્રબાહો, હે વિશ્વરૂપ, ફરી આ ઓળખ્યું-ભાળ્યું સ્વરૂપ ધારણ કરો."},{"ref":"11.47","ch":11,"v":47,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nमया प्रसन्नेन तवार्जुनेदं\nरूपं परं दर्शितमात्मयोगात्।\nतेजोमयं विश्वमनन्तमाद्यं\nयन्मे त्वदन्येन न दृष्टपूर्वम्।।11.47।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nmayā prasannena tavārjunedaṁ\nrūpaṁ paraṁ darśhitam ātma-yogāt\ntejo-mayaṁ viśhvam anantam ādyaṁ\nyan me tvad anyena na dṛiṣhṭa-pūrvam","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O Arjuna, this Cosmic Form has graciously been shown to you by Me through My own Yogic power. It is full of splendour, primeval, and infinite; this Cosmic Form of Mine has never been seen before by anyone other than you.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, Out of grace, O Arjuna, this supreme, radiant, cosmic, infinite, primeval form—which no one other than you has seen before—has been shown to you by Me through the power of My own Yoga.","er":"The Lord said, \"By My grace, O Arjuna, this Supreme Form, luminous, universal, infinite, and primal—never seen before by anyone but you—has been revealed to you through My own free will.\"","gu":"શ્રી કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: હે અર્જુન, મેં પ્રસન્ન થઈ, મારી દિવ્ય યોગ-શક્તિ દ્વારા, આ તેજ:પૂર્ણ, આદ્ય, અનંત, વિશ્વ-સ્વરૂપ — જે આ પૂર્વે અન્ય કોઈએ નજોયું — તે તને બતાવ્યું. આ વૈભવ ફક્ત તારા પ્રત્યેની કૃપાથી પ્રગટ થયો."},{"ref":"11.48","ch":11,"v":48,"sa":"न वेदयज्ञाध्ययनैर्न दानै\nर्न च क्रियाभिर्न तपोभिरुग्रैः।\nएवंरूपः शक्य अहं नृलोके\nद्रष्टुं त्वदन्येन कुरुप्रवीर।।11.48।।","tr":"na veda-yajñādhyayanair na dānair\nna cha kriyābhir na tapobhir ugraiḥ\nevaṁ-rūpaḥ śhakya ahaṁ nṛi-loke\ndraṣhṭuṁ tvad anyena kuru-pravīra","en":"Neither by the study of the Vedas, nor by gifts, nor by sacrifices, nor by severe austerities, can I be seen in this form in the world of men by any other than yourself, O great hero of the Kurus (Arjuna).","es":"Not by the study of the Vedas and sacrifices, not by gifts, not even by rituals, nor by severe austerities, can I, in this form, be perceived in the human world by anyone other than you, O most valiant among the Kurus, who has not received My grace.","er":"Neither through the study of the Vedas, nor by sacrifices, nor by recitations of the scriptures, nor by gifts, nor by rituals, nor by strict austerities can I be realized in a form like this in the world of men by anyone else but you. O Arjuna!","gu":"વેદ-અભ્યાસ, દાન, યજ્ઞ કે તપ — કોઈ પણ ઉપાય દ્વારા મનુષ્ય-લોકમાં આ સ્વરૂપ અન્ય કોઈ નિહાળી શક્યું નથી. તારા સિવાય આ વિશ્વ-દર્શનનો સૌભાગ્ય અન્ય કોઈ માટે સુલભ નથી."},{"ref":"11.49","ch":11,"v":49,"sa":"मा ते व्यथा मा च विमूढभावो\nदृष्ट्वा रूपं घोरमीदृङ्ममेदम्।\nव्यपेतभीः प्रीतमनाः पुनस्त्वं\nतदेव मे रूपमिदं प्रपश्य।।11.49।।","tr":"mā te vyathā mā cha vimūḍha-bhāvo\ndṛiṣhṭvā rūpaṁ ghoram īdṛiṅ mamedam\nvyapeta-bhīḥ prīta-manāḥ punas tvaṁ\ntad eva me rūpam idaṁ prapaśhya","en":"Do not be afraid, nor be bewildered on seeing such a terrible form of Mine; with your fear dispelled and with a gladdened heart, now behold again this former form of Mine.","es":"May you have no fear, and may there be no bewilderment upon seeing this form of Mine so terrible. Becoming free from fear and gladdened in mind once again, behold this earlier form of Mine.","er":"You need not fear any longer, nor be perplexed, looking upon this awe-inspiring form of Mine. Free from fear and with a gladdened heart, behold once again that other form of Mine.","gu":"મારું આ ઉગ્ર સ્વરૂપ નિહાળી ભય કે ભ્રમ ન પામ. ભય ઓગળી ગયો છે — ચિત્ત પ્રફુલ્લિત કરી, ફરી મારું સૌમ્ય, ચિરપરિચિત સ્વરૂપ દ્રઢ ભાવે નિહાળ."},{"ref":"11.50","ch":11,"v":50,"sa":"सञ्जय उवाच\nइत्यर्जुनं वासुदेवस्तथोक्त्वा\nस्वकं रूपं दर्शयामास भूयः।\nआश्वासयामास च भीतमेनं\nभूत्वा पुनः सौम्यवपुर्महात्मा।।11.50।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\nity arjunaṁ vāsudevas tathoktvā\nsvakaṁ rūpaṁ darśhayām āsa bhūyaḥ\nāśhvāsayām āsa cha bhītam enaṁ\nbhūtvā punaḥ saumya-vapur mahātmā","en":"Sanjaya said, Having thus spoken to Arjuna, Krishna again showed His own form. The great Soul, assuming His gentle form, then consoled Arjuna, who was terrified.","es":"Sanjaya said, Thus, having spoken to Arjuna in that manner, Vasudeva showed His own form again. And He, the exalted One, reassured this terrified one by again becoming serene in his form.","er":"Sanjaya said, Having thus spoken to Arjuna, Sri Krsna once more revealed His own form. The Mahatman, assuming a benign form again, reassured him who had been struck with awe.","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: અર્જુનને આ પ્રમાણે કહ્યા પછી, ભગવાન શ્રી કૃષ્ણે ફરી પોતાનું સૌમ્ય, ચતુર્ભુજ સ્વરૂપ ધારણ કર્યું. મહાત્માએ ભયયુક્ત અર્જુનને સ્નેહથી સાંત્વના આપ્યાં."},{"ref":"11.51","ch":11,"v":51,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nदृष्ट्वेदं मानुषं रूपं तवसौम्यं जनार्दन।\nइदानीमस्मि संवृत्तः सचेताः प्रकृतिं गतः।।11.51।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\ndṛiṣhṭvedaṁ mānuṣhaṁ rūpaṁ tava saumyaṁ janārdana\nidānīm asmi saṁvṛittaḥ sa-chetāḥ prakṛitiṁ gataḥ","en":"Arjuna said, \"Having seen this Thy gentle human form, O Krishna, now I am composed and have been restored to my own nature.\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Janardana, having seen this serene human form of Yours, I have now become calm in mind and restored to my own nature.\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"Having beheld Your human and pleasing form, O Krsna, I am now composed in mind and have been restored to my normal nature.\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે કૃષ્ણ, આ સૌમ્ય, મનુષ્ય-સ્વરૂપ ફરી નિહાળ્યા પછી, મારું ચિત્ત સ્થિર થઈ ગયું અને હું ફરી મારા સ્વભાવ પ્રમાણે ગોઠવાઈ ગયો. ભયનો ભાર ઊઠી ગયો, હૃદય ફરી શાંત બન્યું."},{"ref":"11.52","ch":11,"v":52,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nसुदुर्दर्शमिदं रूपं दृष्टवानसि यन्मम।\nदेवा अप्यस्य रूपस्य नित्यं दर्शनकाङ्क्षिणः।।11.52।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nsu-durdarśham idaṁ rūpaṁ dṛiṣhṭavān asi yan mama\ndevā apy asya rūpasya nityaṁ darśhana-kāṅkṣhiṇaḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"It is very hard indeed to see this form of Mine which thou hast seen; even the gods are ever longing to behold it.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"This form of Mine, which you have seen, is very difficult to behold; even the gods are ever desirous of a vision of this form.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"It is very hard to behold this form of Mine which you have seen. Even the gods everlong to behold this form.\"","gu":"શ્રી કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: જે સ્વરૂપ તેં અત્યારે નિહાળ્યું, તે ખૂબ જ દુર્લભ છે — ખુદ દેવગણ પણ આ સ્વરૂપ-દર્શનની ઝંખના સતત કર્યા કરે છે. આ દર્શન-સૌભાગ્ય અત્યંત વિરળ છે."},{"ref":"11.53","ch":11,"v":53,"sa":"नाहं वेदैर्न तपसा न दानेन न चेज्यया।\nशक्य एवंविधो द्रष्टुं दृष्टवानसि मां यथा।।11.53।।","tr":"nāhaṁ vedair na tapasā na dānena na chejyayā\nśhakya evaṁ-vidho draṣhṭuṁ dṛiṣhṭavān asi māṁ yathā","en":"Neither by the Vedas, nor by austerity, nor by gift, nor by sacrifice can I be seen in this form as thou hast seen Me so easily.","es":"Not through the Vedas, nor by austerity, nor by gifts, nor even by sacrifice can I be seen in this form as you have seen Me.","er":"Sri Krishna says, \"I cannot be seen in such a form as You have seen Me, not by the Vedas, nor by austerities, nor by gifts, nor by sacrifice.\"","gu":"ન વેદ-અધ્યયનથી, ન તપ-ત્યાગથી, ન ધર્માદા-દાનથી, ન યજ્ઞ-ક્રિયાઓ દ્વારા — જ્યારે તેં જોયો, તેવો સ્વરૂપે આ દર્શન સ્વ-પ્રયત્નોથી કોઈ માટે શક્ય નથી. આ ઈશ-કૃપા-પ્રાપ્ય અનુભૂતિ છે."},{"ref":"11.54","ch":11,"v":54,"sa":"भक्त्या त्वनन्यया शक्यमहमेवंविधोऽर्जुन।\nज्ञातुं दृष्टुं च तत्त्वेन प्रवेष्टुं च परंतप।।11.54।।","tr":"bhaktyā tv ananyayā śhakya aham evaṁ-vidho ’rjuna\njñātuṁ draṣhṭuṁ cha tattvena praveṣhṭuṁ cha parantapa","en":"But by single-minded devotion, I can be known, seen, and entered into in reality, O Arjuna.","es":"But, O Arjuna, by single-minded devotion am I, in this form, able to be known and seen in reality, and also entered into, O destroyer of foes.","er":"But by single-minded devotion, O Arjuna, it is possible to truly know, to see, and to enter into Me, who am of this form, O harasser of foes.","gu":"પરંતુ, હે અર્જુન, અવ્યભિચારી-અનન્ય ભક્તિ દ્વારા જ આ સ્વ-સ્વરૂપ — જ્ઞાનમાં, સાક્ષાત્-દર્શનમાં અને સ્વ-સ્વરૂપ-પ્રવેશ-રૂપે — સત્યયથ જાણી, દ્ઠઈ, અનુભવી શકાય. ભક્તિ-ઉપાય સર્વ-ઉત્તમ છે."},{"ref":"11.55","ch":11,"v":55,"sa":"मत्कर्मकृन्मत्परमो मद्भक्तः सङ्गवर्जितः।\nनिर्वैरः सर्वभूतेषु यः स मामेति पाण्डव।।11.55।।","tr":"mat-karma-kṛin mat-paramo mad-bhaktaḥ saṅga-varjitaḥ\nnirvairaḥ sarva-bhūteṣhu yaḥ sa mām eti pāṇḍava","en":"He who does all actions for Me, who regards Me as the Supreme, who is devoted to Me, who is free from attachment, who bears no enmity towards any creature, he comes to Me, O Arjuna.","es":"O son of Pandu, he who works for Me, accepts Me as the supreme goal, is devoted to Me, is devoid of attachment and free from enmity towards all beings—he attains Me.","er":"Whoever works for Me, regards Me as the highest and is devoted to Me, free from attachment and without animosity towards any creature, they come to Me, O Arjuna.","gu":"જે ભક્ત સઘળ કર્મ મારા માટે કરે, મને જ પરમ ધ્યેય ગણે, અનન્ય ભક્તિ-ભાવ ધરાવે, સ્નેહ-આસક્તિ-રહિત હોય, અને સઘળ પ્રાણીઓ સાથે વૈર-ભાવ-શૂન્ય હોય — હે અર્જુન, તે ભક્ત મને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"12.1","ch":12,"v":1,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाचएवं सततयुक्ता ये भक्तास्त्वां पर्युपासते।येचाप्यक्षरमव्यक्तं तेषां के योगवित्तमाः।।12.1।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nevaṁ satata-yuktā ye bhaktās tvāṁ paryupāsate\nye chāpy akṣharam avyaktaṁ teṣhāṁ ke yoga-vittamāḥ","en":"Arjuna said, \"Which of them are better versed in Yoga—those who steadfastly worship You, or those who worship the imperishable and the unmanifested?\"","es":"Arjuna said: \"Which of these devotees, who are ever dedicated and meditate on You, and those who meditate on the Unmanifested and Immutable, are the best experiencers of yoga [here, yoga means samadhi, spiritual absorption]?\"","er":"Arjuna said: Which of these has greater knowledge of yoga—those devotees who meditate on You, ever integrated, or those who meditate on the Imperishable and the Unmanifest?","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: જે ભક્ત સ-ભક્તિ આપ-સ-રૂપ ઈશ્વરની ઉપાસના કરે છે, અને જે નિર-આકાર, અવ્યક્ત, અક્ષર-ની ઉપાસના કરે છે — આ બે પૈકી, હે કૃષ્ણ, કયા ભક્ત-ઉપાસક-ની યોગ-નિષ્ઠ ઉત્કૃષ્ઠ ગણાય?"},{"ref":"12.2","ch":12,"v":2,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाचमय्यावेश्य मनो ये मां नित्ययुक्ता उपासते।श्रद्धया परयोपेतास्ते मे युक्ततमा मताः।।12.2।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nmayy āveśhya mano ye māṁ nitya-yuktā upāsate\nśhraddhayā parayopetās te me yuktatamā matāḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"In My opinion, those who fix their minds on Me, worship Me ever steadfastly, and are endowed with supreme faith, are the best in Yoga.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"Those who meditate on Me, fixing their minds on Me with steadfast devotion, endowed with supreme faith—they are considered to be the most perfect yogis according to Me.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"Those who, ever integrated with Me and possessing supreme faith, worship Me, focusing their minds on Me—these are considered by Me to be the highest among the yogis.\"","gu":"શ્રી કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: જે ભક્તો મન મારામાં સ્થિર કરી, અત્યંત શ્રદ્ધાથી મારી ઉપાસના કરે છે — તેમને હું શ્રેષ્ઠ યોગી માનું છું."},{"ref":"12.3","ch":12,"v":3,"sa":"ये त्वक्षरमनिर्देश्यमव्यक्तं पर्युपासते।सर्वत्रगमचिन्त्यं च कूटस्थमचलं ध्रुवम्।।12.3।।","tr":"ye tv akṣharam anirdeśhyam avyaktaṁ paryupāsate\nsarvatra-gam achintyañcha kūṭa-stham achalandhruvam\n sanniyamyendriya-grāmaṁ sarvatra sama-buddhayaḥ\nte prāpnuvanti mām eva sarva-bhūta-hite ratāḥ","en":"Those who worship the imperishable, the indefinable, the unmanifest, the omnipresent, the unthinkable, the immovable, and the eternal.","es":"Those, however, who meditate in every way on the immutable, the indefinable, the unmanifest, which is all-pervasive, incomprehensible, unchanging, immovable, and constant.","er":"But those who meditate on the Imperishable, the indefinable, the unmanifest, omnipresent, unthinkable, common to all beings, immovable, and constant—","gu":"પરંતુ જે લોકો અવિનાશી, અનિર્વચનીય, અવ્યક્ત, સર્વવ્યાપી, અચિંત્ય, અચળ અને નિત્ય તત્ત્વની ઉપાસના કરે છે —"},{"ref":"12.4","ch":12,"v":4,"sa":"संनियम्येन्द्रियग्रामं सर्वत्र समबुद्धयः।ते प्राप्नुवन्ति मामेव सर्वभूतहिते रताः।।12.4।।","tr":"sanniyamyendriya-grāmaṁ sarvatra sama-buddhayaḥ te prāpnuvanti mām eva sarva-bhūta-hite ratāḥ","en":"Having restrained all the senses, being even-minded everywhere, and intent on the welfare of all beings, they verily come unto Me.","es":"By fully controlling all the organs and remaining even-minded at all times, they, engaged in the welfare of all beings, attain Me alone.","er":"Having subdued all the senses, being even-minded, and engaged in the welfare of all beings, they too come to Me only.","gu":"સર્વ ઇન્દ્રિયોને સંયમમાં રાખી, સર્વત્ર સમભાવ ધરી, સર્વ પ્રાણીઓના કલ્યાણમાં રત રહી — તેઓ નિઃસંદેહ મને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"12.5","ch":12,"v":5,"sa":"क्लेशोऽधिकतरस्तेषामव्यक्तासक्तचेतसाम्।\nअव्यक्ता हि गतिर्दुःखं देहवद्भिरवाप्यते।।12.5।।","tr":"kleśho ’dhikataras teṣhām avyaktāsakta-chetasām\navyaktā hi gatir duḥkhaṁ dehavadbhir avāpyate","en":"Greater is their trouble whose minds are set on the unmanifested, for the goal of the unmanifested is very hard for the embodied to reach.","es":"For those whose minds are attached to the Unmanifested, the struggle is greater; for the Goal, which is the Unmanifest, is attained with difficulty by the embodied ones.","er":"Greater is the difficulty for those whose minds are thus attached to the unmanifest, for the way of the unmanifest is hard to reach for embodied beings.","gu":"અવ્યક્તમાં મન લગાડનારાઓને વધુ કષ્ટ ભોગવવું પડે છે, કારણ કે દેહધારી જીવો માટે અવ્યક્ત લક્ષ્ય સુધી પહોંચવું અત્યંત કઠિન છે."},{"ref":"12.6","ch":12,"v":6,"sa":"ये तु सर्वाणि कर्माणि मयि संन्यस्य मत्पराः।अनन्येनैव योगेन मां ध्यायन्त उपासते।।12.6।।","tr":"ye tu sarvāṇi karmāṇi mayi sannyasya mat-paraḥ\nananyenaiva yogena māṁ dhyāyanta upāsate","en":"But to those who worship Me, renouncing all actions in Me, regarding Me as the supreme goal, meditating on Me with single-minded yoga.","es":"As for those who, having dedicated all actions to Me and accepted Me as the supreme, meditate on Me with single-minded concentration only-.","er":"For those who dedicate all their actions to Me, hold Me as their supreme goal, are intent on Me, and worship Me, meditating on Me with exclusive devotion;","gu":"પરંતુ જે ભક્તો સર્વ કર્મો મારે અર્પણ કરી, મને જ પરમ લક્ષ્ય માની, એકાગ્ર ભક્તિથી મારું ધ્યાન ધરે છે —"},{"ref":"12.7","ch":12,"v":7,"sa":"तेषामहं समुद्धर्ता मृत्युसंसारसागरात्।भवामि नचिरात्पार्थ मय्यावेशितचेतसाम्।।12.7।।","tr":"teṣhām ahaṁ samuddhartā mṛityu-saṁsāra-sāgarāt\nbhavāmi na chirāt pārtha mayy āveśhita-chetasām","en":"To those whose minds are set on Me, O Arjuna, verily I soon become the savior out of the ocean of Samsara.","es":"O son of Prtha, for those who have their minds absorbed in Me, I become, without delay, the deliverer from the sea of the world, which is fraught with death.","er":"Those whose minds are thus focused on Me, I soon become their savior from the ocean of mortal life.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જેઓ મારામાં ચિત્ત સ્થિર કરે છે, તેમને હું મૃત્યુ-સંસારરૂપ સાગરમાંથી શીઘ્ર ઉદ્ધાર કરી લઉ છું."},{"ref":"12.8","ch":12,"v":8,"sa":"मय्येव मन आधत्स्व मयि बुद्धिं निवेशय।निवसिष्यसि मय्येव अत ऊर्ध्वं न संशयः।।12.8।।","tr":"mayy eva mana ādhatsva mayi buddhiṁ niveśhaya\nnivasiṣhyasi mayy eva ata ūrdhvaṁ na sanśhayaḥ","en":"Fix your mind on Me, and your intellect in Me. Then you will certainly live in Me alone hereafter.","es":"Fix the mind on Me alone; in Me alone let the intellect rest. There is no doubt that hereafter you will dwell in Me alone.","er":"Focus your mind on Me alone; and let your intellect enter into Me. Then, you will live in Me alone; there is no doubt.","gu":"મારામાં જ મન સ્થિર કર, મારામાં જ બુદ્ધિ ન્યસ્ત કર; ત્યારપછી તું મારામાં જ નિવાસ કરીશ — આમાં કોઈ સંદેહ નથી."},{"ref":"12.9","ch":12,"v":9,"sa":"अथ चित्तं समाधातुं न शक्नोषि मयि स्थिरम्।अभ्यासयोगेन ततो मामिच्छाप्तुं धनञ्जय।।12.9।।","tr":"atha chittaṁ samādhātuṁ na śhaknoṣhi mayi sthiram\nabhyāsa-yogena tato mām ichchhāptuṁ dhanañjaya","en":"If you are unable to fix your mind steadily on Me, then seek to reach Me through the yoga of constant practice, O Arjuna.","es":"If, however, you are unable to establish the mind steadily on Me, then, O Dhananjaya, seek to attain Me through the yoga of practice.","er":"If now you are unable to focus your mind on Me, then seek to reach Me, O Arjuna, through the practice of repetition.","gu":"જો તું મારામાં મન અચળ સ્થિર ન કરી શકે, તો હે અર્જુન, અભ્યાસ-યોગ દ્વારા મને પ્રાપ્ત કરવાનો પ્રયત્ન કર."},{"ref":"12.10","ch":12,"v":10,"sa":"अभ्यासेऽप्यसमर्थोऽसि मत्कर्मपरमो भव।मदर्थमपि कर्माणि कुर्वन् सिद्धिमवाप्स्यसि।।12.10।।","tr":"abhyāse ’py asamartho ’si mat-karma-paramo bhava\nmad-artham api karmāṇi kurvan siddhim avāpsyasi","en":"If you are unable to practice even this Abhyasa Yoga, be intent on doing actions for My sake; even by doing actions for My sake, you will attain perfection.","es":"If you are unable even to practice, be intent on works for Me. By undertaking works for Me as well, you will attain perfection. [Identify with Brahman.]","er":"If you are incapable of even this practice of repetition, then devote yourself to My deeds. For even by working for My sake, you will attain perfection.","gu":"જો અભ્યાસ-યોગ પણ ન કરી શકે, તો મારે અર્થે કર્મ કરવામાં તત્પર રહ; મારા માટે કર્મ કરવાથી તું સિદ્ધિ પ્રાપ્ત કરીશ."},{"ref":"12.11","ch":12,"v":11,"sa":"अथैतदप्यशक्तोऽसि कर्तुं मद्योगमाश्रितः।सर्वकर्मफलत्यागं ततः कुरु यतात्मवान्।।12.11।।","tr":"athaitad apy aśhakto ’si kartuṁ mad-yogam āśhritaḥ\nsarva-karma-phala-tyāgaṁ tataḥ kuru yatātmavān","en":"If you are unable to do even this, then, resort to union with Me and renounce the fruits of all actions with self-control.","es":"If you are unable to do even this, then resort to the Yoga for Me and afterwards, control your mind and renounce the results of all your works.","er":"If you are unable to do even this—that is, take refuge in My Yoga—then, with your self-control, renounce the fruits of every action.","gu":"જો આ પણ ન થઈ શકે, તો મારા શરણમાં આવી, મન સંયમમાં રાખી, સર્વ કર્મોનાં ફળ છોડી દે."},{"ref":"12.12","ch":12,"v":12,"sa":"श्रेयो हि ज्ञानमभ्यासाज्ज्ञानाद्ध्यानं विशिष्यते।ध्यानात्कर्मफलत्यागस्त्यागाच्छान्तिरनन्तरम्।।12.12।।","tr":"śhreyo hi jñānam abhyāsāj jñānād dhyānaṁ viśhiṣhyate\ndhyānāt karma-phala-tyāgas tyāgāch chhāntir anantaram","en":"Better indeed is knowledge than practice; better than knowledge is meditation; better than meditation is the renunciation of the fruits of actions: peace immediately follows renunciation.","es":"Knowledge is certainly superior to practice; meditation surpasses knowledge. The renunciation of the results of works surpasses meditation. From renunciation, peace follows immediately.","er":"Far better is knowledge of the Self than the repeated practice (of remembrance of the Lord). Better is meditation than this knowledge; better is renunciation of the fruits of action than meditation. From such renunciation, peace ensues.","gu":"અભ્યાસ કરતાં જ્ઞાન ચડિયાતું છે; જ્ઞાન કરતાં ધ્યાન ચડિયાતું છે; ધ્યાન કરતાં કર્મ-ફળ-ત્યાગ ચડિયાતો છે — ત્યાગથી તત્કાળ શાંતિ મળે છે."},{"ref":"12.13","ch":12,"v":13,"sa":"अद्वेष्टा सर्वभूतानां मैत्रः करुण एव च।निर्ममो निरहङ्कारः समदुःखसुखः क्षमी।।12.13।।","tr":"adveṣhṭā sarva-bhūtānāṁ maitraḥ karuṇa eva cha\nnirmamo nirahankāraḥ sama-duḥkha-sukhaḥ kṣhamī","en":"He who hates no creature, is friendly and compassionate to all, is free from attachment and egoism, is balanced in pleasure and pain, and is forgiving.","es":"He who is not hateful towards any creature, who is friendly and compassionate, who has no concept of 'mine' and no sense of egoism, who remains the same in sorrow and happiness, and who is forgiving;","er":"He who never hates any being, who is friendly and compassionate, who is free from the feelings of \"I\" and \"mine,\" who looks upon all pain and pleasure equally, and who is enduring;"},{"ref":"12.14","ch":12,"v":14,"sa":"सन्तुष्टः सततं योगी यतात्मा दृढनिश्चयः।मय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः।।12.14।।","tr":"santuṣhṭaḥ satataṁ yogī yatātmā dṛiḍha-niśhchayaḥ\nmayy arpita-mano-buddhir yo mad-bhaktaḥ sa me priyaḥ","en":"Ever content, steady in meditation, self-controlled, possessing firm conviction, with the mind and intellect dedicated to Me, he, My devotee, is dear to Me.","es":"He who is ever content, who is a yogi, who has self-control, who has firm conviction, and who has dedicated his mind and intellect to Me—he who is such a devotee of Mine is dear to Me.","er":"He who is content, who meditates ever, is self-restrained, and is firm in his convictions, and has his mind and reason dedicated to Me—he is dear to Me.","gu":"જે ભક્ત સદા સંતુષ્ટ, ધ્યાનમાં સ્થિર, સ્વ-સંયમી, દૃઢ નિષ્ઠાવાળો અને મન-બુદ્ધિ મને સમર્પિત કરેલ છે — તે મને પ્રિય છે."},{"ref":"12.15","ch":12,"v":15,"sa":"यस्मान्नोद्विजते लोको लोकान्नोद्विजते च यः।हर्षामर्षभयोद्वेगैर्मुक्तो यः स च मे प्रियः।।12.15।।","tr":"yasmān nodvijate loko lokān nodvijate cha yaḥ\nharṣhāmarṣha-bhayodvegair mukto yaḥ sa cha me priyaḥ","en":"He whom the world does not agitate, and who cannot be agitated by the world, and who is freed from joy, anger, fear, and anxiety—he is dear to Me.","es":"He, too, owing to whom the world is not disturbed, and who is not disturbed by the world, who is free from joy, impatience, fear, and anxiety, is dear to me.","er":"He from whom the world has no cause to be frightened, who is not frightened by the world, who is free from joy and impatience, fear, and aversion - he is dear to me."},{"ref":"12.16","ch":12,"v":16,"sa":"अनपेक्षः शुचिर्दक्ष उदासीनो गतव्यथः।सर्वारम्भपरित्यागी यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः।।12.16।।","tr":"anapekṣhaḥ śhuchir dakṣha udāsīno gata-vyathaḥ\nsarvārambha-parityāgī yo mad-bhaktaḥ sa me priyaḥ","en":"He who is free from wants, pure, expert, unconcerned, and free from pain, renouncing all undertakings and commencements, he who is devoted to Me is dear to Me.","es":"He who has no desires, who is pure, dexterous, impartial, free from fear, and who has renounced every undertaking—such a devotee of Mine is dear to Me.","er":"He who is free from desires, who is pure, expert, indifferent, and free from agony, who has renounced every undertaking—he is dear to me.","gu":"જે ભક્ત નિઃસ્પૃહ, શુચિ, નિપુણ, ઉદાસીન, દુઃખ-રહિત અને સર્વ આરંભ છોડી ચૂક્યો છે — તે મને પ્રિય છે."},{"ref":"12.17","ch":12,"v":17,"sa":"यो न हृष्यति न द्वेष्टि न शोचति न काङ्क्षति।शुभाशुभपरित्यागी भक्ितमान्यः स मे प्रियः।।12.17।।","tr":"yo na hṛiṣhyati na dveṣhṭi na śhochati na kāṅkṣhati\nśhubhāśhubha-parityāgī bhaktimān yaḥ sa me priyaḥ","en":"He who neither rejoices nor hates, nor grieves nor desires, renouncing both good and evil, and who is full of devotion, is dear to Me.","es":"He who does not rejoice, nor fret, nor lament, nor hanker; who gives up both good and bad, and is filled with devotion—he is dear to Me.","er":"He who does not rejoice, nor hate, nor grieve, nor desire, who renounces both good and evil, and who is full of devotion to Me—such a devotee is dear to Me.","gu":"જે ન આનંદ પામે, ન ઘૃણા કરે, ન શોક કરે, ન ઇચ્છા રાખે, જે શુભ-અશુભ બંને ત્યજી ભક્તિ-ભાવ ધારણ કરે — તે મને પ્રિય છે."},{"ref":"12.18","ch":12,"v":18,"sa":"समः शत्रौ च मित्रे च तथा मानापमानयोः।शीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु समः सङ्गविवर्जितः।।12.18।।","tr":"samaḥ śhatrau cha mitre cha tathā mānāpamānayoḥ\nśhītoṣhṇa-sukha-duḥkheṣhu samaḥ saṅga-vivarjitaḥ","en":"He who is the same to foe and friend, and also in honor and dishonor, who is the same in cold and heat, in pleasure and pain, and who is free from attachment.","es":"He who is the same towards friend and foe, and in honor and dishonor; who is the same under cold, heat, happiness, and sorrow; who is free from attachment to all.","er":"He who is the same to foe and friend, honor and dishonor, who is alike to both cold and heat, pleasure and pain, and who is free from all attachments;","gu":"જે મિત્ર-શત્રુ, માન-અપમાન, ઠંડી-ગરમી, સુખ-દુઃખ — સૌમાં સમ ભાવ રાખે છે, અને આસક્તિ-રહિત રહે છે — તે ભક્ત મને સમાન રૂપે પ્રિય છે."},{"ref":"12.19","ch":12,"v":19,"sa":"तुल्यनिन्दास्तुतिर्मौनी सन्तुष्टो येनकेनचित्।अनिकेतः स्थिरमतिर्भक्ितमान्मे प्रियो नरः।।12.19।।","tr":"tulya-nindā-stutir maunī santuṣhṭo yena kenachit\naniketaḥ sthira-matir bhaktimān me priyo naraḥ","en":"He to whom censure and praise are equal, who is silent, content with anything, homeless, of a steady mind, and full of devotion; that man is dear to me.","es":"The person to whom denunciation and praise are the same, who is silent, content with anything, homeless, steadfast-minded, and full of devotion is dear to me.","er":"He who regards both blame and praise alike, who is silent and content with any lot, who has no home, who is firm of mind, and who is devoted to Me - such a man is dear to Me.","gu":"જે નિંદા અને સ્તુતિમાં સમાન છે, મૌની છે, જે મળે તેમાં સંતુષ્ટ છે, ઘરરહિત અને સ્થિરમના છે — એવો ભક્ત મને પ્રિય છે."},{"ref":"12.20","ch":12,"v":20,"sa":"ये तु धर्म्यामृतमिदं यथोक्तं पर्युपासते।श्रद्दधाना मत्परमा भक्तास्तेऽतीव मे प्रियाः।।12.20।।","tr":"ye tu dharmyāmṛitam idaṁ yathoktaṁ paryupāsate\nśhraddadhānā mat-paramā bhaktās te ’tīva me priyāḥ","en":"They who follow this immortal Dharma, endowed with faith and regarding Me as their supreme goal, are exceedingly dear to Me.","es":"But those devotees who accept Me as the supreme Goal, and with faith seek for this ambrosia—nectar in the form of virtue—which is indistinguishable from the virtues as stated above, they are very dear to Me.","er":"But those devotees who follow this nectar of virtuous duty, as taught above, who are full of faith and regard Me as the Supreme, are exceedingly dear to Me.","gu":"જેઓ આ અમૃતમય ધર્મને શ્રદ્ધાથી અનુસરે છે અને મને જ પરમ લક્ષ્ય માને છે — એવા ભક્તો મને અત્યંત પ્રિય છે."},{"ref":"13.1","ch":13,"v":1,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nप्रकृतिं पुरुषं चैव क्षेत्रं क्षेत्रज्ञमेव च।\nएतद्वेदितुमिच्छामि ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं च केशव।।13.1।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nprakṛitiṁ puruṣhaṁ chaiva kṣhetraṁ kṣhetra-jñam eva cha\netad veditum ichchhāmi jñānaṁ jñeyaṁ cha keśhava","en":"Arjuna said, \"I wish to learn about Nature and the Spirit, the field and the knower of the field, knowledge and that which ought to be known, O Kesava.\"","es":"Swami Gambhirananda has not translated this verse. Many editions of the Bhagavad Gita do not contain this verse, including the commentary by Shankaracharya. If this verse is included, the total number of verses in the Bhagavad Gita is 701.","er":"This is not a sentence, so there is nothing to fix.","gu":"અર્જુને કહ્યું: હે કૃષ્ણ, હું પ્રકૃતિ અને પુરુષ, ક્ષેત્ર અને ક્ષેત્રજ્ઞ, જ્ઞાન અને જ્ઞેય — એ સૌ વિષે જાણવા ઇચ્છું છું."},{"ref":"13.2","ch":13,"v":2,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाचइदं शरीरं कौन्तेय क्षेत्रमित्यभिधीयते।एतद्यो वेत्ति तं प्राहुः क्षेत्रज्ञ इति तद्विदः।।13.2।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nidaṁ śharīraṁ kaunteya kṣhetram ity abhidhīyate\netad yo vetti taṁ prāhuḥ kṣhetra-jña iti tad-vidaḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O Arjuna, this body is called the field; he who knows it is called the knower of the field by those who know them.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O son of Kunti, this body is referred to as the 'field'. Those who are versed in this call him who is conscious of it the 'knower of the field'.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"O Arjuna, this body is called the Field, Ksetra. Those who know the self call the one who knows it the Field-knower, Ksetrajna.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણે કહ્યું: આ શરીર 'ક્ષેત્ર' કહેવાય છે, અને જે તેને જાણે છે તેને જ્ઞાનીઓ 'ક્ષેત્રજ્ઞ' કહે છે."},{"ref":"13.3","ch":13,"v":3,"sa":"क्षेत्रज्ञं चापि मां विद्धि सर्वक्षेत्रेषु भारत।\nक्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञयोर्ज्ञानं यत्तज्ज्ञानं मतं मम।।13.3।।","tr":"kṣhetra-jñaṁ chāpi māṁ viddhi sarva-kṣhetreṣhu bhārata\nkṣhetra-kṣhetrajñayor jñānaṁ yat taj jñānaṁ mataṁ mama","en":"Do thou also know Me as the knower of the field in all fields, O Arjuna. Knowledge of both the field and the knower of the field is considered by Me to be the knowledge.","es":"And, O scion of the Bharata dynasty, understand Me to be the 'Knower of the field' in all the fields. In My opinion, that is Knowledge which is the knowledge of the field and the knower of the field.","er":"And know Me also as the Knower of all Fields, O Arjuna. In My view, the knowledge of the Field and its Knower is the true knowledge.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, તું મને પણ સઘળાં ક્ષેત્રોમાં ક્ષેત્રજ્ઞ જાણ; ક્ષેત્ર અને ક્ષેત્રજ્ઞ બંનેનું જ્ઞાન — એ જ સાચું જ્ઞાન છે એમ હું માનું છું."},{"ref":"13.4","ch":13,"v":4,"sa":"तत्क्षेत्रं यच्च यादृक् च यद्विकारि यतश्च यत्।स च यो यत्प्रभावश्च तत्समासेन मे श्रृणु।।13.4।।","tr":"tat kṣhetraṁ yach cha yādṛik cha yad-vikāri yataśh cha yat\nsa cha yo yat-prabhāvaśh cha tat samāsena me śhṛiṇu","en":"Hear from Me in brief what the field is, of what nature it is, what its modifications are, whence it is, who He is, and what His powers are.","es":"Hear from Me in brief about all that, what that field is and how it is; what its changes are, and what causes what effect; and who He is, and what His powers are.","er":"Listen briefly from Me what the Field is, what it is like, what its modifications are, what purpose it serves, and what it is; as well as who the Self is and what its powers are.","gu":"ક્ષેત્ર શું છે, તેનો સ્વભાવ, તેના વિકારો, તેનો ઉત્પત્તિ-સ્રોત, ક્ષેત્રજ્ઞ કોણ છે અને તેની શક્તિ — આ બધું મારી પાસેથી સંક્ષેપમાં સાંભળ."},{"ref":"13.5","ch":13,"v":5,"sa":"ऋषिभिर्बहुधा गीतं छन्दोभिर्विविधैः पृथक्।ब्रह्मसूत्रपदैश्चैव हेतुमद्भिर्विनिश्िचतैः।।13.5।।","tr":"ṛiṣhibhir bahudhā gītaṁ chhandobhir vividhaiḥ pṛithak\nbrahma-sūtra-padaiśh chaiva hetumadbhir viniśhchitaiḥ","en":"Sages have sung in many ways, with various distinctive chants and also with suggestive words indicative of the Absolute, full of reasoning and decisive.","es":"It has been sung of in various ways by the Rsis, separately by the different branches of Vedic texts, and also by the rational and convincing sentences themselves which are indicative of and lead to Brahman.","er":"It has been sung by seers in various ways, in various distinctive hymns, and also in the well-reasoned and conclusive words of the Brahma-sutras.","gu":"ઋષિઓએ આ ક્ષેત્ર-ક્ષેત્રજ્ઞ વિષે અનેક પ્રકારે ગાન કર્યું છે, વિવિધ છંદો અને બ્રહ્મસૂત્રોના સૂચક વચનો દ્વારા, તર્ક અને નિશ્ચય સહિત."},{"ref":"13.6","ch":13,"v":6,"sa":"महाभूतान्यहङ्कारो बुद्धिरव्यक्तमेव च।इन्द्रियाणि दशैकं च पञ्च चेन्द्रियगोचराः।।13.6।।","tr":"mahā-bhūtāny ahankāro buddhir avyaktam eva cha\nindriyāṇi daśhaikaṁ cha pañcha chendriya-gocharāḥ","en":"The great elements, egoism, intellect, and also the Unmanifested Nature, the ten senses, and one mind, and the five objects of the senses.","es":"The great elements, egoism, intellect, and the Unmanifest itself; the ten organs and the one, and the five objects of the senses;","er":"The great elements, the Ahankara, the Buddhi, the Avyakta, the ten senses, and the one, in addition, the five objects of the senses;","gu":"પંચ મહાભૂતો, અહંકાર, બુદ્ધિ, અવ્યક્ત પ્રકૃતિ, દશ ઇન્દ્રિયો, એક મન, અને પાંચ ઇન્દ્રિય-વિષયો — આ ક્ષેત્રના ઘટકો છે."},{"ref":"13.7","ch":13,"v":7,"sa":"इच्छा द्वेषः सुखं दुःखं सङ्घातश्चेतनाधृतिः।एतत्क्षेत्रं समासेन सविकारमुदाहृतम्।।13.7।।","tr":"ichchhā dveṣhaḥ sukhaṁ duḥkhaṁ saṅghātaśh chetanā dhṛitiḥ\netat kṣhetraṁ samāsena sa-vikāram udāhṛitam","en":"Desire, hatred, pleasure, pain, the aggregate (body), intelligence, and fortitude—the field has thus been briefly described with its modifications.","es":"Desire, repulsion, happiness, sorrow, the aggregate (of body and organs), sentience, fortitude—this field, together with its modifications, has been spoken of briefly.","er":"Desire, hatred, pleasure, and pain, and the combination that constitutes the basis of consciousness—or the individual self—have been briefly described here, along with their modifications.","gu":"ઇચ્છા, દ્વેષ, સુખ, દુઃખ, દેહ-સમૂહ, ચેતના અને ધૃતિ — આ ક્ષેત્ર અને તેના વિકારોનું સંક્ષિપ્ત વર્ણન છે."},{"ref":"13.8","ch":13,"v":8,"sa":"अमानित्वमदम्भित्वमहिंसा क्षान्तिरार्जवम्।आचार्योपासनं शौचं स्थैर्यमात्मविनिग्रहः।।13.8।।","tr":"amānitvam adambhitvam ahinsā kṣhāntir ārjavam\nāchāryopāsanaṁ śhauchaṁ sthairyam ātma-vinigrahaḥ","en":"Humility, unpretentiousness, non-injury, forgiveness, uprightness, service to the teacher, purity, steadfastness, and self-control.","es":"Humility, unpretentiousness, non-injury, forbearance, sincerity, service to the teacher, cleanliness, steadiness, and control of the body and its organs;","er":"Modesty, absence of ostentation, non-injury, patience, sincerity, service to the preceptor, purity, firmness, and self-restraint;","gu":"નમ્રતા, અહંકારરહિતતા, અહિંસા, ક્ષમા, સરળતા, ગુરુસેવા, પવિત્રતા, સ્થિરતા અને આત્મસંયમ — આ જ્ઞાનના લક્ષણો છે."},{"ref":"13.9","ch":13,"v":9,"sa":"इन्द्रियार्थेषु वैराग्यमनहङ्कार एव च।जन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिदुःखदोषानुदर्शनम्।।13.9।।","tr":"indriyārtheṣhu vairāgyam anahankāra eva cha\njanma-mṛityu-jarā-vyādhi-duḥkha-doṣhānudarśhanam","en":"Indifference to the objects of the senses and also absence of egoism; perceiving the evil in birth, death, old age, sickness, and pain.","es":"Non-attachment to objects of the senses, and also the absence of egotism; seeing the evil in birth, death, aging, diseases, and miseries;","er":"Absence of desire for sense-objects, and also absence of egotism, the recognition of evil in birth, death, old age, disease, and sorrow;","gu":"ઇન્દ્રિય-વિષયો પ્રત્યે વૈરાગ્ય, અહંકારનો અભાવ; જન્મ, મૃત્યુ, વૃદ્ધાવસ્થા, રોગ અને દુઃખમાં દોષ-દર્શન — આ જ્ઞાનનાં ચિહ્નો છે."},{"ref":"13.10","ch":13,"v":10,"sa":"असक्ितरनभिष्वङ्गः पुत्रदारगृहादिषु।नित्यं च समचित्तत्वमिष्टानिष्टोपपत्तिषु।।13.10।।","tr":"asaktir anabhiṣhvaṅgaḥ putra-dāra-gṛihādiṣhu\nnityaṁ cha sama-chittatvam iṣhṭāniṣhṭopapattiṣhu","en":"Non-attachment, non-identification of the Self with son, wife, home, and the rest, and constant even-mindedness in the face of the attainment of both desirable and undesirable.","es":"Non-attachment and absence of fondness with regard to sons, wives, homes, etc., and constant equanimity of the mind with regard to the attainment of both the desirable and the undesirable;","er":"Non-attachment, absence of clinging to son, wife, home, and the like, and constant even-mindedness in regard to all desirable and undesirable events;","gu":"પુત્ર, પત્ની, ઘર આદિ સાથે અનાસક્તિ અને અભેદ-ભાવ; ઇષ્ટ અને અનિષ્ટ ઘટનાઓમાં સદૈવ સમ-ચિત્તતા — આ જ્ઞાનનાં ચિહ્નો છે."},{"ref":"13.11","ch":13,"v":11,"sa":"मयि चानन्ययोगेन भक्ितरव्यभिचारिणी।विविक्तदेशसेवित्वमरतिर्जनसंसदि।।13.11।।","tr":"mayi chānanya-yogena bhaktir avyabhichāriṇī\nvivikta-deśha-sevitvam aratir jana-sansadi","en":"Unswerving devotion to Me through the Yoga of non-separation, resorting to solitary places, and a distaste for the company of people.","es":"And unwavering devotion to Me with single-minded concentration; inclination to retreat to a clean place; lack of delight in a crowd of people;","er":"Constantly devote yourself to Me alone, resort to solitary places, and dislike crowds.","gu":"અવ્યભિચારી ભક્તિ દ્વારા મારી સાથે અભેદ-સ્થિતિ; એકાંત સ્થળો પ્રત્યે પ્રેમ; સાંસારિક લોકોની સંગતિ પ્રત્યે અરુચિ — આ પણ જ્ઞાનનાં ચિહ્નો છે."},{"ref":"13.12","ch":13,"v":12,"sa":"अध्यात्मज्ञाननित्यत्वं तत्त्वज्ञानार्थदर्शनम्।एतज्ज्ञानमिति प्रोक्तमज्ञानं यदतोन्यथा।।13.12।।","tr":"adhyātma-jñāna-nityatvaṁ tattva-jñānārtha-darśhanam\netaj jñānam iti proktam ajñānaṁ yad ato ’nyathā","en":"Constancy in Self-knowledge, the perception of the end of true knowledge—this is declared to be knowledge, and what is opposed to it is ignorance.","es":"Steadfastness in the knowledge of the Self, contemplation on the Goal of the knowledge of Reality—this is spoken of as Knowledge. Ignorance is that which is other than this.","er":"Constant contemplation on the knowledge pertaining to the self, reflection for the attainment of knowledge of the truth—this is declared to be knowledge, and what is contrary to it is ignorance.","gu":"આત્મ-જ્ઞાનમાં નિષ્ઠા અને સાચા જ્ઞાનના ધ્યેયની ઉપલબ્ધિ — આ 'જ્ઞાન' કહેવાય છે; જે આનાથી વિરુદ્ધ છે તે 'અજ્ઞાન' છે."},{"ref":"13.13","ch":13,"v":13,"sa":"ज्ञेयं यत्तत्प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वाऽमृतमश्नुते।अनादिमत्परं ब्रह्म न सत्तन्नासदुच्यते।।13.13।।","tr":"jñeyaṁ yat tat pravakṣhyāmi yaj jñātvāmṛitam aśhnute\nanādi mat-paraṁ brahma na sat tan nāsad uchyate","en":"I will declare that which is to be known, knowing which one attains immortality; the beginningless Supreme Brahman, which is neither being nor non-being.","es":"I shall speak of that which is to be known, by realizing which one attains immortality. The supreme Brahman is without any beginning; that is called neither being nor non-being.","er":"I shall declare that which is to be known, knowing which one attains the immortal Self. It is beginningless Brahman, having Me as the Highest (Anadi Matparam); it is said to be neither being nor non-being.","gu":"હું તે 'જ્ઞેય'નું વર્ણન કરીશ, જેને જાણ્યે મોક્ષ મળે છે — તે અનાદિ પરમ બ્રહ્મ, જે સત્ પણ નથી અને અસત્ પણ નથી."},{"ref":"13.14","ch":13,"v":14,"sa":"सर्वतः पाणिपादं तत्सर्वतोऽक्षिशिरोमुखम्।सर्वतः श्रुतिमल्लोके सर्वमावृत्य तिष्ठति।।13.14।।","tr":"sarvataḥ pāṇi-pādaṁ tat sarvato ’kṣhi-śhiro-mukham\nsarvataḥ śhrutimal loke sarvam āvṛitya tiṣhṭhati","en":"With hands and feet everywhere, with eyes, heads, and mouths everywhere, with ears everywhere, He exists in the worlds, enveloping all.","es":"That Knowable, which has hands and feet everywhere, which has eyes, heads, and mouths everywhere, which has ears everywhere, exists in creatures by pervading them all.","er":"Its hands and feet are everywhere; Its eyes, heads, and mouths are everywhere; Its ears are on all sides; and It exists, encompassing all things.","gu":"તેના હાથ અને પગ સર્વત્ર છે, સર્વત્ર આંખો, મસ્તક અને મુખ છે, સર્વત્ર કાન છે — તે આ સૃષ્ટિમાં સર્વને આવરીને વ્યાપ્ત છે."},{"ref":"13.15","ch":13,"v":15,"sa":"सर्वेन्द्रियगुणाभासं सर्वेन्द्रियविवर्जितम्।असक्तं सर्वभृच्चैव निर्गुणं गुणभोक्तृ च।।13.15।।","tr":"sarvendriya-guṇābhāsaṁ sarvendriya-vivarjitam\nasaktaṁ sarva-bhṛich chaiva nirguṇaṁ guṇa-bhoktṛi cha","en":"Shining by the functions of all the senses, yet without being attached to them; unattached, yet supporting all; devoid of qualities, yet the experiencer of them.","es":"Shining through the functions of all the organs, yet devoid of all the organs; unattached, and verily the supporter of all; without quality, and the perceiver of qualities.","er":"Shining by the functions of the senses, yet devoid of the senses, detached yet supporting all, devoid of the Gunas yet experiencing the Gunas;","gu":"તે સઘળી ઇન્દ્રિયોના વ્યાપારો દ્વારા પ્રકાશિત છે, છતાં ઇન્દ્રિયો વિનાનો છે; અનાસક્ત છે, છતાં સૌનો આધાર છે; ગુણ-રહિત છે, છતાં ગુણોને ભોગવનારો છે."},{"ref":"13.16","ch":13,"v":16,"sa":"बहिरन्तश्च भूतानामचरं चरमेव च।सूक्ष्मत्वात्तदविज्ञेयं दूरस्थं चान्तिके च तत्।।13.16।।","tr":"bahir antaśh cha bhūtānām acharaṁ charam eva cha\nsūkṣhmatvāt tad avijñeyaṁ dūra-sthaṁ chāntike cha tat","en":"It is within and without all beings, both the unmoving and the moving; It is subtle and unknowable, and It is near and far away.","es":"Existing both outside and inside all beings, moving and non-moving, It is incomprehensible due to Its subtlety. It is far away, yet near.","er":"It is within and without all beings; It is unmoving yet moving; It is so subtle that none can comprehend it; It is far away yet very near.","gu":"તે સઘળા પ્રાણીઓની ભીતર અને બહાર છે, ચર અને અચર છે; સૂક્ષ્મ હોવાથી તે અગ્રાહ્ય છે, અત્યંત દૂર છે, છતાં નિકટ પણ છે."},{"ref":"13.17","ch":13,"v":17,"sa":"अविभक्तं च भूतेषु विभक्तमिव च स्थितम्।भूतभर्तृ च तज्ज्ञेयं ग्रसिष्णु प्रभविष्णु च।।13.17।।","tr":"avibhaktaṁ cha bhūteṣhu vibhaktam iva cha sthitam\nbhūta-bhartṛi cha taj jñeyaṁ grasiṣhṇu prabhaviṣhṇu cha","en":"Undivided yet, It exists as if divided in beings; It is to be known as the supporter of beings; It devours and It generates.","es":"The Knowable, though undivided, appears to exist as divided in all beings, and It is the sustainer, devourer, and originator of all beings.","er":"Undivided yet appearing as if divided among beings, this Self is to be known as the supporter of the elements. It devours them and causes their generation.","gu":"તે વિભક્ત નથી, છતાં સઘળા પ્રાણીઓમાં વિભક્ત-સા ભાસે છે; તે પ્રાણીઓનો ધારક, ભક્ષક અને સ્રષ્ટા છે."},{"ref":"13.18","ch":13,"v":18,"sa":"ज्योतिषामपि तज्ज्योतिस्तमसः परमुच्यते।ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं ज्ञानगम्यं हृदि सर्वस्य विष्ठितम्।।13.18।।","tr":"jyotiṣhām api taj jyotis tamasaḥ param uchyate\njñānaṁ jñeyaṁ jñāna-gamyaṁ hṛidi sarvasya viṣhṭhitam","en":"That Light of all lights is said to be beyond darkness: knowledge, the knowable, and the goal of knowledge, seated in the hearts of all.","es":"That is the Light of all lights; It is spoken of as beyond darkness. It is Knowledge, the Knowable, and the Known. It is specially situated in the hearts of all.","er":"The light of all lights is said to be beyond Tamas (darkness); it is known to be knowledge, to be attained through knowledge, and to be present in the hearts of all.","gu":"સઘળા પ્રકાશોનો પ્રકાશ તે અંધકારની પેલે પાર કહેવાય છે; તે જ્ઞાન, જ્ઞેય અને જ્ઞાનનું ગંતવ્ય છે, અને સૌના હૃદયમાં બિરાજે છે."},{"ref":"13.19","ch":13,"v":19,"sa":"इति क्षेत्रं तथा ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं चोक्तं समासतः।मद्भक्त एतद्विज्ञाय मद्भावायोपपद्यते।।13.19।।","tr":"iti kṣhetraṁ tathā jñānaṁ jñeyaṁ choktaṁ samāsataḥ\nmad-bhakta etad vijñāya mad-bhāvāyopapadyate","en":"Thus, the field, as well as knowledge and the knowable, have been briefly stated. My devotee, knowing this, enters into My being.","es":"Thus, in brief, the field, Knowledge, and the Knowable have been spoken of. By understanding this, My devotee becomes qualified for My state.","er":"Thus, the Ksetra, knowledge, and the object of knowledge have been briefly set forth. On knowing this, My devotee becomes fit to attain My state.","gu":"આ પ્રમાણે ક્ષેત્ર, જ્ઞાન અને જ્ઞેય ટૂંકમાં કહેવાયાં છે. મારો ભક્ત આ જાણીને મારા સ્વભાવ-ભાવને પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે."},{"ref":"13.20","ch":13,"v":20,"sa":"प्रकृतिं पुरुषं चैव विद्ध्यनादी उभावपि।विकारांश्च गुणांश्चैव विद्धि प्रकृतिसंभवान्।।13.20।।","tr":"prakṛitiṁ puruṣhaṁ chaiva viddhy anādī ubhāv api\nvikārānśh cha guṇānśh chaiva viddhi prakṛiti-sambhavān","en":"Know that Nature (matter) and the Spirit are both beginningless, and know also that all modifications and qualities are born from Nature.","es":"Know both Nature and the individual soul to be verily without beginning; know the modifications as well as the qualities to be born of Nature.","er":"Know that both Prakṛti and the Self (Puruṣa) are without beginning; know that all modifications and the attributes are born from Prakṛti.","gu":"પ્રકૃતિ અને પુરુષ — એ બંને અનાદિ છે એ જાણ; અને સઘળા વિકારો તથા ત્રણે ગુણો પ્રકૃતિમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે એ પણ જાણ."},{"ref":"13.21","ch":13,"v":21,"sa":"कार्यकारणकर्तृत्वे हेतुः प्रकृतिरुच्यते।पुरुषः सुखदुःखानां भोक्तृत्वे हेतुरुच्यते।।13.21।।","tr":"kārya-kāraṇa-kartṛitve hetuḥ prakṛitir uchyate\npuruṣhaḥ sukha-duḥkhānāṁ bhoktṛitve hetur uchyate","en":"In the production of the effect and the cause, Nature (matter) is said to be the cause; in the experience of pleasure and pain, the soul is said to be the one responsible.","es":"With regard to the source of the body and its organs, Nature is said to be the cause; the soul is the cause so far as the enjoyment of happiness and sorrow is concerned.","er":"The Prakṛti is said to be the cause of agency to the body (Kārya) and sense-organs (Karaṇa); the Self is said to be the cause of experiencing pleasure and pain.","gu":"કાર્ય અને કારણ ઉત્પન્ન કરવામાં પ્રકૃતિ નિમિત્ત છે; સુખ-દુઃખ ભોગવવામાં પુરુષ જ કારણ છે એ કહ્યું છે."},{"ref":"13.22","ch":13,"v":22,"sa":"पुरुषः प्रकृतिस्थो हि भुङ्क्ते प्रकृतिजान्गुणान्।कारणं गुणसङ्गोऽस्य सदसद्योनिजन्मसु।।13.22।।","tr":"puruṣhaḥ prakṛiti-stho hi bhuṅkte prakṛiti-jān guṇān\nkāraṇaṁ guṇa-saṅgo ’sya sad-asad-yoni-janmasu","en":"The soul seated in Nature experiences the qualities born of Nature; attachment to the qualities is the cause of its birth in good and evil wombs.","es":"Since the soul is seated in Nature, therefore it experiences the qualities born of Nature. Contact with the qualities is the cause of its births in good and evil wombs.","er":"(a) Indeed, the self seated in Prakrti experiences the Gunas born of Prakrti.\n(b) Its attachment to these Gunas is the cause of birth in good and evil wombs.","gu":"પ્રકૃતિમાં રહેલો પુરુષ પ્રકૃતિ-જ ગુણોને ભોગવે છે; ગુણો સાથેની આ આસક્તિ જ તેના સારા-નઠારા યોનિઓમાં જન્મ લેવાનું કારણ છે."},{"ref":"13.23","ch":13,"v":23,"sa":"उपद्रष्टाऽनुमन्ता च भर्ता भोक्ता महेश्वरः।परमात्मेति चाप्युक्तो देहेऽस्मिन्पुरुषः परः।।13.23।।","tr":"upadraṣhṭānumantā cha bhartā bhoktā maheśhvaraḥ\nparamātmeti chāpy ukto dehe ’smin puruṣhaḥ paraḥ","en":"The Supreme Soul in this body is also called the observer, the permitter, the sustainer, the enjoyer, the great Lord, and the Supreme Self.","es":"He who is the Witness, the Permitter, the Sustainer, the Experiencer, the great Lord, and who is also spoken of as the transcendental Self, is the supreme Person in this body.","er":"The self in the body is called the spectator, approver, supporter, experiencer, great lord, and supreme self.","gu":"આ શરીરમાં બિરાજેલ આત્મા ઉપદ્રષ્ટા, અનુમંતા, ભર્તા, ભોક્તા, મહેશ્વર અને પરમાત્મા — એ નામોથી ઓળખાય છે."},{"ref":"13.24","ch":13,"v":24,"sa":"य एवं वेत्ति पुरुषं प्रकृतिं च गुणैःसह।सर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि न स भूयोऽभिजायते।।13.24।।","tr":"ya evaṁ vetti puruṣhaṁ prakṛitiṁ cha guṇaiḥ saha\nsarvathā vartamāno ’pi na sa bhūyo ’bhijāyate","en":"He who thus knows the Spirit and Matter together with their qualities, in whatever condition he may be, he is not reborn.","es":"He who knows thus the Person, Nature, and Qualities will not be born again, no matter how he may live.","er":"He who understands the Self and Prakriti, along with the Gunas, will not be born again, no matter what state he may be in.","gu":"જે પ્રકૃતિ અને પુરુષ તથા ગુણો સહિત — એ સઘળું આ પ્રમાણે જાણે છે, તે ગમે તે સ્થિતિમાં હોય, ફરી જન્મ ધારણ કરતો નથી."},{"ref":"13.25","ch":13,"v":25,"sa":"ध्यानेनात्मनि पश्यन्ति केचिदात्मानमात्मना।अन्ये सांख्येन योगेन कर्मयोगेन चापरे।।13.25।।","tr":"dhyānenātmani paśhyanti kechid ātmānam ātmanā\nanye sānkhyena yogena karma-yogena chāpare","en":"Some behold the Self within themselves through meditation, others through the Yoga of knowledge, and still others through the Yoga of action.","es":"Some realize the Self in their intellect through meditation, others through Sankhya-Yoga, and still others through Karma-Yoga, with the help of the internal organ.","er":"Some perceive the Self within the self (body) through meditation of the mind, others through Sankhya Yoga, and still others through Karma Yoga.","gu":"કેટલાક ધ્યાન દ્વારા આત્માને જુએ છે; બીજા જ્ઞાનયોગ દ્વારા; અને અન્ય કર્મયોગ દ્વારા — એ રીતે આ આત્મ-સ્વરૂપ અનુભવે છે."},{"ref":"13.26","ch":13,"v":26,"sa":"अन्ये त्वेवमजानन्तः श्रुत्वाऽन्येभ्य उपासते।तेऽपि चातितरन्त्येव मृत्युं श्रुतिपरायणाः।।13.26।।","tr":"anye tv evam ajānantaḥ śhrutvānyebhya upāsate\nte ’pi chātitaranty eva mṛityuṁ śhruti-parāyaṇāḥ","en":"Others, too, who do not know thus, worship, having heard of It from others; they, too, cross beyond death, regarding what they have heard as the supreme refuge.","es":"Others, again, who do not know thus, take to thinking after hearing from others; they too, who are devoted to hearing, certainly overcome death.","er":"But some, who do not know this, having heard from others, worship accordingly—these too, devoted to what they hear, pass beyond death.","gu":"બીજા કેટલાક, આ પ્રમાણે ન જાણવા છતાં, અન્ય પાસેથી સાંભળીને ઉપાસના કરે છે; તેઓ પણ શ્રવણ-પ્રીતિ ધારણ કરીને મૃત્યુ-સાગર પાર કરી જાય છે."},{"ref":"13.27","ch":13,"v":27,"sa":"यावत्सञ्जायते किञ्चित्सत्त्वं स्थावरजङ्गमम्।क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञसंयोगात्तद्विद्धि भरतर्षभ।।13.27।।","tr":"yāvat sañjāyate kiñchit sattvaṁ sthāvara-jaṅgamam\nkṣhetra-kṣhetrajña-sanyogāt tad viddhi bharatarṣhabha","en":"Wherever a being is born, whether unmoving or moving, know thou, O best of the Bharatas (Arjuna), that it is from the union of the field and its knower.","es":"O scion of the Bharata dynasty, whatever object, moving or non-moving, comes into existence, know that to be from the combination of the field and the Knower of the field!","er":"Whatever being is born, whether it be moving or stationary, know, O Arjuna, that it is through the combination of the Ksetra (body) and Ksetrajna (knower of the Field).","gu":"હે અર્જુન, ચર હો કે અચર — જ્યાં પણ કોઈ પ્રાણી ઉત્પન્ન થાય, તે ક્ષેત્ર અને ક્ષેત્રજ્ઞના સંયોગથી જ ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે — આ જાણ."},{"ref":"13.28","ch":13,"v":28,"sa":"समं सर्वेषु भूतेषु तिष्ठन्तं परमेश्वरम्।विनश्यत्स्वविनश्यन्तं यः पश्यति स पश्यति।।13.28।।","tr":"samaṁ sarveṣhu bhūteṣhu tiṣhṭhantaṁ parameśhvaram\nvinaśhyatsv avinaśhyantaṁ yaḥ paśhyati sa paśhyati","en":"He who sees the Supreme Lord existing truly in all beings, the imperishable within the perishable, sees indeed.","es":"He who sees the Supreme Lord existing truly in all beings, and the Imperishable among the perishable, sees indeed.","er":"Who sees the supreme ruler dwelling alike in all bodies and never perishing, even when they perish, he indeed sees.","gu":"જે સઘળા પ્રાણીઓમાં, ક્ષર-અક્ષર બેઉ ભેદ ઓળંગીને, સમભાવે પ્રભુ-પ્રભાવ જુએ છે — તે ખરેખર જ્ઞાનદ્રષ્ટિ ધરાવે છે."},{"ref":"13.29","ch":13,"v":29,"sa":"समं पश्यन्हि सर्वत्र समवस्थितमीश्वरम्।न हिनस्त्यात्मनाऽऽत्मानं ततो याति परां गतिम्।।13.29।।","tr":"samaṁ paśhyan hi sarvatra samavasthitam īśhvaram\nna hinasty ātmanātmānaṁ tato yāti parāṁ gatim","en":"For he who truly sees the same Lord dwelling everywhere does not destroy the Self by the self; rather, he attains the highest goal.","es":"Since, by truly seeing God, who is present everywhere alike, he does not injure the Self by the Self, he therefore attains the supreme Goal.","er":"For, seeing the ruler abiding alike in every place, he does not injure himself with his own mind and therefore reaches the highest goal.","gu":"જે ખરેખર સર્વત્ર એક જ ઈશ્વરને જુએ છે, તે આત્માને આત્મા વડે નષ્ટ કરતો નથી; આ રીતે તે પરમ ગતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"13.30","ch":13,"v":30,"sa":"प्रकृत्यैव च कर्माणि क्रियमाणानि सर्वशः।यः पश्यति तथाऽऽत्मानमकर्तारं स पश्यति।।13.30।।","tr":"prakṛityaiva cha karmāṇi kriyamāṇāni sarvaśhaḥ\nyaḥ paśhyati tathātmānam akartāraṁ sa paśhyati","en":"He sees, who sees that all actions are performed solely by Nature and that the Self is without action.","es":"And he who sees actions being done in various ways by Nature itself, and also the Self as the non-agent, he sees.","er":"He who sees that all acts are done universally by Prakrti alone, and likewise that the self is not the doer, he indeed sees.","gu":"જે જુએ છે કે સઘળી ક્રિયાઓ માત્ર પ્રકૃતિ દ્વારા જ થઈ રહી છે અને આત્મા નિષ્ક્રિય છે — તે સાચો દ્રષ્ટા છે."},{"ref":"13.31","ch":13,"v":31,"sa":"यदा भूतपृथग्भावमेकस्थमनुपश्यति।तत एव च विस्तारं ब्रह्म सम्पद्यते तदा।।13.31।।","tr":"yadā bhūta-pṛithag-bhāvam eka-stham anupaśhyati\ntata eva cha vistāraṁ brahma sampadyate tadā","en":"When a person sees all beings as resting in the One and emanating from the One alone, they then become Brahman.","es":"When one realizes that the state of diversity of living things is rooted in the One, and that their manifestation also comes from That, then one becomes identified with Brahman.","er":"When he perceives the independent modes of existence of all beings centered in one, and their expansion from it alone, then he attains Brahman.","gu":"જ્યારે મનુષ્ય સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓને એક જ સ્થાનમાં સ્થિત અને એક જ માંથી ઉત્પન્ન થયેલા જુએ છે, ત્યારે તે બ્રહ્મભૂત થઈ જાય છે."},{"ref":"13.32","ch":13,"v":32,"sa":"अनादित्वान्निर्गुणत्वात्परमात्मायमव्ययः।शरीरस्थोऽपि कौन्तेय न करोति न लिप्यते।।13.32।।","tr":"anāditvān nirguṇatvāt paramātmāyam avyayaḥ\nśharīra-stho ’pi kaunteya na karoti na lipyate","en":"Being without beginning, devoid of any qualities, the Supreme Self, imperishable, though dwelling in the body, O Arjuna, neither acts nor is tainted.","es":"Being without beginning and without end, O son of Kunti, this immutable, supreme Self does not act, nor is It affected [Also translated as tainted.-Tr.], although It exists in the body.","er":"This supreme Self, though dwelling in the body, is immutable, O Arjuna, being without beginning. It neither acts nor is tainted, as it is without Gunas.","gu":"આ પરમ આત્મા અનાદિ, ગુણ-રહિત અને અવ્યયી છે — દેહમાં વસ્યો હોવા છતાં, હે અર્જુન, ન તો કર્મ કરે છે, ન તો દોષથી લેપાય છે."},{"ref":"13.33","ch":13,"v":33,"sa":"यथा सर्वगतं सौक्ष्म्यादाकाशं नोपलिप्यते।सर्वत्रावस्थितो देहे तथाऽऽत्मा नोपलिप्यते।।13.33।।","tr":"yathā sarva-gataṁ saukṣhmyād ākāśhaṁ nopalipyate\nsarvatrāvasthito dehe tathātmā nopalipyate","en":"As the all-pervading ether is not tainted, due to its subtlety, so the Self seated everywhere in the body is not tainted either.","es":"As the all-pervading space is not defiled, due to its subtlety, similarly the Self, present everywhere in bodies, is not defiled.","er":"As the all-pervading ether is not tainted due to its subtlety, even so, the self abiding in the body is not tainted everywhere.","gu":"જેમ સર્વત્ર વ્યાપ્ત આકાશ સૂક્ષ્મ હોવાથી ક્યારેય લેપાતો નથી, તેમ સર્વ દેહોમાં સ્થિત આત્મા પણ ક્યારેય દોષથી ખરડાતો નથી."},{"ref":"13.34","ch":13,"v":34,"sa":"यथा प्रकाशयत्येकः कृत्स्नं लोकमिमं रविः।क्षेत्रं क्षेत्री तथा कृत्स्नं प्रकाशयति भारत।।13.34।।","tr":"yathā prakāśhayaty ekaḥ kṛitsnaṁ lokam imaṁ raviḥ\nkṣhetraṁ kṣhetrī tathā kṛitsnaṁ prakāśhayati bhārata","en":"Just as the one sun illuminates the entire world, so too does the Lord of the field (Supreme Self) illuminate the entire field, O Arjuna.","es":"As the single sun illuminates this entire world, similarly, O descendant of the Bharata dynasty, the Knower of the field illuminates the entire field.","er":"As the one sun illuminates this entire world, so does the Knower of the Field (Ksetrin, the self), O Arjuna, illuminate the entire Field (the body).","gu":"જેમ એક સૂર્ય આ સમગ્ર જગતને પ્રકાશિત કરે છે, તેમ ક્ષેત્રનો જ્ઞાતા — ઈશ્વર — સમગ્ર ક્ષેત્રને પ્રકાશિત કરે છે, હે અર્જુન."},{"ref":"13.35","ch":13,"v":35,"sa":"क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञयोरेवमन्तरं ज्ञानचक्षुषा।भूतप्रकृतिमोक्षं च ये विदुर्यान्ति ते परम्।।13.35।।","tr":"kṣhetra-kṣhetrajñayor evam antaraṁ jñāna-chakṣhuṣhā\nbhūta-prakṛiti-mokṣhaṁ cha ye vidur yānti te param","en":"They who, by the eye of knowledge, perceive the distinction between the field and its knower, as well as the liberation from the Nature of being, go to the Supreme.","es":"Those who, through the eye of wisdom, know the distinction between the field and the Knower of the field, and the annihilation of the Matrix of beings, reach the Supreme.","er":"Those who thus discern, with the eye of knowledge, the difference between the body or the Field (Ksetra) and the knower of the body or Field-knower (Ksetrajna), and the means of deliverance from the manifested Prakrti, they attain the Supreme.","gu":"જ્ઞાનની આંખ વડે ક્ષેત્ર અને ક્ષેત્રજ્ઞ વચ્ચેનો ભેદ તથા પ્રકૃતિ-બંધનમાંથી જીવની મુક્તિ જોનારા — તે પરમ ધ્યેયને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"14.1","ch":14,"v":1,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाचपरं भूयः प्रवक्ष्यामि ज्ञानानां ज्ञानमुत्तमम्।यज्ज्ञात्वा मुनयः सर्वे परां सिद्धिमितो गताः।।14.1।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nparaṁ bhūyaḥ pravakṣhyāmi jñānānāṁ jñānam uttamam\nyaj jñātvā munayaḥ sarve parāṁ siddhim ito gatāḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"I will again declare to thee that supreme knowledge, the best of all knowledge, having known which all the sages have gone to supreme perfection after this life.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"I shall speak again of the supreme knowledge, the best of all knowledge, by realizing which all the contemplatives have reached the highest perfection from here.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"I shall declare again another kind of knowledge: It is the best of all forms of knowledge, by knowing which all the sages have attained the state of perfection beyond this world.\"","gu":"શ્રીભગવાન બોલ્યા: હું ફરી એ સર્વોત્તમ જ્ઞાન — જ્ઞાનોમાં શ્રેષ્ઠ — તને કહીશ, જે જાણીને સઘળા ઋષિઓ પરમ સિદ્ધિ પામ્યા છે."},{"ref":"14.2","ch":14,"v":2,"sa":"इदं ज्ञानमुपाश्रित्य मम साधर्म्यमागताः।सर्गेऽपि नोपजायन्ते प्रलये न व्यथन्ति च।।14.2।।","tr":"idaṁ jñānam upāśhritya mama sādharmyam āgatāḥ\nsarge ’pi nopajāyante pralaye na vyathanti cha","en":"Those who, having taken refuge in this knowledge, have attained unity with Me, are neither born at the time of creation nor disturbed at the time of dissolution.","es":"Those who attain identity with Me by resorting to this Knowledge are not born even during creation, nor do they suffer pain during dissolution.","er":"Resorting to this knowledge, partaking in My Nature, they are not born at the time of creation nor do they suffer at the time of dissolution.","gu":"જેઓ આ જ્ઞાનનો આશ્રય લઈ મારી સાથે એકતા પ્રાપ્ત કર્યા છે, તેઓ સૃષ્ટિ સમયે ફરી જન્મ લેતા નથી, ન તો પ્રલય સમયે વ્યથા પામે છે."},{"ref":"14.3","ch":14,"v":3,"sa":"मम योनिर्महद्ब्रह्म तस्मिन् गर्भं दधाम्यहम्।संभवः सर्वभूतानां ततो भवति भारत।।14.3।।","tr":"mama yonir mahad brahma tasmin garbhaṁ dadhāmy aham\nsambhavaḥ sarva-bhūtānāṁ tato bhavati bhārata","en":"My womb is the great Brahma; in it I place the germ; thence, O Arjuna, is the birth of all beings.","es":"My womb is the great sustainer. In it, I place the seed. From that, O scion of the Bharata dynasty, all things are born.","er":"My womb is the great Brahman (i.e. Prakṛti). In it, I lay the germ. From that, O Arjuna, comes the birth of all beings.","gu":"મહત્ બ્રહ્મ મારી ઉદર-ભૂમિ છે; તેમાં હું બીજ સ્થાપું છું; હે અર્જુન, તેમાંથી જ સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓનો જન્મ થાય છે."},{"ref":"14.4","ch":14,"v":4,"sa":"सर्वयोनिषु कौन्तेय मूर्तयः सम्भवन्ति याः।तासां ब्रह्म महद्योनिरहं बीजप्रदः पिता।।14.4।।","tr":"sarva-yoniṣhu kaunteya mūrtayaḥ sambhavanti yāḥ\ntāsāṁ brahma mahad yonir ahaṁ bīja-pradaḥ pitā","en":"Whatever forms are produced, O Arjuna, in any womb whatsoever, the great Brahma is their womb, and I am the seed-giving father.","es":"O son of Kunti, whatever forms are born from all the wombs, of them the great sustainer is the womb; I am the father who deposits the seed.","er":"Whatever forms are produced in any womb, O Arjuna, the Prakṛti is their great womb, and I am the sowing father.","gu":"જે-જે કોઈ ઉદરમાંથી જે-જે સ્વરૂપ ઉત્પન્ન થાય, તે સૌની ઉદર-ભૂમિ મહત્ બ્રહ્મ છે, અને હું બીજ-પ્રદ પિતા છું."},{"ref":"14.5","ch":14,"v":5,"sa":"सत्त्वं रजस्तम इति गुणाः प्रकृतिसंभवाः।निबध्नन्ति महाबाहो देहे देहिनमव्ययम्।।14.5।।","tr":"sattvaṁ rajas tama iti guṇāḥ prakṛiti-sambhavāḥ\nnibadhnanti mahā-bāho dehe dehinam avyayam","en":"These qualities, O Arjuna, born of Nature, bind fast in the body of the embodied, the indestructible: purity, passion, and inertia.","es":"O mighty-armed one, the qualities, viz. sattva, rajas, and tamas, born of Nature, are the immutable embodiments belonging to the body.","er":"The Gunas of Sattva, Rajas, and Tamas arise from Prakrti and bind the immutable Self in the body, O Arjuna.","gu":"સત્ત્વ, રજ અને તમ — આ ત્રણ ગુણ પ્રકૃતિમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન છે; હે અર્જુન, તે અવિનાશી જીવાત્માને દેહમાં દૃઢતાપૂર્વક બાંધે છે."},{"ref":"14.6","ch":14,"v":6,"sa":"तत्र सत्त्वं निर्मलत्वात्प्रकाशकमनामयम्।सुखसङ्गेन बध्नाति ज्ञानसङ्गेन चानघ।।14.6।।","tr":"tatra sattvaṁ nirmalatvāt prakāśhakam anāmayam\nsukha-saṅgena badhnāti jñāna-saṅgena chānagha","en":"Of these, sattva, which is luminous and healthy due to its stainlessness, binds one by attachment to happiness and knowledge, O sinless one.","es":"Among them, sattva, being pure and nirmala (pure-transparent, i.e., capable of resisting any form of ignorance, and hence an illuminator, i.e. a revealer of Consciousness), is harmless. O sinless one, it binds through attachment to happiness and attachment to knowledge.","er":"Of these, sattva, being without impurity, is luminous and free from morbidity. It binds, O Arjuna, through attachment to pleasure and knowledge.","gu":"તે ત્રણ ગુણોમાંથી સત્ત્વ પ્રકાશમય અને નિર્મળ છે — તે સુખ અને જ્ઞાનની આસક્તિના બંધનથી જીવાત્માને બાંધે છે, હે નિષ્પાપ અર્જુન."},{"ref":"14.7","ch":14,"v":7,"sa":"रजो रागात्मकं विद्धि तृष्णासङ्गसमुद्भवम्।तन्निबध्नाति कौन्तेय कर्मसङ्गेन देहिनम्।।14.7।।","tr":"rajo rāgātmakaṁ viddhi tṛiṣhṇā-saṅga-samudbhavam\ntan nibadhnāti kaunteya karma-saṅgena dehinam","en":"Know, O Arjuna, that Rajas is of the nature of passion, the source of thirst and attachment; it binds fast the embodied one by attachment to action.","es":"Know rajas to be of the nature of passion, born of hankering and attachment. O son of Kunti, it binds the embodied one through attachment to action.","er":"Know, O Arjuna, that Rajas is of the nature of passion springing from thirst and attachment. It binds the embodied self with attachment to action.","gu":"જાણ કે રજ તો રાગના સ્વભાવવાળો છે, તૃષ્ણા અને આસક્તિનો ઉત્પત્તિ-સ્ત્રોત છે; તે જીવાત્માને કર્મ-આસક્તિના બંધનથી દૃઢપણે બાંધે છે."},{"ref":"14.8","ch":14,"v":8,"sa":"तमस्त्वज्ञानजं विद्धि मोहनं सर्वदेहिनाम्।प्रमादालस्यनिद्राभिस्तन्निबध्नाति भारत।।14.8।।","tr":"tamas tv ajñāna-jaṁ viddhi mohanaṁ sarva-dehinām\npramādālasya-nidrābhis tan nibadhnāti bhārata","en":"But know thou Tamas to be born of ignorance, deluding all embodied beings; it binds fast, O Arjuna, through heedlessness, indolence, and sleep.","es":"On the other hand, know tamas, which deludes all embodied beings, to be born of ignorance. O scion of the Bharata dynasty, it binds through inadvertence, laziness, and sleep.","er":"Know that Tamas is born of false knowledge and deludes all embodied beings. It binds, O Arjuna, with negligence, indolence, and sleep.","gu":"જાણ કે તમ અજ્ઞાનથી ઉત્પન્ન થયેલો છે, જે સઘળા દેહધારીઓને મોહિત કરે છે; તે પ્રમાદ, આળસ અને નિદ્રાના બંધનથી દૃઢપણે બાંધે છે, હે અર્જુન."},{"ref":"14.9","ch":14,"v":9,"sa":"सत्त्वं सुखे सञ्जयति रजः कर्मणि भारत।ज्ञानमावृत्य तु तमः प्रमादे सञ्जयत्युत।।14.9।।","tr":"sattvaṁ sukhe sañjayati rajaḥ karmaṇi bhārata\njñānam āvṛitya tu tamaḥ pramāde sañjayaty uta","en":"Sattva attaches to happiness, Rajas to action, O Arjuna, while Tamas, verily shrouding knowledge, attaches to heedlessness.","es":"O scion of the Bharata dynasty, sattva attaches one to happiness, rajas to action, while tamas, obscuring knowledge, leads to inadvertence as well.","er":"Sattva generates attachment to pleasure, Rajas to action, O Arjuna. But Tamas, obscuring knowledge, generates attachment to negligence.","gu":"સત્ત્વ સુખ સાથે જોડાય છે, રજસ ક્રિયા સાથે, હે અર્જુન; અને તમસ જ્ઞાનને ઢાંકીને પ્રમાદ સાથે જોડાય છે."},{"ref":"14.10","ch":14,"v":10,"sa":"रजस्तमश्चाभिभूय सत्त्वं भवति भारत।रजः सत्त्वं तमश्चैव तमः सत्त्वं रजस्तथा।।14.10।।","tr":"rajas tamaśh chābhibhūya sattvaṁ bhavati bhārata\nrajaḥ sattvaṁ tamaśh chaiva tamaḥ sattvaṁ rajas tathā","en":"Now, O Arjuna, Sattva prevails, having overpowered Rajas and Tamas; then Rajas, having overpowered Sattva and Tamas; and then Tamas, having overpowered Sattva and Rajas.","es":"O scion of the Bharata dynasty, sattva increases by subduing rajas and tamas; rajas increases by overpowering sattva and tamas; and tamas increases by dominating over sattva and rajas.","er":"Prevailing over Rajas and Tamas, Sattva predominates, O Arjuna. Prevailing over Tamas and Sattva, Rajas predominates. Prevailing over Rajas and Sattva, Tamas predominates.","gu":"ક્યારેક સત્ત્વ રજસ અને તમસને દબાવીને પ્રબળ બને છે; ક્યારેક રજસ સત્ત્વ અને તમસને, અને ક્યારેક તમસ સત્ત્વ અને રજસને દબાવી દે છે."},{"ref":"14.11","ch":14,"v":11,"sa":"सर्वद्वारेषु देहेऽस्मिन्प्रकाश उपजायते।ज्ञानं यदा तदा विद्याद्विवृद्धं सत्त्वमित्युत।।14.11।।","tr":"sarva-dvāreṣhu dehe ’smin prakāśha upajāyate\njñānaṁ yadā tadā vidyād vivṛiddhaṁ sattvam ity uta","en":"When the wisdom-light shines through every gate of this body, then it may be known that Sattva is predominant.","es":"When the illumination of knowledge radiates through all the doors of the senses in this body, then one should know that sattva has greatly increased.","er":"When knowledge, like light, illuminates from all gateways (i.e., the senses), then one should know that Sattva prevails.","gu":"જ્યારે આ શરીરના પ્રત્યેક દ્વારમાં જ્ઞાનનો પ્રકાશ ફેલાય, ત્યારે સમજો કે સત્ત્વ ગુણ પ્રધાન છે."},{"ref":"14.12","ch":14,"v":12,"sa":"लोभः प्रवृत्तिरारम्भः कर्मणामशमः स्पृहा।रजस्येतानि जायन्ते विवृद्धे भरतर्षभ।।14.12।।","tr":"lobhaḥ pravṛittir ārambhaḥ karmaṇām aśhamaḥ spṛihā\nrajasy etāni jāyante vivṛiddhe bharatarṣhabha","en":"Greed, activity, the undertaking of actions, restlessness, and longing—these arise when Rajas is predominant, O Arjuna.","es":"O best of the Bharata dynasty, when rajas becomes predominant, these come into being: avarice, restlessness, undertaking of actions, agitation, and craving.","er":"Greed, activity, undertaking of work, restlessness, and longing—these arise, O Arjuna, when Rajas predominates.","gu":"લોભ, ક્રિયાશીલતા, કર્મોનો આરંભ, ચંચળતા અને તૃષ્ણા — આ સઘળું રજસ ગુણ પ્રબળ થાય ત્યારે ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે, હે અર્જુન."},{"ref":"14.13","ch":14,"v":13,"sa":"अप्रकाशोऽप्रवृत्तिश्च प्रमादो मोह एव च।तमस्येतानि जायन्ते विवृद्धे कुरुनन्दन।।14.13।।","tr":"aprakāśho ’pravṛittiśh cha pramādo moha eva cha\ntamasy etāni jāyante vivṛiddhe kuru-nandana","en":"Darkness, inertia, carelessness, and delusion—these arise when Tamas is predominant, O Arjuna.","es":"O descendant of the Kuru dynasty, when tamas predominates, these come into being without exception: non-discrimination, inactivity, inadvertence, and delusion.","er":"Non-illumination, inactivity, negligence, and even delusion—these arise, O Arjuna, when Tamas prevails.","gu":"અંધકાર, જડતા, બેદરકારી અને ભ્રમ — આ સઘળું તમસ ગુણ પ્રધાન થાય ત્યારે ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે, હે અર્જુન."},{"ref":"14.14","ch":14,"v":14,"sa":"यदा सत्त्वे प्रवृद्धे तु प्रलयं याति देहभृत्।तदोत्तमविदां लोकानमलान्प्रतिपद्यते।।14.14।।","tr":"yadā sattve pravṛiddhe tu pralayaṁ yāti deha-bhṛit\ntadottama-vidāṁ lokān amalān pratipadyate","en":"If the embodied one meets death when Sattva is predominant, then they attain the spotless worlds of the knowers of the Highest.","es":"When an embodied one undergoes death while sattva is exclusively predominant, then he attains the untainted worlds of those who know the highest (entities).","er":"If the embodied self dissolves when Sattva prevails, then it proceeds to the pure worlds of those who know the highest.","gu":"જો દેહધારી સત્ત્વ ગુણ પ્રધાન હોય ત્યારે મૃત્યુ પામે, તો તે પરમ જ્ઞાનીઓના નિર્મળ લોકોને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"14.15","ch":14,"v":15,"sa":"रजसि प्रलयं गत्वा कर्मसङ्गिषु जायते।तथा प्रलीनस्तमसि मूढयोनिषु जायते।।14.15।।","tr":"rajasi pralayaṁ gatvā karma-saṅgiṣhu jāyate\ntathā pralīnas tamasi mūḍha-yoniṣhu jāyate","en":"Meeting death in Rajas, he is born among those who are attached to action; and dying in Tamas, he is born in the womb of the thoughtless.","es":"When one dies while rajas predominates, they are born among people attached to activity. Similarly, when one dies while tamas predominates, they take birth among the stupid species.","er":"(a) When Rajas is prevalent, one meets with dissolution and is born among those attached to work.\n(b) Similarly, when Tamas prevails, one who has met with dissolution is born in the womb of beings lacking intelligence.","gu":"રજસ ગુણ પ્રધાન હોય ત્યારે મૃત્યુ પામ્યે, ક્રિયાસક્ત જનોમાં જન્મ થાય છે; અને તમસ ગુણ વખતે મૃત્યુ પામ્યે, મૂઢ યોનિઓમાં જન્મ થાય છે."},{"ref":"14.16","ch":14,"v":16,"sa":"कर्मणः सुकृतस्याहुः सात्त्विकं निर्मलं फलम्।रजसस्तु फलं दुःखमज्ञानं तमसः फलम्।।14.16।।","tr":"karmaṇaḥ sukṛitasyāhuḥ sāttvikaṁ nirmalaṁ phalam\nrajasas tu phalaṁ duḥkham ajñānaṁ tamasaḥ phalam","en":"They say that the fruit of good action is Sattvic and pure; indeed, the fruit of Rajas is pain, and the fruit of Tamas is ignorance.","es":"They say that the result of good work is pure and is born of Sattva. But the result of Rajas is sorrow; the result of Tamas is ignorance.","er":"It is said that the fruit of a good deed is pure and of the nature of Sattva; the fruit of Rajas is pain; and the fruit of Tamas is ignorance.","gu":"સારાં કર્મનું ફળ સાત્ત્વિક અને પવિત્ર છે; રજસ કર્મનું ફળ દુઃખ છે; અને તમસ કર્મનું ફળ અજ્ઞાન છે."},{"ref":"14.17","ch":14,"v":17,"sa":"सत्त्वात्सञ्जायते ज्ञानं रजसो लोभ एव च।प्रमादमोहौ तमसो भवतोऽज्ञानमेव च।।14.17।।","tr":"sattvāt sañjāyate jñānaṁ rajaso lobha eva cha\npramāda-mohau tamaso bhavato ’jñānam eva cha","en":"From Sattva arises knowledge, and greed from Rajas; heedlessness and delusion arise from Tamas, and also ignorance.","es":"From sattva is born knowledge, and from rajas, avarice indeed. From tamas are born inadvertence, delusion, and ignorance, to be sure.","er":"From Sattva arises knowledge, from Rajas arises greed, from Tamas arises negligence and delusion, and from it arises ignorance.","gu":"સત્ત્વ ગુણથી જ્ઞાન ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે; રજસ ગુણથી લોભ; અને તમસ ગુણથી પ્રમાદ, ભ્રમ તેમ જ અજ્ઞાન ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે."},{"ref":"14.18","ch":14,"v":18,"sa":"ऊर्ध्वं गच्छन्ति सत्त्वस्था मध्ये तिष्ठन्ति राजसाः।जघन्यगुणवृत्तिस्था अधो गच्छन्ति तामसाः।।14.18।।","tr":"ūrdhvaṁ gachchhanti sattva-sthā madhye tiṣhṭhanti rājasāḥ\njaghanya-guṇa-vṛitti-sthā adho gachchhanti tāmasāḥ","en":"Those seated in Sattva ascend; those of Rajasic nature dwell in the middle; and those of Tamasic nature, abiding in the function of the lowest Guna, descend.","es":"People who conform to sattva go higher up; those who conform to rajas stay in the middle; those who conform to tamas, who conform to the actions of the lowest quality, go down.","er":"Those who rest in Sattva ascend upwards; those who abide in Rajas stay in the middle; and those, abiding in the tendencies of Tamas descend downwards.","gu":"સત્ત્વ ગુણમાં સ્થિત જનો ઊર્ધ્વ ગતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે; રાજસી સ્વભાવના જનો મધ્યમ સ્થાને રહે છે; અને તામસી ગુણ ધરાવતા જનો નીચે, અધોગતિ તરફ જાય છે."},{"ref":"14.19","ch":14,"v":19,"sa":"नान्यं गुणेभ्यः कर्तारं यदा द्रष्टानुपश्यति।गुणेभ्यश्च परं वेत्ति मद्भावं सोऽधिगच्छति।।14.19।।","tr":"nānyaṁ guṇebhyaḥ kartāraṁ yadā draṣhṭānupaśhyati\nguṇebhyaśh cha paraṁ vetti mad-bhāvaṁ so ’dhigachchhati","en":"When the seer beholds no agent other than the Gunas and knows that which is higher than them, he attains to My Being.","es":"When the witness sees none other than the qualities as the agent, and knows that which is superior to the qualities, he attains My nature.","er":"When the seer beholds no agent of action other than the Gunas, and knows what is beyond the Gunas, he attains to My state.","gu":"જ્યારે દ્રષ્ટા ગુણો સિવાય બીજો કોઈ કર્તા નથી એ જુએ, અને ગુણોથી પર જે છે તેને ઓળખે, ત્યારે તે વ્યક્તિ મારા સ્વરૂપને પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે."},{"ref":"14.20","ch":14,"v":20,"sa":"गुणानेतानतीत्य त्रीन्देही देहसमुद्भवान्।जन्ममृत्युजरादुःखैर्विमुक्तोऽमृतमश्नुते।।14.20।।","tr":"guṇān etān atītya trīn dehī deha-samudbhavān\njanma-mṛityu-jarā-duḥkhair vimukto ’mṛitam aśhnute","en":"The embodied one, having crossed beyond these three Gunas from which the body is evolved, is freed from birth, death, decay, and pain, and attains immortality.","es":"Having transcended these three qualities, which are the origin of the body, the embodied one becomes free from birth, death, old age, and sorrows, and experiences Immortality.","er":"The embodied Self, crossing beyond these three Gunas that arise in the body, and being freed from birth, death, aging, and pain, attains immortality.","gu":"દેહ ધારી, જે ત્રણ ગુણોથી — જેમાંથી આ શરીર જન્મ્યું છે — ઉપર ઊઠે છે, તે જન્મ, મૃત્યુ, વૃદ્ધાવસ્થા અને દુઃખથી મુક્ત થઈ અમૃત્વ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"14.21","ch":14,"v":21,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाचकैर्लिंगैस्त्रीन्गुणानेतानतीतो भवति प्रभो।किमाचारः कथं चैतांस्त्रीन्गुणानतिवर्तते।।14.21।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nkair liṅgais trīn guṇān etān atīto bhavati prabho\nkim āchāraḥ kathaṁ chaitāns trīn guṇān ativartate","en":"Arjuna said, \"What are the marks of one who has transcended the three qualities, O Lord? What is their conduct, and how do they go beyond these three qualities?\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Lord, by what signs is one known who has gone beyond these three qualities? What is their behavior, and how do they transcend these three qualities?\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"What are the marks of a person who has transcended the three Gunas? What is their behavior? And how do they transcend the three Gunas?\"","gu":"અર્જુને પૂછ્યું: હે પ્રભો, ત્રણ ગુણોને ઓળંગી ગયેલ વ્યક્તિનાં ચિહ્નો કયાં છે? તેનું આચરણ કેવું હોય, અને ત્રણ ગુણોથી પર કઈ રીતે જવાય?"},{"ref":"14.22","ch":14,"v":22,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाचप्रकाशं च प्रवृत्तिं च मोहमेव च पाण्डव।न द्वेष्टि सम्प्रवृत्तानि न निवृत्तानि काङ्क्षति।।14.22।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nprakāśhaṁ cha pravṛittiṁ cha moham eva cha pāṇḍava\nna dveṣhṭi sampravṛittāni na nivṛittāni kāṅkṣhati","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"When light, activity, and delusion are present, he does not hate them, nor does he long for them when they are absent.","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"O son of Pandu, he neither dislikes illumination (knowledge), activity, nor delusion when they appear, nor does he long for them when they disappear.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"He does not hate illumination, nor activity, nor even delusion, O Arjuna, while these prevail, nor does He long for them when they cease.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: જ્યારે પ્રકાશ, ક્રિયા અને ભ્રમ ઉપસ્થિત હોય, ત્યારે જ્ઞાની તેમનાથી દ્વેષ કરતો નથી; અને જ્યારે તે અભાવ હોય, ત્યારે તેમની ઝંખના પણ કરતો નથી."},{"ref":"14.23","ch":14,"v":23,"sa":"उदासीनवदासीनो गुणैर्यो न विचाल्यते।गुणा वर्तन्त इत्येव योऽवतिष्ठति नेङ्गते।।14.23।।","tr":"udāsīna-vad āsīno guṇair yo na vichālyate\nguṇā vartanta ity evaṁ yo ’vatiṣhṭhati neṅgate","en":"He who, seated like one unconcerned, is not moved by the dualities, and who, knowing that the dualities are active, is self-centered and does not move.","es":"He who, sitting like one indifferent, is not distracted by the three qualities; he who, thinking that the qualities alone act, remains firm and does not move surely;","er":"He who sits like one unconcerned, undisturbed by the Gunas; who knows, 'It is the Gunas that are in motion,' and so remains unshaken;","gu":"જે ઉદાસીન ભાવે બેઠો હોય, ગુણો વડે ચલિત ન થાય, ગુણો જ ક્રિયાશીલ છે એ જાણે, અને અડગ રહે, ડગે નહીં — તે વ્યક્તિ ત્રણ ગુણોને ઓળંગી ગઈ છે એમ કહેવાય."},{"ref":"14.24","ch":14,"v":24,"sa":"समदुःखसुखः स्वस्थः समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः।तुल्यप्रियाप्रियो धीरस्तुल्यनिन्दात्मसंस्तुतिः।।14.24।।","tr":"sama-duḥkha-sukhaḥ sva-sthaḥ sama-loṣhṭāśhma-kāñchanaḥ\ntulya-priyāpriyo dhīras tulya-nindātma-sanstutiḥ","en":"Who is the same in pleasure and pain, who dwells in the Self, to whom a clod of earth, a stone, and gold are all alike, who is the same to the dear and the unfriendly, who is firm, and to whom censure and praise are one and the same.","es":"He to whom sorrow and happiness are alike, who is established in his own Self, to whom a lump of earth, iron, and gold are the same, to whom the agreeable and the disagreeable are the same, who is wise, to whom censure and his own praise are the same;","er":"He who is alike in pleasure and pain, who dwells in his Self, who looks upon a clod, a stone, and a piece of gold as of equal value, who remains the same towards things dear and hateful, and who is intelligent, who regards both blame and praise of himself as equal.","gu":"જે સુખ અને દુઃખમાં સમાન રહે છે, જે આત્મામાં સ્થિત છે, જેને માટે માટી, પથ્થર અને સોનું બધાં સમાન છે, જે પ્રિય અને અપ્રિય પ્રત્યે સમભાવ ધરાવે છે — તે સ્થિર અને ગુણાતીત મહાપુરુષ છે."},{"ref":"14.25","ch":14,"v":25,"sa":"मानापमानयोस्तुल्यस्तुल्यो मित्रारिपक्षयोः।सर्वारम्भपरित्यागी गुणातीतः स उच्यते।।14.25।।","tr":"mānāpamānayos tulyas tulyo mitrāri-pakṣhayoḥ\nsarvārambha-parityāgī guṇātītaḥ sa uchyate","en":"Who is the same in honor and dishonor, the same to friend and foe, abandoning all undertakings, he is said to have transcended the dualities.","es":"He who is the same under honor and dishonor, who is equitably disposed towards both friends and foes, who has renounced all undertakings—he is said to have gone beyond dualities.","er":"He who is the same in honor and dishonor, and the same to friend and foe, and who has abandoned all enterprises—he is said to have risen above the Gunas.","gu":"જે માન અને અપમાનમાં સમાન છે, મિત્ર અને શત્રુ પ્રત્યે સમભાવ ધરાવે છે, અને સર્વ ઉદ્યમોનો ત્યાગ કર્યો છે — તે વ્યક્તિ ત્રણ ગુણોથી પર થઈ ગઈ છે એમ કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"14.26","ch":14,"v":26,"sa":"मां च योऽव्यभिचारेण भक्ितयोगेन सेवते।स गुणान्समतीत्यैतान् ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते।।14.26।।","tr":"māṁ cha yo ’vyabhichāreṇa bhakti-yogena sevate\nsa guṇān samatītyaitān brahma-bhūyāya kalpate","en":"And he who serves Me with unwavering devotion, he, crossing beyond the dualities, is fit for becoming Brahman.","es":"And he who serves Me through the unswerving Yoga of Devotion, he, having gone beyond these qualities, qualifies for becoming Brahman.","er":"And he who, with unwavering devotion through Yoga, serves Me, he, transcending the Gunas, becomes fit for the state of Brahman.","gu":"જે અવિચળ ભક્તિ દ્વારા મારી સેવા કરે છે, તે ત્રણ ગુણોને ઓળંગીને બ્રહ્મ બનવાને પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે."},{"ref":"14.27","ch":14,"v":27,"sa":"ब्रह्मणो हि प्रतिष्ठाऽहममृतस्याव्ययस्य च।शाश्वतस्य च धर्मस्य सुखस्यैकान्तिकस्य च।।14.27।।","tr":"brahmaṇo hi pratiṣhṭhāham amṛitasyāvyayasya cha\nśhāśhvatasya cha dharmasya sukhasyaikāntikasya cha","en":"For I am the abode of Brahman, the immortal, immutable, and everlasting Dharma, and absolute bliss.","es":"For I am the Abode of Brahman—the indestructible, immutable, eternal, Dharma, and absolute Bliss.","er":"For I am the ground of Brahman, the immortal, immutable, and eternal Dharma, and perfect bliss.","gu":"કારણ કે હું જ બ્રહ્મનું આશ્રયસ્થાન છું — અમૃત, અવ્યય, સનાતન ધર્મ, અને સંપૂર્ણ આનંદનો આધાર."},{"ref":"15.1","ch":15,"v":1,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाचऊर्ध्वमूलमधःशाखमश्वत्थं प्राहुरव्ययम्।छन्दांसि यस्य पर्णानि यस्तं वेद स वेदवित्।।15.1।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nūrdhva-mūlam adhaḥ-śhākham aśhvatthaṁ prāhur avyayam\nchhandānsi yasya parṇāni yas taṁ veda sa veda-vit","en":"The Blessed Lord said: They (the wise) speak of the indestructible peepul tree, with its roots above and branches below, whose leaves are the meters or hymns; he who knows it is a knower of the Vedas.","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"They say that the peepul tree, which has its roots upward and its branches downward, and of which the Vedas are the leaves, is imperishable. He who realizes it is a knower of the Vedas.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"They speak of an immutable Asvattha tree with its roots above and branches below; its leaves are the Vedas. He who knows it knows the Vedas.\"","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ કહ્યું: જ્ઞાનીઓ અવિનાશી અશ્વત્થ વૃક્ષ (સંસારના) ની વાત કરે છે, જેનાં મૂળ ઉપર છે અને શાખાઓ નીચે, અને જેનાં પાન વેદ-ઋચાઓ છે; જે આ વૃક્ષને ઓળખે છે, તે વેદ જાણનારો છે."},{"ref":"15.2","ch":15,"v":2,"sa":"अधश्चोर्ध्वं प्रसृतास्तस्य शाखा गुणप्रवृद्धा विषयप्रवालाः।अधश्च मूलान्यनुसन्ततानि कर्मानुबन्धीनि मनुष्यलोके।।15.2।।","tr":"adhaśh chordhvaṁ prasṛitās tasya śhākhā\nguṇa-pravṛiddhā viṣhaya-pravālāḥ\nadhaśh cha mūlāny anusantatāni\nkarmānubandhīni manuṣhya-loke","en":"Its branches spread below and above, nourished by the Gunas; its buds are sense-objects, and its roots stretch forth below in the world of men, originating action.","es":"The branches of that Tree, extending downwards and upwards, are strengthened by the qualities and have sense-objects as their shoots. And the roots, which are followed by actions, spread downwards in the human world [According to A.G. and M.S. manusya-loke means a body distinguished by Brahminhood etc.].","er":"(a) Its branches extend both above and below, nourished by the Gunas. Their shoots are sense objects. \n(b) And their secondary roots extend downwards, resulting in actions that bind in the world of humans.","gu":"તેની શાખાઓ ત્રણ ગુણો દ્વારા પોષિત થઈ નીચે અને ઉપર ફેલાયેલી છે, અને ઇન્દ્રિય-વિષયો તેની કળીઓ છે; તેનાં મૂળ મનુષ્ય-જગતમાં નીચે સુધી ફેલાઈ, કર્મ દ્વારા જીવોને બાંધે છે."},{"ref":"15.3","ch":15,"v":3,"sa":"न रूपमस्येह तथोपलभ्यते नान्तो न चादिर्न च संप्रतिष्ठा।अश्वत्थमेनं सुविरूढमूल मसङ्गशस्त्रेण दृढेन छित्त्वा।।15.3।।","tr":"na rūpam asyeha tathopalabhyate\nnānto na chādir na cha sampratiṣhṭhā\naśhvattham enaṁ su-virūḍha-mūlam\nasaṅga-śhastreṇa dṛiḍhena chhittvā","en":"Its form is not perceived here as such, nor its end, origin, foundation, or resting place; having cut asunder this firmly rooted peepul tree with the strong axe of non-attachment.","es":"Its form is not perceived here in that way; nor its end, nor beginning, nor its continuance. After felling this Peepul tree whose roots are well developed, with the strong sword of detachment.","er":"Its form is not perceived here, nor its end, nor its beginning, nor its support. Having cut off this firmly-rooted Asvattha with the strong axe of detachment.","gu":"આ સંસાર-વૃક્ષનું સ્વરૂપ અહીં પ્રત્યક્ષ જણાતું નથી — ન તો તેનો અંત, ન ઉત્પત્તિ, ન આધાર, ન વિશ્રામ-સ્થળ; અનાસક્તિ રૂપી તીક્ષ્ણ કુઠારથી આ દૃઢ-મૂળ અશ્વત્થ વૃક્ષને છેદીને —"},{"ref":"15.4","ch":15,"v":4,"sa":"ततः पदं तत्परिमार्गितव्य यस्मिन्गता न निवर्तन्ति भूयः।तमेव चाद्यं पुरुषं प्रपद्ये यतः प्रवृत्तिः प्रसृता पुराणी।।15.4।।","tr":"tataḥ padaṁ tat parimārgitavyaṁ\nyasmin gatā na nivartanti bhūyaḥ\ntam eva chādyaṁ puruṣhaṁ prapadye\nyataḥ pravṛittiḥ prasṛitā purāṇī","en":"Then, that goal should be sought for, to which, having gone, none returns again. I seek refuge in that Primeval Purusha, from whence streamed forth the ancient activity or energy.","es":"Thereafter, that state must be sought, going where they do not return again: I take refuge in that Primeval Person Himself, from whom the eternal Manifestation has ensued.","er":"Then, one should seek that goal, attaining which one never returns. One should seek refuge with that Primal Person from whom this ancient activity streamed forth.","gu":"— ત્યારે તે ધ્યેયને શોધવો જોઈએ, જ્યાં પહોંચ્યા પછી કોઈ પાછો ફરતો નથી; હું તે આદ્ય પુરુષની શરણ લઉ છું, જેમાંથી આ પ્રાચીન સૃષ્ટિ-પ્રવાહ ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે."},{"ref":"15.5","ch":15,"v":5,"sa":"निर्मानमोहा जितसङ्गदोषा अध्यात्मनित्या विनिवृत्तकामाः।द्वन्द्वैर्विमुक्ताः सुखदुःखसंज्ञै र्गच्छन्त्यमूढाः पदमव्ययं तत्।।15.5।।","tr":"nirmāna-mohā jita-saṅga-doṣhā\nadhyātma-nityā vinivṛitta-kāmāḥ\ndvandvair vimuktāḥ sukha-duḥkha-sanjñair\ngachchhanty amūḍhāḥ padam avyayaṁ tat","en":"Free from pride and delusion, victorious over the evil of attachment, dwelling constantly in the Self, their desires having completely turned away, freed from the pairs of opposites known as pleasure and pain, they, the undeluded, reach the eternal goal.","es":"The wise ones, free from pride and non-discrimination, who have conquered the evil of association [hatred and love arising from association with foes and friends], who are ever devoted to spirituality, completely free from desires, and free from the dualities of happiness and sorrow, reach that undecaying state.","er":"Without the delusion of perverse notions concerning the self, victorious over the evil of attachment, ever devoted to the Self, turned away from desires and liberated from dualities such as pleasure and pain, the undeluded go to that imperishable state.","gu":"અહંકાર અને ભ્રાંતિથી મુક્ત, આસક્તિ-રૂપ દોષ પર વિજય મેળવ્યો છે, સદા આત્મામાં સ્થિત, ઇચ્છાઓ શાંત થઈ ગઈ છે, સુખ-દુઃખ આદિ દ્વંદ્વોથી મુક્ત — આવા નિર્ભ્રાંત જ્ઞાની લોકો અવ્યયપદ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"15.6","ch":15,"v":6,"sa":"न तद्भासयते सूर्यो न शशाङ्को न पावकः।यद्गत्वा न निवर्तन्ते तद्धाम परमं मम।।15.6।।","tr":"na tad bhāsayate sūryo na śhaśhāṅko na pāvakaḥ\nyad gatvā na nivartante tad dhāma paramaṁ mama","en":"Neither does the sun illuminate there, nor the moon, nor the fire; having gone there, they do not return; that is My supreme abode.","es":"Neither the sun nor the moon nor fire illuminates That. That is My supreme Abode, to which they do not return.","er":"That supreme light, upon reaching which they do not return any more, is Mine; neither the sun nor the moon nor the fire illuminates It.","gu":"ત્યાં ન સૂર્ય પ્રકાશ આપે, ન ચંદ્ર, ન અગ્નિ; ત્યાં પહોંચ્યા પછી કોઈ પાછો ફરતો નથી — તે મારું પરમ ધામ છે."},{"ref":"15.7","ch":15,"v":7,"sa":"ममैवांशो जीवलोके जीवभूतः सनातनः।मनःषष्ठानीन्द्रियाणि प्रकृतिस्थानि कर्षति।।15.7।।","tr":"mamaivānśho jīva-loke jīva-bhūtaḥ sanātanaḥ\nmanaḥ-ṣhaṣhṭhānīndriyāṇi prakṛiti-sthāni karṣhati","en":"An eternal portion of Myself having become a living soul in the world of life, draws to itself the five senses, with the mind as the sixth, abiding in Nature.","es":"It is indeed a part of Mine that, becoming the eternal individual soul in the region of living beings, draws the organs, which have the mind as their sixth, and which abide in Nature.","er":"An everlasting part of Myself, having become the bound self in the world of life, attracts the senses, of which the mind is the sixth, and which abide in Prakriti.","gu":"આ જીવ-જગતમાં, જીવ-આત્મા મારો સનાતન અંશ છે; ચેતન-સ્વભાવમાં સ્થિત મન સહિત છ ઇન્દ્રિયોને તે ખેંચે છે."},{"ref":"15.8","ch":15,"v":8,"sa":"शरीरं यदवाप्नोति यच्चाप्युत्क्रामतीश्वरः।गृहीत्वैतानि संयाति वायुर्गन्धानिवाशयात्।।15.8।।","tr":"śharīraṁ yad avāpnoti yach chāpy utkrāmatīśhvaraḥ\ngṛihītvaitāni sanyāti vāyur gandhān ivāśhayāt","en":"When the Lord, as the individual soul, obtains a body and when He leaves it, He takes these with Him, just as the wind takes the scents from their seats (flowers, etc.).","es":"When the master leaves it and even when he assumes a body, he departs taking these with him, just as the wind carries away odours from their receptacles.","er":"Whatever body its lord acquires and from whatever body it departs, it goes on its way, taking these senses as the wind carries scents from their places.","gu":"જ્યારે ઈશ્વર (જીવ-રૂપે) શરીર ધારણ કરે અને જ્યારે છોડે, ત્યારે આ ઇન્દ્રિયોને પોતાની સાથે લઈ જાય છે — જેમ વાયુ ફૂલોમાંથી સુગંધ ઉઠાવી લઈ જાય."},{"ref":"15.9","ch":15,"v":9,"sa":"श्रोत्रं चक्षुः स्पर्शनं च रसनं घ्राणमेव च।अधिष्ठाय मनश्चायं विषयानुपसेवते।।15.9।।","tr":"śhrotraṁ chakṣhuḥ sparśhanaṁ cha rasanaṁ ghrāṇam eva cha\nadhiṣhṭhāya manaśh chāyaṁ viṣhayān upasevate","en":"Presiding over the ears, eyes, touch, taste, smell, and mind, it enjoys the objects of the senses.","es":"This one enjoys the objects by presiding over the ears, eyes, skin, tongue, nose, and mind.","er":"Presiding over the ear, the eye, the sense of touch, the tongue, the nose, and the mind, It experiences these objects of the senses.","gu":"કાન, આંખ, સ્પર્શ, રસ, ગંધ — અને મન — આ બધા ઉપર અધ્યક્ષ બની, તે ઇન્દ્રિય-વિષયોનો ઉપભોગ કરે છે."},{"ref":"15.10","ch":15,"v":10,"sa":"उत्क्रामन्तं स्थितं वापि भुञ्जानं वा गुणान्वितम्।विमूढा नानुपश्यन्ति पश्यन्ति ज्ञानचक्षुषः।।15.10।।","tr":"utkrāmantaṁ sthitaṁ vāpi bhuñjānaṁ vā guṇānvitam\nvimūḍhā nānupaśhyanti paśhyanti jñāna-chakṣhuṣhaḥ","en":"The deluded do not see Him who departs, stays, and enjoys; but those who possess the eye of knowledge behold Him.","es":"Persons who are diversely deluded do not see it even when it is leaving, residing, experiencing, or in association with the qualities; those with the eye of knowledge see.","er":"The deluded do not perceive it conjoined with the Gunas when departing, staying, or experiencing. Those who have the eye of knowledge, however, see it.","gu":"જ્ઞાન-ચક્ષુ વિહીન મૂઢ જન, જે આ ઈશ્વર-ચૈતન્ય શરીર છોડે છે, ટકે છે, અને ભોગ અનુભવે છે — તેને જોઈ શકતા નથી; પરંતુ જ્ઞાનની આંખ ધરાવનાર સ્પષ્ટ જોઈ શકે છે."},{"ref":"15.11","ch":15,"v":11,"sa":"यतन्तो योगिनश्चैनं पश्यन्त्यात्मन्यवस्थितम्।यतन्तोऽप्यकृतात्मानो नैनं पश्यन्त्यचेतसः।।15.11।।","tr":"yatanto yoginaśh chainaṁ paśhyanty ātmany avasthitam\nyatanto ‘py akṛitātmāno nainaṁ paśhyanty achetasaḥ","en":"The yogis striving for perfection behold Him dwelling in the Self; but, the unrefined and unintelligent, even though striving, do not see Him.","es":"And the diligent yogis see this one existing within themselves. The non-discriminating ones who lack self-control, however, do not see this one, even though they are diligent.","er":"The striving yogis perceive it established in themselves. But, though striving, those of unrefined minds, devoid of intelligence, do not perceive it.","gu":"સ્વ-સાક્ષાત્કાર માટે પ્રયત્ન કરનારા યોગીઓ, આત્મામાં સ્થિત આ ઈશ્વર-ચૈતન્યને દેખે છે; પરંતુ જેઓ અજ્ઞાની છે અને જેમનો આત્મા અસ્ફુટ છે, તેઓ પ્રયત્ન કરવા છતાં તેને જોઈ શકતા નથી."},{"ref":"15.12","ch":15,"v":12,"sa":"यदादित्यगतं तेजो जगद्भासयतेऽखिलम्।यच्चन्द्रमसि यच्चाग्नौ तत्तेजो विद्धि मामकम्।।15.12।।","tr":"yad āditya-gataṁ tejo jagad bhāsayate ’khilam\nyach chandramasi yach chāgnau tat tejo viddhi māmakam","en":"That light which resides in the sun, illuminating the whole world; that which is in the moon and in the fire—know that light to be Mine.","es":"That light in the sun which illuminates the whole world, that which is in the moon, and that which is in fire—know that light to be Mine.","er":"Know that the brilliance which illumines the whole universe in the sun, the moon, and fire is Mine.","gu":"સૂર્યમાં જે પ્રકાશ સમગ્ર જગતને પ્રકાશિત કરે છે, ચંદ્રમાં અને અગ્નિમાં જે તેજ છે — તે સઘળું તેજ મારું જ છે, એમ જાણ."},{"ref":"15.13","ch":15,"v":13,"sa":"गामाविश्य च भूतानि धारयाम्यहमोजसा।पुष्णामि चौषधीः सर्वाः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः।।15.13।।","tr":"gām āviśhya cha bhūtāni dhārayāmy aham ojasā\npuṣhṇāmi chauṣhadhīḥ sarvāḥ somo bhūtvā rasātmakaḥ","en":"Permeating the earth, I support all beings with My energy; and having become the watery moon, I nourish all herbs.","es":"And entering the Earth, I sustain the beings through My power; and nourish all the plants by becoming Soma, which is of the nature of sap.","er":"And, entering the earth, I uphold all beings with My strength. I nourish all herbs, becoming the juicy Soma.","gu":"હું પૃથ્વીમાં પ્રવેશ કરીને મારી શક્તિ વડે સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓને ધારણ કરું છું, અને રસ-સ્વરૂપ ચંદ્ર બનીને સઘળી વનસ્પતિઓનું પોષણ કરું છું."},{"ref":"15.14","ch":15,"v":14,"sa":"अहं वैश्वानरो भूत्वा प्राणिनां देहमाश्रितः।प्राणापानसमायुक्तः पचाम्यन्नं चतुर्विधम्।।15.14।।","tr":"ahaṁ vaiśhvānaro bhūtvā prāṇināṁ deham āśhritaḥ\nprāṇāpāna-samāyuktaḥ pachāmy annaṁ chatur-vidham","en":"Having become the fire Vaisvanara, I abide in the bodies of living beings and, associated with the Prana and the Apana, digest the fourfold food.","es":"Taking the form of Vaisvanara, and residing in the bodies of creatures, I, in association with Prana and Apana, digest the four kinds of food.","er":"Becoming the digestive fire, I function within the bodies of all living beings. In union with the inward and outward breath, I digest the four kinds of food.","gu":"હું જઠરાગ્નિ વૈશ્વાનરરૂપ બનીને પ્રાણીઓના શરીરમાં રહું છું, અને પ્રાણ-અપાન સહિત ચારે પ્રકારના અન્નનું પાચન કરું છું."},{"ref":"15.15","ch":15,"v":15,"sa":"सर्वस्य चाहं हृदि सन्निविष्टो मत्तः स्मृतिर्ज्ञानमपोहनं च।वेदैश्च सर्वैरहमेव वेद्यो वेदान्तकृद्वेदविदेव चाहम्।।15.15।।","tr":"sarvasya chāhaṁ hṛidi sanniviṣhṭo\nmattaḥ smṛitir jñānam apohanaṁ cha\nvedaiśh cha sarvair aham eva vedyo\nvedānta-kṛid veda-vid eva chāham","en":"And I am seated in the hearts of all; from Me come memory and knowledge, as well as their absence. I am verily That which has to be known by all the Vedas; I am indeed the author of the Vedanta and the knower of the Vedas.","es":"And I am seated in the hearts of all. From Me come memory, knowledge, and their loss. I alone am the object to be known through all the Vedas; I am also the originator of the Vedanta, and I Myself am the knower of the Vedas.","er":"And I am seated in the hearts of all. From Me come memory, knowledge, and their removal too. Indeed, I alone am to be known from all the Vedas. I bring about the fruition of the Vedic rituals; I alone am the knower of the Vedas.","gu":"હું સૌના હૃદયમાં બિરાજેલો છું; મારી પાસેથી જ સ્મૃતિ, જ્ઞાન અને વિસ્મૃતિ (ભૂલ) ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે. સઘળા વેદો વડે જાણવા યોગ્ય હું જ છું, વેદાન્તનો કર્તા અને વેદોનો જ્ઞાતા પણ હું જ છું."},{"ref":"15.16","ch":15,"v":16,"sa":"द्वाविमौ पुरुषौ लोके क्षरश्चाक्षर एव च।क्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि कूटस्थोऽक्षर उच्यते।।15.16।।","tr":"dvāv imau puruṣhau loke kṣharaśh chākṣhara eva cha\nkṣharaḥ sarvāṇi bhūtāni kūṭa-stho ’kṣhara uchyate","en":"Two Purushas there are in this world: the perishable and the imperishable. All beings are perishable, and the Kutastha—the unchanging—is called the imperishable.","es":"There are two kinds of people in the world: the mutable and the immutable. The mutable consists of all things; the one existing as Maya is referred to as the immutable.","er":"There are two kinds of persons spoken of in the sastra: the perishable (ksara) and the imperishable (aksara). All beings are perishable, while the imperishable is called the unchanging (kutastha).","gu":"આ જગતમાં બે પ્રકારના પુરુષ છે — ક્ષર (નાશવંત) અને અક્ષર (અવિનાશી). સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓ ક્ષર છે, અને જે કૂટસ્થ-અચળ છે તેને અક્ષર કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"15.17","ch":15,"v":17,"sa":"उत्तमः पुरुषस्त्वन्यः परमात्मेत्युदाहृतः।यो लोकत्रयमाविश्य बिभर्त्यव्यय ईश्वरः।।15.17।।","tr":"uttamaḥ puruṣhas tv anyaḥ paramātmety udāhṛitaḥ\nyo loka-trayam āviśhya bibharty avyaya īśhvaraḥ","en":"But distinct is the Supreme Purusha, called the highest Self, indestructible and Lord, who pervades the three worlds and sustains them.","es":"But the Supreme Person is different; He is spoken of as the transcendental Self, permeating the three worlds and upholding them, and He is the imperishable God.","er":"There is a Supreme Person other than these. He is referred to as the Supreme Self (Paramatma) in all the Vedas. He, as the Immutable One and the Lord, enters the threefold world and supports it.","gu":"પરંતુ ઉભય (ક્ષર-અક્ષર)થી ઉત્તમ અન્ય પુરુષ છે — પરમ આત્મા — જે ત્રણે લોકમાં પ્રવેશી સૌને ધારણ કરનારો અવિનાશી ઈશ્વર છે."},{"ref":"15.18","ch":15,"v":18,"sa":"यस्मात्क्षरमतीतोऽहमक्षरादपि चोत्तमः।अतोऽस्मि लोके वेदे च प्रथितः पुरुषोत्तमः।।15.18।।","tr":"yasmāt kṣharam atīto ’ham akṣharād api chottamaḥ\nato ’smi loke vede cha prathitaḥ puruṣhottamaḥ","en":"As I transcend the perishable and am even higher than the imperishable, I am declared to be the highest Purusha in the world and in the Vedas.","es":"Since I am transcendental to the mutable and above even the immutable, therefore I am well known in the world and in the Vedas as the supreme Person.","er":"Because I transcend the perishable person and am also higher than the imperishable one, therefore I am referred to in the Smrti and the Veda as the Supreme Person (Purusotama).","gu":"કારણ કે હું ક્ષરથી પર છું અને અક્ષરથી પણ ઉત્તમ છું, તેથી લોકમાં અને વેદોમાં પુરુષોત્તમ તરીકે ઓળખાઉં છું."},{"ref":"15.19","ch":15,"v":19,"sa":"यो मामेवमसम्मूढो जानाति पुरुषोत्तमम्।स सर्वविद्भजति मां सर्वभावेन भारत।।15.19।।","tr":"yo mām evam asammūḍho jānāti puruṣhottamam\nsa sarva-vid bhajati māṁ sarva-bhāvena bhārata","en":"He who, undeluded, knows Me as the highest Purusha, he, knowing all, worships Me with his whole being (heart), O Arjuna.","es":"O scion of the Bharata dynasty, he who, being free from delusion, knows Me, the supreme Person, thus, is all-knowing and adores Me with his whole being.","er":"He who, without delusion, thus knows Me as the Supreme Self, knows all, O Arjuna, and worships Me in every way.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે અજ્ઞાન-રહિત પુરુષ મને આ પ્રમાણે પુરુષોત્તમ તરીકે ઓળખે છે, તે સર્વજ્ઞ બની સઘળા ભાવ-ભક્તિ સાથે મને ભજે છે."},{"ref":"15.20","ch":15,"v":20,"sa":"इति गुह्यतमं शास्त्रमिदमुक्तं मयाऽनघ।एतद्बुद्ध्वा बुद्धिमान्स्यात्कृतकृत्यश्च भारत।।15.20।।","tr":"iti guhyatamaṁ śhāstram idam uktaṁ mayānagha\netad buddhvā buddhimān syāt kṛita-kṛityaśh cha bhārata","en":"Thus, I have imparted to you this most secret science, O sinless one; by knowing this, one becomes wise, and all their duties are accomplished, O Arjuna.","es":"O sinless one, I have thus uttered this most secret scripture. Understanding this, one becomes wise and fulfills their duties, O scion of the Bharata dynasty.","er":"Thus, O sinless one, this most mysterious doctrine has been imparted by Me. By understanding this, one will become truly wise and fulfill their duty.","gu":"હે નિષ્પાપ અર્જુન, આ અત્યંત ગુહ્ય શાસ્ત્ર મેં તને કહ્યું; આ જ્ઞાન ધારણ કરવાથી માણસ જ્ઞાન-સ્વરૂપ બને છે અને તેનાં સઘળાં કર્તવ્ય સિદ્ધ થઈ જાય છે, હે ભારત."},{"ref":"16.1","ch":16,"v":1,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nअभयं सत्त्वसंशुद्धिः ज्ञानयोगव्यवस्थितिः।\nदानं दमश्च यज्ञश्च स्वाध्यायस्तप आर्जवम्।।16.1।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nabhayaṁ sattva-sanśhuddhir jñāna-yoga-vyavasthitiḥ\ndānaṁ damaśh cha yajñaśh cha svādhyāyas tapa ārjavam","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Fearlessness, purity of heart, steadfastness in knowledge and yoga, almsgiving, control of the senses, sacrifice, study of scriptures, austerity, and straightforwardness.","es":"The Blessed Lord said: Fearlessness, purity of mind, persistence in knowledge and yoga, charity, control of the external organs, sacrifice, scriptural study, austerity, and rectitude.","er":"The Lord said, \"Fearlessness, purity of mind, devotion to meditation on the knowledge of the self, alms-giving, self-control, worship, study of the Vedas, austerity, and uprightness—","gu":"શ્રી કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: અભય, અંતઃકરણની શુદ્ધિ, જ્ઞાન-યોગ-વ્યવસ્થામાં દૃઢ નિષ્ઠા, દાન, ઇન્દ્રિય-સંયમ, યજ્ઞ, સ્વાધ્યયાય, તપ અને સરળતા —"},{"ref":"16.2","ch":16,"v":2,"sa":"अहिंसा सत्यमक्रोधस्त्यागः शान्तिरपैशुनम्।दया भूतेष्वलोलुप्त्वं मार्दवं ह्रीरचापलम्।।16.2।।","tr":"ahinsā satyam akrodhas tyāgaḥ śhāntir apaiśhunam\ndayā bhūteṣhv aloluptvaṁ mārdavaṁ hrīr achāpalam","en":"Harmlessness, truth, absence of anger, renunciation, peacefulness, absence of crookedness, compassion for beings, non-covetousness, gentleness, modesty, and absence of fickleness.","es":"Non-injury, truthfulness, absence of anger, renunciation, control of the inner self, absence of vilification, kindness to creatures, non-covetousness, gentleness, modesty, and freedom from restlessness;","er":"Non-injury, truth, freedom from anger, renunciation, tranquility, non-slandering of others, compassion for all beings, freedom from desire, gentleness, a sense of shame, and freedom from fickleness;","gu":"અહિંસા, સત્ય, ક્રોધ-ત્યાગ, વૈરાગ્ય, શાંતિ, નિંદા ન કરવી, સઘળાં પ્રાણીઓ પ્રત્યે દયા, લોભ-રાહિત્ય, કોમળતા, લજ્જા અને ચપળતાનો અભાવ —"},{"ref":"16.3","ch":16,"v":3,"sa":"तेजः क्षमा धृतिः शौचमद्रोहो नातिमानिता।\nभवन्ति सम्पदं दैवीमभिजातस्य भारत।।16.3।।","tr":"tejaḥ kṣhamā dhṛitiḥ śhaucham adroho nāti-mānitā\nbhavanti sampadaṁ daivīm abhijātasya bhārata","en":"Vigor, forgiveness, fortitude, purity, absence of hatred, absence of pride—these belong to one born for a divine state, O Arjuna.","es":"Vigour, forgiveness, fortitude, purity, freedom from malice, absence of haughtiness—these, O scion of the Bharata dynasty, are the qualities of one born destined to have the divine nature.","er":"Grandeur, patience, fortitude, purity, freedom from hatred and over-pride—these, O Arjuna, belong to one who is born to a divine destiny.","gu":"તેજ, ક્ષમા, ધૈર્ય, પવિત્રતા, દ્વેષ-રાહિત્ય અને અભિમાનનો અભાવ — આ ગુણો, હે અર્જુન, દૈવી સ્વભાવ સાથે જન્મેલા પુરુષનાં છે."},{"ref":"16.4","ch":16,"v":4,"sa":"दम्भो दर्पोऽभिमानश्च क्रोधः पारुष्यमेव च।अज्ञानं चाभिजातस्य पार्थ सम्पदमासुरीम्।।16.4।।","tr":"dambho darpo ’bhimānaśh cha krodhaḥ pāruṣhyam eva cha\najñānaṁ chābhijātasya pārtha sampadam āsurīm","en":"Hypocrisy, arrogance, and self-conceit, anger, harshness, and ignorance—these belong to one who is born for a demoniacal state, O Partha.","es":"O son of Prtha, the attributes of one destined to have the demoniacal nature are religious ostentation, pride, haughtiness, self-conceit, anger, rudeness, and ignorance.","er":"Pompousness, arrogance, self-conceit, wrath, rudeness, and ignorance—these, O Arjuna, belong to one who is born with a demonic destiny.","gu":"દંભ, ઘમંડ, અભિમાન, ક્રોધ, કઠોરતા અને અજ્ઞાન — આ, હે અર્જુન, આસુરી સ્વભાવ સાથે જન્મેલા પુરુષનાં લક્ષણો છે."},{"ref":"16.5","ch":16,"v":5,"sa":"दैवी सम्पद्विमोक्षाय निबन्धायासुरी मता।मा शुचः सम्पदं दैवीमभिजातोऽसि पाण्डव।।16.5।।","tr":"daivī sampad vimokṣhāya nibandhāyāsurī matā\nmā śhuchaḥ sampadaṁ daivīm abhijāto ’si pāṇḍava","en":"The divine nature is deemed conducive to liberation, and the demonic to bondage. Grieve not, O Arjuna, for you are born with divine endowments.","es":"The divine nature is Liberation, while the demoniacal is considered to be an inevitable bondage. Do not grieve, O son of Pandu! You are destined to possess the divine nature.","er":"The divine destiny is said to lead to liberation, while the demoniac to bondage. Do not grieve, O Arjuna, for you are born with a divine destiny.","gu":"દૈવી સ્વભાવ મોક્ષ તરફ લઈ જાય છે અને આસુરી સ્વભાવ બંધનમાં નાખે છે; હે અર્જુન, શોક ન કર — તું દૈવી સ્વભાવ સાથે જ જન્મ્યો છે."},{"ref":"16.6","ch":16,"v":6,"sa":"द्वौ भूतसर्गौ लोकेऽस्मिन् दैव आसुर एव च।दैवो विस्तरशः प्रोक्त आसुरं पार्थ मे श्रृणु।।16.6।।","tr":"dvau bhūta-sargau loke ’smin daiva āsura eva cha\ndaivo vistaraśhaḥ prokta āsuraṁ pārtha me śhṛiṇu","en":"There are two types of beings in this world: the divine and the demoniacal. The divine has been described at length; hear from Me, O Arjuna, about the demoniacal.","es":"In this world, there are two kinds of creation of beings: the divine and the demoniacal. The divine has been spoken of elaborately. Hear about the demoniacal from Me, O son of Prtha.","er":"There are two types of beings in this world: the divine and the demoniac. The divine have been described at length. Hear from Me, O Arjuna, about the demoniac.","gu":"આ સૃષ્ટિમાં બે પ્રકારનાં પ્રાણીઓ છે — દૈવ-સ્વભાવી અને આસુર-સ્વભાવી. દૈવ-સ્વભાવ વિસ્તારથી કહ્યો; હવે, હે અર્જુન, આસુર-સ્વભાવ વિષે મારી પાસેથી સાંભળ."},{"ref":"16.7","ch":16,"v":7,"sa":"प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च जना न विदुरासुराः।न शौचं नापि चाचारो न सत्यं तेषु विद्यते।।16.7।।","tr":"pravṛittiṁ cha nivṛittiṁ cha janā na vidur āsurāḥ\nna śhauchaṁ nāpi chāchāro na satyaṁ teṣhu vidyate","en":"The demoniacal do not know what to do and what to refrain from; they have neither purity, nor right conduct, nor truth.","es":"Neither do the demoniacal persons understand what should be done and what should not be done; nor do they possess purity, good conduct, or truthfulness.","er":"The demoniacal men neither know action nor renunciation. They have no cleanliness, nor right conduct, nor truth.","gu":"આસુરી સ્વભાવવાળા મનુષ્યો શું કરવું અને શું ન કરવું તે જાણતા નથી; તેમનામાં ન તો પવિત્રતા છે, ન સદાચાર, ન સત્ય."},{"ref":"16.8","ch":16,"v":8,"sa":"असत्यमप्रतिष्ठं ते जगदाहुरनीश्वरम्।अपरस्परसम्भूतं किमन्यत्कामहैतुकम्।।16.8।।","tr":"asatyam apratiṣhṭhaṁ te jagad āhur anīśhvaram\naparaspara-sambhūtaṁ kim anyat kāma-haitukam","en":"They say, \"This universe is without truth, without a moral basis, without a God, brought about by mutual union, with lust as its cause; what else?\"","es":"They say that the world is unreal, having no basis, and without a God. It is born of mutual union brought about by passion! What other cause could there be?","er":"They maintain: 'The universe is without truth, with no foundation, and without a Lord (Isvara). What else could exist without mutual causation? It has lust as its cause.'","gu":"તેઓ કહે છે: 'આ જગત સત્ય વિનાનું, નૈતિક આધાર વિનાનું અને ઈશ્વર વિનાનું છે; કેવળ કામવાસના ભેગા મળવાથી ઉત્પન્ન થયું છે — બીજું શું?' "},{"ref":"16.9","ch":16,"v":9,"sa":"एतां दृष्टिमवष्टभ्य नष्टात्मानोऽल्पबुद्धयः।प्रभवन्त्युग्रकर्माणः क्षयाय जगतोऽहिताः।।16.9।।","tr":"etāṁ dṛiṣhṭim avaṣhṭabhya naṣhṭātmāno ’lpa-buddhayaḥ\nprabhavanty ugra-karmāṇaḥ kṣhayāya jagato ’hitāḥ","en":"Holding this view, these ruined souls of small intellect and fierce deeds come forth as enemies of the world, intent on its destruction.","es":"Holding onto this view, those of depraved character, poor intellect, and given to fearful and harmful actions, wax strong and bring ruin to the world.","er":"Holding this view, these men of lost souls and feeble understanding do cruel deeds, leading to the destruction of the world.","gu":"આ દૃષ્ટિ રાખીને, ઓછી બુદ્ધિ અને ઘોર કર્મોવાળા આ નષ્ટ આત્માઓ જગતના વિનાશ માટે તેના શત્રુ બનીને ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે."},{"ref":"16.10","ch":16,"v":10,"sa":"काममाश्रित्य दुष्पूरं दम्भमानमदान्विताः।मोहाद्गृहीत्वासद्ग्राहान्प्रवर्तन्तेऽशुचिव्रताः।।16.10।।","tr":"kāmam āśhritya duṣhpūraṁ dambha-māna-madānvitāḥ\nmohād gṛihītvāsad-grāhān pravartante ’śhuchi-vratāḥ","en":"Filled with insatiable desires, full of hypocrisy, pride, and arrogance, holding evil ideas due to delusion, they work with impure intentions.","es":"Giving themselves up to insatiable passion, filled with vanity, pride, and arrogance, adopting bad adjectives due to delusion, and having impure resolves, they engage in actions.","er":"Turning to insatiable desires, seizing through delusion unjustly acquired wealth, and following impious vows, they act, full of ostentation, pride, and arrogance.","gu":"અતૃપ્ત કામનાઓથી ભરેલા, દંભ, અહંકાર અને મદથી ભ્રષ્ટ, મોહ વડે ખોટા વિચારો ધારણ કરીને, અશુદ્ધ સંકલ્પો સાથે તેઓ કાર્ય કરે છે."},{"ref":"16.11","ch":16,"v":11,"sa":"चिन्तामपरिमेयां च प्रलयान्तामुपाश्रिताः।कामोपभोगपरमा एतावदिति निश्िचताः।।16.11।।","tr":"chintām aparimeyāṁ cha pralayāntām upāśhritāḥ\nkāmopabhoga-paramā etāvad iti niśhchitāḥ","en":"Giving themselves over to immeasurable cares that end only with death, regarding the gratification of lust as their highest aim, and feeling sure that that is all.","es":"Beset with innumerable cares that end only with death, holding that the enjoyment of desirable objects is the highest goal, they feel sure that this is all.","er":"Obsessed by unlimited cares that end with dissolution, looking upon the enjoyment of desires as their highest aim, and convinced that this is all;","gu":"મૃત્યુ સુધી જ ખૂટે એવી અસંખ્ય ચિંતાઓમાં ડૂબેલા, ભોગ-વિલાસને જ સર્વોચ્ચ ધ્યેય માનનારા, 'આ જ સત્ય છે' એવો દૃઢ વિશ્વાસ ધરાવનારા —"},{"ref":"16.12","ch":16,"v":12,"sa":"आशापाशशतैर्बद्धाः कामक्रोधपरायणाः।ईहन्ते कामभोगार्थमन्यायेनार्थसञ्चयान्।।16.12।।","tr":"āśhā-pāśha-śhatair baddhāḥ kāma-krodha-parāyaṇāḥ\nīhante kāma-bhogārtham anyāyenārtha-sañchayān","en":"Bound by a hundred ties of hope, given over to lust and anger, they strive to obtain hoards of wealth by unlawful means for sensual enjoyment.","es":"Bound by hundreds of shackles in the form of hope, giving themselves wholly to passion and anger, they endeavor to amass wealth through foul means for the enjoyment of desirable objects.","er":"Bound by hundreds of fetters of hopes, given over to desire and anger, they strive unjustly to gather wealth for the gratification of their desires.","gu":"આશાની સો-સો ગ્રંથિઓથી બંધાઈ, કામ અને ક્રોધમાં ડૂબી, ઇન્દ્રિય-ભોગ માટે અન્યાયયુક્ત ઉપાયો વડે ધન-સંગ્રહ કરવા માટે પ્રયત્ન કરે છે."},{"ref":"16.13","ch":16,"v":13,"sa":"इदमद्य मया लब्धमिमं प्राप्स्ये मनोरथम्।इदमस्तीदमपि मे भविष्यति पुनर्धनम्।।16.13।।","tr":"idam adya mayā labdham imaṁ prāpsye manoratham\nidam astīdam api me bhaviṣhyati punar dhanam","en":"\"I have gained this today; I will fulfill this desire of mine; this is mine, and this wealth will be mine in the future.\"","es":"'I have gained this today; I will acquire this desired object. This is in hand; and this wealth will also come to me.'","er":"'This I have gained today, and this desire I shall attain. This wealth is mine, and this will also be mine hereafter.","gu":"'આ આજે મળ્યું; હવે આ ઇચ્છા પૂર્ણ કરીશ; આ મારું છે અને ભવિષ્યમાં આ ધન પણ મારું જ થશે' — એવો ભ્રમ તેઓ રાખે છે."},{"ref":"16.14","ch":16,"v":14,"sa":"असौ मया हतः शत्रुर्हनिष्ये चापरानपि।ईश्वरोऽहमहं भोगी सिद्धोऽहं बलवान्सुखी।।16.14।।","tr":"asau mayā hataḥ śhatrur haniṣhye chāparān api\nīśhvaro ’ham ahaṁ bhogī siddho ’haṁ balavān sukhī","en":"\"I have slain that enemy, and I shall slay others too. I am the Lord; I enjoy, I am perfect, powerful, and happy.\"","es":"'I have slain that enemy, and I shall slay others too. I am the Lord, the Enjoyer, firmly established, powerful and joyous.'","er":"'I have slain this enemy, and I shall slay others too. I am the Lord, the enjoyer, the successful one, the strong one, and the happy one.'","gu":"'મેં તે શત્રુને માર્યો, હવે બીજાઓને પણ મારીશ; હું ઈશ્વર છું, ભોક્તા છું, સિદ્ધ, બળવાન અને સુખી છું' — એમ અભિમાન સાથે બોલે છે."},{"ref":"16.15","ch":16,"v":15,"sa":"आढ्योऽभिजनवानस्मि कोऽन्योऽस्ति सदृशो मया।यक्ष्ये दास्यामि मोदिष्य इत्यज्ञानविमोहिताः।।16.15।।","tr":"āḍhyo ’bhijanavān asmi ko ’nyo ’sti sadṛiśho mayā\nyakṣhye dāsyāmi modiṣhya ity ajñāna-vimohitāḥ\n aneka-chitta-vibhrāntā moha-jāla-samāvṛitāḥ\nprasaktāḥ kāma-bhogeṣhu patanti narake ’śhuchau","en":"\"I am wealthy and born into a noble family. Who is my equal? I shall perform sacrifices, give charity, and rejoice,\" thus deluded by ignorance.","es":"'I am wealthy and of noble birth; who else is like me? I shall perform sacrifices; I shall give, I shall rejoice'- thus, they are deluded by a lack of discernment in diverse ways.","er":"'I am wealthy and high-born; who else is equal to me? I shall sacrifice, I shall give alms, I shall rejoice.' Thus they think, deluded by ignorance.","gu":"'હું ધનવાન છું, ઉચ્ચ કુળમાં જન્મ્યો છું; મારા જેવો કોણ? હું યજ્ઞ કરીશ, દાન આપીશ, આનંદ ભોગવીશ' — અજ્ઞાનથી ભ્રષ્ટ થઈ આ પ્રમાણે તેઓ વિચારે છે."},{"ref":"16.16","ch":16,"v":16,"sa":"अनेकचित्तविभ्रान्ता मोहजालसमावृताः।प्रसक्ताः कामभोगेषु पतन्ति नरकेऽशुचौ।।16.16।।","tr":"aneka-citta-vibhrāntā moha-jāla-samāvṛtāḥ prasaktāḥ kāma-bhogeṣu patanti narake 'śucau","en":"Bewildered by many fancies, entangled in the snare of delusion, addicted to the gratification of lust, they fall into a foul hell.","es":"Bewildered by numerous thoughts, ensnared in the net of delusion, and engrossed in the enjoyment of desirable objects, they fall into a foul hell.","er":"Bewildered by numerous thoughts, ensnared in the net of delusion, addicted to sensual pleasures, they fall into a wretched Naraka.","gu":"અનેક સ્વૈચ્છિક ભ્રાંતિઓ વડે મૂંઝાયેલા, મોહના ફાંદામાં ફસાયેલા, ઇન્દ્રિય-સુખ પ્રત્યે આસક્ત — આ મનુષ્યો અઘોર નર્કમાં પડે છે."},{"ref":"16.17","ch":16,"v":17,"sa":"आत्मसम्भाविताः स्तब्धा धनमानमदान्विताः।यजन्ते नामयज्ञैस्ते दम्भेनाविधिपूर्वकम्।।16.17।।","tr":"ātma-sambhāvitāḥ stabdhā dhana-māna-madānvitāḥ\nyajante nāma-yajñais te dambhenāvidhi-pūrvakam","en":"Self-conceited, stubborn, filled with pride and intoxication of wealth, they perform sacrifices in name only for ostentation, contrary to scriptural ordinances.","es":"Self-conceited, haughty, filled with pride and intoxicated by wealth, they perform sacrifices that are only in name, ostentatiously and without regard for the injunctions.","er":"Self-conceited, self-sufficient, intoxicated by wealth and pride, they perform sacrifices in name only, ostentatiously and not according to the injunctions of the scriptures.","gu":"આત્મ-ગૌરવમાં ડૂબેલા, હઠીલા, ધન-મદ અને ઘમંડથી ભરેલા, તેઓ શાસ્ત્ર-વિધિ વિના, માત્ર દેખાવ ખાતર નામ-માત્ર યજ્ઞ કરે છે."},{"ref":"16.18","ch":16,"v":18,"sa":"अहङ्कारं बलं दर्पं कामं क्रोधं च संश्रिताः।मामात्मपरदेहेषु प्रद्विषन्तोऽभ्यसूयकाः।।16.18।।","tr":"ahankāraṁ balaṁ darpaṁ kāmaṁ krodhaṁ cha sanśhritāḥ\nmām ātma-para-deheṣhu pradviṣhanto ’bhyasūyakāḥ","en":"Given over to egoism, power, haughtiness, lust, and anger, these malicious people hate Me in their own bodies and in the bodies of others.","es":"Resorting to egotism, power, arrogance, passion, and anger, hating Me in their own and others' bodies, they become envious by nature.","er":"Depending on their egoism, power, and pride, as well as their desires and wrath, these malicious men hate Me in their own bodies and in those of others.","gu":"અહંકાર, બળ, ઘમંડ, કામ અને ક્રોધ પ્રત્યે આસક્ત આ દ્વેષી મનુષ્યો પોતાના અને અન્ય લોકોના દેહમાં રહેલા મારી સાથે ઘૃણા રાખે છે."},{"ref":"16.19","ch":16,"v":19,"sa":"तानहं द्विषतः क्रूरान्संसारेषु नराधमान्।क्षिपाम्यजस्रमशुभानासुरीष्वेव योनिषु।।16.19।।","tr":"tān ahaṁ dviṣhataḥ krūrān sansāreṣhu narādhamān\nkṣhipāmy ajasram aśhubhān āsurīṣhv eva yoniṣhu","en":"Those cruel haters, the worst among men in the world, I hurl those evil-doers into the wombs of demons only.","es":"I cast forever those hateful, cruel, evil-doers in the worlds, the vilest of human beings, verily into the demonic classes.","er":"Those who are hateful, cruel, the vilest and most inauspicious of mankind, I hurl forever into the cycles of births and deaths, into the wombs of demons.","gu":"તે ક્રૂર, ઘૃણ્ય, મનુષ્યોમાં અધમ — આ પાપ-કર્મીઓને હું વારંવાર આસુરી યોનિઓમાં ફેંક્યા કરું છું."},{"ref":"16.20","ch":16,"v":20,"sa":"असुरीं योनिमापन्ना मूढा जन्मनि जन्मनि।मामप्राप्यैव कौन्तेय ततो यान्त्यधमां गतिम्।।16.20।।","tr":"āsurīṁ yonim āpannā mūḍhā janmani janmani\nmām aprāpyaiva kaunteya tato yānty adhamāṁ gatim","en":"Entering into demoniacal wombs and deluded, birth after birth, they do not attain Me, thus falling, O Arjuna, into a condition still lower than that.","es":"Being born among the demoniacal species in birth after birth, the souls, without ever reaching Me, O son of Kunti, attain conditions lower than that.","er":"Fallen into demoniac wombs in birth after birth, these deluded men, not attaining Me, further sink down to the lowest level, O Arjuna.","gu":"આસુરી યોનિઓ પ્રાપ્ત કરીને, ભ્રમ-ગ્રસ્ત, જન્મ-જન્મ ભટકીને, મને ન પ્રાપ્ત કરી શકતાં, હે અર્જુન, તેઓ અત્યંત અધઃ ગતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"16.21","ch":16,"v":21,"sa":"त्रिविधं नरकस्येदं द्वारं नाशनमात्मनः।कामः क्रोधस्तथा लोभस्तस्मादेतत्त्रयं त्यजेत्।।16.21।।","tr":"tri-vidhaṁ narakasyedaṁ dvāraṁ nāśhanam ātmanaḥ\nkāmaḥ krodhas tathā lobhas tasmād etat trayaṁ tyajet","en":"There are three gates to this hell, destructive of the self: lust, anger, and greed; therefore, one should abandon these three.","es":"This door to hell, which destroys the soul, is of three kinds—passion, anger, and greed. Therefore, one should forsake these three.","er":"Desire, wrath, and greed—these are the three gateways to Naraka, ruinous to the self. Therefore, one should abandon these three."},{"ref":"16.22","ch":16,"v":22,"sa":"एतैर्विमुक्तः कौन्तेय तमोद्वारैस्त्रिभिर्नरः।आचरत्यात्मनः श्रेयस्ततो याति परां गतिम्।।16.22।।","tr":"etair vimuktaḥ kaunteya tamo-dvārais tribhir naraḥ\nācharaty ātmanaḥ śhreyas tato yāti parāṁ gatim","en":"A person who is liberated from these three gates of darkness, O Arjuna, practices what is beneficial for them and thus goes to the Supreme Goal.","es":"O son of Kunti, a person who is free from these three doors to darkness strives for the good of the soul; thereby, they attain the highest Goal.","er":"One who has been released from these three gates of darkness, O Arjuna, works for the benefit of the self; thus, they reach the supreme state.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે મનુષ્ય આ ત્રણ નર્ક-દ્વારોથી મુક્ત થાય છે, તે આત્માના કલ્યાણ માટે ઉચિત આચરણ કરી પરમ ગતિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"16.23","ch":16,"v":23,"sa":"यः शास्त्रविधिमुत्सृज्य वर्तते कामकारतः।न स सिद्धिमवाप्नोति न सुखं न परां गतिम्।।16.23।।","tr":"yaḥ śhāstra-vidhim utsṛijya vartate kāma-kārataḥ\nna sa siddhim avāpnoti na sukhaṁ na parāṁ gatim","en":"He who, having cast aside the ordinances of the scriptures, acts under the impulse of desire, does not attain perfection, nor happiness, nor the Supreme Goal.","es":"Ignoring the precepts of the scriptures, he who acts under the impulse of passion does not attain perfection, nor happiness, nor the supreme goal.","er":"He who, abandoning the injunctions of the Sastras, acts under the influence of desire, attains neither perfection nor pleasure, nor the supreme state.","gu":"જે મનુષ્ય શાસ્ત્રવિધિને છોડીને ઇચ્છાના આવેગથી કાર્ય કરે છે, તેને સિદ્ધિ મળતી નથી, સુખ મળતું નથી, અને પરમ ગતિ પણ પ્રાપ્ત થતી નથી."},{"ref":"16.24","ch":16,"v":24,"sa":"तस्माच्छास्त्रं प्रमाणं ते कार्याकार्यव्यवस्थितौ।ज्ञात्वा शास्त्रविधानोक्तं कर्म कर्तुमिहार्हसि।।16.24।।","tr":"tasmāch chhāstraṁ pramāṇaṁ te kāryākārya-vyavasthitau\njñātvā śhāstra-vidhānoktaṁ karma kartum ihārhasi","en":"Therefore, let the scripture be thy authority in determining what ought to be done and what ought not to be done. Having known what is said in the ordinance of the scriptures, thou shouldst act in this world.","es":"Therefore, the scripture is your authority as regards determining what should be done and what should not be done. After understanding your duty as presented by scriptural injunction, you ought to perform it here.","er":"Therefore, let the Sastra be your authority for determining what should be done and what should not be done. Knowing what is enjoined in the injunctions of the Sastra, you should perform work here.","gu":"માટે કર્તવ્ય અને અકર્તવ્યની વ્યવસ્થા કરવામાં શાસ્ત્ર જ તારો પ્રમાણ છે. શાસ્ત્રના આદેશ સમજીને, તારે અહીં કર્મ કરવું જોઈએ."},{"ref":"17.1","ch":17,"v":1,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाचये शास्त्रविधिमुत्सृज्य यजन्ते श्रद्धयाऽन्विताः।तेषां निष्ठा तु का कृष्ण सत्त्वमाहो रजस्तमः।।17.1।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nye śhāstra-vidhim utsṛijya yajante śhraddhayānvitāḥ\nteṣhāṁ niṣhṭhā tu kā kṛiṣhṇa sattvam āho rajas tamaḥ","en":"Arjuna said, \"What is the condition of those who, disregarding the injunctions of the scriptures, perform sacrifice with faith—is it Sattva, Rajas, or Tamas, O Krishna?\"","es":"Arjuna said, But, O Krsna, what is the state of those who, endued with faith, perform sacrifices, distribute wealth, etc. in honour of gods and others, while ignoring the injunctions of the scriptures? Is it sattva, rajas, or tamas?","er":"Arjuna said, \"Now, O Krsna, what is the position or basis of those who, despite leaving aside the injunction of the Sastra, still worship with faith? Is it Sattva, Rajas, or Tamas?\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યો: જે લોકો શાસ્ત્રવિધિ છોડીને શ્રદ્ધાપૂર્વક યજ્ઞ કરે છે, તેઓની સ્થિતિ કેવી છે — શું તે સાત્ત્વિક છે, રાજસ છે કે તામસ?"},{"ref":"17.2","ch":17,"v":2,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाचत्रिविधा भवति श्रद्धा देहिनां सा स्वभावजा।सात्त्विकी राजसी चैव तामसी चेति तां श्रृणु।।17.2।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\ntri-vidhā bhavati śhraddhā dehināṁ sā svabhāva-jā\nsāttvikī rājasī chaiva tāmasī cheti tāṁ śhṛiṇu","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"There are threefold faiths inherent in the nature of the embodied: the sattvic (pure), the rajasic (passionate), and the tamasic (dark). Hear of them.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"That faith of the embodied beings, born of their own nature, is threefold—born of sattva, rajas, and tamas. Hear about it.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"The faith of embodied beings is threefold, born of their own nature and constituted of Sattva, Rajas, and Tamas. Now, listen to me about it.\"","gu":"કૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: દેહધારીઓની સ્વભાવ-જન્ય શ્રદ્ધા ત્રણ પ્રકારની હોય છે — સાત્ત્વિક, રાજસ અને તામસ. આ વિષે સાંભળ."},{"ref":"17.3","ch":17,"v":3,"sa":"सत्त्वानुरूपा सर्वस्य श्रद्धा भवति भारत।श्रद्धामयोऽयं पुरुषो यो यच्छ्रद्धः स एव सः।।17.3।।","tr":"sattvānurūpā sarvasya śhraddhā bhavati bhārata\nśhraddhā-mayo ‘yaṁ puruṣho yo yach-chhraddhaḥ sa eva saḥ","en":"The faith of each is in accordance with their nature, O Arjuna. People consist of their faith; as a person's faith is, so are they.","es":"O scion of the Bharata dynasty, the faith of all beings is in accordance with their minds. This person is composed of faith as the dominant factor. He is indeed what his faith is.","er":"O Arjuna, the faith of everyone is in accordance with their inner organ (Antahkarana). Each person consists of faith; whatever their faith is, that is who they are.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, દરેક મનુષ્યની શ્રદ્ધા તેના સ્વભાવ અનુસાર હોય છે. મનુષ્ય શ્રદ્ધામય છે — જેવી તેની શ્રદ્ધા, તેવો તે પોતે છે."},{"ref":"17.4","ch":17,"v":4,"sa":"यजन्ते सात्त्विका देवान्यक्षरक्षांसि राजसाः।प्रेतान्भूतगणांश्चान्ये यजन्ते तामसा जनाः।।17.4।।","tr":"yajante sāttvikā devān yakṣha-rakṣhānsi rājasāḥ\npretān bhūta-gaṇānśh chānye yajante tāmasā janāḥ","en":"The sattvic, or pure, men worship the gods; the rajasic, or passionate, worship the yakshas and rakshasas; the others, the tamasic or deluded people, worship ghosts and hosts of nature-spirits.","es":"Those with sattva quality worship the gods; those with rajas, the demigods and demons; and those with tamas, ghosts and hosts of spirits.","er":"The sattvic types worship the gods; the rajasic types worship yaksas and rakshasas; and the others, the tamasic types, worship the departed ancestors and hosts of bhutas.","gu":"સાત્ત્વિક લોકો દેવોની પૂજા કરે છે; રાજસ લોકો યક્ષ અને રાક્ષસોની ઉપાસના કરે છે; અને તામસ લોકો પ્રેત તથા ભૂત-ગણોની ભક્તિ કરે છે."},{"ref":"17.5","ch":17,"v":5,"sa":"अशास्त्रविहितं घोरं तप्यन्ते ये तपो जनाः।दम्भाहङ्कारसंयुक्ताः कामरागबलान्विताः।।17.5।।","tr":"aśhāstra-vihitaṁ ghoraṁ tapyante ye tapo janāḥ\ndambhāhankāra-sanyuktāḥ kāma-rāga-balānvitāḥ","en":"Those men who practice terrific austerities not prescribed by the scriptures, given to hypocrisy and egoism, driven by the force of lust and attachment.","es":"Those persons who, given to ostentation and pride, and possessed of passion, attachment, and strength, undertake severe austerities not sanctioned by the scriptures;","er":"Those men who practice terrible austerities not enjoined by the scriptures, given to ostentation and conceit, and prompted by the force of sensual desires and passions;","gu":"જે લોકો શાસ્ત્રમાં ન જણાવેલ ભયંકર તપ આચરે છે, દંભ અને અહંકારથી ઘેરાયેલા, કામ-રાગના વેગથી પ્રેરિત —"},{"ref":"17.6","ch":17,"v":6,"sa":"कर्षयन्तः शरीरस्थं भूतग्राममचेतसः।मां चैवान्तःशरीरस्थं तान्विद्ध्यासुरनिश्चयान्।।17.6।।","tr":"karṣhayantaḥ śharīra-sthaṁ bhūta-grāmam achetasaḥ\nmāṁ chaivāntaḥ śharīra-sthaṁ tān viddhy āsura-niśhchayān","en":"Know thou these to be of demonical resolves, senselessly torturing all the elements in the body and Me who dwell in the body.","es":"(And those who,) being non-discriminating, torture all the organs in the body as well as even Me who reside in the body—know them to be possessed of demoniacal conviction.","er":"These foolish men, who torture the group of elements in their bodies and Me, who dwell within the body—know them to be demoniacal in their resolves.","gu":"શરીરના સઘળા ઇન્દ્રિય-ઘટકોને અને અંતઃકરણમાં વસતા મને નિષ્ઠુરતાથી પીડે છે — તેઓને આસુરી નિશ્ચયયુક્ત જાણ."},{"ref":"17.7","ch":17,"v":7,"sa":"आहारस्त्वपि सर्वस्य त्रिविधो भवति प्रियः।यज्ञस्तपस्तथा दानं तेषां भेदमिमं श्रृणु।।17.7।।","tr":"āhāras tv api sarvasya tri-vidho bhavati priyaḥ\nyajñas tapas tathā dānaṁ teṣhāṁ bhedam imaṁ śhṛiṇu","en":"The food that is dear to each is threefold, as well as sacrifice, austerity, and almsgiving. Hear the distinction of these.","es":"Food, which is dear to all, is of three kinds; likewise, sacrifices, austerity, and charity are also of three kinds. Listen to this classification of them.","er":"Even the food that is dear to all is threefold; so too are sacrifices, austerities, and gifts. Listen to this distinction among them.","gu":"જે ભોજન દરેકને પ્રિય છે તે પણ ત્રણ પ્રકારનું હોય છે, એ જ રીતે યજ્ઞ, તપ અને દાન પણ. આ ભેદ સાંભળ."},{"ref":"17.8","ch":17,"v":8,"sa":"आयुःसत्त्वबलारोग्यसुखप्रीतिविवर्धनाः।रस्याः स्निग्धाः स्थिरा हृद्या आहाराः सात्त्विकप्रियाः।।17.8।।","tr":"āyuḥ-sattva-balārogya-sukha-prīti-vivardhanāḥ\nrasyāḥ snigdhāḥ sthirā hṛidyā āhārāḥ sāttvika-priyāḥ","en":"The foods that increase life, purity, strength, health, joy, and cheerfulness (good appetite), which are savory, oily, substantial, and agreeable, are dear to the Sattvic (pure) people.","es":"Foods that augment life, firmness of mind, strength, health, happiness, and delight, and which are succulent, oleaginous, substantial, and agreeable, are dear to one endowed with sattva.","er":"Foods that promote longevity, intellectual alertness, strength, health, pleasure, and happiness, and those that are sweet, oily, substantial, and agreeable, are dear to sattvic men.","gu":"આયુ, સત્ત્વ, બળ, આરોગ્ય, સુખ અને આનંદ વધારે એવાં — સ્વાદિષ્ટ, ચીકણાં, ટકાઉ અને મનભાવ્યાં ભોજન સાત્ત્વિક પ્રકૃતિના લોકોને પ્રિય હોય છે."},{"ref":"17.9","ch":17,"v":9,"sa":"कट्वम्ललवणात्युष्णतीक्ष्णरूक्षविदाहिनः।आहारा राजसस्येष्टा दुःखशोकामयप्रदाः।।17.9।।","tr":"kaṭv-amla-lavaṇāty-uṣhṇa- tīkṣhṇa-rūkṣha-vidāhinaḥ\nāhārā rājasasyeṣhṭā duḥkha-śhokāmaya-pradāḥ","en":"The foods that are bitter, sour, salty, overly hot, pungent, dry, and burning are liked by the Rajasic and are productive of pain, grief, and disease.","es":"Foods that are bitter, sour, salty, very hot, pungent, dry, and burning, producing pain, sorrow, and disease, are dear to one who has rajas.","er":"Foods that are bitter, sour, very salty, excessively heating, highly pungent, dry, and burning are all dear to Rajasika men; they cause pain, sorrow, and disease.","gu":"કડવાં, ખાટાં, ખારાં, ઘણાં ઉષ્ણ, તીખાં, રૂક્ષ અને દાહકારક ભોજન રાજસ ગુણવાળા ઇચ્છે છે — એ દુ:ખ, શોક અને રોગ ઉત્પન્ન કરે છે."},{"ref":"17.10","ch":17,"v":10,"sa":"यातयामं गतरसं पूति पर्युषितं च यत्।उच्छिष्टमपि चामेध्यं भोजनं तामसप्रियम्।।17.10।।","tr":"yāta-yāmaṁ gata-rasaṁ pūti paryuṣhitaṁ cha yat\nuchchhiṣhṭam api chāmedhyaṁ bhojanaṁ tāmasa-priyam","en":"That which is stale, tasteless, putrid, rotten, rejected, and impure is the food liked by the Tamasic.","es":"Food that is not properly cooked, lacking in essence, putrid and stale, as well as that which is unfit for sacrifice, is dear to one possessed of tamas.","er":"That food which is stale, tasteless, putrid, decayed, rejected, unclean, is dear to those of a Tamasic nature.","gu":"જે ભોજન વાસી, સ્વાદ-વગરનું, દૂષિત, સડેલું, ઉચ્છિષ્ટ અને અશુદ્ધ છે — એ ભોજન તામસ ગુણ ધરાવતા લોકોને પ્રિય હોય છે."},{"ref":"17.11","ch":17,"v":11,"sa":"अफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्यज्ञो विधिदृष्टो य इज्यते।यष्टव्यमेवेति मनः समाधाय स सात्त्विकः।।17.11।।","tr":"aphalākāṅkṣhibhir yajño vidhi-driṣhṭo ya ijyate\nyaṣhṭavyam eveti manaḥ samādhāya sa sāttvikaḥ","en":"That sacrifice which is offered by men without desire for reward, as enjoined by the ordinance (scripture), with a firm faith that doing so is their duty, is Sattvic or pure.","es":"That sacrifice which is in accordance with the injunctions, performed by persons who do not hanker after results, and with the mental conviction that it is surely obligatory, is done through sattva.","er":"The sacrifice (worship) marked by Sattva is what is offered by those who desire no fruit and have the conviction that it should be performed as prescribed in the scriptures.","gu":"ફળની ઇચ્છા ન રાખીને, શાસ્ત્ર-વિધિ અનુસાર 'આ ઉચિત છે' એ દૃઢ ભાવથી જે યજ્ઞ કરવામાં આવે છે — તે સાત્ત્વિક યજ્ઞ છે."},{"ref":"17.12","ch":17,"v":12,"sa":"अभिसंधाय तु फलं दम्भार्थमपि चैव यत्।इज्यते भरतश्रेष्ठ तं यज्ञं विद्धि राजसम्।।17.12।।","tr":"abhisandhāya tu phalaṁ dambhārtham api chaiva yat\nijyate bharata-śhreṣhṭha taṁ yajñaṁ viddhi rājasam","en":"The sacrifice that is offered, O Arjuna, seeking a reward and for show, know that to be a Rajasic Yajna.","es":"But that sacrifice which is performed with an aim for a result, as well as for show—know that sacrifice to be done through rajas, O greatest among the descendants of Bharata.","er":"But that sacrifice which is offered with the intention of gaining a reward and for the sake of show, know it, O Arjuna, to be Rajasic.","gu":"હે ભારતશ્રેષ્ઠ, ફળ ઇચ્છીને અથવા દેખાડા માટે જે યજ્ઞ કરવામાં આવે છે — તેને રાજસ જાણ."},{"ref":"17.13","ch":17,"v":13,"sa":"विधिहीनमसृष्टान्नं मन्त्रहीनमदक्षिणम्।श्रद्धाविरहितं यज्ञं तामसं परिचक्षते।।17.13।।","tr":"vidhi-hīnam asṛiṣhṭānnaṁ mantra-hīnam adakṣhiṇam\nśhraddhā-virahitaṁ yajñaṁ tāmasaṁ parichakṣhate","en":"They declare that sacrifice to be Tamasic which is contrary to the ordinances of the scriptures, in which no food is distributed, and which is devoid of mantras, gifts, and faith.","es":"They declare that sacrifice as 'done through tamas' which is contrary to injunction, in which no food is distributed, in which no mantras are used, in which no offerings are made to priests, and which is devoid of faith.","er":"That sacrifice which is devoid of authority, which uses offerings not sanctioned by the Sastras, which is performed without recitation of hymns and devoid of gifts and faith - that, they say, is marked by Tamas.","gu":"શાસ્ત્ર-વિધિ વિરુદ્ધ, અન્ન-વિતરણ વિના, મંત્ર, દક્ષિણા અને શ્રદ્ધા વિના જે યજ્ઞ કરવામાં આવે છે — તે તામસ યજ્ઞ કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"17.14","ch":17,"v":14,"sa":"देवद्विजगुरुप्राज्ञपूजनं शौचमार्जवम्।ब्रह्मचर्यमहिंसा च शारीरं तप उच्यते।।17.14।।","tr":"deva-dwija-guru-prājña- pūjanaṁ śhaucham ārjavam\nbrahmacharyam ahinsā cha śhārīraṁ tapa uchyate","en":"Worship of the gods, the twice-born, the teachers, and the wise; purity, straightforwardness, celibacy, and non-injury are all called the austerities of the body.","es":"The worship of gods, twice-borns, venerable persons, and the wise; purity, straightforwardness, celibacy, and non-injury—these are said to be bodily austerities.","er":"Worshiping the gods, the twice-born, the preceptors, the enlightened ones, practicing purity, uprightness, continence, and non-injury—these are called austerity of the body.","gu":"દેવો, દ્વિજો, ગુરુઓ અને જ્ઞાનીઓની પૂજા; શૌચ, સરળતા, બ્રહ્મચર્ય અને અહિંસા — આ સઘળાં શારીરિક તપ કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"17.15","ch":17,"v":15,"sa":"अनुद्वेगकरं वाक्यं सत्यं प्रियहितं च यत्।स्वाध्यायाभ्यसनं चैव वाङ्मयं तप उच्यते।।17.15।।","tr":"anudvega-karaṁ vākyaṁ satyaṁ priya-hitaṁ cha yat\nsvādhyāyābhyasanaṁ chaiva vāṅ-mayaṁ tapa uchyate","en":"Speech that causes no excitement, is truthful, pleasant, and beneficial; the practice of studying the Vedas is called austerity of speech.","es":"That speech which causes no pain, which is true, agreeable, and beneficial; as well as the practice of studying the scriptures—is said to be the austerity of speech.","er":"Speech that causes no shock, is true, pleasant, and beneficial, and also the practice of reciting scriptures, is called the austerity of speech.","gu":"જે વાણી ઉદ્વેગ ન ઉત્પન્ન કરે, સત્ય હોય, પ્રિય અને હિતકારી હોય, તથા નિત્ય સ્વાધ્યાયનો અભ્યાસ — આ વાણીનું તપ કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"17.16","ch":17,"v":16,"sa":"मनःप्रसादः सौम्यत्वं मौनमात्मविनिग्रहः।भावसंशुद्धिरित्येतत्तपो मानसमुच्यते।।17.16।।","tr":"manaḥ-prasādaḥ saumyatvaṁ maunam ātma-vinigrahaḥ\nbhāva-sanśhuddhir ity etat tapo mānasam uchyate","en":"Serenity of mind, good-heartedness, self-control, and purity of nature—this is called mental austerity.","es":"Tranquility of mind, gentleness, reticence, withdrawal of the mind, purity of heart—these are what are called mental austerities.","er":"Serenity of mind, benevolence, silence, self-control, and purity of mind—these are known as austerity of the mind.","gu":"મનની પ્રસન્નતા, સૌમ્ય સ્વભાવ, મૌન, આત્મ-સંયમ અને ભાવ-શુદ્ધિ — આ મનનું તપ કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"17.17","ch":17,"v":17,"sa":"श्रद्धया परया तप्तं तपस्तत्ित्रविधं नरैः।अफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्युक्तैः सात्त्विकं परिचक्षते।।17.17।।","tr":"śhraddhayā parayā taptaṁ tapas tat tri-vidhaṁ naraiḥ\naphalākāṅkṣhibhir yuktaiḥ sāttvikaṁ parichakṣhate","en":"This threefold austerity, practiced by steadfast men, with the utmost faith, desiring no reward, is called Sattvic.","es":"When that threefold austerity is undertaken with supreme faith by people who do not hanker after results and are self-controlled, they speak of it as being born of sattva.","er":"The threefold austerity, practiced with supreme faith by men who desire no fruit and are devoted—they call it austerity of Sattva.","gu":"આ ત્રિવિધ તપ, ફળની ઇચ્છા વિના, પરમ શ્રદ્ધાથી, અને ધ્યેયમાં સ્થિર રહી જ્યારે પ્રયોગ થાય, ત્યારે તે સાત્ત્વિક તપ કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"17.18","ch":17,"v":18,"sa":"सत्कारमानपूजार्थं तपो दम्भेन चैव यत्।क्रियते तदिह प्रोक्तं राजसं चलमध्रुवम्।।17.18।।","tr":"satkāra-māna-pūjārthaṁ tapo dambhena chaiva yat\nkriyate tad iha proktaṁ rājasaṁ chalam adhruvam","en":"The austerity that is practiced with the aim of gaining good reception, honor, and worship, and with hypocrisy, is said to be Rajasic, unstable, and transient.","es":"That austerity which is undertaken for earning a name, being honored and worshipped, and also ostentatiously—that is spoken of as born of rajas, belonging to this world, uncertain, and transitory.","er":"That austerity, practiced with ostentation for the sake of gaining respect, praise, and reverence, is here said to be Rajasa. It is unsteady and impermanent.","gu":"સત્કાર, માન અને પૂજા પ્રાપ્ત કરવા માટે, અને ઢોંગ સહિત જે તપ કરવામાં આવે — તે અહીં રાજસ તપ કહેવાય છે; તે અસ્થિર અને ક્ષણભંગુર છે."},{"ref":"17.19","ch":17,"v":19,"sa":"मूढग्राहेणात्मनो यत्पीडया क्रियते तपः।परस्योत्सादनार्थं वा तत्तामसमुदाहृतम्।।17.19।।","tr":"mūḍha-grāheṇātmano yat pīḍayā kriyate tapaḥ\nparasyotsādanārthaṁ vā tat tāmasam udāhṛitam","en":"That austerity which is practised out of a foolish notion, with self-torture, or for the purpose of destroying another, is declared to be of the Tamasic nature.","es":"That austerity which is undertaken with a foolish intent, causing pain to oneself or for the destruction of others, is said to be born of tamas.","er":"That austerity which is practised from deluded notions by means of self-torture or to injure another is said to be Tamasika.","gu":"જે તપ મૂઢ ધારણાઓથી, આત્મ-પીડા સહિત, અથવા બીજાને નષ્ટ કરવાના ઉદ્દેશ્યથી કરવામાં આવે — તે તામસ તપ ઘોષિત કરવામાં આવ્યું છે."},{"ref":"17.20","ch":17,"v":20,"sa":"दातव्यमिति यद्दानं दीयतेऽनुपकारिणे।देशे काले च पात्रे च तद्दानं सात्त्विकं स्मृतम्।।17.20।।","tr":"dātavyam iti yad dānaṁ dīyate ‘nupakāriṇe\ndeśhe kāle cha pātre cha tad dānaṁ sāttvikaṁ smṛitam","en":"That gift which is given to one who does nothing in return, knowing it to be a duty to give in a suitable place and time to a worthy person, is held to be Sattvic.","es":"That gift is referred to as born of sattva which is given with the idea that it should be given, to one who will not serve in return, at the right place, right time, and to the right person.","er":"Gifts given with the feeling that it is one's own duty to give, to one who makes no return, at the proper place and time to the deserving person—that is said to be sattvika.","gu":"દેવું ન હોય એવા પ્રત્યે, ફળની આશા વિના, ઉચિત સ્થળે, ઉચિત સમયે, અને યોગ્ય પાત્રને જ્યારે દાન દેવામાં આવે — તે સાત્ત્વિક દાન ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"17.21","ch":17,"v":21,"sa":"यत्तु प्रत्युपकारार्थं फलमुद्दिश्य वा पुनः।दीयते च परिक्लिष्टं तद्दानं राजसं स्मृतम्।।17.21।।","tr":"yat tu pratyupakārārthaṁ phalam uddiśhya vā punaḥ\ndīyate cha parikliṣhṭaṁ tad dānaṁ rājasaṁ smṛitam","en":"And, that gift which is given with the intention of receiving something in return, or expecting a reward, or begrudgingly, is considered to be Rajasic.","es":"But the gift which is given expecting reciprocation, or with a desire for its result, and grudgingly, is considered to be born of rajas.","er":"But that which is given as a consideration for something received or in expectation of a future reward, or grudgingly, is called a Rajasika gift.","gu":"જે દાન બદલામાં કંઈ મળવાની ઇચ્છાથી, અથવા ફળની અપેક્ષાથી, કે અનિચ્છાએ દેવામાં આવે — તે રાજસ દાન કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"17.22","ch":17,"v":22,"sa":"अदेशकाले यद्दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च दीयते।असत्कृतमवज्ञातं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम्।।17.22।।","tr":"adeśha-kāle yad dānam apātrebhyaśh cha dīyate\nasat-kṛitam avajñātaṁ tat tāmasam udāhṛitam","en":"The gift that is given in the wrong place and at the wrong time, to unworthy persons, without respect or with insult, is declared to be of a Tamasic nature.","es":"The gift which is made at an inappropriate place and time, and to undeserving persons, without proper respect and with disdain, is declared to be born of tamas.","er":"That gift which is given at the wrong place, wrong time, to an unworthy recipient, without due respect and with contempt, is called the gift of a Tamasa nature.","gu":"જે દાન અયોગ્ય સ્થળે અને અકાળે, અયોગ્ય પાત્રને, અસત્કાર સહિત અથવા અવજ્ઞાપૂર્વક આપવામાં આવે — તે તામસ દાન ઘોષિત કરવામાં આવ્યું છે."},{"ref":"17.23","ch":17,"v":23,"sa":"तत्सदिति निर्देशो ब्रह्मणस्त्रिविधः स्मृतः।ब्राह्मणास्तेन वेदाश्च यज्ञाश्च विहिताः पुरा।।17.23।।","tr":"oṁ tat sad iti nirdeśho brahmaṇas tri-vidhaḥ smṛitaḥ\nbrāhmaṇās tena vedāśh cha yajñāśh cha vihitāḥ purā","en":"\"Om Tat Sat\": This has been declared to be the triple designation of Brahman. By that, the Brahmanas, the Vedas, and the sacrifices were created formerly.","es":"\"Om-tat-sat\" - this is considered to be the threefold designation of Brahman. The Brahmanas, Vedas, and sacrifices were ordained by that in days of yore.","er":"Om, Tat, Sat—thus, Brahman is denoted by this threefold expression. In the past, Brahmanas, the Vedas, and sacrifices were ordained in association with these.","gu":"'ૐ તત્ સત્' — આ બ્રહ્મની ત્રિવિધ ઓળખ ઘોષિત કરવામાં આવી છે; પ્રાચીન કાળમાં બ્રાહ્મણો, વેદો, અને યજ્ઞો આ દ્વારા નિર્ધારિત કરવામાં આવ્યાં હતાં."},{"ref":"17.24","ch":17,"v":24,"sa":"तस्मादोमित्युदाहृत्य यज्ञदानतपःक्रियाः।प्रवर्तन्ते विधानोक्ताः सततं ब्रह्मवादिनाम्।।17.24।।","tr":"tasmād oṁ ity udāhṛitya yajña-dāna-tapaḥ-kriyāḥ\npravartante vidhānoktāḥ satataṁ brahma-vādinām","en":"Therefore, with the utterance of \"Om,\" the acts of sacrifice, gift, and austerity, as enjoined in the scriptures, are always begun by the students of Brahman.","es":"Therefore, acts of sacrifice, charity, and austerity, as prescribed through injunctions, of those who study and expound the Vedas, always commence after uttering the syllable ‘Om’.","er":"Therefore, the Veda-enjoined sacrificial acts, gifts, and austerities, expounded by the Vedas, or those belonging to the first three stations, are always begun after pronouncing Om at the beginning.","gu":"તેથી, 'ૐ' ઉચ્ચારણ સાથે, શાસ્ત્ર-વિધાનમાં નિર્ધારિત યજ્ઞ, દાન અને તપનાં કાર્યો, બ્રહ્મ-જ્ઞાનીઓ દ્વારા સદૈવ આરંભ કરવામાં આવે છે."},{"ref":"17.25","ch":17,"v":25,"sa":"तदित्यनभिसन्धाय फलं यज्ञतपःक्रियाः।दानक्रियाश्च विविधाः क्रियन्ते मोक्षकाङ्क्षि।।17.25।।","tr":"tad ity anabhisandhāya phalaṁ yajña-tapaḥ-kriyāḥ\ndāna-kriyāśh cha vividhāḥ kriyante mokṣha-kāṅkṣhibhiḥ","en":"Uttering \"Tat,\" without aiming for the fruits, are the acts of sacrifice, austerity, and the various acts of gifts performed by those seeking liberation.","es":"After uttering the word \"tat,\" acts of sacrifice and austerity, as well as various acts of charity, are performed without regard for results by persons aspiring for liberation.","er":"Acts of sacrifice, austerity, and various gifts are performed without aiming at a reward by those who seek release, after pronouncing Tat.","gu":"'તત્' ઉચ્ચારી, ફળની ઇચ્છા વિના — યજ્ઞ, તપ અને અનેક પ્રકારનાં દાનનાં કાર્યો, મોક્ષ-ઇચ્છુ સાધકો દ્વારા સંપન્ન કરવામાં આવે છે."},{"ref":"17.26","ch":17,"v":26,"sa":"सद्भावे साधुभावे च सदित्येतत्प्रयुज्यते।प्रशस्ते कर्मणि तथा सच्छब्दः पार्थ युज्यते।।17.26।।","tr":"sad-bhāve sādhu-bhāve cha sad ity etat prayujyate\npraśhaste karmaṇi tathā sach-chhabdaḥ pārtha yujyate","en":"The word \"Sat\" is used to refer to reality and goodness; likewise, O Arjuna, the word \"Sat\" is used to refer to an auspicious act.","es":"This word \"sat\" is used with regard to something coming into being and someone becoming good. Likewise, O son of Prtha, the word \"sat\" is used with regard to an auspicious rite.","er":"This term \"Sat\" is used in the sense of existence and goodness. And so also, O Arjuna, the word \"Sat\" is applied to an auspicious action.","gu":"'સત્' શબ્દ સત્ય અને શ્રેષ્ઠતાને દર્શાવવા વપરાય છે; હે અર્જુન, 'સત્' શબ્દ શુભ-કાર્ય માટે પણ પ્રયોગ થાય છે."},{"ref":"17.27","ch":17,"v":27,"sa":"यज्ञे तपसि दाने च स्थितिः सदिति चोच्यते।कर्म चैव तदर्थीयं सदित्येवाभिधीयते।।17.27।।","tr":"yajñe tapasi dāne cha sthitiḥ sad iti chochyate\nkarma chaiva tad-arthīyaṁ sad ity evābhidhīyate","en":"Steadfastness in sacrifice, austerity, and gift is also called 'Sat', and action in connection with these, or for the sake of the Supreme, is also called 'Sat'.","es":"And the steadfastness in sacrifice, austerity, and charity is spoken of as sat (good). And even the action meant for these is, indeed, called as sat.","er":"Devotion to sacrifice, austerity, and gifts is also referred to as Sat; and thus, any action for such purposes is known as Sat.","gu":"યજ્ઞ, તપ, અને દાનમાં સ્થિરતા પણ 'સત્' કહેવાય છે; અને પ્રભુ-અર્થે કરવામાં આવેલ કર્મ 'સત્' ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"17.28","ch":17,"v":28,"sa":"अश्रद्धया हुतं दत्तं तपस्तप्तं कृतं च यत्।असदित्युच्यते पार्थ न च तत्प्रेत्य नो इह।।17.28।।","tr":"aśhraddhayā hutaṁ dattaṁ tapas taptaṁ kṛitaṁ cha yat\nasad ity uchyate pārtha na cha tat pretya no iha","en":"Whatever is sacrificed, given, or performed, and whatever austerity is practiced without faith, it is called 'Asat', O Arjuna; it is of no value here or hereafter (after death).","es":"O son of Prtha, whatever is offered in sacrifice and given in charity, as also whatever austerity is undertaken or whatever is done without faith, is said to be of no avail. And it is of no consequence after death, nor here.","er":"Whatever offering or gift is made, whatever austerity is practiced, and whatever action is performed without faith, that is called Asat, O Arjuna. It is of no value here or hereafter.","gu":"જે કંઈ યજ્ઞ, દાન, અથવા તપ, શ્રદ્ધા વિના કરવામાં આવે — તે 'અસત્' કહેવાય છે, હે અર્જુન; તે ન આ લોકમાં ફળ આપે છે, ન પરલોકમાં."},{"ref":"18.1","ch":18,"v":1,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाच\nसंन्यासस्य महाबाहो तत्त्वमिच्छामि वेदितुम्।\nत्यागस्य च हृषीकेश पृथक्केशिनिषूदन।।18.1।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nsannyāsasya mahā-bāho tattvam ichchhāmi veditum\ntyāgasya cha hṛiṣhīkeśha pṛithak keśhi-niṣhūdana","en":"Arjuna said, \"O mighty-armed Hrishikesa, I desire to know the essence or truth of renunciation and abandonment severally, O slayer of Kesi.\"","es":"Arjuna said, O mighty-armed Hrsikesa, O slayer of Kesi, I want to know separately the truth about sannyasa as well as about tyaga.","er":"Arjuna said, \"I desire to know the truth about renunciation and abnegation separately, O Krishna.\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે મહાબાહો, હે હૃષીકેશ, હું સંન્યાસ અને ત્યાગના સ્વભાવને અલગ-અલગ જાણવા ઇચ્છું છું."},{"ref":"18.2","ch":18,"v":2,"sa":"श्री भगवानुवाच\nकाम्यानां कर्मणां न्यासं संन्यासं कवयो विदुः।\nसर्वकर्मफलत्यागं प्राहुस्त्यागं विचक्षणाः।।18.2।।","tr":"śhrī-bhagavān uvācha\nkāmyānāṁ karmaṇāṁ nyāsaṁ sannyāsaṁ kavayo viduḥ\nsarva-karma-phala-tyāgaṁ prāhus tyāgaṁ vichakṣhaṇāḥ","en":"The Blessed Lord said, \"The sages understand sannyasa to be the renunciation of action with desire; the wise declare the abandonment of the fruits of all actions to be tyaga.\"","es":"The Blessed Lord said, \"The learned ones know sannyasa to be the giving up of actions done with a desire for reward. The adepts call the abandonment of the results of all works 'tyaga'.\"","er":"The Lord said, \"The sages hold that Sannyasa is the giving up of all works motivated by desire, and the wise declare Tyaga to be the abandonment of the fruits of all works.","gu":"શ્રીકૃષ્ણ બોલ્યા: કામના-પ્રેરિત કર્મોના ત્યાગને જ્ઞાનીઓ સંન્યાસ કહે છે, અને સર્વ કર્મોના ફળના ત્યાગને વિદ્વાનો ત્યાગ કહે છે."},{"ref":"18.3","ch":18,"v":3,"sa":"त्याज्यं दोषवदित्येके कर्म प्राहुर्मनीषिणः।\nयज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यमिति चापरे।।18.3।।","tr":"tyājyaṁ doṣha-vad ity eke karma prāhur manīṣhiṇaḥ\nyajña-dāna-tapaḥ-karma na tyājyam iti chāpare","en":"Some philosophers declare that actions should be abandoned as evil; while others declare that acts of sacrifice, gift, and austerity should not be relinquished.","es":"Some learned persons say that action, beset with evil as it is, should be abandoned, and others say that the practice of sacrifice, charity, and austerity should not be abandoned.","er":"Some sages say that all actions should be abandoned as evil; others declare that works such as sacrifices, gifts, and austerities should not be abandoned.","gu":"કેટલાક વિચારકો કહે છે કે કર્મ દોષ-રૂપ હોવાથી ત્યજવું જોઈએ, જ્યારે બીજા કહે છે કે યજ્ઞ, દાન અને તપ-કર્મ ત્યજવાં ન જોઈએ."},{"ref":"18.4","ch":18,"v":4,"sa":"निश्चयं श्रृणु मे तत्र त्यागे भरतसत्तम।त्यागो हि पुरुषव्याघ्र त्रिविधः संप्रकीर्तितः।।18.4।।","tr":"niśhchayaṁ śhṛiṇu me tatra tyāge bharata-sattama\ntyāgo hi puruṣha-vyāghra tri-vidhaḥ samprakīrtitaḥ","en":"Hear from Me the conclusion or the final truth about this abandonment, O best of the Bharatas; abandonment, indeed, O best of men, has been declared to be of three kinds.","es":"O the most excellent among the descendants of Bharata, hear from Me the firm conclusion regarding that tyaga. For, O greatest among men, tyaga has been clearly declared to be of three kinds.","er":"Listen to My decision, O Arjuna, concerning abandonment; for abandonment is declared to be of three kinds.","gu":"હે ભરતવંશ-શ્રેષ્ઠ, ત્યાગ વિષે મારો નિર્ણય સાંભળો — ત્યાગ ત્રણ પ્રકારનો કહ્યો છે."},{"ref":"18.5","ch":18,"v":5,"sa":"यज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यं कार्यमेव तत्।यज्ञो दानं तपश्चैव पावनानि मनीषिणाम्।।18.5।।","tr":"yajña-dāna-tapaḥ-karma na tyājyaṁ kāryam eva tat\nyajño dānaṁ tapaśh chaiva pāvanāni manīṣhiṇām","en":"Acts of sacrifice, gift, and austerity should not be abandoned, but should be performed; for sacrifice, gift, and austerity are the purifiers of the wise.","es":"The practice of sacrifice, charity, and austerity should not be abandoned; it should certainly be undertaken. Sacrifice, charity, and austerity are indeed the purifiers of the wise.","er":"(a) The acts of sacrifice, gifts, and austerities should not be relinquished; but should be performed...\n(b) ...For sacrifices, gifts, and austerities are the means of purification for the wise.","gu":"યજ્ઞ, દાન અને તપ-કર્મ ત્યજવાં ન જોઈએ, પરંતુ જરૂર કરવાં જોઈએ; કારણ કે આ ત્રણ જ્ઞાનીઓ માટે પવિત્ર કરનારાં છે."},{"ref":"18.6","ch":18,"v":6,"sa":"एतान्यपि तु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलानि च।कर्तव्यानीति मे पार्थ निश्िचतं मतमुत्तमम्।।18.6।।","tr":"etāny api tu karmāṇi saṅgaṁ tyaktvā phalāni cha\nkartavyānīti me pārtha niśhchitaṁ matam uttamam","en":"But even these actions should be performed, leaving aside attachment and the desire for rewards, O Arjuna; this is my certain and most assured conviction.","es":"But even these actions must be undertaken by renouncing attachment and hankering for results. This is My firm and definitive conclusion, O Partha.","er":"It is My decided and final view that even these acts should be done, O Arjuna, with relinquishment of attachment and the forsaking of the fruits thereof.","gu":"પરંતુ હે અર્જુન, આ કર્મો પણ આસક્તિ અને ફળ છોડીને કરવાં જોઈએ — આ મારો દૃઢ અને ઉત્તમ મત છે."},{"ref":"18.7","ch":18,"v":7,"sa":"नियतस्य तु संन्यासः कर्मणो नोपपद्यते।मोहात्तस्य परित्यागस्तामसः परिकीर्तितः।।18.7।।","tr":"niyatasya tu sannyāsaḥ karmaṇo nopapadyate\nmohāt tasya parityāgas tāmasaḥ parikīrtitaḥ","en":"Verily, the renunciation of obligatory action is not proper; the abandonment of the same out of delusion is declared to be Tamasic.","es":"Abandoning one's daily obligatory acts is not justifiable; giving up those through delusion is said to be rooted in tamas.","er":"But the renunciation of obligatory acts is not proper; abandonment of these through delusion is declared to be of a Tamasic nature.","gu":"નિત્ય-નિયત કર્મનો ત્યાગ ઉચિત નથી; મોહ-વશ તેનો ત્યાગ કરવો તે તામસ ત્યાગ કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"18.8","ch":18,"v":8,"sa":"दुःखमित्येव यत्कर्म कायक्लेशभयात्त्यजेत्।स कृत्वा राजसं त्यागं नैव त्यागफलं लभेत्।।18.8।।","tr":"duḥkham ity eva yat karma kāya-kleśha-bhayāt tyajet\nsa kṛitvā rājasaṁ tyāgaṁ naiva tyāga-phalaṁ labhet","en":"He who abandons action out of fear of bodily trouble (because it is painful), does not obtain the merit of renunciation by performing such Rajasic renunciation.","es":"Whatever action one may relinquish merely as being painful, out of fear of physical suffering, he, having resorted to renunciation based on rajas, will surely not acquire the fruits of renunciation.","er":"He who renounces acts that are painful out of fear of bodily suffering performs a Rajasika abandonment; however, he does not gain the fruit of such abandonment.","gu":"જે કર્મ કષ્ટ-દાયી છે એ ભ્રમ-ભયથી ત્યજે, તે રાજસ ત્યાગ કરે છે — અને તેને ત્યાગનું ફળ પ્રાપ્ત થતું નથી."},{"ref":"18.9","ch":18,"v":9,"sa":"कार्यमित्येव यत्कर्म नियतं क्रियतेऽर्जुन।सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलं चैव स त्यागः सात्त्विको मतः।।18.9।।","tr":"kāryam ity eva yat karma niyataṁ kriyate ‘rjuna\nsaṅgaṁ tyaktvā phalaṁ chaiva sa tyāgaḥ sāttviko mataḥ","en":"Whatever obligatory action is done, O Arjuna, merely because it ought to be done, abandoning attachment and also the desire for reward, that renunciation is regarded as sattvic (pure).","es":"Whatever obligatory duty is performed just because it is a bounden duty, O Arjuna, by giving up attachment and the results as well—that renunciation is considered to be based on sattva.","er":"When actions are performed as they ought to be done, O Arjuna, renouncing attachment and the results thereof, such abandonment is regarded as Sattvika.","gu":"જે કર્તવ્ય-કર્મ 'કરવું જ જોઈએ' એ ભાવથી, આસક્તિ અને ફળ ત્યજીને કરવામાં આવે — તે ત્યાગ સાત્ત્વિક ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"18.10","ch":18,"v":10,"sa":"न द्वेष्ट्यकुशलं कर्म कुशले नानुषज्जते।त्यागी सत्त्वसमाविष्टो मेधावी छिन्नसंशयः।।18.10।।","tr":"na dveṣhṭy akuśhalaṁ karma kuśhale nānuṣhajjate\ntyāgī sattva-samāviṣhṭo medhāvī chhinna-sanśhayaḥ","en":"The man of renunciation, pervaded by purity, intelligent, and with his doubts cut asunder, does not hate an unpleasant task nor is he attached to a pleasant one.","es":"The man of renunciation, imbued with sattva, wise and free from doubts, does not hate unbecoming action, nor does he become attached to becoming activity.","er":"One who has abandoned, imbued with Sattva, wise, and whose doubts have been dispelled—such a person neither hates disagreeable acts nor clings to agreeable ones.","gu":"સત્ત્વ-ગુણ-સ્થિત, બુદ્ધિમાન, સંશય-રહિત ત્યાગી અપ્રિય કર્મ પ્રત્યે દ્વેષ નથી રાખતો, ન તો પ્રિય કર્મ પ્રત્યે આસક્ત થાય છે."},{"ref":"18.11","ch":18,"v":11,"sa":"न हि देहभृता शक्यं त्यक्तुं कर्माण्यशेषतः।यस्तु कर्मफलत्यागी स त्यागीत्यभिधीयते।।18.11।।","tr":"na hi deha-bhṛitā śhakyaṁ tyaktuṁ karmāṇy aśheṣhataḥ\nyas tu karma-phala-tyāgī sa tyāgīty abhidhīyate","en":"Indeed, it is not possible for an embodied being to completely abandon actions; however, he who relinquishes the rewards of actions is truly called a man of renunciation.","es":"Since it is not possible for one who holds onto a body to give up actions entirely, therefore he who renounces the results of his actions is called a man of renunciation.","er":"For, it is impossible for one who has a body to completely abandon actions. But he who gives up the results of his works is called the one who has abandoned them.","gu":"શરીર ધારણ કરનાર જીવ માટે કર્મ સર્વ-સર્વ ત્યજવું સંભવ નથી; પરંતુ જે કર્મ-ફળ ત્યજે છે, તે જ ખરો ત્યાગી કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"18.12","ch":18,"v":12,"sa":"अनिष्टमिष्टं मिश्रं च त्रिविधं कर्मणः फलम्।भवत्यत्यागिनां प्रेत्य न तु संन्यासिनां क्वचित्।।18.12।।","tr":"aniṣhṭam iṣhṭaṁ miśhraṁ cha tri-vidhaṁ karmaṇaḥ phalam\nbhavaty atyāgināṁ pretya na tu sannyāsināṁ kvachit","en":"The threefold fruit of action (evil, good, and mixed) accrues after death to those who do not abandon it, but never to those who do.","es":"The threefold results of actions—the undesirable, the desirable, and the mixed—accrue after death to those who do not resort to renunciation, but never to those who resort to renunciation.","er":"Undesirable, desirable, and mixed—thus, threefold is the fruit of work that accrues after death to those who have not renounced; but to those who have renounced, none accrues whatsoever.","gu":"ત્યાગ ન કરનારાઓને મૃત્યુ પછી ત્રિ-વિધ ફળ — અનિષ્ટ, ઇષ્ટ અને મિશ્ર — પ્રાપ્ત થાય છે; પરંતુ જે ત્યાગ કરે છે, તેને કદી નહિ."},{"ref":"18.13","ch":18,"v":13,"sa":"पञ्चैतानि महाबाहो कारणानि निबोध मे।सांख्ये कृतान्ते प्रोक्तानि सिद्धये सर्वकर्मणाम्।।18.13।।","tr":"pañchaitāni mahā-bāho kāraṇāni nibodha me\nsānkhye kṛitānte proktāni siddhaye sarva-karmaṇām","en":"Learn from Me, O mighty-armed Arjuna, these five causes, as declared in the Sankhya system, for the accomplishment of all actions.","es":"O mighty-armed one, learn from Me these five factors for the accomplishment of all actions, which have been spoken of in the Vedanta, in which actions terminate.","er":"Learn from Me, O Arjuna, these five causes for the accomplishment of all acts, as described in Sankhya-krtanta—the science of exact understanding of things—for the accomplishment of works.","gu":"હે મહાબાહો, સર્વ કર્મોની સિદ્ધિ માટે સાંખ્ય-શાસ્ત્રમાં કહેલાં આ પાંચ કારણો મારી પાસેથી જાણો."},{"ref":"18.14","ch":18,"v":14,"sa":"अधिष्ठानं तथा कर्ता करणं च पृथग्विधम्।विविधाश्च पृथक्चेष्टा दैवं चैवात्र पञ्चमम्।।18.14।।","tr":"adhiṣhṭhānaṁ tathā kartā karaṇaṁ cha pṛithag-vidham\nvividhāśh cha pṛithak cheṣhṭā daivaṁ chaivātra pañchamam","en":"The body, the doer, the various senses, the different functions of various kinds, and the presiding deity—the fifth.","es":"The locus, the agent, the different kinds of organs, the many and varied activities, and the divine are the fifth here.","er":"The seat of action, the agent, the various kinds of organs, the different and distinctive functions of vital air, and the fifth among these—Divinity—all these.","gu":"અધિષ્ઠાન (શરીર), કર્તા (જીવ), વિવિધ ઇન્દ્રિયો, ભિન્ન-ભિન્ન ક્રિયાઓ, અને પાંચમું — અધિષ્ઠાતૃ-દેવ — આ પાંચ કારણો છે."},{"ref":"18.15","ch":18,"v":15,"sa":"शरीरवाङ्मनोभिर्यत्कर्म प्रारभते नरः।न्याय्यं वा विपरीतं वा पञ्चैते तस्य हेतवः।।18.15।।","tr":"śharīra-vāṅ-manobhir yat karma prārabhate naraḥ\nnyāyyaṁ vā viparītaṁ vā pañchaite tasya hetavaḥ","en":"Whatever action a person performs with their body, speech, and mind, whether right or wrong, these five are its causes.","es":"Whatever action a person performs with their body, speech, and mind, whether it be just or its opposite, these five are the causes of it.","er":"For whatever action a person undertakes with their body, speech, and mind, whether right or wrong, i.e., enjoined or forbidden by the Sastras, the following five are its causes:","gu":"મનુષ્ય શરીર, વાણી, અથવા મન વડે જે કોઈ ઉચિત-અનુચિત કર્મ કરે, તે સઘળાના આ પ્રમાણે પાંચ જ કારણ-ભૂત છે."},{"ref":"18.16","ch":18,"v":16,"sa":"तत्रैवं सति कर्तारमात्मानं केवलं तु यः।पश्यत्यकृतबुद्धित्वान्न स पश्यति दुर्मतिः।।18.16।।","tr":"tatraivaṁ sati kartāram ātmānaṁ kevalaṁ tu yaḥ\npaśhyaty akṛita-buddhitvān na sa paśhyati durmatiḥ","en":"Now, such being the case, verily he who, owing to an untrained understanding, looks upon his Self, which is isolated, as the agent, he of perverted intelligence does not see.","es":"Therefore, anyone whose intellect is imperfect and perceives the Absolute Self as the agent, does not perceive properly and has a distorted intellect.","er":"Therefore, he who, due to his uncultivated understanding, perceives only the self as the agent, he of wicked mind does not truly perceive.","gu":"જે અણઘડ સમજણને કારણે શુદ્ધ આત્માને જ કર્તા માને છે, તે વ્યક્તિ ખોટી સમજ ધરાવે છે અને સત્ય જોઈ શકતી નથી."},{"ref":"18.17","ch":18,"v":17,"sa":"यस्य नाहंकृतो भावो बुद्धिर्यस्य न लिप्यते।हत्वापि स इमाँल्लोकान्न हन्ति न निबध्यते।।18.17।।","tr":"yasya nāhankṛito bhāvo buddhir yasya na lipyate\nhatvā ‘pi sa imāl lokān na hanti na nibadhyate","en":"He who is free from the egoistic notion, whose intelligence is not tainted by good or evil, though he slays these people, he does not slay, nor is he bound by the action.","es":"He who has no feeling of egoism, whose intellect is untainted, he does not kill, nor does he become bound—even by killing these creatures!","er":"He who is free from the notion of 'I am the doer,' and whose understanding is not tainted, does not slay, even though he slays all these men, nor is he bound.","gu":"જે અહંકારના ભાવથી મુક્ત છે અને જેની બુદ્ધિ કલુષિત નથી, તે આ લોકોને મારે તો પણ ખરેખર મારતો નથી અને તે બંધનમાં પડતો નથી."},{"ref":"18.18","ch":18,"v":18,"sa":"ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं परिज्ञाता त्रिविधा कर्मचोदना।करणं कर्म कर्तेति त्रिविधः कर्मसंग्रहः।।18.18।।","tr":"jñānaṁ jñeyaṁ parijñātā tri-vidhā karma-chodanā\nkaraṇaṁ karma karteti tri-vidhaḥ karma-saṅgrahaḥ","en":"Knowledge, the knowable, and the knower form the threefold impulse for action; the organ, the action, and the agent form the threefold basis of action.","es":"Knowledge, the object of knowledge, and the knower—these are the threefold inducements to action. The comprehension of actions comes under three heads: the instruments, the object, and the subject.","er":"Knowledge, the object of knowledge, and the knower are the threefold incitements to action. The instrument, the act, and the agent are the threefold constituents of action.","gu":"જ્ઞાન, જ્ઞેય અને જ્ઞાતા — આ ત્રણ ક્રિયાની ત્રિવિધ પ્રેરણા છે; ઇન્દ્રિય, ક્રિયા અને કર્તા — આ ત્રણ ક્રિયાનો ત્રિવિધ આધાર છે."},{"ref":"18.19","ch":18,"v":19,"sa":"ज्ञानं कर्म च कर्ता च त्रिधैव गुणभेदतः।प्रोच्यते गुणसंख्याने यथावच्छृणु तान्यपि।।18.19।।","tr":"jñānaṁ karma cha kartā cha tridhaiva guṇa-bhedataḥ\nprochyate guṇa-saṅkhyāne yathāvach chhṛiṇu tāny api","en":"Knowledge, action, and actor are declared in the science of the Gunas (Sankhya philosophy) to be of three kinds only, according to the distinction of the Gunas. Of these, hear duly.","es":"Knowledge, action, and agent are stated in the teaching about the gunas to be only of three kinds, according to the differences of the gunas. Hear about them also as they are.","er":"Knowledge, action, and agent are declared in the science of the Gunas to be of three kinds, according to the difference in the Gunas. Listen to them also as they are.","gu":"ગુણોના ભેદ અનુસાર, જ્ઞાન, ક્રિયા અને કર્તાના ત્રણ-ત્રણ પ્રકાર ગુણ-વિજ્ઞાનમાં કહ્યા છે; તે પણ યોગ્ય રીતે સાંભળ."},{"ref":"18.20","ch":18,"v":20,"sa":"सर्वभूतेषु येनैकं भावमव्ययमीक्षते।अविभक्तं विभक्तेषु तज्ज्ञानं विद्धि सात्त्विकम्।।18.20।।","tr":"sarva-bhūteṣhu yenaikaṁ bhāvam avyayam īkṣhate\navibhaktaṁ vibhakteṣhu taj jñānaṁ viddhi sāttvikam","en":"That by which one sees the indestructible Reality in all beings, not separate in any of them—know that knowledge to be Sattvic.","es":"Know that knowledge to originate from sattva, through which one sees a single, undecaying, undivided entity in all the diversified things.","er":"Know that knowledge to be sattvika, by which one sees in all beings an immutable existence, undivided even in the divided.","gu":"જે જ્ઞાન વડે મનુષ્ય સર્વ પ્રાણીઓમાં એક અવિનાશી તત્ત્વ નિહાળે છે, જે કોઈ પ્રાણીમાં અળગું નથી — તે જ્ઞાન સાત્ત્વિક છે."},{"ref":"18.21","ch":18,"v":21,"sa":"पृथक्त्वेन तु यज्ज्ञानं नानाभावान्पृथग्विधान्।वेत्ति सर्वेषु भूतेषु तज्ज्ञानं विद्धि राजसम्।।18.21।।","tr":"pṛithaktvena tu yaj jñānaṁ nānā-bhāvān pṛithag-vidhān\nvetti sarveṣhu bhūteṣhu taj jñānaṁ viddhi rājasam","en":"But that knowledge which sees in all beings various entities of distinct kinds as being distinct from one another, know thou that knowledge to be Rajasic.","es":"But know that knowledge to originate from rajas, which amidst all things apprehends the different entities of various kinds as distinct [as possessing distinct selves].","er":"But that knowledge which sees all beings, due to their individual nature, as distinct entities—know that knowledge to be Rajasic.","gu":"જે જ્ઞાન સર્વ પ્રાણીઓમાં ભિન્ન-ભિન્ન જીવ-સત્તાઓ જૂજવી રીતે જુએ છે — તે જ્ઞાનને રાજસિક જાણ."},{"ref":"18.22","ch":18,"v":22,"sa":"यत्तु कृत्स्नवदेकस्मिन्कार्ये सक्तमहैतुकम्।अतत्त्वार्थवदल्पं च तत्तामसमुदाहृतम्।।18.22।।","tr":"yat tu kṛitsna-vad ekasmin kārye saktam ahaitukam\natattvārtha-vad alpaṁ cha tat tāmasam udāhṛitam","en":"But that which clings to one single effect as if it were the whole, without reason, without any foundation in Truth, and is trivial—that is declared to be Tamasic.","es":"But that (knowledge) is said to be born of tamas which is confined to one form as if it were all, which is irrational, unconcerned with truth, and trivial.","er":"But that knowledge is declared to be Tamasika which clings to one single act as if it were the whole, which is not based on reason, and which is false and insignificant.","gu":"જે જ્ઞાન એક જ ઘટ-ક્રિયાને સમગ્ર સત્ય માની ચોંટી રહે છે, વિવેક વગર, સત્ય-ભૂમિ વગર, અને ક્ષુલ્લક છે — તે તામસિક કહ્યું છે."},{"ref":"18.23","ch":18,"v":23,"sa":"नियतं सङ्गरहितमरागद्वेषतः कृतम्।अफलप्रेप्सुना कर्म यत्तत्सात्त्विकमुच्यते।।18.23।।","tr":"niyataṁ saṅga-rahitam arāga-dveṣhataḥ kṛitam\naphala-prepsunā karma yat tat sāttvikam uchyate","en":"An action that is ordained, free from attachment, done without love or hatred, and without desire for reward is declared to be Sattvic.","es":"The daily obligatory action which is performed without attachment and without likes or dislikes, by one who does not hanker for rewards, is said to be born of sattva.","er":"That obligatory act is said to be Sattvika, which is done without attachment, without desire or aversion, and by one who seeks no fruit.","gu":"જે ક્રિયા શાસ્ત્રાનુસાર, આસક્તિ-રહિત, રાગ-દ્વેષ વિના, ફળની ઇચ્છા વગર થાય — તે ક્રિયા સાત્ત્વિક ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"18.24","ch":18,"v":24,"sa":"यत्तु कामेप्सुना कर्म साहङ्कारेण वा पुनः।क्रियते बहुलायासं तद्राजसमुदाहृतम्।।18.24।।","tr":"yat tu kāmepsunā karma sāhankāreṇa vā punaḥ\nkriyate bahulāyāsaṁ tad rājasam udāhṛitam","en":"But that action which is done by one longing for the fulfillment of desires or gain with egotism or with much effort is declared to be Rajasic (passionate).","es":"But that action is said to be born of rajas which is done by one desirous of results or by one who is egotistical, and which is highly strenuous.","er":"But that act is said to be Rajasic, which is performed with great effort by one who seeks to gratify their desires and under the prompting of egoism.","gu":"જે ક્રિયા ઇચ્છા કે લાભ માટે, અહંકાર સહિત, ઘણા પ્રયત્નથી થાય — તે ક્રિયા રાજસિક ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"18.25","ch":18,"v":25,"sa":"अनुबन्धं क्षयं हिंसामनपेक्ष्य च पौरुषम्।मोहादारभ्यते कर्म यत्तत्तामसमुच्यते।।18.25।।","tr":"anubandhaṁ kṣhayaṁ hinsām anapekṣhya cha pauruṣham\nmohād ārabhyate karma yat tat tāmasam uchyate","en":"That action which is undertaken from delusion, without regard for the consequences, loss, injury, and one's own ability, is declared to be Tamasic (dark).","es":"That action is said to be born of tamas which is undertaken out of delusion, without consideration of its consequences, loss, harm, and ability.","er":"That act is said to be Tamasika which is undertaken through delusion, without regard to consequences, loss, injury, and one's own capacity.","gu":"જે ક્રિયા ભ્રમ-ભ્રાંતિથી, ફળ-હાનિ-ઈજા અને પોતાની શક્તિ-અશક્તિ ચકાસ્યા વગર, ઉઠાવવામાં આવે — તે ક્રિયા તામસિક ગણાય છે."},{"ref":"18.26","ch":18,"v":26,"sa":"मुक्तसङ्गोऽनहंवादी धृत्युत्साहसमन्वितः।सिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योर्निर्विकारः कर्ता सात्त्विक उच्यते।।18.26।।","tr":"mukta-saṅgo ‘nahaṁ-vādī dhṛity-utsāha-samanvitaḥ\nsiddhy-asiddhyor nirvikāraḥ kartā sāttvika uchyate","en":"An agent who is free from attachment, non-egoistic, endowed with firmness and enthusiasm, and unaffected by success or failure, is considered to be of a Sattvic (pure) nature.","es":"[Ast. introduces this verse with 'Idanim kartrbhedah ucyate, Now is being stated the distinctions among the agents.'-Tr.] The agent who is free from attachment [Attachment to results or the idea of agentship.], not egotistical, endowed with fortitude and diligence, and unperturbed by success and failure is said to be possessed of sattva.","er":"That agent is said to be Sattvika, who is free from attachment, who does not boast of himself, who is endowed with steadiness and zeal, and who is unaffected by success and failure.","gu":"જે કર્તા આસક્તિ-રહિત, અહં-શૂન્ય, ઉત્સાહ અને ધૈર્યયુક્ત, સિદ્ધિ-અસિદ્ધિ ઉભયથી અળગો રહે — તે સાત્ત્વિક કહેવાય."},{"ref":"18.27","ch":18,"v":27,"sa":"रागी कर्मफलप्रेप्सुर्लुब्धो हिंसात्मकोऽशुचिः।हर्षशोकान्वितः कर्ता राजसः परिकीर्तितः।।18.27।।","tr":"rāgī karma-phala-prepsur lubdho hinsātmako ‘śhuchiḥ\nharṣha-śhokānvitaḥ kartā rājasaḥ parikīrtitaḥ","en":"Passionate, desiring to obtain the reward of their actions, greedy, cruel, impure, moved by joy and sorrow, such an agent is said to be Rajasic.","es":"The agent who has attachment, who is desirous of the results of actions, covetous, cruel by nature, unclean, and subject to joy and sorrow, is declared to be possessed of rajas.","er":"That doer is called Rajasika who is passionate, who seeks the fruits of his actions, who is greedy, harmful, and impure, and who is swayed by delight and grief.","gu":"જે કર્તા રાગી છે, ક્રિયાનાં ફળ ઝંખે છે, લોભી, ક્રૂર, અપવિત્ર, તથા સુખ-દુઃખ વડે હલતો-ડૂલતો રહે — તે રાજસિક ગણાય."},{"ref":"18.28","ch":18,"v":28,"sa":"अयुक्तः प्राकृतः स्तब्धः शठो नैष्कृतिकोऽलसः।विषादी दीर्घसूत्री च कर्ता तामस उच्यते।।18.28।।","tr":"ayuktaḥ prākṛitaḥ stabdhaḥ śhaṭho naiṣhkṛitiko ‘lasaḥ\nviṣhādī dīrgha-sūtrī cha kartā tāmasa uchyate","en":"Unsteady, vulgar, inflexible, deceitful, malicious, lazy, despondent, and procrastinating—such an agent is called Tamasic.","es":"The agent who is unsteady, naive, inflexible, deceitful, wicked, lazy, sullen, and procrastinating is said to be possessed of tamas.","er":"That doer is said to be Tamasika who is unqualified, unrefined, obstinate, depraved, dishonest, indolent, despondent, and lethargic.","gu":"જે કર્તા ચંચળ, અઘડ, કઠોર, ઢોંગી, દ્વેષી, આળસુ, ખિન્ન અને ઢીલ કરનાર છે — તે કર્તા તામસિક કહેવાય."},{"ref":"18.29","ch":18,"v":29,"sa":"बुद्धेर्भेदं धृतेश्चैव गुणतस्त्रिविधं श्रृणु।प्रोच्यमानमशेषेण पृथक्त्वेन धनञ्जय।।18.29।।","tr":"buddher bhedaṁ dhṛiteśh chaiva guṇatas tri-vidhaṁ śhṛiṇu\nprochyamānam aśheṣheṇa pṛithaktvena dhanañjaya","en":"Hear thou the threefold division of intellect and firmness, according to the Gunas, as I declare them fully and distinctly, O Arjuna.","es":"O Dhananjaya, listen to the classification of the intellect and fortitude, which is threefold according to the gunas, while it is being stated in detail and separately.","er":"Hear now, O Arjuna, the threefold division of Buddhi (reason) and Dhrti (fortitude) according to the Gunas, to be fully and severally set forth.","gu":"ગુણ-ભેદ પ્રમાણે બુદ્ધિ અને ધૃતિ — ઉભયના ત્રિવિધ ભેદ હું સ્પષ્ટ રીતે અને સંપૂર્ણ વર્ણવું છું, તે ધ્યાનથી સાંભળ."},{"ref":"18.30","ch":18,"v":30,"sa":"प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च कार्याकार्ये भयाभये।बन्धं मोक्षं च या वेत्ति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी।।18.30।।","tr":"pravṛittiṁ cha nivṛittiṁ cha kāryākārye bhayābhaye\nbandhaṁ mokṣhaṁ cha yā vetti buddhiḥ sā pārtha sāttvikī","en":"The intellect which knows the path of work and renunciation, what should be done and what should not be done, fear and fearlessness, bondage and liberation—that intellect is Sattvic (pure), O Arjuna.","es":"O Partha, that intellect is born of sattva which understands action and withdrawal, duty and what is not duty, the sources of fear and fearlessness, as well as bondage and freedom.","er":"That Buddhi, O Arjuna, which knows activity and renunciation, what should be done and what should not be done, fear and fearlessness, bondage and release—that Buddhi is Sattvika.","gu":"જે બુદ્ધિ પ્રવૃત્તિ-નિવૃત્તિ, કર્તવ્ય-અકર્તવ્ય, ભય-અભય, અને બંધ-મોક્ષ — આ સૌ જાણે — તે બુદ્ધિ સાત્ત્વિક છે."},{"ref":"18.31","ch":18,"v":31,"sa":"यया धर्ममधर्मं च कार्यं चाकार्यमेव च।अयथावत्प्रजानाति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ राजसी।।18.31।।","tr":"yayā dharmam adharmaṁ cha kāryaṁ chākāryam eva cha\nayathāvat prajānāti buddhiḥ sā pārtha rājasī","en":"That by which one wrongly understands dharma and adharma, and also what ought to be done and what ought not to be done—that intellect, O Arjuna, is rajasic (passionate).","es":"O Partha, that intellect is born of rajas with which one wrongly understands virtue and vice, as well as what ought to be done and ought not to be done.","er":"The Buddhi that gives an erroneous knowledge of Dharma and Adharma (its opposite) and also of what should be done and what should not be done, O Arjuna, is Rajasic.","gu":"જે બુદ્ધિ ધર્મ અને અધર્મને ખોટી રીતે સમજે છે, અને શું કરવું જોઈએ તથા શું ન કરવું જોઈએ તે બાબતમાં ભ્રમિત રહે છે — તે બુદ્ધિ રાજસી છે."},{"ref":"18.32","ch":18,"v":32,"sa":"अधर्मं धर्ममिति या मन्यते तमसाऽऽवृता।सर्वार्थान्विपरीतांश्च बुद्धिः सा पार्थ तामसी।।18.32।।","tr":"adharmaṁ dharmam iti yā manyate tamasāvṛitā\nsarvārthān viparītānśh cha buddhiḥ sā pārtha tāmasī","en":"That intellect, O Arjuna, which is enveloped in darkness and sees Adharma as Dharma and all things perverted, is Tamasic (dark).","es":"O Partha, that intellect is born of tamas which, being covered by darkness, considers vice as virtue, and indeed perceives all things contrary to what they are.","er":"That Buddhi, O Arjuna, which, enveloped in darkness, regards Adharma as Dharma and reverses every value, is Tamasika.","gu":"જે બુદ્ધિ અંધકારમાં ઢંકાઈ ગઈ છે અને અધર્મને ધર્મ સમજે છે, તથા દરેક વસ્તુને વિકૃત રૂપમાં જુએ છે — હે અર્જુન, તે બુદ્ધિ તામસી છે."},{"ref":"18.33","ch":18,"v":33,"sa":"धृत्या यया धारयते मनःप्राणेन्द्रियक्रियाः।योगेनाव्यभिचारिण्या धृतिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी।।18.33।।","tr":"dhṛityā yayā dhārayate manaḥ-prāṇendriya-kriyāḥ\nyogenāvyabhichāriṇyā dhṛitiḥ sā pārtha sāttvikī","en":"The unwavering firmness, through which Yoga restrains the functions of the mind, life-force, and senses—that firmness, O Arjuna, is Sattvic (pure).","es":"O Partha, the firmness that is unfailing through concentration, with which one restrains the functions of the mind, vital forces, and the organs—that firmness is born of sattva.","er":"That fortitude, by which one maintains the unwavering activities of the mind and vital force, and these sense-organs, through yoga—that fortitude is of the nature of sattva.","gu":"જે અચળ ધૈર્ય દ્વારા યોગ મન, પ્રાણ અને ઇન્દ્રિયોની વૃત્તિઓને સ્થિર રાખે છે — તે ધૈર્ય સાત્ત્વિક છે."},{"ref":"18.34","ch":18,"v":34,"sa":"यया तु धर्मकामार्थान् धृत्या धारयतेऽर्जुन।प्रसङ्गेन फलाकाङ्क्षी धृतिः सा पार्थ राजसी।।18.34।।","tr":"yayā tu dharma-kāmārthān dhṛityā dhārayate ‘rjuna\nprasaṅgena phalākāṅkṣhī dhṛitiḥ sā pārtha rājasī","en":"But that, O Arjuna, by which one holds fast to Dharma (duty), enjoyment of pleasures, and earning of wealth, on account of attachment and desire for reward—that firmness, O Arjuna, is Rajasic (passionate).","es":"But, O Partha, the steadfastness with which one holds on to righteousness, covetable things, and wealth, desiring their fruits as the occasion for each arises, that steadfastness is born of rajas.","er":"That dhṛti, O Arjuna, by which one, who is desirous of fruits, longs for them with intense attachment and holds fast to duty, desire, and wealth—that dhṛti is rajasika.","gu":"પરંતુ હે અર્જુન, જે ધૈર્ય દ્વારા કોઈ વ્યક્તિ આસક્તિ અને ફળની ઇચ્છાથી ધર્મ, ભોગ અને ધનને દૃઢપણે વળગી રહે છે — તે ધૈર્ય રાજસી છે."},{"ref":"18.35","ch":18,"v":35,"sa":"यया स्वप्नं भयं शोकं विषादं मदमेव च।न विमुञ्चति दुर्मेधा धृतिः सा पार्थ तामसी।।18.35।।","tr":"yayā svapnaṁ bhayaṁ śhokaṁ viṣhādaṁ madam eva cha\nna vimuñchati durmedhā dhṛitiḥ sā pārtha tāmasī","en":"That firmness, O Arjuna, by which a stupid man does not abandon sleep, fear, grief, despair, and conceit, is Tamasic.","es":"That firmness is considered to be born of tamas, due to which a person with a corrupt intellect does not give up sleep, fear, sorrow, despondency, as well as sensuality.","er":"That Dhrti, by which a foolish person does not give up sleep, fear, grief, depression, and passion, O Arjuna, is of the nature of Tamas.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે ધૈર્ય દ્વારા એક મૂઢ વ્યક્તિ નિદ્રા, ભય, શોક, નિરાશા અને ઘમંડ ત્યજ્યા વગર વળગી રહે છે — તે ધૈર્ય તામસી છે."},{"ref":"18.36","ch":18,"v":36,"sa":"सुखं त्विदानीं त्रिविधं श्रृणु मे भरतर्षभ।अभ्यासाद्रमते यत्र दुःखान्तं च निगच्छति।।18.36।।","tr":"sukhaṁ tv idānīṁ tri-vidhaṁ śhṛiṇu me bharatarṣhabha\nabhyāsād ramate yatra duḥkhāntaṁ cha nigachchhati\n yat tad agre viṣham iva pariṇāme ‘mṛitopamam\ntat sukhaṁ sāttvikaṁ proktam ātma-buddhi-prasāda-jam","en":"And now, O Arjuna, hear from Me of the threefold pleasure, in which one rejoices through practice and surely comes to the end of pain.","es":"Now hear from Me, O scion of the Bharata dynasty, as regards the three kinds of joy: That in which one delights due to habit, and certainly attains the cessation of sorrows; [S. and S.S. take the second line of this verse along with the next verse referring to sattvika happiness.-Tr.]","er":"Now hear from Me, O Arjuna, the threefold division of pleasure৷৷ that in which one rejoices through long practice and in which one comes to the end of pain.","gu":"અને હવે, હે અર્જુન, મારી પાસેથી ત્રણ પ્રકારના સુખ વિષે સાંભળ, જેનો અભ્યાસ કરવાથી મનુષ્ય આનંદ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે અને દુઃખનો અંત પામે છે."},{"ref":"18.37","ch":18,"v":37,"sa":"यत्तदग्रे विषमिव परिणामेऽमृतोपमम्।तत्सुखं सात्त्विकं प्रोक्तमात्मबुद्धिप्रसादजम्।।18.37।।","tr":"yat tad agre viṣam iva pariṇāme 'mṛtopamam tat sukhaṁ sāttvikaṁ proktam ātma-buddhi-prasāda-jam","en":"That which is like poison at first but in the end like nectar—that happiness is declared to be sattvic, born of the purity of one's own mind due to self-realization.","es":"That which is like poison in the beginning, but is likened to nectar in the end, and which arises from the purity of one's intellect—that joy is spoken of as born of sattva.","er":"That which, at first, is like a poison but becomes like an elixir in the end, born from the serene state of mind focused on the Self—such pleasure is said to be Sattvika.","gu":"જે સુખ પ્રારંભમાં ઝેર જેવું લાગે છે પણ અંતે અમૃત સમાન બને છે — તે સ્વચ્છ મન અને બુદ્ધિની શુદ્ધિમાંથી, આત્મજ્ઞાનમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન થયેલ સુખ સાત્ત્વિક છે."},{"ref":"18.38","ch":18,"v":38,"sa":"विषयेन्द्रियसंयोगाद्यत्तदग्रेऽमृतोपमम्।परिणामे विषमिव तत्सुखं राजसं स्मृतम्।।18.38।।","tr":"viṣhayendriya-sanyogād yat tad agre ’mṛitopamam\npariṇāme viṣham iva tat sukhaṁ rājasaṁ smṛitam","en":"That happiness which arises from the contact of the senses with the objects, which is initially like nectar but eventually like poison, is said to be Rajasic.","es":"That joy is referred to as born of rajas, which, arising from the contact of the organs and their objects, is like nectar in the beginning but like poison in the end.","er":"That pleasure which arises from the contact of senses with their objects, which is like elixir at first but like poison in the end, is said to be Rajasic.","gu":"જે સુખ ઇન્દ્રિયો અને વિષયોના સંપર્કથી ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે, જે શરૂઆતમાં અમૃત સમાન પણ છેવટે ઝેર જેવું બની જાય છે — તે સુખ રાજસી કહેવાય છે."},{"ref":"18.39","ch":18,"v":39,"sa":"यदग्रे चानुबन्धे च सुखं मोहनमात्मनः।निद्रालस्यप्रमादोत्थं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम्।।18.39।।","tr":"yad agre chānubandhe cha sukhaṁ mohanam ātmanaḥ\nnidrālasya-pramādotthaṁ tat tāmasam udāhṛitam","en":"That happiness which at first, as well as in the end, deludes the self, and which arises from sleep, indolence, and heedlessness—that is declared to be Tamasic.","es":"That joy is said to be born of tamas, which, both in the beginning and in the end, is delusive to oneself and arises from sleep, laziness, and inadvertence.","er":"That pleasure which, at the beginning and end, deludes the self, through sleep, sloth, and error, is declared to be tamasic.","gu":"જે સુખ આત્માને આ અવસ્થામાં અને અંતે પણ મોહિત કરે છે, જે નિદ્રા, આળસ અને અસાવધાનીમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન થાય છે — તે સુખ તામસી છે."},{"ref":"18.40","ch":18,"v":40,"sa":"न तदस्ति पृथिव्यां वा दिवि देवेषु वा पुनः।सत्त्वं प्रकृतिजैर्मुक्तं यदेभिः स्यात्ित्रभिर्गुणैः।।18.40।।","tr":"na tad asti pṛithivyāṁ vā divi deveṣhu vā punaḥ\nsattvaṁ prakṛiti-jair muktaṁ yad ebhiḥ syāt tribhir guṇaiḥ","en":"There is no being on earth or in heaven among the gods that is liberated from the three qualities born of Nature.","es":"There is no entity in the world, nor among the gods in heaven, that can be free from these three gunas born of Nature.","er":"There is no creature, on earth or among the gods in heaven, that is exempt from these three Gunas born of Prakrti.","gu":"પૃથ્વી પર અથવા દેવો વચ્ચે સ્વર્ગમાં એવું કોઈ પ્રાણી નથી જે પ્રકૃતિમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન ત્રણ ગુણોથી મુક્ત હોય."},{"ref":"18.41","ch":18,"v":41,"sa":"ब्राह्मणक्षत्रियविशां शूद्राणां च परंतप।कर्माणि प्रविभक्तानि स्वभावप्रभवैर्गुणैः।।18.41।।","tr":"brāhmaṇa-kṣhatriya-viśhāṁ śhūdrāṇāṁ cha parantapa\nkarmāṇi pravibhaktāni svabhāva-prabhavair guṇaiḥ","en":"Of Brahmanas, Kshatriyas, Vaisyas, and Sudras, O Arjuna, the duties are distributed according to the qualities born of their own nature.","es":"O scorcher of enemies, the duties of the Brahmanas, Ksatriyas, Vaisyas, and Sudras have been fully classified according to the gunas born from Nature.","er":"The duties of the Brahmanas, Ksatriyas, Vaisyas, and Sudras are clearly divided, O Arjuna, according to their Gunas, born of their nature.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, બ્રાહ્મણ, ક્ષત્રિય, વૈશ્ય અને શૂદ્રના કર્તવ્યો તેમના પોતાના સ્વભાવમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન ગુણો અનુસાર વહેંચવામાં આવ્યા છે."},{"ref":"18.42","ch":18,"v":42,"sa":"शमो दमस्तपः शौचं क्षान्तिरार्जवमेव च।ज्ञानं विज्ञानमास्तिक्यं ब्रह्मकर्म स्वभावजम्।।18.42।।","tr":"śhamo damas tapaḥ śhauchaṁ kṣhāntir ārjavam eva cha\njñānaṁ vijñānam āstikyaṁ brahma-karma svabhāva-jam","en":"Serenity, self-restraint, austerity, purity, forgiveness, and uprightness, as well as knowledge, realization, and belief in God, are the duties of Brahmanas, born of their own nature.","es":"The natural duties of the Brahmanas are the control of the internal and external organs, austerity, purity, forgiveness, straightforwardness, knowledge, as well as wisdom [Knowledge refers to the understanding of subjects presented by the scriptures; wisdom means making them matters of one's own experience.], and faith.","er":"The control of the senses and mind, austerity, purity, forbearance, uprightness, knowledge, special knowledge, and faith—all these constitute the duty of a Brahmana, born of his inherent nature.","gu":"શાંતિ, આત્મસંયમ, તપ, પવિત્રતા, ક્ષમા, સરળતા, જ્ઞાન, અનુભવ અને ઈશ્વર પ્રત્યે શ્રદ્ધા — આ સ્વભાવ અનુસાર બ્રાહ્મણના કર્તવ્યો છે."},{"ref":"18.43","ch":18,"v":43,"sa":"शौर्यं तेजो धृतिर्दाक्ष्यं युद्धे चाप्यपलायनम्।दानमीश्वरभावश्च क्षात्रं कर्म स्वभावजम्।।18.43।।","tr":"śhauryaṁ tejo dhṛitir dākṣhyaṁ yuddhe chāpy apalāyanam\ndānam īśhvara-bhāvaśh cha kṣhātraṁ karma svabhāva-jam","en":"Prowess, splendor, firmness, dexterity, and not fleeing from battle, generosity, and lordliness are the duties of the Kshatriyas, born of their own nature.","es":"The natural duties of the Ksatriyas are heroism, boldness, fortitude, capability, and not retreating from battle, generosity, and lordliness.","er":"Valor, invincibility, steadiness, dexterity, and not fleeing in battle, generosity, and regality are the duties of a Kshatriya, born of his inherent nature.","gu":"શૌર્ય, તેજ, ધૈર્ય, કુશળતા, યુદ્ધમાંથી ન ભાગવું, ઉદારતા અને નેતૃત્વ — આ સ્વભાવ અનુસાર ક્ષત્રિયના કર્તવ્યો છે."},{"ref":"18.44","ch":18,"v":44,"sa":"कृषिगौरक्ष्यवाणिज्यं वैश्यकर्म स्वभावजम्।परिचर्यात्मकं कर्म शूद्रस्यापि स्वभावजम्।।18.44।।","tr":"kṛiṣhi-gau-rakṣhya-vāṇijyaṁ vaiśhya-karma svabhāva-jam\nparicharyātmakaṁ karma śhūdrasyāpi svabhāva-jam","en":"Agriculture, cattle-rearing, and trade are the duties of the Vaisya (merchant), born of their own nature; and service is the duty of the Sudra (servant-class), born of their own nature.","es":"The natural duties of the Vaisyas are agriculture, cattle-rearing, and trading. The natural duty of the Sudras, too, is in the form of service.","er":"Agriculture, cattle-breeding, and trade are the duties of the Vaisya, born of their nature. And the duty of a Sudra is one of service, born of their nature.","gu":"ખેતી, ગૌ-સેવા અને વ્યાપાર — આ સ્વભાવ અનુસાર વૈશ્યના કર્તવ્યો છે; અને સ્વભાવ અનુસાર શૂદ્રનું કર્તવ્ય સેવા છે."},{"ref":"18.45","ch":18,"v":45,"sa":"स्वे स्वे कर्मण्यभिरतः संसिद्धिं लभते नरः।स्वकर्मनिरतः सिद्धिं यथा विन्दति तच्छृणु।।18.45।।","tr":"sve sve karmaṇy abhirataḥ sansiddhiṁ labhate naraḥ\nsva-karma-nirataḥ siddhiṁ yathā vindati tach chhṛiṇu","en":"Each person devoted to their own duty attains perfection. How they attain perfection while being engaged in their own duty, hear now.","es":"Being devoted to his own duty, one attains complete success. Hear how one devoted to their own duty achieves success.","er":"Devoting oneself to one's duty, one attains perfection. Hear now how one devoted to their own duty attains perfection.","gu":"દરેક વ્યક્તિ પોતાના કર્તવ્ય પ્રત્યે સમર્પિત રહી સિદ્ધિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે. જે પ્રકારે પોતાના કર્તવ્ય પ્રત્યે સમર્પિત વ્યક્તિ સિદ્ધિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે, તે સાંભળ."},{"ref":"18.46","ch":18,"v":46,"sa":"यतः प्रवृत्तिर्भूतानां येन सर्वमिदं ततम्।स्वकर्मणा तमभ्यर्च्य सिद्धिं विन्दति मानवः।।18.46।।","tr":"yataḥ pravṛittir bhūtānāṁ yena sarvam idaṁ tatam\nsva-karmaṇā tam abhyarchya siddhiṁ vindati mānavaḥ","en":"He from whom all the beings have evolved and by whom all this is pervaded, worshipping Him with his own duty, one attains perfection.","es":"A human being achieves success by adoring, through his own duties, Him from whom is the origin of creatures and by whom all this is pervaded.","er":"From whom all beings arise and by whom all this is pervaded—by worshipping Him with one's own duty, one reaches perfection.","gu":"જેનાથી સર્વ પ્રાણીઓ ઉત્પન્ન થયા છે અને જેણે આ સઘળું વ્યાપ્ત કર્યું છે, તેની પોતાના કર્તવ્ય દ્વારા ઉપાસના કરીને મનુષ્ય સિદ્ધિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"18.47","ch":18,"v":47,"sa":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात्।स्वभावनियतं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम्।।18.47।।","tr":"śhreyān swa-dharmo viguṇaḥ para-dharmāt sv-anuṣhṭhitāt\nsvabhāva-niyataṁ karma kurvan nāpnoti kilbiṣham","en":"Better is one's own duty, even if it is destitute of merits, than the duty of another well performed. He who does the duty ordained by his own nature incurs no sin.","es":"One's own duty, though defective, is superior to another's duty well performed. By performing a duty according to one's own nature, one does not incur sin.","er":"Better is one's own duty, though ill done, than the duty of another, though well-performed. When one does the duty ordained by their own nature, they incur no stain.","gu":"ગુણરહિત હોવા છતાં પોતાનો ધર્મ શ્રેષ્ઠ છે, બીજાના સારી રીતે આચરેલા ધર્મ કરતાં; પોતાના સ્વભાવ પ્રમાણે નિર્ધારિત કર્તવ્ય કરનારને પાપ લાગતું નથી."},{"ref":"18.48","ch":18,"v":48,"sa":"सहजं कर्म कौन्तेय सदोषमपि न त्यजेत्।सर्वारम्भा हि दोषेण धूमेनाग्निरिवावृताः।।18.48।।","tr":"saha-jaṁ karma kaunteya sa-doṣham api na tyajet\nsarvārambhā hi doṣheṇa dhūmenāgnir ivāvṛitāḥ","en":"One should not, O Arjuna, abandon the duty to which one is born, though it may be faulty; for, all undertakings are enveloped by evil, just as fire is by smoke.","es":"O son of Kunti, one should not give up the duty to which one is born, even though it be imperfect. For all undertakings are surrounded by evil, as fire is with smoke.","er":"One should not relinquish one's work, O Arjuna, though it may be imperfect; for, all endeavors are enveloped by imperfections as fire is by smoke."},{"ref":"18.49","ch":18,"v":49,"sa":"असक्तबुद्धिः सर्वत्र जितात्मा विगतस्पृहः।नैष्कर्म्यसिद्धिं परमां संन्यासेनाधिगच्छति।।18.49।।","tr":"asakta-buddhiḥ sarvatra jitātmā vigata-spṛihaḥ\nnaiṣhkarmya-siddhiṁ paramāṁ sannyāsenādhigachchhati","en":"He whose intellect is unattached everywhere, who has subdued his self, from whom desire has fled, he attains the supreme state of freedom from action through renunciation.","es":"He whose intellect remains unattached to everything, who has conquered his internal organs and is desireless, attains through monasticism the supreme perfection consisting of the state of one free from duties.","er":"He whose understanding is unattached on all sides, whose self is controlled, who is free from desires—he attains the supreme perfection transcending all activity through renunciation.","gu":"જેની બુદ્ધિ સર્વત્ર અનાસક્ત છે, જેણે મનને વશ કર્યું છે, જેની ઇચ્છાઓ નષ્ટ થઈ ગઈ છે — સંન્યાસ દ્વારા તે ક્રિયારહિતતાની પરમ અવસ્થા પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"18.50","ch":18,"v":50,"sa":"सिद्धिं प्राप्तो यथा ब्रह्म तथाप्नोति निबोध मे।समासेनैव कौन्तेय निष्ठा ज्ञानस्य या परा।।18.50।।","tr":"siddhiṁ prāpto yathā brahma tathāpnoti nibodha me\nsamāsenaiva kaunteya niṣhṭhā jñānasya yā parā","en":"Learn from Me, O Arjuna, in brief how one who has attained perfection reaches Brahman—the Eternal, that supreme state of knowledge.","es":"Understand for certain from Me, in brief indeed, O son of Kunti, that process by which one who has achieved success attains Brahman, which is the supreme consummation of knowledge.","er":"Learn from me, O Arjuna, in brief how one who has attained perfection attains the Brahman—the supreme consummation of knowledge.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, જે સિદ્ધિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે તે બ્રહ્મ — જ્ઞાનની સર્વોચ્ચ અવસ્થા — કેવી રીતે પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે, તે મારી પાસેથી સંક્ષેપમાં જાણ."},{"ref":"18.51","ch":18,"v":51,"sa":"बुद्ध्या विशुद्धया युक्तो धृत्याऽऽत्मानं नियम्य च।शब्दादीन् विषयांस्त्यक्त्वा रागद्वेषौ व्युदस्य च।।18.51।।","tr":"buddhyā viśhuddhayā yukto dhṛityātmānaṁ niyamya cha\nśhabdādīn viṣhayāns tyaktvā rāga-dveṣhau vyudasya cha","en":"Endowed with a pure intellect, controlling the self through firmness, relinquishing sound and other objects and abandoning attraction and hatred.","es":"Endowed with a pure intellect and controlling oneself with fortitude, one should reject the objects beginning from sound [sound, touch, form, color, taste, and smell - Tr.] and eliminate attachment and hatred.","er":"Endowed with a purified understanding, subduing the mind with steadiness, relinquishing sound and other objects of the senses and casting aside love and hate;","gu":"શુદ્ધ બુદ્ધિ ધારણ કરીને, દૃઢ સંકલ્પ વડે આત્માને વશ રાખીને, શબ્દ આદિ વિષયોનો ત્યાગ કરીને, અને રાગ-દ્વેષ છોડીને —"},{"ref":"18.52","ch":18,"v":52,"sa":"विविक्तसेवी लघ्वाशी यतवाक्कायमानसः।ध्यानयोगपरो नित्यं वैराग्यं समुपाश्रितः।।18.52।।","tr":"vivikta-sevī laghv-āśhī yata-vāk-kāya-mānasaḥ\ndhyāna-yoga-paro nityaṁ vairāgyaṁ samupāśhritaḥ","en":"Dwelling in solitude, eating sparingly, with speech, body, and mind subdued, always engaged in meditation and concentration, and resorting to dispassion.","es":"One who resorts to solitude, eats sparingly, has control over their speech, body, and mind, for whom meditation and concentration are ever the highest duty, and who is possessed of dispassion;","er":"Resorting to solitude, eating sparingly, restraining speech, body, and mind, ever engaged in the yoga of meditation and taking refuge in dispassion;","gu":"એકાંતમાં વાસ કરીને, ઓછું ખાઈને, વાણી, શરીર અને મન સંયત રાખીને, સદા ધ્યાન અને સમાધિમાં રત રહીને, વૈરાગ્યનો આશ્રય લઈને —"},{"ref":"18.53","ch":18,"v":53,"sa":"अहङ्कारं बलं दर्पं कामं क्रोधं परिग्रहम्।विमुच्य निर्ममः शान्तो ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते।।18.53।।","tr":"ahankāraṁ balaṁ darpaṁ kāmaṁ krodhaṁ parigraham\nvimuchya nirmamaḥ śhānto brahma-bhūyāya kalpate","en":"Having abandoned egoism, strength, arrogance, desire, anger, and covetousness, and being free from the notion of 'mine' and peaceful, he is fit for becoming Brahman.","es":"Having discarded egotism, force, pride, desire, anger, and superfluous possessions, and being free from the idea of possession and serene, that person is fit for becoming Brahman.","er":"Forsaking egoism, power, pride, desire, wrath, and possessions, with no feeling of 'mine' and tranquil, he becomes worthy of the state of Brahman.","gu":"અહંકાર, બળ, ઘમંડ, કામ, ક્રોધ અને પરિગ્રહ છોડીને; 'મારું' ની ભાવનાથી મુક્ત થઈ, શાંત ચિત્તે — આ વ્યક્તિ બ્રહ્મ બનવાને યોગ્ય છે."},{"ref":"18.54","ch":18,"v":54,"sa":"ब्रह्मभूतः प्रसन्नात्मा न शोचति न काङ्क्षति।समः सर्वेषु भूतेषु मद्भक्तिं लभते पराम्।।18.54।।","tr":"brahma-bhūtaḥ prasannātmā na śhochati na kāṅkṣhati\nsamaḥ sarveṣhu bhūteṣhu mad-bhaktiṁ labhate parām","en":"Becoming Brahman, serene in the Self, he neither grieves nor desires; he is the same to all beings, and obtains supreme devotion to Me.","es":"One who has become Brahman and has attained the blissful Self does not grieve nor desire. Becoming the same towards all beings, he attains supreme devotion to Me.","er":"Having realized the state of Brahman, tranquil, he neither grieves nor craves. Regarding all beings alike, he attains supreme devotion to Me.","gu":"બ્રહ્મ સ્વરૂપ બનીને, આત્મામાં પ્રસન્ન થઈ, ન શોક કરે, ન ઇચ્છા કરે; સર્વ પ્રાણીઓ પ્રત્યે સમભાવ રાખી, મારી પરા ભક્તિ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"18.55","ch":18,"v":55,"sa":"भक्त्या मामभिजानाति यावान्यश्चास्मि तत्त्वतः।ततो मां तत्त्वतो ज्ञात्वा विशते तदनन्तरम्।।18.55।।","tr":"bhaktyā mām abhijānāti yāvān yaśh chāsmi tattvataḥ\ntato māṁ tattvato jñātvā viśhate tad-anantaram","en":"By devotion, he knows Me in truth, who and what I am; then, having known Me in truth, he immediately enters into the Supreme.","es":"Through devotion, he knows Me in reality, as to what and who I am. Then, having known Me truly, he enters into Me immediately afterward.","er":"Through devotion, he comes to know Me fully—who and what I am in reality, who I am and how I am. Knowing Me thus in truth, he forthwith enters into Me.","gu":"ભક્તિ વડે મને સત્ય સ્વરૂપે જાણી શકાય છે — હું કોણ છું અને શું છું; મને સાચી રીતે જાણ્યા પછી, ભક્ત તત્કાળ મારામાં પ્રવેશ પામે છે."},{"ref":"18.56","ch":18,"v":56,"sa":"सर्वकर्माण्यपि सदा कुर्वाणो मद्व्यपाश्रयः।मत्प्रसादादवाप्नोति शाश्वतं पदमव्ययम्।।18.56।।","tr":"sarva-karmāṇy api sadā kurvāṇo mad-vyapāśhrayaḥ\nmat-prasādād avāpnoti śhāśhvataṁ padam avyayam","en":"Having taken refuge in Me and doing all actions, by My grace he obtains the eternal, indestructible state of being.","es":"Ever engaging in all actions, one to whom I am the refuge, attains the eternal, immutable state through my grace.","er":"Taking refuge in Me and performing all works constantly, one, by My grace, attains the eternal and immutable abode.","gu":"સઘળાં કર્મો મારા આશ્રયે કરીને, મારી કૃપા વડે, ભક્ત શાશ્વત, અવિનાશી અવસ્થા પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"18.57","ch":18,"v":57,"sa":"चेतसा सर्वकर्माणि मयि संन्यस्य मत्परः।बुद्धियोगमुपाश्रित्य मच्चित्तः सततं भव।।18.57।।","tr":"chetasā sarva-karmāṇi mayi sannyasya mat-paraḥ\nbuddhi-yogam upāśhritya mach-chittaḥ satataṁ bhava","en":"Mentally renouncing all actions in Me, having Me as the highest goal, and resorting to the yoga of discrimination, do thou ever fix thy mind on Me.","es":"Mentally surrendering all actions to Me and accepting Me as the supreme, keep your mind ever fixed on Me by resorting to the concentration of your intellect.","er":"Surrender all your actions to Me with your mind, keep Me as your goal, and practice Buddhi-yoga, focusing your thoughts on Me always.","gu":"મનથી સઘળાં કર્મો મને અર્પણ કરી, મને પરમ ધ્યેય માની, ભેદ-વિવેકના યોગનો આશ્રય લઈ, સદૈવ તારું મન મારામાં સ્થિર કર."},{"ref":"18.58","ch":18,"v":58,"sa":"मच्चित्तः सर्वदुर्गाणि मत्प्रसादात्तरिष्यसि।अथ चेत्त्वमहङ्कारान्न श्रोष्यसि विनङ्क्ष्यसि।।18.58।।","tr":"mach-chittaḥ sarva-durgāṇi mat-prasādāt tariṣhyasi\natha chet tvam ahankārān na śhroṣhyasi vinaṅkṣhyasi","en":"Fixing your mind on Me, you shall, by My grace, overcome all obstacles; but if you will not hear Me due to egoism, you shall perish.","es":"Having your mind fixed on Me, you will cross over all difficulties by My grace. If, however, you do not listen out of egotism, you will be destroyed.","er":"Focusing your thoughts on Me, you shall, by My grace, cross over all difficulties. If, however, out of self-conceit, you do not heed Me, you will perish."},{"ref":"18.59","ch":18,"v":59,"sa":"यदहङ्कारमाश्रित्य न योत्स्य इति मन्यसे।मिथ्यैष व्यवसायस्ते प्रकृतिस्त्वां नियोक्ष्यति।।18.59।।","tr":"yad ahankāram āśhritya na yotsya iti manyase\nmithyaiṣha vyavasāyas te prakṛitis tvāṁ niyokṣhyati","en":"If, filled with egoism, thou thinkest, \"I will not fight,\" then thy resolve is vain; nature will compel thee.","es":"Though you think 'I shall not fight', relying on egotism, this determination of yours is vain. Your nature will impel you!","er":"If, in your self-conceit, you think, 'I will not fight,' your resolve is futile. Nature will compel you.","gu":"જો અહંકારથી ભરેલો 'હું નહીં લડું' એવો નિર્ણય કરે, તો તારો આ સંકલ્પ વ્યર્થ છે; તારી પ્રકૃતિ તને ફરજ પાડશે."},{"ref":"18.60","ch":18,"v":60,"sa":"स्वभावजेन कौन्तेय निबद्धः स्वेन कर्मणा।कर्तुं नेच्छसि यन्मोहात्करिष्यस्यवशोऽपि तत्।।18.60।।","tr":"swbhāva-jena kaunteya nibaddhaḥ svena karmaṇā\nkartuṁ nechchhasi yan mohāt kariṣhyasy avaśho ’pi tat","en":"O Arjuna, bound by your own Karma (action) born of your own nature, that which from delusion you wish not to do, even that you shall do helplessly.","es":"Being bound by your own duty, born of nature, O son of Kunti, you will, being helpless, verily do that which you do not wish to do, owing to indiscretion.","er":"O Arjuna, bound by your own duty born out of your own inner disposition, and having no control over your own will, you will be compelled to do that very thing which you now do not desire to do through delusion.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, તારી પ્રકૃતિમાંથી ઉત્પન્ન તારા કર્મ વડે બદ્ધ, ભ્રમ વશ તું જે ન કરવા ઇચ્છે, તે પણ તું પરવશ થઈ કરીશ."},{"ref":"18.61","ch":18,"v":61,"sa":"ईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां हृद्देशेऽर्जुन तिष्ठति।भ्रामयन्सर्वभूतानि यन्त्रारूढानि मायया।।18.61।।","tr":"īśhvaraḥ sarva-bhūtānāṁ hṛid-deśhe ‘rjuna tiṣhṭhati\nbhrāmayan sarva-bhūtāni yantrārūḍhāni māyayā","en":"The Lord dwells in the hearts of all beings, O Arjuna, causing all beings, by His illusory power, to revolve as if mounted on a machine.","es":"O Arjuna, the Lord resides in the region of the hearts of all creatures, revolving through Maya all the creatures as though mounted on a machine!","er":"The Lord, O Arjuna, abides in the heart of every being, spinning them round and round, as if mounted on a wheel, by His power.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, ઈશ્વર સઘળા પ્રાણીઓના હૃદયમાં વાસ કરે છે, પોતાની માયા-શક્તિ વડે સઘળા પ્રાણીઓને — જાણે યંત્ર પર સ્થિત હોય — ભ્રમાવે છે."},{"ref":"18.62","ch":18,"v":62,"sa":"तमेव शरणं गच्छ सर्वभावेन भारत।तत्प्रसादात्परां शान्तिं स्थानं प्राप्स्यसि शाश्वतम्।।18.62।।","tr":"tam eva śharaṇaṁ gachchha sarva-bhāvena bhārata\ntat-prasādāt parāṁ śhāntiṁ sthānaṁ prāpsyasi śhāśhvatam","en":"Fly to Him for refuge with all your being, O Arjuna; by His grace you will obtain supreme peace and the eternal abode.","es":"Take refuge in Him alone with your whole being, O scion of the Bharata dynasty. Through His grace, you will attain supreme peace and the eternal abode.","er":"Seek refuge in Him alone, O Arjuna, with the entirety of your being. By His grace, you shall find supreme peace and an eternal abode.","gu":"હે અર્જુન, સર્વ ભાવ વડે તેના જ શરણ જા; તેની કૃપા વડે તું પરમ શાંતિ અને શાશ્વત ધામ પ્રાપ્ત કરીશ."},{"ref":"18.63","ch":18,"v":63,"sa":"इति ते ज्ञानमाख्यातं गुह्याद्गुह्यतरं मया।विमृश्यैतदशेषेण यथेच्छसि तथा कुरु।।18.63।।","tr":"iti te jñānam ākhyātaṁ guhyād guhyataraṁ mayā\nvimṛiśhyaitad aśheṣheṇa yathechchhasi tathā kuru","en":"Thus, wisdom more secret than secrecy itself has been declared to you by me. Reflect on it fully, then act as you wish.","es":"To you I have imparted this knowledge, which is more secret than any secret. Ponder over this as a whole and do as you like.","er":"Thus, the knowledge, the mystery of mysteries, has been declared to you by Me. Reflecting on it fully, do as you will.","gu":"આ પ્રમાણે મેં તને બધા રહસ્યો કરતાં વધુ ગુહ્ય એવું જ્ઞાન કહ્યું — તું એને સારી રીતે વિચારી, પછી જેવી ઇચ્છા થાય તેવું કર."},{"ref":"18.64","ch":18,"v":64,"sa":"सर्वगुह्यतमं भूयः श्रृणु मे परमं वचः।इष्टोऽसि मे दृढमिति ततो वक्ष्यामि ते हितम्।।18.64।।","tr":"sarva-guhyatamaṁ bhūyaḥ śhṛiṇu me paramaṁ vachaḥ\niṣhṭo ‘si me dṛiḍham iti tato vakṣhyāmi te hitam","en":"Hear again My supreme word, most secret of all; for you are dearly beloved of Me, I will tell you what is good.","es":"Listen again to My highest utterance, which is the most profound of all. Since you are ever dear to Me, I shall speak what is beneficial to you.","er":"Hear again My supreme word, the most secret of all; as I am exceedingly fond of you, I am telling you what is good for you.","gu":"ફરી એક વાર સૌથી ગુહ્ય, મારો પરમ ઉપદેશ સાંભળ — તું મને અત્યંત પ્રિય છે, તેથી તારા ભલા માટે હું આ વાત કહું છું."},{"ref":"18.65","ch":18,"v":65,"sa":"मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु।मामेवैष्यसि सत्यं ते प्रतिजाने प्रियोऽसि मे।।18.65।।","tr":"man-manā bhava mad-bhakto mad-yājī māṁ namaskuru\nmām evaiṣhyasi satyaṁ te pratijāne priyo ‘si me","en":"Fix your mind on Me, be devoted to Me, sacrifice to Me, bow down to Me. You will come to Me; I truly promise you this, for you are dear to Me.","es":"Fix your mind on Me, be devoted to Me, offer sacrifices to Me, and bow down to Me. Thus, you will come to Me alone. I promise you this truth, for you are dear to Me.","er":"Focus your mind on Me. Be My devotee. Worship Me. Prostrate before Me. You will come to Me alone. I promise you truly; for you are dear to Me.","gu":"મારામાં મન લગાવ, મારો ભક્ત બન, મને પૂજ, મને પ્રણામ કર — તું મને જ પ્રાપ્ત થઈશ, આ હું તને સત્ય વચન આપું છું, કારણ કે તું મને પ્રિય છે."},{"ref":"18.66","ch":18,"v":66,"sa":"सर्वधर्मान्परित्यज्य मामेकं शरणं व्रज।अहं त्वा सर्वपापेभ्यो मोक्षयिष्यामि मा शुचः।।18.66।।","tr":"sarva-dharmān parityajya mām ekaṁ śharaṇaṁ vraja\nahaṁ tvāṁ sarva-pāpebhyo mokṣhayiṣhyāmi mā śhuchaḥ","en":"Abandon all duties and take refuge in Me alone; I will liberate you from all sins; do not grieve.","es":"Abandon all forms of rites and duties, and take refuge in Me alone. I will free you from all sins; do not grieve.","er":"Relinquishing all Dharmas completely, seek Me alone for refuge. I will release you from all sins; grieve not."},{"ref":"18.67","ch":18,"v":67,"sa":"इदं ते नातपस्काय नाभक्ताय कदाचन।न चाशुश्रूषवे वाच्यं न च मां योऽभ्यसूयति।।18.67।।","tr":"idaṁ te nātapaskyāya nābhaktāya kadāchana\nna chāśhuśhruṣhave vāchyaṁ na cha māṁ yo ‘bhyasūtayi","en":"Never speak this to one who is devoid of austerities or devotion, who does not render service, who does not desire to listen, or who cavils at Me.","es":"This (that I have taught) should never be taught to one who is devoid of austerities, one who is not a devotee, one who does not render service, or one who cavils at Me.","er":"Never should this be told by you to one who is not austere, who is not a devotee, nor to one who has no desire to listen, nor certainly to him who speaks ill of Me.","gu":"આ જ્ઞાન ક્યારેય એ વ્યક્તિને ન કહેવું જે તપ-ભક્તિ વિનાનો હોય, સેવા ન કરતો હોય, સાંભળવાની ઇચ્છા ન ધરાવતો હોય, અથવા જે મારી નિંદા કરતો હોય."},{"ref":"18.68","ch":18,"v":68,"sa":"य इमं परमं गुह्यं मद्भक्तेष्वभिधास्यति।भक्ितं मयि परां कृत्वा मामेवैष्यत्यसंशयः।।18.68।।","tr":"ya idaṁ paramaṁ guhyaṁ mad-bhakteṣhv abhidhāsyati\nbhaktiṁ mayi parāṁ kṛitvā mām evaiṣhyaty asanśhayaḥ","en":"He who, with supreme devotion to Me, teaches this supreme secret to My devotees, shall undoubtedly come to Me.","es":"He who, entertaining supreme devotion to Me, speaks of this highest secret to My devotees, will without doubt reach Me alone.","er":"He who proclaims this supreme mystery among My devotees shall come to Me, acquiring supreme devotion towards Me. There is no doubt about this.","gu":"જે વ્યક્તિ મારા ભક્તોને આ પરમ ગુહ્ય ઉપદેશ, મારા ઉત્કૃષ્ટ ભક્તિભાવ સાથે, ઉપદેશ આપે છે, તે નિઃશંક મને જ પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"18.69","ch":18,"v":69,"sa":"न च तस्मान्मनुष्येषु कश्िचन्मे प्रियकृत्तमः।भविता न च मे तस्मादन्यः प्रियतरो भुवि।।18.69।।","tr":"na cha tasmān manuṣhyeṣhu kaśhchin me priya-kṛittamaḥ\nbhavitā na cha me tasmād anyaḥ priyataro bhuvi","en":"There is no one among men who does service dearer to Me, nor shall there be anyone on earth dearer to Me than him.","es":"And compared to him, no other human is better at accomplishing what is dear to Me. Furthermore, there will be no one else in the world dearer to Me than him.","er":"There is no one among men who does dearer service to Me than him. Nor shall there be anyone on earth dearer to Me than him.","gu":"મનુષ્યોમાં એ વ્યક્તિ કરતાં મને વધુ પ્રિય સેવા કરનાર કોઈ નથી, અને ભવિષ્યમાં પૃથ્વી પર કોઈ એના કરતાં મને વધારે વ્હાલું નહીં હોય."},{"ref":"18.70","ch":18,"v":70,"sa":"अध्येष्यते च य इमं धर्म्यं संवादमावयोः।ज्ञानयज्ञेन तेनाहमिष्टः स्यामिति मे मतिः।।18.70।।","tr":"adhyeṣhyate cha ya imaṁ dharmyaṁ saṁvādam āvayoḥ\njñāna-yajñena tenāham iṣhṭaḥ syām iti me matiḥ","en":"And he who studies this sacred dialogue of ours, by him I shall have been worshipped through the sacrifice of wisdom; such is my conviction.","es":"And he who will study this sacred conversation between us two, which is conducive to virtue, by him I shall be adored through the Sacrifice of Knowledge. This is My judgment.","er":"And he who will study our dialogue, which is consistent with Dharma, by him I shall be worshipped through the sacrifice of knowledge; that is My view.","gu":"અને જે આ આપણા પવિત્ર સંવાદનો અભ્યાસ કરે છે, તે વ્યક્તિ દ્વારા જ્ઞાનયજ્ઞ વડે મારી ઉપાસના થઈ છે — એ મારો મત છે."},{"ref":"18.71","ch":18,"v":71,"sa":"श्रद्धावाननसूयश्च श्रृणुयादपि यो नरः।सोऽपि मुक्तः शुभाँल्लोकान्प्राप्नुयात्पुण्यकर्मणाम्।।18.71।।","tr":"śhraddhāvān anasūyaśh cha śhṛiṇuyād api yo naraḥ\nso ‘pi muktaḥ śhubhāl lokān prāpnuyāt puṇya-karmaṇām","en":"Also, the man who hears this, full of faith and free from malice, shall attain to the happy worlds of those of righteous deeds, and be liberated.","es":"Any man who, being reverent and free from caviling, listens to this (teaching) with reverence, he too, becoming free, shall attain the blessed worlds of those who perform virtuous deeds.","er":"And the man who listens to it with faith and without cavil, he too shall be released and shall reach the auspicious realms of those who have performed virtuous deeds.","gu":"જે વ્યક્તિ આ સંવાદ શ્રદ્ધા અને દ્વેષ વગર સાંભળે છે, તે પણ મુક્ત થઈ, પુણ્યકર્મ કરનારાઓના શ્રેષ્ઠ લોકોને પ્રાપ્ત કરે છે."},{"ref":"18.72","ch":18,"v":72,"sa":"कच्चिदेतच्छ्रुतं पार्थ त्वयैकाग्रेण चेतसा।कच्चिदज्ञानसंमोहः प्रनष्टस्ते धनञ्जय।।18.72।।","tr":"kachchid etach chhrutaṁ pārtha tvayaikāgreṇa chetasā\nkachchid ajñāna-sammohaḥ pranaṣhṭas te dhanañjaya","en":"Has this been heard, O Arjuna, with one-pointed focus? Has the delusion of your ignorance been destroyed, O Dhananjaya?","es":"O Partha, have you listened to this with a one-pointed mind? O Dhananjaya, has your delusion caused by ignorance been dispelled?","er":"Have you heard this, O Arjuna, with a single-minded focus? Has your delusion, caused by ignorance, been dispelled?","gu":"હે અર્જુન, શું તેં આ એકચિત્તે સાંભળ્યું? હે ધનંજય, શું અજ્ઞાનથી ઉત્પન્ન તારો ભ્રમ નષ્ટ થઈ ગયો?"},{"ref":"18.73","ch":18,"v":73,"sa":"अर्जुन उवाचनष्टो मोहः स्मृतिर्लब्धा त्वत्प्रसादान्मयाच्युत।स्थितोऽस्मि गतसन्देहः करिष्ये वचनं तव।।18.73।।","tr":"arjuna uvācha\nnaṣhṭo mohaḥ smṛitir labdhā tvat-prasādān mayāchyuta\nsthito ‘smi gata-sandehaḥ kariṣhye vachanaṁ tava","en":"Arjuna said, \"My delusion has been destroyed, for I have gained my knowledge (memory) through Your grace, O Krishna. I am now free from doubts. I will act according to Your word.\"","es":"Arjuna said, \"O Acyuta, my delusion has been destroyed and my memory has been regained through Your grace. I stand with my doubt removed; I shall follow Your instructions.\"","er":"Arjuna said, \"My delusion has been destroyed, and, by Your grace, O Krsna, I have gained knowledge (Smrti). Freed from doubts, I stand steadfast, and I will fulfill Your will.\"","gu":"અર્જુન બોલ્યા: હે કૃષ્ણ, આપની કૃપાથી મારો ભ્રમ નષ્ટ થઈ ગયો અને મને સ્મૃતિ પ્રાપ્ત થઈ — હું સ્થિર છું, મારો સંશય ગયો; હું આપના વચન પ્રમાણે કાર્ય કરીશ."},{"ref":"18.74","ch":18,"v":74,"sa":"सञ्जय उवाचइत्यहं वासुदेवस्य पार्थस्य च महात्मनः।संवादमिममश्रौषमद्भुतं रोमहर्षणम्।।18.74।।","tr":"sañjaya uvācha\nity ahaṁ vāsudevasya pārthasya cha mahātmanaḥ\nsaṁvādam imam aśhrauṣham adbhutaṁ roma-harṣhaṇam","en":"Sanjaya said, Thus, I have heard this wonderful dialogue between Krishna and the high-souled Arjuna, which causes one's hair to stand on end.","es":"Sanjaya said, \"I thus heard this conversation between Vasudeva and the great-souled Partha, which is unique and makes one's hair stand on end.\"","er":"Sanjaya said, Thus I have heard this wondrous dialogue between Vasudeva and the great-minded Arjuna, which makes my hair stand on end.","gu":"સંજય બોલ્યા: આ પ્રમાણે મેં શ્રીકૃષ્ણ અને મહાત્મા અર્જુન વચ્ચેનો આ અદ્ભુત, રોમાંચ ઉત્પન્ન કરનારો સંવાદ સાંભળ્યો."},{"ref":"18.75","ch":18,"v":75,"sa":"व्यासप्रसादाच्छ्रुतवानेतद्गुह्यमहं परम्।योगं योगेश्वरात्कृष्णात्साक्षात्कथयतः स्वयम्।।18.75।।","tr":"vyāsa-prasādāch chhrutavān etad guhyam ahaṁ param\nyogaṁ yogeśhvarāt kṛiṣhṇāt sākṣhāt kathayataḥ svayam","en":"Through the grace of Vyasa, I have heard this supreme and most secret Yoga, directly from Krishna, the Lord of Yoga, Himself declaring it.","es":"Through the favor of Vyasa, I heard this secret concerning the supreme Yoga from Krishna, the Lord of Yogas, while He Himself was speaking!","er":"By the grace of Vyasa, I have heard this supreme mystery of Yoga, declared in person by Krsna, the Lord of Yoga.","gu":"વ્યાસ મહર્ષિની કૃપાથી, સ્વયં યોગેશ્વર ભગવાન શ્રીકૃષ્ણ પાસેથી સીધો, આ પરમ ગુહ્ય અને ઉત્કૃષ્ટ યોગ મેં સાંભળ્યો."},{"ref":"18.76","ch":18,"v":76,"sa":"राजन्संस्मृत्य संस्मृत्य संवादमिममद्भुतम्।केशवार्जुनयोः पुण्यं हृष्यामि च मुहुर्मुहुः।।18.76।।","tr":"rājan sansmṛitya sansmṛitya saṁvādam imam adbhutam\nkeśhavārjunayoḥ puṇyaṁ hṛiṣhyāmi cha muhur muhuḥ","en":"O King, remembering this wonderful and holy dialogue between Krishna and Arjuna, I continually rejoice.","es":"And, O King, while repeatedly remembering this unique, sacred dialogue between Kesava and Arjuna, I rejoice every moment.","er":"O King, remembering again and again this wondrous and auspicious dialogue between Sri Krishna and Arjuna, I rejoice time and again.","gu":"હે રાજન, શ્રીકૃષ્ણ અને અર્જુન વચ્ચેના આ અદ્ભુત અને પવિત્ર સંવાદને વારંવાર સ્મરણ કરી, હું વારંવાર આનંદ અનુભવું છું."},{"ref":"18.77","ch":18,"v":77,"sa":"तच्च संस्मृत्य संस्मृत्य रूपमत्यद्भुतं हरेः।\nविस्मयो मे महान् राजन् हृष्यामि च पुनः पुनः।।18.77।।","tr":"tach cha sansmṛitya saṁsmṛitya rūpam aty-adbhutaṁ hareḥ\nvismayo ye mahān rājan hṛiṣhyāmi cha punaḥ punaḥ","en":"And, remembering again and again that most wonderful form of Hari, I am filled with great wonder, O King; and I rejoice again and again.","es":"O King, repeatedly recollecting that greatly extraordinary form of Hari, I am struck with wonder and rejoice again and again.","er":"And, remembering over and over again that most marvelous form of Hari, great is my amazement, O King, and I rejoice again and again.","gu":"અને હે રાજન, ભગવાન હરિના તે અત્યંત અદ્ભુત વિશ્વરૂપને વારંવાર સ્મરણ કરી, મારો આશ્ચર્ય ઘણો મોટો છે, અને હું વારંવાર આનંદ અનુભવું છું."},{"ref":"18.78","ch":18,"v":78,"sa":"यत्र योगेश्वरः कृष्णो यत्र पार्थो धनुर्धरः।\nतत्र श्रीर्विजयो भूतिर्ध्रुवा नीतिर्मतिर्मम।।18.78।","tr":"yatra yogeśhvaraḥ kṛiṣhṇo yatra pārtho dhanur-dharaḥ\ntatra śhrīr vijayo bhūtir dhruvā nītir matir mama","en":"Wherever Krishna, the Lord of Yoga, is; and wherever Arjuna, the wielder of the bow, is; there is prosperity, victory, happiness, and a firm policy; this is my conviction.","es":"Where there is Krishna, the Lord of yogas, and where there is Partha, the wielder of the bow, there is fortune, victory, prosperity, and unfailing prudence. Such is my conviction.","er":"Wherever there is Sri Krsna, the Lord of Yoga, and Arjuna the archer, there is always fortune, victory, wealth, and sound morality. This is my firm conviction."}];

